66eaca3d434416cd1bd18050,Stephen Njoku,+23408034093719,chidi_stephen@yahoo.com,Nigeria,"Plot 1, 3, 5, Sir Sam Ihionu Avenue,\nNkpikpa Layout,Onitsha – Owerri Road,\nOnitsha, Anambra State.\nSeptember 18, 2024.\nhttps://www.linkedin.com/in/njoku-stephen-25491a65/\nDear Sir,                                                                                  \nApplication for the Post of “Finance Manager – Remote (Nigeria)”\nI humbly wish to apply for the above stated position in your organization as advertised. \nI have worked in Oil and Gas, Manufacturing, Transport, Logistics, Hospitality and Power/Energy sectors as Project/Senior Accountant/Internal Auditor/Cost Controller/Supply Chain/Warehouse Management/Operations Manager/Treasury Manager/Finance & Admin as can be verified in my accompanying CV, cumulatively for over 15 years. I have excellent organizational skills, a keen eye for detail, and the ability to handle multiple administrative tasks efficiently.\nPlease my strength lies in below competencies and skills:\n•	Demonstrated communication, presentation and organizational skills.\n•	Strong project coordination skills.\n•	Flexibility and ability to multi-task under pressure and meet deadlines.\n•	Proven ability to work creatively and independently both in the field and in the office.\n•	Advanced proficiency in written and spoken English.\n•	Ability to work well with a diverse group of partners both local and international.\n•	Good ICT skills in Microsoft word, Excel and power point.\n•	Track record of showing proactivity and leadership\n•	Proven ability to interact effectively with a broad range of internal and external partners, including international organizations, government officials, and NGO counterparts.\n•	Experience of using communications professionally to promote organizations.\nMy candid commitment to duties if given the opportunity will not be in doubt with a notice period of one month.\n\nThanks for your strict confidentiality.\n\n\nYours faithfully\nNJOKU STEPHEN CHIDI.\nTel. +2348034093719.    \n",https://www.linkedin.com/in/njoku-stephen-25491a65/,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1726663227225_Njoku Resume 2.pdf,66e3fe18acb6dc9af303e69f,Financial Manager,2024-09-18T12:40:29.625Z,2024-09-18T12:40:29.625Z,,,,,,,,,
66eaca60434416cd1bd18055,Ephraim Idenyi,+23408142302171,Ephraimidemyi@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I'm a 11 years experience professional in accounting and finance . \nI worked at A T Folowosele & Associate an accounting firm of chartered accountants were I learnt and performed several task including tax, auditing, financial analysis which includes investment appraisal financial research and financial analytics. In my time working  at A T F, some of our client  were in the banking and financial sector, public sector, listed companies, companies opening new branches, non governmental organisations especially humanitarian organisations were we performed services like payroll, cost, project analysis and audit. The experience gave me an insight of these agencies and companies to which I had to gain basic understanding of their business sector even before providing them services. I worked there from November 2013 to April 2016. \nI also worked at Transcorp Hilton Hotel Abuja from May 2016 to November 2020. I worked in internal control as an o finance supervisor and income auditor. This included daily, weekly and monthly  revenue and inventory analysis, resource control, cost analysis, operational audit and other internal control task. During this time I learnt how to manage operations under pressure as I was a supervisor for over 4 years. I was a  middle man between operations staff and management were I reported to management on how operations were going and also forwarded and ensured the implementation of management policies including budget and internal control. I used a few accounting software's during this time most notable Oracle ERP which is a centralised software with several functions.\nI’ve worked at Green Acres Hospital Abuja as the finance manager and accountant for over 2 years from March 2021 till present. During this time, I’ve assisted in implementing new control procedures as the company has been transitioning from a small hospital to an expanding hospital. I give long term investment advise to owners, do performance evaluation, cost analysis and long-term budget for the company. This is along with my daily work of supervising operations, recording transactions, preparing monthly financial statement, implementation of control processes. I’ve introduced and used integrated system which included an accounting and inventory function and management information system.\nI work as a General Manager at Legend Internet Limited. As the General Manager, I’m the acting CFO. I oversee the Finance Department. This means I’m responsible for financing options, investment assessments and control process especially when it comes to budget. I take part in strategy creation and implementation.\nI’m ACCA qualified.\nMy skills includes good use of several accounting software's, Microsoft word, PowerPoint, excel. Working well under pressure, great knowledge of accounting standards and tax laws, great abilities in implementation of internal control rules, team player and a good team leader, a great listener, professional competence and integrity.",https://www.linkedin.com/in/ephraim-idenyi-b1626a80?utm_source=share&utm_campaign=share_via&utm_content=profile&utm_medium=ios_app,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1726663261577_Main main CV.docx,66e3fe18acb6dc9af303e69f,Financial Manager,2024-09-18T12:41:04.677Z,2024-09-18T12:41:04.677Z,,,,,,,,,
