67123842cb112788c38cae1f,Ikechukwu Oyibo ,+2348055608145,i_oyibo@yahoo.com,Nigeria,"My name is Ikechukwu Oyibo, from Delta State, Nigeria. I live at 10 Egole Dichie Avenue Rock Stone Ville Estate Bakery Badore Ajah. I have worked as a finance executive trainee at Initiative Finance Limited where I performed excellently well. I have also worked as a sale clerk and also a teller in intercontinental bank now Access bank. I look forward to joining your five star team to contribute to the growth of the organization and also I am open to learning new things. Thank you.",,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1729247296423_Oyibo Ikechukwu CV-1-1.docx,67113e3ecb112788c38cad6a,Financial Analyst Intern,2024-10-18T10:28:18.549Z,2024-10-18T10:28:18.549Z,,,,,,,,,
67123c78cb112788c38cae27,Queen Onyeulo,+2348147525961,nnennaonyeulo@gmail.com,Nigeria,"My name is Queen Onyeulo, a graduate of Bsc. Accounting from the University of Lagos.\n\nI discovered my passion for Finance in 2022 during my Service year, where I volunteered as the Financial Secretary and Junior Account Officer in NGO organizations. I realized the importance of understanding numbers and money for sustainability and growth.\n\nI have a career prospect in Financial Advisory and I believe that this program will help me understand what is required of me.\n\nThank you.",,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1729248373799_queen's cv.pdf,67113e3ecb112788c38cad6a,Financial Analyst Intern,2024-10-18T10:46:16.345Z,2024-10-18T10:46:16.345Z,,,,,,,,,
67123d04cb112788c38cae2c,OLABANJI SUNDAY DARAMOLA,+2348068568151,okikioluwa2016@gmail.com,Nigeria,"Dynamic Chartered Accountant with over 7 years of expertise in auditing, account management, asset management, compliance, risk management, investigation, and internal control. Committed to providing technical support to enhance productivity, ensuring operational objectives are met and exceeded.\n\nAREAS OF EXPERTISE\nProficient in diverse software, ensuring seamless financial operations. Microsoft Office is utilized for data analysis and effective communication. Adept in Sage 300 ERP and Sage X3, managing complex financial processes is a forte. Additionally, my expertise extends to Busy Accounting Software, SAP IVEND Till Management, Dolphin SAP, and CaseWare Auditing Software for enhanced financial control. Key financial domains covered include Financial Reporting, Strategic Business Reviews, Financial Analysis, Profitability Analysis, and Cash Management, ensuring optimal economic performance and strategic decision-making.\n",https://www.linkedin.com/in/olabanji-daramola-aca-0b4b9713a/,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1729248514026_OLABANJI DARAMOLA RESUME 2024 NEW PDF.pdf,67113e3ecb112788c38cad6a,Financial Analyst Intern,2024-10-18T10:48:36.540Z,2024-10-18T10:48:36.540Z,,,,,,,,,
67123f5fcb112788c38cae4b,Muyiwa Omowunmi Kafayat,+2348115421976,muyiwaomowunmikafayat@gmail.com,Nigeria,"A detail-oriented professional with strong analytical and problem-solving skills, I excel in collaborative settings to ensure regulatory compliance and drive organizational success. I possess proven expertise in management, focusing on financial accounting, risk management, and compliance. With excellent organizational and interpersonal skills, I am eager to leverage my knowledge of auditing and KYC to transition into a finance role within a financial institution.",,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1729249117243_Omowunmi Muyiwa - Full CV.pdf,67113e3ecb112788c38cad6a,Financial Analyst Intern,2024-10-18T10:58:39.524Z,2024-10-18T10:58:39.524Z,,,,,,,,,
6712400dcb112788c38cae53,Esther Blessing,+23407036538747,estheradeola539@gmail.com,Nigeria,"Dear Hiring Manager,\n\nI hope you are doing well. My name is Esther Adeola, and I am writing to express my interest in the Finance Analyst Internship position. I hold a degree in Economics from Osun State University, and I have developed a passion for finance, data analysis, and reporting through both my academic journey and hands-on experiences.\n\nDuring my time as a volunteer at Skillup Life, I gained valuable experience analyzing financial statements, preparing reports, and assisting in investment planning. I have also honed my skills in SQL, Excel, and data visualization through various projects, allowing me to deliver accurate financial insights. I am particularly drawn to this internship because it aligns with my career goal of becoming a skilled financial analyst and offers the opportunity to apply my knowledge while learning from industry experts.\n\nI am excited about the prospect of joining your team to contribute my skills and grow within the finance industry. I would be thrilled to discuss how I can bring value to your organization in more detail.\n\nThank you for considering my application. I look forward to your response.\n\nBest regards,\nEsther Adeola",http://be.net/estheradeola23,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1729249290745_ESTHER ADEOLA BLESSING.pdf,67113e3ecb112788c38cad6a,Financial Analyst Intern,2024-10-18T11:01:33.333Z,2024-10-18T11:01:33.333Z,,,,,,,,,
67124060cb112788c38cae5b,Sobowale Oluwafunmibi Grace,+2349028092228,oluwafunmibisobowale@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I'm Oluwafunmibi, a skilled accountant who has a deep interest in process optimization, financial analysis and business analysis. I've demonstrated success in developing and implementing Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs) for financial operations, assuring revenue, and preparing comprehensive financial reports. I've developed my analytical abilities throughout my profession by gaining useful expertise in cash flow management, inventory tracking, and account reconciliation.\n\nIn my current role at N.A.C.K Apparel, a fashion retail and manufacturing company, I play a key part in managing financial operations, including reconciling bank statements and ledgers, ensuring accurate financial reporting, and developing systems to monitor and improve operational efficiency.\n\nI am committed to continuous learning and professional development, and I am actively pursuing more certifications and roles to improve my financial analysis skills.\n\nOutside of my professional life, I enjoy playing chess and watching crime movies. Both activities challenge my strategic thinking and problem-solving skills, which I find valuable not only in my personal life but also in my approach to financial analysis.\n\nI am excited to apply my skills and analytical mindset in a finance analyst role, where I can contribute to informed decision-making and optimize financial processes that drive organizational growth.",www.linkedin.com/in/oluwafunmibisobowale,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1729249374041_Grace Oluwafunmibi Sobowale Resume for Financial Analyst Intern.pdf,67113e3ecb112788c38cad6a,Financial Analyst Intern,2024-10-18T11:02:56.245Z,2024-10-18T11:02:56.245Z,,,,,,,,,
