671246e2cb112788c38cae85,Evelyn Ikerekhalu (Inegbenije),+2347038058424,evelynikerekhalu@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am an enthusiastic, passionate, and committed goal-getter. Although I earned my degree in Actuarial Science and hold a diploma in Accounting, I have been able to leverage both skills by continually developing myself through various online courses in accounting, finance, work ethics, experience, and work productivity. One of such certifications is from the McKinsey Forward program.\n\nMy quest for innovation and excellent service led me to develop skills in using AI to address challenges in finance and accounting, such as automating repetitive tasks and monitoring data. Through my experience with the ALX program, supported by Mastercard’s AI Career Essentials, I recognized great opportunities for optimization, efficiency, and time management, which can be directed toward data analysis, reporting, and data visualization for better decision-making, as well as using market trends for financial decisions.\n\nI am interested in this role because I have been with Kitovu for over four years, and our financial records are primarily centered around agriculture, technology, and finance. To enhance productivity and growth, diversity is essential. I firmly believe we grow when we invest in skills and experience and conquer new milestones. I believe i will contribute to Tobams, Even as Tobams will create an environment for growth, new skill set and experience for me.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n",https://www.linkedin.com/in/evelyn-inegbenije/,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1729251039975_Evelyn's Resume profile -pdf.pdf,67113e3ecb112788c38cad6a,Financial Analyst Intern,2024-10-18T11:30:42.733Z,2024-10-18T11:30:42.733Z,,,,,,,,,
