67128455cb112788c38cafc4,Iheanacho Mary,+2348151340842,mary.iheanacho007@gmail.com,Nigeria,"\nI am a certified chartered accountant ACA with a BSc in Accounting and Finance from Landmark University in Nigeria.\n\nI am confident that my attention to detail, analytical mindset, and strong communication skills make me a suitable candidate for this role.\n\nI have attached my Curriculum Vitae for your review, which outlines my academic qualifications, relevant experience, and key achievements. I am eager to further discuss how my background and skills align with the requirements in your firm. \n\nI am excited at the prospect of bringing my skill and experience. I look forward to hearing from you at your earliest convenience, to discuss how my experience will prove valuable to this role.\nThank you for your time and consideration.\nWarm regards,\n\nIHEANACHO MARY\n+2348151340842",,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1729266771352_IHEANACHO CHIBUZOR MARY - CV (1).pdf,67113e3ecb112788c38cad6a,Financial Analyst Intern,2024-10-18T15:52:53.893Z,2024-10-18T15:52:53.893Z,,,,,,,,,
67128470cb112788c38cafca,Aribisala Aanuoluwapo Jemimah,+2349165470132,aribisalaaanuoluwapo583@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am excited to submit my application for the role of Financial Analyst. Throughout my academic journey and research work, I have developed a solid foundation in financial analysis, statistical knowledge, and data analytics, along with some coding skills. During my four years at the Federal University of Agriculture, Abeokuta, I gained a comprehensive understanding of financial principles and accrual data. I also applied various tools, such as R programming, Microsoft Excel, Power BI, and the Statistical Package for Social Sciences (SPSS), to conduct financial analysis and data management. Additionally, I have experience using LaTeX for presenting complex financial data and reports. Earlier this year, I further enhanced my skills by completing an online course on Coursera, focusing on data analysis. This course covered topics such as financial data repositories, data wrangling, Relational Database Management Systems (RDBMS), and Structured Query Languages (SQL). My internship at Meri Skills also provided me with hands-on experience in financial analysis using Power BI, Microsoft Excel, and Tableau, allowing me to deepen my knowledge in financial modeling and forecasting. I am confident that I can make a meaningful contribution to the financial analysis team, leveraging my attention to detail and strong analytical skills to help the company maintain its competitive edge. I am eager to apply my financial expertise and develop my skills further in a real-world setting. I look forward to the opportunity to discuss how I can contribute to your team.",,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1729266798209_Jemimah Aribisala 2.pdf,67113e3ecb112788c38cad6a,Financial Analyst Intern,2024-10-18T15:53:20.891Z,2024-10-18T15:53:20.891Z,,,,,,,,,
