67128a9dcb112788c38cb00b,Emmanuel Aiyerogbon,+23408131028565,emmanuelaiyerogbon@gmail.com,Nigeria,"Dear Hiring Manager,\n\nAll roads lead to becoming a valuable professional and to help create and build a better and positive change in the world. I am writing to express my interest in the role of a finance intern.\n\nI obtained a Bachelor of Science (B.Sc.) degree in Accounting from Federal University, Oye-Ekiti, Ekiti, Nigeria, with a Second Class Upper (4.16). I am an associate member of the Institute of Chartered Accountant of Nigeria (ICAN) and Accounting Technician Scheme (ICAN/ATS).\n\nRegarding work experience, I work as an account payables associate at Lafarge Africa Plc, where all discrepancies with suppliers/vendors are settled. I play a key role in the department, among many others.\n\nI previously worked as a finance analyst at Indicina Technologies Limited. I was saddled with preparing monthly management reports, bank reconciliation, and creating invoices on QuickBooks, among many others. I also developed a model for Indicina to analyze monthly variances for each department. I was regarded as a first-rate employee by my manager (before she left) having acknowledged the impact of my work and presence in the department.\n\nI became the set man of the finance team at Indicina within the space of 10 months on the recommendation of the CEO after seeing the impact of my enthusiasm and dedication on the finance team and the company as a whole.\n\nDuring my undergraduate studies, I have led in various capacities. I represented my department in the Accounting Student Representative Council (ASRC) where I was made the Head of Budget and Finance for the Council. Also, I led a group of 15 members to do a presentation on a business case study and also led a team of 20 students to write an article suitable for publication. I was one of the departmental tutors during my 300 and 400 level.\n\nI have assisted quite a number of undergraduate and master students in the analysis and interpretation of data for their projects using SPSS and E-views. In carrying out these responsibilities, I demonstrated emotional intelligence, analytical skills, research skills, communication skills, time management, presentation skills, problem solving, team collaboration, critical thinking, interpersonal relationship, peer tutoring, among others. \n\nFurthermore, I am delighted to mention that I was a top-10 finalist at the EY Young Tax Professional of the Year 2023 Competition and also a 3 times recipient of the National Merit Scholarship Award by TotalEnergies Nigeria Limited.\n\nI do not doubt that I will become a first-rate employee at the firm and a valuable professional that brings a better change to the world in the years to come if I am given the required opportunity and platform to grow. I am sure I will bring a lot of progress to the team.\n\nThank you in advance for considering my application. I look forward to hearing from you soon and discussing how I can contribute to your team.\n\nBest regards, \nEmmanuel Aiyerogbon.",,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1729268378766_Emmanuel Aiyerogbon CV.pdf,67113e3ecb112788c38cad6a,Financial Analyst Intern,2024-10-18T16:19:41.459Z,2024-10-18T16:19:41.459Z,,,,,,,,,
67128c3ecb112788c38cb018,Ridwanulahi Ayomide Animasahun,+23408111249522,ridwanulahianimasahun@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am a passionate, all-round individual with a diverse range of interests and experiences. I find immense joy in exploring various cultures and gaining a deeper appreciation for the world's diversity.\nI also enjoy writing and speaking, which I have honed through involvement in the Nigerian Economics Students Association, where I served as a volunteer tutor and chairman of the Debating Society. These roles allowed me to craft compelling arguments and engage in thought-provoking discussions.\nMy proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite and Python programming, coupled with my professional accounting and finance trainings (ACA and CFA Level 1), has equipped me with valuable technical skills, facilitating my role as a  analyst and content writer for the Student Investment Society at my university.\nMy active involvement in student organisations like the developer’s community, the Hult Prize Foundation, and leadership roles underscores my dedication to personal growth and community engagement.",,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1729268796099_Ridwanulahi Animasahun Resume_S.pdf,67113e3ecb112788c38cad6a,Financial Analyst Intern,2024-10-18T16:26:38.473Z,2024-10-18T16:26:38.473Z,,,,,,,,,
