67129366cb112788c38cb040,Ikilizi Mefue Shekinah,+2347082636675,ikilizimefueshekinah@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am a passionate and motivated individual who has recently completed comprehensive training in data analysis, with a strong desire to apply my skills and contribute to your team.\nDuring my training, I gained a solid foundation in various data analysis tools and techniques, including Excel, SQL, Python, R, Tableau, IBM SPSS, PowerBI. I have also developed a keen understanding of data cleaning, data visualization, and statistical analysis. Although I am at the beginning of my career, I am eager to leverage my knowledge and enthusiasm to make meaningful contributions to your organization.\nEnclosed is my CV, which provides further details about my education, skills, and training. I am confident that my proactive attitude, willingness to learn, and ability to adapt quickly will enable me to effectively support data analysis projects at your organization.\nI believe I am prepared to handle the exciting challenges this position presents and I am elated about the opportunity to discuss how my background, training, and enthusiasm for data analysis align with the goals of your organization. Thank you for considering my application. I look forward to the possibility of contributing to your team and growing as a data analyst. ",https://www.linkedin.com/posts/shekinah-ikilizi-868431267_enhancing-employee-well-being-insights-from-activity-7245329560580329473-whyE?utm_source=share&utm_medium=member_ios,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1729270627606_Ikilizi Mefue Shekinah's cv.pdf,67113e3ecb112788c38cad6a,Financial Analyst Intern,2024-10-18T16:57:10.315Z,2024-10-18T16:57:10.315Z,,,,,,,,,
67129469cb112788c38cb048,Chibuzor Caleb ,+2348062938865,chibuzorcaleb65@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I'm a finance and data analytics professional with an academic background in Financial Management Technology passionate about using technology to drive growth, increase profit, and mitigate risks for organizations. \nI have experience  in financial and data analysis using tools like  Excel, PowerBI, and SQL.\nI'm a certified Financial Modelling and Valuation Analyst (FMVA) and Business Intelligence and Data Analyst (BIDA) with Coorparate Finance Institute (CFI)",https://mavenanalytics.io/profile/Chibuzor-Caleb/172554848,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1729270886968_Chibuzor_Caleb-CV.pdf,67113e3ecb112788c38cad6a,Financial Analyst Intern,2024-10-18T17:01:29.560Z,2024-10-18T17:01:29.560Z,,,,,,,,,
671294e9cb112788c38cb04d,Adekunle rihannat,+2348130893925,adekunlerihannat@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am a driven aspiring data analyst with a  foundation in statistical analysis, which I believe closely aligns with the core skills needed in financial analysis. Through my hands-on experience in data analysis, I have developed proficiency in analyzing complex datasets, identifying trends, and delivering insights that support decision-making. My ability to work with statistical tools and methodologies has equipped me with a keen eye for detail and the ability to interpret data accurately-skills that are crucial in financial forecasting and market analysis. I am eager to apply this experience and my passion for numbers to a financial analyst role, where I can grow, learn and contribute meaningfully.",https://github.com/RihannatAdekunle,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1729271014867_Adekunle RIhannat CV Pdf.pdf,67113e3ecb112788c38cad6a,Financial Analyst Intern,2024-10-18T17:03:37.753Z,2024-10-18T17:03:37.753Z,,,,,,,,,
67129661cb112788c38cb053,Olusola Agbojo,+2348165588490,olusolaentheous@gmail.com,Nigeria,"Dear Hiring Manager,\nI am excited to apply for the Financial Anaylst Intern position at Tobams Group, as advertised. With a robust background in sales, financial market analysis, and relationship management, coupled with a strong proficiency in identifying and capitalizing on new business opportunities, I am confident in my ability to contribute effectively to your team.\n\nAt Euro Exim Bank, I successfully identified and generated new sales opportunities, strengthening customer relationships and ensuring compliance with AML, KYC, and CTF requirements. My tenure as a Portfolio Manager at FundedNext and MyForexFunds (freelance) further honed my skills in market research, risk management, and strategic trading, allowing me to build portfolios and drive profitability even in fluctuating financial conditions.\n\nMy career highlights include building investment portfolios from modest beginnings to significant values, showcasing my ability to generate and sustain growth in the financial market. My educational background in Economics and Development Studies, Financial Accounting and Finance, combined with ongoing professional certifications, underpins my strong analytical and quantitative skills, essential for a successful Wealth Manager.\n\nI am confident that my background, coupled with my passion for financial markets and dedication to client success, will enable me to contribute effectively to your team.\n\nThank you for considering my application. I look forward to the opportunity to discuss how my experience and skills align with the goals of your Company's. Please find my resume attached for your review. \n\nYours sincerely,\n\nOlusola Agbojo",https://www.linkedin.com/in/agbojo-olusola-entheous,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1729271390169_Agbojo Olosola.pdf,67113e3ecb112788c38cad6a,Financial Analyst Intern,2024-10-18T17:09:53.744Z,2024-10-18T17:09:53.744Z,,,,,,,,,
6712979fcb112788c38cb05e,Kareem Kareem Akande,+2348111131144,kareemkakkr@gmail.com,Nigeria,"My name is Kareem Kareem (AAT, ACA) and I am writing to express my interest in the Financial Analyst internship . I recently concluded my university degree with a First Class degree in Accounting. Identifying financial mismanagement as a major social development challenge in my community ignited my finance and accounting (F&A) interest. Relying on my exceptional discipline and time management skills, I have recorded major achievements in the course of my journey.\nA recent highlight being my involvement in a business challenge sponsored by MSIM. While on the program, I was selected to work on a team in the marketing segment of the challenge, a field I had no experience in. We were tasked with first highlighting the challenges involved in distributing an ESG package to different markets and then co-creating a marketing campaign to resolve said challenges. I had the responsibility of carrying out extensive research to identify what campaign strategy would be most effective, and the necessary considerations to include in the campaign to ensure optimum resonance within the target markets. Leveraging my leadership and presentation skills against the time constraints and complexities of this challenge, I was able to coordinate team efforts to not only win the challenge but also earn us the reputation of being the best team since inception of the challenge.\nMy dynamism and multi-tasking skills were put to the test in my final year as not only was I completing my degree, but I was also preparing to represent my university in the biggest sports competition in Africa (All-African University Games). Prioritization and time-management earned me not only a first class degree with distinctions in all my modules, but also 3 medals-2 gold and 1 bronze-at the end of the series. I particularly credit my commitment to a detailed preparation and training schedule and willingness to make changes where necessary.\nWith social development being the driving force for my achievements and my professional journey being a long-term goal. I have taken on shorter-term projects to insulate the impact of macroeconomic challenges on members of my community. One such project is an annual charity initiative which provides feeding to 300 people for a minimum of 30 days in the 2nd quarter of the year. To ensure efforts were targeted and optimized, demographic research was done to identify the locations and time for highest impact. 2024’s drive was recorded as the third successful implementation of the initiative. My reputation for accountability and execution earned me lead project manager ensuring logistics were seamless and financials were transparent.\nI am excited about the opportunity to further expand my knowledge on the practical aspects of Finance and how the financial markets play a pivotal role in the world economy. I am confident that this experience would be crucial for personal development. I welcome the opportunity to\ndiscuss my application further and learn more about your firm.\nThank you for your time and consideration.",,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1729271709236_KAREEM KAREEM cv.pdf,67113e3ecb112788c38cad6a,Financial Analyst Intern,2024-10-18T17:15:11.621Z,2024-10-18T17:15:11.621Z,,,,,,,,,
67129998cb112788c38cb069,Abisola Ojebola,+23408157422669,ojebolaabisola@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I’m Abisola Ojebola, a medical doctor with the Osun State Health Management Board. I graduated with honors from Obafemi Awolowo University, achieving 9 distinctions out of 12 in medical school. I have a strong passion for business, management, and finance, which led me to pursue online certifications in Investment Foundations and Business Analysis. I’m also currently enrolled with the CFA Institute and successfully passed the CFA Level 1 exam in August 2024.\n\nAs the only girl in a family of six, I've developed strong collaborative and teamwork skills. In my free time, I enjoy cooking and experimenting with new recipes, and I'm also learning French to broaden my horizons.",,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1729272214214_Abisola Ojebola's Resume (1).pdf,67113e3ecb112788c38cad6a,Financial Analyst Intern,2024-10-18T17:23:36.276Z,2024-10-18T17:23:36.276Z,,,,,,,,,
671299dbcb112788c38cb06f,Ayinde Blessing Temitope ,+2349035098466,contactblessingayinde@gmail.com,Nigeria,"My name is Blessing Ayinde, a Chartered Accountant and a first-class graduate in Accounting from Babcock University. I have about 2 years of experience in corporate reporting, tax management, budgeting, data analysis, preparing and analyzing financial statements and ensuring compliance with regulatory standards.\n\nI have a solid knowledge and understanding of basic accounting principles and am proficient in using ERP software and advanced Excel tools such as VLOOKUP, pivot tables, data validation, and SUMIFS functions. My goal is always to be a solution provider for business challenges, both within and beyond the corporate environment.\n\nI am committed to maintaining the highest ethical standards while delivering accurate and insightful financial insights. My focus is on achieving exceptional results, fostering continuous improvement, and contributing to the financial success of any organization I work with.\n\n",https://www.linkedin.com/in/blessing-ayinde?utm_source=share&utm_campaign=share_via&utm_content=profile&utm_medium=android_app,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1729272278669_Blessing Ayinde_CV.pdf,67113e3ecb112788c38cad6a,Financial Analyst Intern,2024-10-18T17:24:43.668Z,2024-10-18T17:24:43.668Z,,,,,,,,,
