671301e8cb112788c38cb250,Timothy Okpara Abi,+23407035543585,abitimothy4real@gmail.com,Nigeria,"No: 1 Old Abua Road Ahoada, Rivers State, Nigeria.\nTel: 07035543585\nEmail: abitimothy4real@gmail.com \nThe Hiring Manager,\nThroughout my career, I have contributed to positive business results through an effective \nand efficient understanding of regulatory framework that governs accounting information, \nFinancial Modeling, Payroll Management, account payable, Filing Tax Return, prepare \nmonthly financial statement, analyzing financial statement, expenditure, strict compliance \nto accounting guidelines and standard, & budgeting. I have used Quick book, ERP, Wave, \nSage 50, to improve account Process, Team management and collaboration, Data Analysis, \nDesign and implement operational strategies in line with General Accepted Accounting \nPractice (GAAP), International Financial Reporting Standard (IFRS), International \nAccounting Standard (IAS),\nI have skills in various accounting packages with expert in Financial Modeling, financial \naccounting, taxation, management account, budgeting & forecasting, using IFRS IAS and \nGeneral Accepted Accounting Practice (GAAP) as a guide to examine accounting data. I have\ngood analytics skills, prioritization, methodological Approach to Task and follow-through \nof key organizational projects, Team Building and collaboration. \nMy strengths and qualifications are an ideal match to the accountant requirements, and I \nwill bring immediate value to your organization. \nIn my former role as an accountant, I exercised a calculated analytical, methodical \napproach to problem-solving. While I am independently motivated,\nI appreciate collective efforts and collaboration productively within group settings and \nintegrity.\nMoreover, I am competent in clients’ management, data modeling and forecasting, data \ngathering, analysis, and problem-solving ethical and standard settings.\nI am proficiency in the use of Quick book, Wave, ERP accounting software’s, MS Office tools \nand other accounting packages. This opportunity is especially exciting, as my professional \ngoals are aligned with your organizational mission, vision, and values.\nFurthermore, my analytical, detailed, communication, problem-solving skills, and \ninnovation abilities with my good business acumen will serve to support your continued \norganizational growth and development.\nTo illustrate the scope of my career history and professional competencies, please take a \nmoment to review the enclosed CV.\nI am grateful for your evaluation of my credentials and look forward to your response. \nYours sincerely, \nTimothy Okpara Ab",,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1729298918687_ABI TIMOTHY OKPARA CV 2024.pdf,67113e3ecb112788c38cad6a,Financial Analyst Intern,2024-10-19T00:48:40.959Z,2024-10-19T00:48:40.959Z,,,,,,,,,
671302e6cb112788c38cb255,Abiola Balogun,+23409027988174,abiolabalogun.h@gmail.com,Nigeria,"Abiola holds a bachelor’s degree in Mechanical Engineering and is also a Google-certified Data Analyst. His technical skills include Excel, SQL, R programming, Looker Studio, and Power BI. Abiola's problem-solving and analytical mindset enable companies to stay ahead in a rapidly evolving market. He is passionate about using data analysis to drive impactful change. His background includes experience in data analysis, problem-solving, business intelligence, strategic thinking, and critical thinking, which he has applied to engaging stakeholders, solving business problems, and providing actionable insights.",https://sites.google.com/view/abiola-balogun/portfolio,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1729299171999_abiola balogun - Resume.pdf,67113e3ecb112788c38cad6a,Financial Analyst Intern,2024-10-19T00:52:54.553Z,2024-10-19T00:52:54.553Z,,,,,,,,,
67130a6ecb112788c38cb25d,Ayomide Pereao ,+2348118368768,ayomidepereao@gmail.com,Nigeria,"My name is Ayomide Pereao, I am a graduate of Finance from the university of Lagos, Nigeria. I am self-driven and always eager to learn how to unlock value in an organization.\n\nI have previously worked as a research analyst intern at PFI-CAPITAL, reporting to the research analyst and helping curate data in global stock markets and macroeconomic variables. I have also worked as an assistant project manager at Space Universe Africa, where I worked with the project manager and collaborated with other teams. \n\nRecently, I received a global financial analyst certificate at Edubridge Academy where I learnt Excel, financial analysis and financial modelling.  \n\nI believe my experience and eagerness to work are key success factors for me to not just excel but be value-adding in the organization. ",,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1729301099652_Pereao Ayo Cv.pdf,67113e3ecb112788c38cad6a,Financial Analyst Intern,2024-10-19T01:25:02.590Z,2024-10-19T01:25:02.590Z,,,,,,,,,
67130cdacb112788c38cb267,Joseph Ozolua ,+2347087461145,ozoluajoseph@yahoo.com,Nigeria,"My name is Joseph Ozolua, I have a Bachelor of Science in Insurance from the University of Benin and relevant professional experience in the financial and insurance sectors, I am excited about the opportunity to contribute to your team.\n\nIn my current role as a Finance Assistant at African Alliance Insurance, I have honed my skills in financial data analysis, bank reconciliations, and finance support. I manage daily and monthly bank reconciliations, assist in budgeting processes, and maintain accurate financial records. My proactive approach in identifying and rectifying discrepancies has enhanced the accuracy of financial reporting.\n\nPreviously, as an Underwriter at AIICO Insurance PLC, I developed a more efficient filing system and was actively involved in underwriting, claim investigation, and property inspection. My ability to streamline processes and improve organizational efficiency was well received by my team and supervisors.\n\nAdditionally, my role as a Store Keeper at TWS Cards and various leadership positions, such as Team Leader for group projects. These experiences have equipped me with a solid foundation in both finance and professional capacities, making me a well-rounded candidate.\n\nMy proficiency with Excel, MS Word, Xero accounting software  and Integrated business systems, combined with my strong communication and problem-solving skills, will enable me to effectively support your finance and insurance operations.\n\nThank you for considering my application. I look forward to the opportunity to discuss how my background, skills, and certifications align with the needs of your team.\nRegards,\nJoseph Ozolua \n07087461145",,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1729301719502_Joseph Ozolua.pdf,67113e3ecb112788c38cad6a,Financial Analyst Intern,2024-10-19T01:35:22.019Z,2024-10-19T01:35:22.019Z,,,,,,,,,
67130e4bcb112788c38cb26e,charles isaac,+23407089097689,charlesisaac266@gmail.com,Nigeria,"Data Analyst with extensive experience in utilizing advanced analytical tools such as SQL, Python, Excel, and Business Intelligence platforms to collect, clean, and analyze large datasets. Proficient in designing and automating data processes, creating insightful reports and dashboards, and delivering actionable insights that inform strategic business decisions. Expertise includes data migration, ETL processes, financial and customer data analysis, risk assessment, and optimization of SQL queries for efficiency. Adept at collaborating with cross-functional teams to address data needs and present complex data findings in a clear, impactful manner.",https://www.linkedin.com/in/isaac-charles-ba8a80196/,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1729302089056_charles isaac-resume.pdf,67113e3ecb112788c38cad6a,Financial Analyst Intern,2024-10-19T01:41:31.635Z,2024-10-19T01:41:31.635Z,,,,,,,,,
6713175acb112788c38cb27f,Eneghetaziba Anita Eze,+2348187581714,ezeanitae@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am a highly motivated, results-driven, forward-thinking accountant with a strong focus on delivering value through innovative, tech-savvy solutions. With my educational background in accounting, finance, and commercial training, combined with my proactive working style, proficiency in Excel, and strong communication skills, I am confident in my ability to contribute effectively to the team.\n\nPassionate about learning and growing in the finance field, I seek to gain hands-on experience in financial analysis, reporting, modeling, budgeting, forecasting, and data management while contributing to a dynamic start-up environment.\n\nI have a foundation in accounting principles and practices. I am particularly adept at using various remote working and IT systems, including Excel, Google Spreadsheet, etc., which I understand is advantageous for this role. My independent and proactive working style ensures that I can take initiative and work effectively without constant supervision\n\nFurthermore, I possess excellent communication skills, both written and verbal, which enable me to interact effectively with colleagues and external stakeholders. My expert attention to detail skills allows me to articulate complex information clearly and concisely, ensuring smooth communication across all levels of the organization.\n\nI thrive in collaborative environments and quickly adapt to challenging situations. I am seeking a role where I can utilize my skills to plan, manage, and execute complex projects as part of a dynamic team. With excellent presentation abilities, I bring a proactive approach to problem-solving and analytical thinking. I approach challenges with enthusiasm, persistence, resilience, and determination, consistently driving results.\n\nI want to develop my potential in an organization dedicated to nurturing talent and providing ample opportunities for career advancement and extraordinary development possibilities to be a specialist in solving real-world financial analysis tasks, collaborating with experienced professionals, and growing my expertise in a supportive and engaging environment. I want to work with a goal-getting company with corporate work ethics in a multicultural environment and moral principles that impact life-changing values. \n\nI am excited about the opportunity to bring my skills and enthusiasm to this company as a Financial Analyst Intern. I am confident that my eagerness to learn and diligence for excellent performance will make me a valuable asset to your team.\n\nThank you.\n",,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1729304408277_E. Anita Eze - CV.pdf,67113e3ecb112788c38cad6a,Financial Analyst Intern,2024-10-19T02:20:10.493Z,2024-10-19T02:20:10.493Z,,,,,,,,,
671319c6cb112788c38cb287,Osagie Ikekhua,+2348034770348,ikekhua.osagie@yahoo.com,Nigeria,"Dear Hiring Professional,\n\nI hope this message finds you well. I am writing to apply for the Financial Analyst Intern role, as advertised. I am a second-class upper graduate from the Department of Finance of the University of Lagos. I am eager to bring my skills and experience to a new challenge and contribute to the success of your firm.\n\nDuring my academic journey, I developed a strong foundation in accounting principles, financial analysis, and data management. I am well-versed in financial statement analysis, budgeting, and forecasting. My coursework has also provided me with a solid understanding of taxation and auditing practices.\n\nIn addition to my academic background, I have gained practical experience through an internship where I had the opportunity to apply my knowledge in real-world scenarios. In my current role at Syscodes Communication Ltd, I gained valuable skills which honed my attention to detail, analytical thinking, and problem-solving abilities. I am confident in my ability to handle complex financial transactions and ensure accurate and timely reporting. One of my strengths are my proficiency in ERP accounting software, Microsoft Office Suite especially Excel and Google Workplace. I am adept at utilizing these tools to streamline processes, improve efficiency, and maintain accurate records.\n\nFurthermore, I possess excellent communication skills, both written and verbal, which allows me to effectively collaborate with cross-functional teams. I am a proactive learner, always seeking opportunities to expand my knowledge and stay up-to-date with industry trends and best practices. I believe that my passion for numbers, attention to detail, and interpersonal skills make me an ideal fit for your team.\n\nThank you for considering my application. I look forward to hearing from you soon.\n\nRegards, \n\nOsagie Ikekhua\n",,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1729305027718_Osagie Ikekhua.pdf,67113e3ecb112788c38cad6a,Financial Analyst Intern,2024-10-19T02:30:30.123Z,2024-10-19T02:30:30.123Z,,,,,,,,,
