6713463fcb112788c38cb38e,Andy Ndubuisi Joseph,+23408120638670,andyjoseph40@yahoo.com,Nigeria,"I'm currently working as a business and financial analyst for a startup health organization, where I’m helping design a financial model that will guide the company’s growth over the next 10 years. In this role, I analyze financial data, create forecasts, and evaluate various scenarios to ensure we’re making sound strategic decisions. It's given me valuable experience in building financial models, understanding key business drivers, and aligning data insights with our long-term goals.\n\nI’m excited about the financial analyst intern position because it aligns with the work I’m already doing, and I’m eager to deepen my expertise in financial analysis. I enjoy using data to tell a story, solve problems, and support decision-making, and I believe this role would be a great way to apply my skills while learning more about the financial industry.",https://github.com/andyjoseph40,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1729316413364_Andy Ndubuisi Joseph CV.pdf,67113e3ecb112788c38cad6a,Financial Analyst Intern,2024-10-19T05:40:15.238Z,2024-10-19T05:40:15.238Z,,,,,,,,,
67134873cb112788c38cb39a,Olamide Fashola,+2342348037051044,1olamide.fashola@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I hold a B.sc in Finance from the University of Lagos, where I gained a solid foundation in financial \nanalysis, accounting, and business management. Additionally, I have of experience working as a Financial Analyst at my previous company, where I have successfully managed financial planning, forecasting, and budgeting processes. Through my work, I have developed a keen eye for detail, a strategic mindset, and the ability to identify and analyze financial trends to support effective decision-making.\n\nIn my role as a Financial Manager, I have been responsible for conducting in-depth financial analysis, preparing financial reports, and providing recommendations to senior management to optimize financial performance. I have also been involved in implementing cost control measures, streamlining financial processes, and ensuring compliance with regulatory requirements. My strong proficiency in financial modelling, data analysis, and advanced Excel skills have allowed me to deliver accurate and actionable insights to drive business growth.\n\nFurthermore, I have developed a comprehensive understanding of accounting principles, financial \nstatements, and general ledger management. I have expertise in preparing financial statements, \nreconciling accounts and analyzing variances to ensure accurate and timely financial reporting. I am \nproficient in using accounting software and I possess a solid understanding of taxation regulations and compliance.\n\nI am proficient in utilizing various financial software and tools, including Excel, Zoho books, and Xero. My strong quantitative and analytical skills enable me to identify trends, detect anomalies, and make data driven recommendations. I am also well-versed in regulatory compliance and have a deep understanding of accounting standards such as IFRS.\n\nApart from my technical skills, I am a highly motivated and organized professional with excellent \ncommunication and interpersonal abilities. I thrive in collaborative environments and have a proven track record of building strong relationships with stakeholders across departments. I am accustomed to working under tight deadlines and managing multiple priorities while maintaining a high level of accuracy and attention to detail.\n\nI am excited about the opportunity to join the dynamic team and contribute to its growth and financial success. I am confident that my skills and qualifications align perfectly with the requirements of this role. I look forward to discussing how my expertise can benefit your organization in more detail.\n\nThank you. \n\nYours sincerely, \nFashola Olamide Temitope",,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1729316976614_FASHOLA'S CV (2).pdf,67113e3ecb112788c38cad6a,Financial Analyst Intern,2024-10-19T05:49:39.245Z,2024-10-19T05:49:39.245Z,,,,,,,,,
67134987cb112788c38cb3a1,Adebiyi Iyanuoluwa Anjolaoluwa ,+2348143060534,anjolaiyanu@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am a recent graduate of the university of Nigeria nsukka where I studied Business Education and finished with second class upper division, I have an AAT certification(association of accounting technician) and in the last ICAN May2024 exams I became a qualified chartered accountant. Not only that, I obtained the award of the best qualifying student for the diet.\n\nI have a very good analytical skills and a good knowledge of the computation and interpretation of financial ratios which was displayed in writing professional exams and in my previous roles as a junior accountant and as a finance intern.\nIf I am being selected for this role, I will be bringing in my previous knowledge of finance as well as the use of accounting software such as Excel,sage and quickbooks.\nI am an individual who believe so much in giving attention to details and listening to instructions, with all these, I believe I will be a good fit for the role.",https://www.linkedin.com/in/iyanuoluwa-adebiyi-aat-qualified-aca-5207311b8?utm_source=share&utm_campaign=share_via&utm_content=profile&utm_medium=android_app,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1729317252900_Iyanuoluwaâs Cv .pdf,67113e3ecb112788c38cad6a,Financial Analyst Intern,2024-10-19T05:54:15.185Z,2024-10-19T05:54:15.185Z,,,,,,,,,
