67139a19cb112788c38cb630,Daniel Adeshina,+2349132367622,danielxiah@gmail.com,Nigeria,"Thank you for the opportunity to share more about myself. My name is Daniel Adeshina and I recently graduated with a First Class degree in Economics from the University of Lagos, where I developed a strong passion for finance and financial analysis. I have always been fascinated by how financial data drives business decisions and growth, which led me to pursue several internships and certifications that further honed my technical skills and analytical abilities. My academic background, combined with hands-on experience, has equipped me with a robust foundation to excel as a Financial Analyst Intern at Tobams Group.\n\nI have interned at leading financial institutions, including ARM Holding Co. Limited, where I worked as a Summer Analyst. There, I had the opportunity to assist in evaluating key financial metrics for deals, contributing to financial modeling and performing extensive financial analysis that shaped critical business decisions. This role significantly sharpened my skills in financial modeling, data analysis, and valuation. My experience working closely with senior professionals instilled a strong understanding of key financial ratios and the importance of delivering accurate, data-driven insights.\n\nOne of my most significant strengths is my analytical ability. In my most recent internship at KPMG as a Summer Audit Intern, I was responsible for analyzing financial statements and identifying variances in client reports. My ability to pay close attention to detail while keeping the broader financial goals in mind allowed me to deliver precise and actionable insights, contributing to process improvement and client satisfaction. In line with Tobams Group’s expectations for this role, I am highly proficient in Microsoft Excel and have hands-on experience with financial modeling tools, which I leveraged to streamline complex data sets into clear and concise reports during my internships.\n\nWhat excites me about this opportunity at Tobams Group is the prospect of working within a dynamic startup environment where I can directly apply the skills I have acquired in financial analysis and reporting. I am eager to contribute to the team by supporting the preparation of financial statements, developing models for new business initiatives, and participating in the budgeting and forecasting process. The mentorship and growth opportunities offered by Tobams Group align perfectly with my career aspirations of becoming an exceptional financial analyst.\n\nIn addition to my technical skills, I bring a collaborative mindset and strong communication abilities. I believe that finance is not just about crunching numbers; it’s about conveying the story behind the numbers. My experience in presenting financial findings to various stakeholders has given me the confidence to clearly articulate complex financial insights in a way that is both meaningful and actionable.\n\nUltimately, my goal is to leverage my expertise in financial analysis to contribute to the success of Tobams Group while continuing to grow as a finance professional. I am confident that my background in financial modeling, coupled with my eagerness to learn and adapt, makes me a strong fit for this role. I am excited about the possibility of joining your team and contributing to the company’s continued growth",https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1rdRgF-BRsDcgjCD-_63OphCTv0vEhWZX?usp=sharing,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1729337879255_Resume Daniel CF.pdf,67113e3ecb112788c38cad6a,Financial Analyst Intern,2024-10-19T11:38:01.323Z,2024-10-19T11:38:01.323Z,,,,,,,,,
67139e6acb112788c38cb63d,Stephen Njoku,+23408034093719,chidi_stephen@yahoo.com,Nigeria,"My name is Stephen Njoku, Nigerian of Imo State origin, B. Sc. Accounting, MBA Finance and ACMA Certified.\nI am an experienced finance and Accounting, Audit professional of 15 years+. I am well-equipped to handle bookkeeping accounting, financial analysis, auditing, controls, compliance review, reporting on Assets, Liabilities, Equity, Profitability analysis, Expenses and Income (Revenue) using Quickbook, Tally ERP, SAGE, Excel, etc. I understand the importance of accurate book keeping, internal controls and regulatory compliance when it comes to finance and accounting which is a primary source to financial analysis.  \nI have gained my skills in the course of my career over years in reviewing policies and procedures manuals, internal audit reports writing, and financial statements - all key areas of focus for your project. \nMy attention to detail will ensure that no potential gaps or issues are left unturned in your existing frameworks. Moreover, my experience in analyzing past reports, attention to detail, problem-solving, and effective communication makes my qualifications stand out. \nI am eager to discuss further with you in details if invited.\nBest regards,\nStephen Njoku\n",https://www.linkedin.com/in/njoku-stephen-25491a65/,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1729338984006_Njoku Resume 2.pdf,67113e3ecb112788c38cad6a,Financial Analyst Intern,2024-10-19T11:56:26.313Z,2024-10-19T11:56:26.313Z,,,,,,,,,
