6713f9bbcb112788c38cb78d,Favour Noah Timighe ,+23409060261138,noahfavourite@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am a problem solver committed to turning complex data into clear and actionable insights that drive business growth. I have strong proficiency in SQL, Power Bi and Excel which I use for data cleaning, analysis, and visualization, enabling organizations to make informed decisions based on reliable data. My analytical mindset allows me to identify trends, uncover hidden patterns, and develop data-driven strategies that align with business objectives.\n\nI am constantly seeking to improve my knowledge and staying updated with industry trends.  My goal is to help organizations harness the power of data to achieve their objectives and drive continuous improvement.",https://github.com/noahfavourite,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1729362361127_Favour Noah Timighe - Data Analyst.pdf,67113e3ecb112788c38cad6a,Financial Analyst Intern,2024-10-19T18:26:03.906Z,2024-10-19T18:26:03.906Z,,,,,,,,,
6713f9dccb112788c38cb792,IyinOluwa Badejo,+23409023428792,iyinoluwa8@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am a detail-oriented data analyst with a strong foundation in accounting, audit, and risk control. With a first-class honors degree in Accounting from Christopher University, I have worked on ensuring the accuracy of financial statements, performing tax audits, and conducting risk assessments to maintain compliance with regulatory standards. My experience also includes working as an Accounting and Administrative Intern, where I assisted with audits and the preparation of financial statements for multiple companies. \n\nIn addition to my audit and risk control expertise, I have developed strong data analysis skills, creating interactive dashboards and leveraging tools like Power BI, Excel, SQL, and Python to extract actionable insights. I am passionate about using data to drive decision-making and have applied my skills to projects across the financial and sports sectors. I am eager to contribute to solutions that combine risk management and data-driven strategies.",,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1729362394018_BADEJO IYINOLUWA CV...pdf,67113e3ecb112788c38cad6a,Financial Analyst Intern,2024-10-19T18:26:36.986Z,2024-10-19T18:26:36.986Z,,,,,,,,,
6713fbaacb112788c38cb798,Emehinola Ayooluwa ,+2347062439054,emehinolayo@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I'm Ayooluwa Emehinola , a seasoned Chartered Accountant with over 4 years of hands-on experience in financial management, auditing, and financial analysis. Holding a professional certification from ICAN. I possess a deep understanding of financial principles, regulations, and standards.\n\nMy expertise includes:\n\n•⁠  ⁠Financial statement preparation and auditing\n•⁠  ⁠Budgeting and forecasting\n•⁠  ⁠Financial modeling and analysis\n•⁠  ⁠Tax planning and compliance\n•⁠  ⁠Financial reporting and presentation\n\nThroughout my career, I've worked in Consulting, Banking, and Non Profit Industries , developing and implementing financial strategies to drive business growth and improve profitability. My strong analytical skills, attention to detail, and excellent communication abilities enable me to provide actionable insights and effective solutions.\n\nI'm passionate about staying up-to-date with industry trends and best practices, ensuring my expertise remains relevant and valuable to organizations. I'm excited to leverage my skills and experience to contribute to a dynamic team and drive business success.""",https://www.linkedin.com/in/ayooluwa-emehinola-644063157?utm_source=share&utm_campaign=share_via&utm_content=profile&utm_medium=ios_app,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1729362855924_EMEHINOLA AYOOLUWA CV IN PDF UPDATED.pdf,67113e3ecb112788c38cad6a,Financial Analyst Intern,2024-10-19T18:34:18.942Z,2024-10-19T18:34:18.942Z,,,,,,,,,
6713fe1bcb112788c38cb7a4,Temitope Ogunniyi,+2348087422093,teeyioguns@gmail.com,Nigeria,"My name is Temitope Ogunniyi, with background in Economics and I am currently pursuing a PhD degree in Economics.  I have passion for Financial/Data Analysis, I am confident in my ability to contribute meaningfully to your team.\nMy career/academic journey and Google Data Analytics has equipped me with a solid understanding of analytical concepts and problem-solving techniques. I have also applied these skills extensively in my coursework, such as analyzing the impact of exchange rate fluctuations on Nigeria's economic growth and capstone project. I recently completed a short internship course on data analysis with Accenture North America where I had hands on experience on data cleaning and management, data modelling, analysis and presentation. I am a collaborative individual who thrives in team environments. I am eager to learn from the experienced financial analysts at Tobams Group and contribute my skills to achieving shared objectives.\nI am highly motivated and dedicated to professional growth. I am excited about the opportunity to learn new skills and contribute to the success of Tobams Group financial analysis initiatives.\nI am a fast learner, adaptable, and detail-oriented with a strong work ethics.\n",,"https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1729363481376_OGUNNIYI, TEMITOPE.docx",67113e3ecb112788c38cad6a,Financial Analyst Intern,2024-10-19T18:44:43.240Z,2024-10-19T18:44:43.240Z,,,,,,,,,
