6714a02dcb112788c38cb950,Daniel Chigbogu Enujuba,+2348135982074,enujubadaniel65@gmail.com,Nigeria,"\n I am Daniel Chigbogu Enujuba, a recent graduate with a Master's Degree in Economics from the University of Lagos and a Diploma in Financial Analysis from Edubridge. I have a strong passion for finance and have developed skills in financial analysis, modeling, and reporting through both my education and hands-on experience.\n\nIn my most recent role as a Junior Researcher at Rhodium, I conducted in-depth financial analysis and market research, supporting senior analysts in making informed investment decisions. This experience honed my ability to analyze financial data and derive actionable insights.\n\nAdditionally, I have served as a Store Manager at Bokku! Discount Grocery Store, where I was responsible for managing inventory levels and ensuring accurate financial reporting. This role taught me the importance of operational efficiency and loss prevention, and it further developed my analytical and problem-solving skills.\n\nI thrive in dynamic environments and am eager to learn and contribute to a team. I am excited about the opportunity to apply my financial knowledge and skills in a practical setting, and I am looking forward to contributing to Tobams Group as a Financial Analyst Intern.\n\n",,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1729404970916_DANIEL CHIGBOGU ENUJUBA 24.pdf,67113e3ecb112788c38cad6a,Financial Analyst Intern,2024-10-20T06:16:13.251Z,2024-10-20T06:16:13.251Z,,,,,,,,,
6714a27ecb112788c38cb95c,Igun Yetunde Abosede ,+2349013672832,igun_yetunde@outlook.com,Nigeria,"My name is Igun Yetunde Abosede. I have a Post-graduate degree in Accounting from Nigerian College of Accountancy and I’m currently working as a bank teller.\n\nI have a strong passion for strategic planning and data analysis, and I’ve developed skills in market research, data entry, and executive virtual assistant .\nBeyond the technical side of my work, I thrive on problem-solving and enjoy the challenge of finding new ways to connect brands with their audiences. My colleagues often describe me as detail-oriented and proactive, and I take pride in being someone who is dependable and willing to go the extra mile to deliver results.\n\nLooking to the future, I’m excited about the direction my career is heading. My goal is to continue honing my skills in marketing and eventually take on a leadership role where I can mentor others and help shape larger strategies. I’m especially interested in this so i can have the first hand experience aside from the ones i gain through training.\n\nIn summary, I consider myself someone who is passionate about learning and growth, both professionally and personally. I believe in staying curious, embracing challenges, and always striving to improve, whether that’s through my work,or my interactions with others.",,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1729405563192_IGUN ABOSEDE YETUNDE-1.pdf,67113e3ecb112788c38cad6a,Financial Analyst Intern,2024-10-20T06:26:06.233Z,2024-10-20T06:26:06.233Z,,,,,,,,,
6714a33acb112788c38cb964,Ademola Abioye ,+2348121863532,demolaabioye17@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am Ademola Abioye,  a recent first class graduate of Accounting from Ajayi Crowther University \nI am someone that loves to learn and is always attentive.\nI have various skills which should be able to help me advance into whatever I am put into, and I work well in teams.\nThis is just a little that I can say, but if you are willing to employ someone who will maintain the standard of excellence you've set and work with you to advanced-I am that guy.\n",https://www.linkedin.com/in/ademola-abioye-aat-004766270?utm_source=share&utm_campaign=share_via&utm_content=profile&utm_medium=android_app,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1729405747664_ABIOYE ADEMOLA PRECIOUS CV-1.pdf,67113e3ecb112788c38cad6a,Financial Analyst Intern,2024-10-20T06:29:14.499Z,2024-10-20T06:29:14.499Z,,,,,,,,,
6714a3cfcb112788c38cb96a,Damilola Oshinowo ,+2349033146526,oshinowodamilola11@gmail.com,Nigeria,My name is Damilola and I currently work as an investment banking intern at the Norrenberger financial group. My love for numbers and quantitative analysis led me to study accounting at Obafemi Awolowo University where I finished with a second class upper. \nAt this stage of my career I am looking to learn as much as possible and build competence in the field of finance.,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1729405900123_Damilola Oshinowo [Resume].pdf,67113e3ecb112788c38cad6a,Financial Analyst Intern,2024-10-20T06:31:43.507Z,2024-10-20T06:31:43.507Z,,,,,,,,,
6714a4c3cb112788c38cb970,Yusuf Muhammad Mustafa,+23409030997538,yusufmm13@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am a graduate of architecture who, after 5 years of experience in the real estate and construction industry, sought a new challenge and a change in career path and transitioned into finance and investment 2 years ago. \nPresently, I trade foreign exchange on a retail(CFD) basis, but on the professional level, I recently took the level 1 certification exams for The Chartered Stockbroker's Institute, Leaving me with just one more level to go.\nCoupled together, my experience both with trading Fx and preparing for the examinations have exposed me to financial statement and asset analysis, Business and assets appraisals and above all Investment analysis and procedures",,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1729406144997_Yusuf CV Finanace Research Consultant.pdf,67113e3ecb112788c38cad6a,Financial Analyst Intern,2024-10-20T06:35:47.052Z,2024-10-20T06:35:47.052Z,,,,,,,,,
6714a7afcb112788c38cb97f,Adeoluwakitan Adeleke,+23408021198026,adexbryant@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am Adeleke Adeoluwakitan, a graduate student pursuing an MSc in Economics with a passion for transitioning into the finance industry. My academic journey, combined with hands-on experience in accounting and finance-related roles, has equipped me with a solid understanding of financial systems. In my previous positions, including as a Trade Finance specialist at Euro Exim Bank and a Financial Assistant at the Network for Health Equity & Development, I contributed to managing financial operations, preparing financial documents, and supporting the reconciliation of accounts. Through these roles, I developed strong accounting skills and intermediate proficiency in using accounting software such as QuickBooks.\n\nWhile I am currently in the process of acquiring financial analyst skills, I have a keen interest in applying these competencies to real-world financial challenges. I have started pursuing online certifications and plan to expand my qualifications by undertaking the Corporate Finance Institute(CFI) and Chatererd Financial Analyst(CFA) programs in the near future. I am particularly drawn to this internship at Tobams Group because it presents a valuable opportunity to further my growth in financial analysis, reporting, and modeling, allowing me to develop the expertise required to succeed in the finance sector.\n\nMy goal is to leverage this internship as a stepping stone into a full-fledged career as a financial analyst, where I can combine my academic knowledge, growing technical skills, and practical experience to contribute meaningfully to a dynamic financial environment.",,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1729406892391_CV Adeoluwakitan Adeleke.pdf,67113e3ecb112788c38cad6a,Financial Analyst Intern,2024-10-20T06:48:15.611Z,2024-10-20T06:48:15.611Z,,,,,,,,,
6714a838cb112788c38cb986,OLOYEDE GANIYU,+23408083374198,oloyegan98@gmail.com,Nigeria,"My name is Ganiyu, I recently graduated with a Bachelor degree in Economics, where I gained a strong foundation in financial analysis, economic modelling, and data interpretation. In addition, I have earned certifications in Financial Modelling & Valuation (FMVA) and Business Intelligence & Data Analytics (BIDA), which have further sharpened my technical and analytical skills.\nI recently work as an Assistant Accountant at a firm specializing in generator engine repairs and sales. In this role, I handle a variety of financial responsibilities, including managing financial records and analyzing financial statements. This position has enhanced my attention to detail and problem-solving capabilities, both of which are critical in finance.\nI am proficient in financial analysis tools such as Excel, EViews, and Stata, which I have applied in both my academic and professional work. My long-term goal is to apply my analytical skills to help businesses make data-driven financial decisions. I am particularly drawn to this Financial Analyst Intern role because it aligns with my aspirations to grow in the finance sector while leveraging my economics background to contribute to meaningful financial evaluations and strategies.\n",www.linkedin.com/in/ganiyu-oloyede-40780b221,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1729407030354_LMy Resume (3) L (1).pdf,67113e3ecb112788c38cad6a,Financial Analyst Intern,2024-10-20T06:50:32.345Z,2024-10-20T06:50:32.345Z,,,,,,,,,
