6717bc3ddd7522120ce48790,Glory Essah,+2348058257832,gloryessah@gmail.com,Nigeria,"My career started in the fast-paced environment of a traditional newsroom, where I sharpened my writing skills under the pressure of deadlines and breaking news. But as the media world evolved, I felt the need to shift my focus toward a different kind of storytelling—one that focused more on connecting with and engaging an audience.\n\nThat’s when I made the move into content writing. I began creating blog posts and persuasive copy that informed, inspired, and connected with readers. However, I wanted to see more direct results from my work—to know that my writing was making a real difference for businesses.\n\nThis led me to the exciting field of digital marketing, specifically social media. Here, I saw firsthand how brands could build genuine, lasting connections with their audiences in real time. Watching startups grow into established names through strategic social media campaigns ignited my passion for this area.\n\nI saw how social media could not only boost brand growth but also create engaged communities around a business. Through smart, well-crafted content, these communities grow, driving brand loyalty and helping businesses meet their goals. This realization solidified my focus on social media marketing.\n\nToday, I use my diverse writing experience and deep understanding of social media to help brands grow. I’m not just a content creator—I’m a strategic storyteller. I craft engaging narratives that speak directly to your audience through content, targeted campaigns, and data-driven insights.\n\n",https://gloryessah.my.canva.site/,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1729608763177_Digital Marketing CV- Glory Essah .docx (2).pdf,67175c7b301a84ab876896e6,Social Media Management Intern,2024-10-22T14:52:45.671Z,2024-10-22T14:52:45.671Z,,,,,,,,,
