6717c2cfdd7522120ce48884,Moyefola Adeyemi,+23408086617450,moyefola2012@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am a recent graduate of Obafemi Awolowo University Ile-Ife with a degree in Management and Accounting.Also, a member of the Associate Accounting Technicians(AAT)by the ICAN professional body in Nigeria.\n\nI have had experience with social media and content creation by headlining the social media team for my graduating class successfully.\n\nI have also mastered effective communication and interpersonal skills. \nI thrive on organization and am incredibly detail oriented. My time management is impeccable and I am able to handle a number of tasks at once. \n\nI am excited about the opportunity to contribute to the success of your team and would welcome the chance to discuss how my skills and qualifications align with your needs. Thank you for considering my application. I look forward to the possibility of joining your team and contributing to its continued growth.",https://www.linkedin.com/in/moyefola-adeyemi-39893519a?utm_source=share&utm_campaign=share_via&utm_content=profile&utm_medium=android_app,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1729610445528_Moyefola CV (1).pdf,67175c7b301a84ab876896e6,Social Media Management Intern,2024-10-22T15:20:47.614Z,2024-10-22T15:20:47.614Z,,,,,,,,,
6717c32bdd7522120ce48892,Rotimi Amurawaiye,+2348108318352,adeoluwarotimi3@gmail.com,Nigeria,"Hi hiring manager,\nI understand reading a lot of these applications isn’t how you want to spend your day so I'll keep this brief.\n\nMy name is Rotimi, and I'm a 19-year-old UI/UX designer from Nigeria. I kicked off my design journey in September 2021, initially just as a fun summer project. You know, something to pass the time. But somewhere between figuring out auto layout and aligning buttons, I realized I was hooked\n\nAs for my experience, I’ve designed everything from landing pages to mobile applications, and I like to think my work speaks for itself though I wouldn't mind if it shouted a bit more. I'm all about results and making sure the end product is as user-friendly as it is visually appealing. And while I have my strengths, I'm always eager to learn and adapt to new trends in the industry.\n\nThank you for reading this, can't wait to hear back from you. Cheers!",https://www.behance.net/rotimijnr4,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1729610534660_MY OFFICIAL DESIGN RESUME.pdf,6717598e301a84ab876896e0,Product (UI/UX) Designer Intern,2024-10-22T15:22:19.474Z,2024-10-22T15:22:19.474Z,,,,,,,,,
6717c342dd7522120ce4889b,Anuoluwapo Afolabi,+2349056804329,haandu18@gmail.com,Nigeria,"Hello, I'm Anuoluwapo Afolabi, a highly motivated and creative Social Media Manager with a passion for digital marketing. \n\nWith a strong background in managing social media accounts for Morainbow Down Syndrome Foundation and Kopahouses, I've developed a solid understanding of social media platforms and their role in shaping brand identities.\n\nAs a social media enthusiast with experience in video editing, content scheduling, and team coordination, I've successfully enhanced brand visibility and engagement. I'm well-versed in social media management tools like Hootsuite, Buffer, Canva, and Google Analytics.\n\nI hold certifications from Hubspot Academy and the Digital Marketing Institute (DMSI), demonstrating my expertise in digital marketing strategies and best practices.\n\nI'm impressed by Tobams Group's commitment to innovative marketing strategies and excited about the opportunity to contribute to the team. My strengths include:\n\n- Creative content creation (written, visual, and video)\n- Social media analytics and data-driven decision-making\n- Excellent communication and collaboration skills\n- Ability to work independently and adapt to fast-paced environments\n\nI'm looking forward to applying my skills and knowledge to develop and execute social media strategies that align with Tobams Group's business objectives.\n\nI'm excited about the prospect of joining Tobams Group's marketing team and contributing to the company's success.",https://sites.google.com/d/1yq8p_GIlboawq0XXXplh6QWKdjueBkFx/edit?ouid=111006943024901538456,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1729610559313_Anu's Resume.pdf,67175c7b301a84ab876896e6,Social Media Management Intern,2024-10-22T15:22:42.004Z,2024-10-22T15:22:42.004Z,,,,,,,,,
6717c445dd7522120ce488b1,Rita Echere,+2348146790213,chetachiechere@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am Chetachi Rita Echere, an enthusiastic and motivated product designer with hands-on experience in user-centered design and visual aesthetics. I have worked on various design projects, including e-commerce platforms, mobile apps, and finance applications, where I developed wireframes, mockups, and prototypes using tools like Figma, Figjam, and Miro.\n\nI am passionate about learning and applying user research and design principles to create intuitive and visually compelling products. Through my recent certifications from Google and Microsoft, I have deepened my understanding of UX design and gained skills in working within agile teams to meet deadlines. My goal is to continue growing as a designer by contributing innovative ideas and designs to your team.\n\nWith my strong attention to detail, creativity, and collaborative spirit, I am excited about the opportunity to contribute and learn as part of your product design team",https://www.behance.net/ritaechere,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1729610818148_latest latest Rita Echere CV (1).pdf,6717598e301a84ab876896e0,Product (UI/UX) Designer Intern,2024-10-22T15:27:01.031Z,2024-10-22T15:27:01.031Z,,,,,,,,,
