6717d0c3dd7522120ce489ec,Onojomofia stanley omoefe,+2348167662268,onojomofiastanley@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am a passionate product designer and a graduate from ESAE University, eager to expand my skill set and gain practical experience in the field. As a junior designer, I have developed a solid foundation in user-centered design principles, wireframing, and prototyping through academic projects and personal work. I’m particularly interested in improving my design thinking, UX/UI design, and problem-solving skills through real-world challenges.\n\nI am seeking an internship opportunity where I can collaborate with experienced designers, learn from industry best practices, and contribute to impactful projects. My goal is to refine my design process, improve my proficiency with tools like Figma and Sketch, and develop a deeper understanding of how to balance user needs with business objectives. I am dedicated to continuous learning and excited to contribute to a team that values creativity and innovation.",https://www.behance.net/gallery/207172735/NestNext-saving-App,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1729614017105_Stanley Ab.pdf,6717598e301a84ab876896e0,Product (UI/UX) Designer Intern,2024-10-22T16:20:19.756Z,2024-10-22T16:20:19.756Z,,,,,,,,,
6717d1addd7522120ce48a10,DANIEL OMOTOSO,+23408149162437,danielomotoso52@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am Omotoso Daniel, a Product Designer with a strong background in creating user-centered solutions. Currently, I work at Wave Africa, a credit-tech startup dedicated to improving access to credit for federal civil servants in Nigeria.\n\nIn my role, I led user research to uncover the challenges faced by our target audience, ranging from millennials to baby boomers. This research revealed significant pain points, such as tedious documentation processes and lengthy approval times.\n\nTo address these issues, I collaborated with cross-functional teams to redesign the user journey, implementing streamlined onboarding processes that led to onboarding over 10,000 users within three months. I also contributed to developing an admin dashboard that significantly reduced credit approval times from two days to under 15 minutes.\n\nI thrive on teamwork and believe that effective collaboration is essential in design. My experience has taught me the importance of empathy and understanding user needs, which I prioritize in all my design projects.\n\nI'm passionate about leveraging my skills to create impactful user experiences and am excited about the opportunity to contribute to new projects that prioritize design and user satisfaction.",https://www.behance.net/omotoso-daniel,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1729614251423_Daniel Omotoso CV(1).pdf,6717598e301a84ab876896e0,Product (UI/UX) Designer Intern,2024-10-22T16:24:13.849Z,2024-10-22T16:24:13.849Z,,,,,,,,,
6717d298dd7522120ce48a44,Adetutu Bello,+2348166786283,adetutu.bello2019@gmail.com,Nigeria," I'm Adetutu Bello, a highly motivated and creative individual passionate about social media management. I'm excited to apply for the Social Media Manager Intern position at Tobams Group.\n\nWith experience managing my personal social media accounts, I've developed skills in:\n\n- Content creation\n- Content calendar planning\n- Community management\n- Graphics design with Canva\n- Social media analytics\n\nI'm eager to learn from experienced professionals and contribute to Tobams Group's online presence. As a quick learner and team player, I'm confident my skills and enthusiasm make me an ideal candidate.\n\n",,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1729614486383_Adetutu's_CV.pdf,67175c7b301a84ab876896e6,Social Media Management Intern,2024-10-22T16:28:08.562Z,2024-10-22T16:28:08.562Z,,,,,,,,,
6717d367dd7522120ce48a5d,Mojeed Adebayo ,+2348111451637,adebayodayo33@gmail.com,Nigeria,"As a product designer I have approximately one year of experience in UX design, I am confident in my ability to create user-centered designs that drive business results.\n\nThroughout my career, I have had the opportunity to work on various projects, including the design of HRM software and the UI redesign of a patient management software, utilizing the design thinking process. My proficiency in UI design tools such as Figma, basic frontend development, and Microsoft Office applications has enabled me to effectively collaborate with cross-functional teams and deliver high-quality designs.\n\nI am eager to learn more about this opportunity and discuss how my skills and experience align with the company's goals. I look forward to the opportunity to meet with you to explore this position further.\n\n",https://medium.com/@adebayodayo33/mojeed-adebayo-13df3e80dbc3,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1729614692513_MOJEED DAYO ADEBAYO - product design CV.PDF,6717598e301a84ab876896e0,Product (UI/UX) Designer Intern,2024-10-22T16:31:35.070Z,2024-10-22T16:31:35.070Z,,,,,,,,,
