67180455dd7522120ce4930b,Evelyn Ikerekhalu,+2347038058424,evelynikerekhalu@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am an enthusiastic, passionate, and committed goal-getter. With a degree in Actuarial Science and a diploma in Accounting, I have effectively leveraged both qualifications by continuously developing myself through various online courses in accounting, finance, work ethics, experience, and work productivity. One of these certifications is from the McKinsey Forward program.\n\nMy pursuit of innovation and excellent service has led me to develop skills in using AI to address challenges in finance and accounting, such as automating repetitive tasks and monitoring data. Through my experience with the AI Career Essentials (AiCE), I identified significant opportunities for efficiency and time management, which can be applied to data analysis, reporting and visualization for better decision-making, and leveraging market trends for financial decisions.\n\nMy usual routine includes bank transaction records and postings, reconciliation, financial preparation, year-end account closure, budgeting, financial modeling with scenario building, and other workflows.\n\nWhy apply for an internship? I am someone who firmly believes in growth through overcoming new challenges and change acts as a catalyst for that progress, and even after the organized webinar, I am reapplying because I view this as a valuable opportunity for mutual exchange in areas I am familiar with.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n",https://www.linkedin.com/in/evelyn-inegbenije/,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1729627219365_Evelyn's Resume profile -pdf.pdf,6717cc6cdd7522120ce48975,Financial Analyst Intern,2024-10-22T20:00:21.969Z,2024-10-22T20:00:21.969Z,,,,,,,,,
