67189fa9dd7522120ce4969d,Kareem Kareem Akande,+2348111131144,kareemkakkr@gmail.com,Nigeria," \n\nMy name is Kareem Kareem and I have just concluded my university degree in Accounting achieving a first class at the University of Lagos. My ability to lead and collaborate effectively within a team coupled with my exceptional time management and discipline, proven through balancing college activities and exams with professional exam preparation, underscore my readiness to handle multiple tasks and meaningfully contribute to due diligence, fundraising and investor relations efforts that will ensure the achievement of both the segment’s and company’s goals.\nA recent highlight in my journey was my involvement in a business challenge sponsored by Morgan Stanley Investment Management (MSIM). In summer 2024, initially I was one of 55 selected globally to take part in this challenge. I was then part of a team of 10 tasked with creating a marketing strategy and campaign to raise awareness into the investment management industry. Due to the time constraint attached with this challenge, I quickly suggested that we broke ourselves into teams, and I was a part of the engagement and connection team. I and my team-mate came up with an in person channel that will facilitate physical connections, and as a result of my contribution in this challenge, I was rewarded with the opportunity to present to MSIM executives at the end of the week. As a result of being selected as one of 25 to take part in the business challenge set up by MSIM, we had the direct responsibility of coming up with a presentation that highlighted the challenges and solutions that would be considered in distributing an ESG strategy to institutional investors in different markets. The pressure of ensuring that our recommendations and solutions were authentic and appropriate was paramount as we were presenting to MSIM executives. Due to the complexity of this challenge, I had to analyse both quantitative and qualitative data on the different considerations that had to be looked at in solving this challenge. In working with so many people, I ensured that we were always communicating by devising the use of ‘google docs’ to facilitate not only intra- department communication but also inter-department communication. With my team’s and I collaboration in this work, we were greatly commended for not only a well-thought out presentation but also for being the best team since the inception of the annual challenge set by MSIM.\n\nInspired by observing financial mismanagement in my community, I am driven to expanding my knowledge on private markets investing, and as a result creating awareness for safe and secure investment opportunities for my community. My goal is to leverage my accounting and finance knowledge, including my ICAN certification and experience from this internship opportunity. I believe this program will enhance my skills and support my professional development. I look forward to discussing my application and learning more UBS\nIn recent times, I have had the challenge of balancing demanding responsibilities. I was faced with the dilemma of participating in the biggest sport competition for universities in Nigeria while also preparing for the Institute of Chartered Accountants of Nigeria (ICAN) exams ( the highest level of membership for accountants in Nigeria). It was at this moment in my life that I really understood the saying “Time is a Luxury”. I had to practice for the competition every day of the week and also had to study everyday for my professional exams. It was both mentally and physically tasking as I had to be time-disciplined and also be\nable to alter my focus to the activity I was carrying out at each particular time. This was a very\ninteresting experience for me, and my discipline and time-management skills resulted in me passing my professional exams and also ended up losing at the latter stages in the competition.\nIn addition to the above, my leadership experience extends to organizing community initiatives.\nLast year, I co-led a Ramadan charity drive where we raised donations to provide food for less\nprivilege families. The complexity of this particular donation was that we had 5 days to pull off\nthis feat. To be able to achieve this goal we set for ourselves, I had to first collate all the responsibilities I thought would help us achieve our goal and then share it to the rest of the team members. With every member having a clear and specific responsibility to carry out, we were able to achieve our all time high in money raised and as a result, we were able to impact more families across numerous states in Nigeria.\nI also enjoy reading on finance articles and papers published by seasoned professionals on their views about certain interesting topics surrounding the industry.",,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1729666983586_KAREEM KAREEM cv.pdf,6717cc6cdd7522120ce48975,Financial Analyst Intern,2024-10-23T07:03:05.989Z,2024-10-23T07:03:05.989Z,,,,,,,,,
6718a0abdd7522120ce496aa,Peace Onyedikachi Anyiamuka,+2349012389141,peaceanyiamuka@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am Peace Onyedikachi Anyiamuka a social media manager with experience in B2B campaigns and tech content. I studied History and International Studies at Tai Solarin University and i am passionate about business and tech startups. I am from Imo State, Nigeria, and values family and collaboration.",https://peace-kachi-anyiamuka.my.canva.site/white-slate-grey-company-dynamic-neons-company-website,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1729667241695_CV 2.pdf,67175c7b301a84ab876896e6,Social Media Management Intern,2024-10-23T07:07:23.955Z,2024-10-23T07:07:23.955Z,,,,,,,,,
6718a126dd7522120ce496b1,"Amao, Precious Oyinkansola ",+23408027479248,amaopressy123@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I'm Precious, a creative and driven individual with a passion for storytelling and social media. As a former TV producer at Soundcity, I honed my skills in content creation, production, and audience engagement.\n\nWith a background in television production, I've developed a unique understanding of what captivates audiences and drives conversations. My experience has equipped me with:\n\n•⁠  ⁠Strong content creation and storytelling skills\n•⁠  ⁠Excellent writing and editing abilities\n•⁠  ⁠Proficiency in scriptwriting and production\n•⁠  ⁠Familiarity with social media platforms and trends\n\nAs a freelancer, I continue to produce and write scripts for various clients, showcasing my versatility and adaptability.\n\nI'm excited to bring my expertise to a social media internship, leveraging my skills to craft compelling content, grow online communities, and drive engagement.",https://www.linkedin.com/in/amao-precious-907379277?trk=public-profile-join-page,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1729667363248_DOC-20240924-WA0000..pdf,67175c7b301a84ab876896e6,Social Media Management Intern,2024-10-23T07:09:26.570Z,2024-10-23T07:09:26.570Z,,,,,,,,,
