67193a01aa636ae4bac9845e,Muritala Olashile Aminat,+2347084871318,muritalaolashile2005@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I'm Olashile Aminat Muritala, an undergraduate of Computer science major. I'm really passionate about product design and making things easy to use and aesthetically pleasing to users. I also wear hat of community management so I have good communication and management skills.\nI'm currently hunting for opportunities to improve on my skills, work with experts, learn on the job and also collaborate with people in the space to build amazing products.",https://dribbble.com/Aminat_Olashile,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1729706495911_Muritala Olashile's Resume.pdf,6717598e301a84ab876896e0,Product (UI/UX) Designer Intern,2024-10-23T18:01:37.935Z,2024-10-23T18:01:37.935Z,,,,,,,,,
67193b2caa636ae4bac98478,Iyekolo Toluwalase ,+23407062843294,iyekolotoluwalase@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I’m Toluwalase Iyekolo, a mass communication student at the University of Lagos.\n\nI started gaining insights on social media management while working as an administrative assistant for a PR agency where I helped with creating templates for content calendars, generating leads, scheduling meetings for the team, and maintaining a great rapport with our clients.\n\nFurthermore, I have worked as an admin assistant for an IT coaching school making use of google tools along with project management softwares to the smooth enrollment of students and created designs for a Nigerian culture-based page on Twitter and with this foundation I would love to take my experience to the next step.\n\nMy journey continued as a content manager for an organization by developing content strategies to engage SheCanDo's audience, collaborating with the Graphic Designer and Social Media Manager to plan and manage content and maintain a content calendar for the team.\n\nWith my journey in these roles, I have learned the skills of creative thinking, taking quick action and taking charge of projects. I have harnessed skills in time management, writing, media management and maintaining good relations with the public which I believe will make me a good fit for the role \n\nI’m a firm believer in teamwork, always willing to take advice and apologize for my mistakes.\n\nThank you for your time and consideration. I’m genuinely excited about the possibility of learning from the company  and contributing to the amazing work being done. And I look forward to hearing back from you.",,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1729706793324_Resume.pdf,67175c7b301a84ab876896e6,Social Media Management Intern,2024-10-23T18:06:36.441Z,2024-10-23T18:06:36.441Z,,,,,,,,,
