671fc5afaa636ae4bac9958a,Rita Echere,+2348146790213,chetachiechere@gmail.com,Nigeria,"Am an Energetic Product Designer, skilled in FIGMA, ADOBE-XD, UX research and HTML/CSS. She has completed several projects, including design of an ecommerce Webapp, mobile to do list and also finance Apps. I am a Multi-talented designer able to take on any required task and adapt to changing conditions with resourceful and hardworking mindset eager to contribute to team success through hard work, attention to detail and excellent organizational skills. Clear understanding of research and analysis and ready to advance professionally. Motivated to learn, grow and excel in an Industry. improving customer satisfaction, proven success",https://www.behance.net/ritaechere    projects I worked on Public transportation system   https://www.figma.com/proto/Iiuwg7k4x3rWAjC8aO9GUl/APP-DESIGN?node-id=1261-4874&node-type=frame&t=zMCB6Wt2AXAZbYf3-0&scaling=scale-down&content-scaling=fixed&page-id=1261%3A2&starting-point-node-id=1261%3A4874&show-proto-sidebar=1   School base system prototype   https://www.figma.com/proto/PbvS670Ck3boGcuq6HPfg2/school-base-system?node-id=1-9655&node-type=frame&t=6TtUjGVVbxYXUU8E-0&scaling=min-zoom&content-scaling=fixed&page-id=0%3A1&starting-point-node-id=1%3A9655,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1730135469388_latest latest Rita Echere CV (1).pdf,6717598e301a84ab876896e0,Product (UI/UX) Designer Intern,2024-10-28T17:11:11.999Z,2024-10-28T17:11:11.999Z,,,,,,,,,
671fc64caa636ae4bac995a4,Madueke Ijeoma Mary,+2349071958336,maduekemary23@gmail.com,Nigeria,"\nMy name is Madueke Ijeoma, and I'm eager to contribute my skills and passion to Tobams Group as a Social Media Intern. \n\nDuring my internship at Automatic Pallet, a digital marketing agency, I gained valuable experience in digital marketing, including hosting our podcast, “Automatic Inbound Marketing.” This role exposed me to industry experts and allowed me to develop a deep understanding of audience engagement and content creation. \n\nI'm proficient in utilizing tools like Google Keyword Planner to optimize content for search engines and have a keen eye for social media trends and analytics.\n\n I'm excited to leverage my knowledge and skills to help Tobams Group elevate its social media presence and achieve its online goal.\n\nBeyond my professional experiences, I'm passionate about content creation and have honed my skills through my own YouTube channel. This venture has provided me with firsthand knowledge of social media algorithms, audience growth strategies, and video editing techniques. I'm confident in my ability to create engaging content that resonates with target audiences and drives meaningful interactions.\n I was opportuned to intern at Royal priss hair hub where I was tasked with creating engaging Linkedin contents.\nI am also very confident in my ability to learn quickly and adapt to new environments.\n\nI do hope that you kindly consider my application and give me a chance to grow and add value to Tobams Group.\n\nThank you.\n",,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1730135625939_My Resume.pdf,67175c7b301a84ab876896e6,Social Media Management Intern,2024-10-28T17:13:48.687Z,2024-10-28T17:13:48.687Z,,,,,,,,,
671fc709aa636ae4bac995c2,Sulaiman Aishat,+23409151885051,hellodeesha@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I'm Aishat Sulaiman, a recent graduate with passion for design and a desire to learn on the job. I have been in my current role for one (1) year now were I've been really entrenched end to end in the design process. I started my career from my Mom's Training Business Centre where i learned Canva, Adobe etc.\n\nThis role has really helped me honed my skills in creating seamless and intuitive design interfaces. \nNow I'm looking for my next career opportunity to take my career further. \n\nOne of my strengths is being a good listener. I understand how to uncover someone's motivation and what drives them by listening to what they are saying but also understanding what's not being said. I feel like I do good job of kind parsing out that. \n\nIn terms of my weaknesses,\nI would say I have a hard time saying no to the point where I'm a team player. I want to help out my team and collaborate with them but I'm learning that I need to self-regulate so I'm not overwhelming myself. First thing I like to do is to understand the problem and I do that by conducting competitive research. \n\nRecently, I was doing a personal project on the bank app in Nigeria. I was checking Stanbic IBTC bank and GT Bank. I realized Stanbic Bank has a better feature eg. Call Center & Face Login which is relevant for people who forgot their password while the call center you can reached out to customer services. while GT Bank lack those two features.\n\nI also like to make sure I build a good rapport with all my teammate to make sure I get their perspective and input on what I'm working on as early as possible and to have in it mind, we are to get the best end result.\n\nUhm, I have the skills in Figma, Prototype and wireframe which are major tool as a UI /UX designer. I am a fast learner and a team player. My passion for design has been from my childhood and I believe I can grow with the organization to add my skills and values to the reputable organization.\n",https://www.figma.com/proto/mAcFyWRJ5CuH38ccqyHgRh/MY-NEW-PROJECT-ACTIVITY?node-id=5-106&t=sbyTBnLIsXW0BE4V-1&starting-point-node-id=5%3A106,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1730135815057_Aishat Sulaiman CV..pdf,6717598e301a84ab876896e0,Product (UI/UX) Designer Intern,2024-10-28T17:16:57.046Z,2024-10-28T17:16:57.046Z,,,,,,,,,
671fc805aa636ae4bac995e9,Victory Esther Aduroja ,+2348138314029,victoryaduroja@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I'm a social media manager with hands on experience creating compelling and human related centered content, developing effective strategies and leveraging analytics to drive brand growth. I am proficient in content creation for various audience and platforms. I am also skilled at facilitating community growth through customer focused approach.\nI have adequately managed brand page using compelling content and copies and a well crafted strategy. I have crafted and executed content that increased brand awareness, reach and content that interaction by over 200% across various platforms.\n\nI have established content calendar and strategy leading to 50% in website traffic from all social media channels in one month. \n\nConsistently monitored page analytics providing working strategies to improve brand content direction.\nI would appreciate the opportunity to connect and discuss this further. Thank you for considering my application. I look forward to the possibility of contributing to your team.",,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1730136067259_ADUROJA VICTORY ESTHER C.V (2).docx,67175c7b301a84ab876896e6,Social Media Management Intern,2024-10-28T17:21:09.230Z,2024-10-28T17:21:09.230Z,,,,,,,,,
671fca23aa636ae4bac9963c,Wale Gabriel,+23409128913734,gabrielwale77@gmail.com,Nigeria,"About Me:\n\nI am an aspiring social media manager and the CEO of a budding creative agency, with hands-on experience managing social media for several organizations, including churches and companies. My work is driven by a commitment to understanding audiences, researching trends, and creating tailored, impactful content. I’m passionate about blending creativity with strategy to enhance engagement and authenticity across social media platforms.\n\nIn my current roles, I actively use social media monitoring tools like Brand24 to stay ahead of trends and refine my approach. I believe that this internship with Tobams Group would offer invaluable opportunities to deepen my knowledge, access advanced tools, and gain insights that would benefit both my personal growth and my agency’s goals.\n\nI am dedicated, optimistic, and detail-oriented, always focused on increasing engagement and showcasing originality and beauty in content. With my experience and proactive approach, I’m excited to bring fresh, unique ideas to Tobams Group, committed to making a lasting impact.\n\n",	https://t.me/+mgKPoCwOYVwxZWE0,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1730136608149_Wale_Gabriel_Resume.pdf,67175c7b301a84ab876896e6,Social Media Management Intern,2024-10-28T17:30:11.285Z,2024-10-28T17:30:11.285Z,,,,,,,,,
671fca2baa636ae4bac99641,Fakunle Oriyomi,+2348136540443,oriyomifakunle@gmail.com,Nigeria,"My name is Fakunke Oriyomi, a graduate of Obafemi Awolowo University. I studied public administration and always eager to learn more and take on new challenge.\nI am an affiliate marketer and have been able close good deals for my company and had built a strong client base through my good communication skills. I look forward to opportunities to learn more and widen my scope of knowledge.",https://www.linkedin.com/in/fakunle-oriyomi-9a1428150?utm_source=share&utm_campaign=share_via&utm_content=profile&utm_medium=android_app,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1730136617072_fakunle's CV.pdf,67175c7b301a84ab876896e6,Social Media Management Intern,2024-10-28T17:30:19.603Z,2024-10-28T17:30:19.603Z,,,,,,,,,
671fd0ceaa636ae4bac996f1,Ojon Chimezie Anthony,+2347037144489,ojonchimezieanthony@gmail.com,Nigeria,"Hello, I’m Ojon Chimezie Anthony, a Nigerian and a Social Media Manager with a Professional Diploma in Social Media Management and Advertising Certification from Digital Marketing Institute (DMSI). I have experience from my internship at NOQUA Ltd, where I developed and implemented social media strategies, created engaging content, and conducted market research.\n\nI’m passionate about driving brand engagement and visibility, and I excel at aligning content with marketing goals to foster meaningful connections with audiences. I can’t wait to explore this new role and leverage my skills in innovative marketing initiatives to help your business thrive. I’m particularly drawn to Tobams Group because of your commitment to shaping the future of tech talent development in Africa. I admire how you specialize in talent acquisition and skill development initiatives, creating pathways for African talent to thrive on the global stage. This aligns with my passion for making a positive impact through strategic collaborations.",https://www.canva.com/design/DAGOslqoyDs/-124-O1A7ZT32D8BQ8_VTA/edit?utm_content=DAGOslqoyDs&utm_campaign=designshare&utm_medium=link2&utm_source=sharebutton,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1730138316569_Chimezie_Anthony O CV.docx,67175c7b301a84ab876896e6,Social Media Management Intern,2024-10-28T17:58:38.367Z,2024-10-28T17:58:38.367Z,,,,,,,,,
