671fd296aa636ae4bac99850,Oluwatoni Ajibare,+23409097784204,oluwatoniajibare@gmail.com,Nigeria,"My name is Oluwatoni Ajibare. I’m a recent graduate of the University of Lagos where I studied petroleum and gas engineering. I got into product design while I was a student and over the years I’ve developed a strong interest in solving problems and creating products that impact lives positively. I’m constantly on the hunt for opportunities to improve user experiences and become a well rounded product designer myself. Outside of work, I love to read books, write, try new places and I’m a huge fitness enthusiast. I’m excited for the opportunity to contribute to a team that creates experiences that better the lives of many.",https://www.behance.net/d3792a52,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1730138772280_OLUWATONI AJIBARE_ PRODUCT DESIGN.pdf,6717598e301a84ab876896e0,Product (UI/UX) Designer Intern,2024-10-28T18:06:14.323Z,2024-10-28T18:06:14.323Z,,,,,,,,,
671fd2adaa636ae4bac9985a,Divine Ikechukwu,+2348036155976,ikechukwudivine17@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I’m a passionate content creator and aspiring product designer with a unique blend of skills and interests that align well with this role. \n\nI have hands-on experience in UI/UX design through a recent project in the frozen food industry, where I helped develop a product catalog app. This project introduced me to the nuances of user-centered design, effective collaboration with stakeholders, and the importance of a thoughtful, impactful user interface.\n\nIn addition to design, I’m passionate about self-development, operations management, and making meaningful change. I bring a keen eye for detail, a strong desire to learn, and an enthusiasm for creating thoughtful, user-friendly designs. I look forward to bringing my diverse skill set and passion to this internship and to contribute to innovative projects",https://www.behance.net/ikechukwudivine1,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1730138794998_UX RESUME.pdf,6717598e301a84ab876896e0,Product (UI/UX) Designer Intern,2024-10-28T18:06:37.641Z,2024-10-28T18:06:37.641Z,,,,,,,,,
671fd2b2aa636ae4bac99860,Madukwe Kelechi Joy,+2348149091475,madukwejoy19@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I have five years of diverse experience, primarily as an Assistant Manager at Affid, an NGO focused on community development. In this role, I coordinated various projects, enhancing program effectiveness and fostering community engagement. My experience also includes working as a content creator and social media manager,  i have cap cut certification and am able to use canva the likes with already made videos which can be shared if selected, where I developed engaging content strategies that significantly increased our online presence and outreach.\n\nAdditionally, I held a graduate trainee role where I gained insights into organizational dynamics and operational efficiency, and I have experience as a  teacher, which honed my communication and leadership skills.\n\nI am particularly excited about this opportunity with Tobams Group because of your innovative approach to investment and commitment to social impact, which resonates with my background in the NGO sector. Outside of work, I enjoy creating content that inspires and educates, aligning my personal passion with my professional pursuits.""\n",www.linkedin.com/in/madukwe-kelechi-60b646174,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1730138800457_KELECHI-JOY-RESUME (1)(24).pdf,67175c7b301a84ab876896e6,Social Media Management Intern,2024-10-28T18:06:42.226Z,2024-10-28T18:06:42.226Z,,,,,,,,,
671fd2c1aa636ae4bac99866,Fakokunde Azeezat Abiola ,+2348034955547,jollyb06@gmail.com,Nigeria,"\nI'm a product designer focused on creating user-centered solutions that blend functionality with aesthetic appeal. My background includes experience in UX/UI design, prototyping, and iterative testing. I believe in the importance of understanding user needs and behaviors to inform design decisions. My approach is collaborative, working closely with cross-functional teams to bring innovative ideas to life while ensuring a seamless user experience. I'm passionate about leveraging design to solve real-world problems and enhance everyday interactions.",https://www.behance.net/biolafakokunde,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1730138815125_My Product Designing CV.pdf,6717598e301a84ab876896e0,Product (UI/UX) Designer Intern,2024-10-28T18:06:57.357Z,2024-10-28T18:06:57.357Z,,,,,,,,,
671fd2c7aa636ae4bac9986b,faith oyeniyi,+23408062527593,faithoyeniyi21@gmail.com,Nigeria,"Dear Hiring Manager, \n\nI am writing this letter to emphasize my excitement at the prospect of joining you and your team as a Product Design Intern at Tobams Group.\n\nOver the course of two (2) years in UX Design, I have attained significant experience working on a variety of production websites and apps, designing primarily in Figma and Adobe Illustrator, working directly with corporate leadership and clients, and helping the software development teams. I believe I would be an excellent addition to the team.\n\nAs a UX/UI Designer, I have consistently delivered on expectations, assisted several teams, designed numerous sites and apps to production, and collaborated with other engineers, designers, product managers and other members of my teams with tools such as Figma, Adobe Creative cloud, Miro, Balsamiq mockups and so on. My most recent role was as a UX designer at Pyramid Finance, where I was been responsible for designing wireframes as well as promotional materials of the Company's finance news platform.\n\nI also have experience working both synchronously and asynchronously in fully remote settings across different time zones. This is evident in my collaboration and leading of a few cross-functional teams across the globe.\nThank you for considering my application. I look forward to the possibility of discussing how my experience aligns with your goals and needs in more details.\n",https://behance.net/faithoyeniyi21,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1730138821345_Oyeniyi Faith's UX.docx.pdf,6717598e301a84ab876896e0,Product (UI/UX) Designer Intern,2024-10-28T18:07:03.095Z,2024-10-28T18:07:03.095Z,,,,,,,,,
