671fd514aa636ae4bac9997c,Ifeoluwapo Soderu,+2348101035765,jics.ux@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am a product designer with about 2 years of experience. I have a solid foundation in design thinking methodology, design principles, design tools like Figma, Adobe XD, Photoshop, and I am enthusiastic about solving problems with digital products. I have never had an internship or job experience but throughout my academic and project experiences, I have worked on various design challenges that helped me grow my problem-solving abilities and collaboration skills.  An interesting fact about me is that I alongside my team members, won the Pharmaceutical association of Nigerian students health Hackathon, where we presented a digital solution to the problem of lack of health record in Nigeria.\nI am excited about the opportunity to learn and contribute to meaningful projects and I believe this internship would be a fantastic opportunity to further develop my expertise while contributing to your team.",https://www.behance.net/IfeoluwapoSoderu,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1730139409993_SODERU IFEOLUWAPO RESUME.pdf,6717598e301a84ab876896e0,Product (UI/UX) Designer Intern,2024-10-28T18:16:52.525Z,2024-10-28T18:16:52.525Z,,,,,,,,,
671fd56eaa636ae4bac9998a,Banjo Esther Olawunmi,+2349169673673,banjoesther29@gmail.com,Nigeria,"As a dedicated social media manager, I specialize in helping business owners elevate their brands by creating meaningful engagement and interaction with their target audience. My expertise lies in driving traffic and connecting businesses to prospective customers. With a strong focus on analytics, I ensure that every effort is data-driven, optimizing performance and delivering measurable results.\n\nI possess essential skills such as creativity, scheduling posts, community engagement, tracking posts engagement, and designing with Canva. I have the knowledge of how to use Buffer for timely and effective content posting.\n\nI love learning and see myself grow positively.",,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1730139499560_Esther's Resume.pdf,67175c7b301a84ab876896e6,Social Media Management Intern,2024-10-28T18:18:22.696Z,2024-10-28T18:18:22.696Z,,,,,,,,,
671fd5b7aa636ae4bac99996,Temisan Orru,+2348165391290,misanorru@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I’m Orru Temisan, a product designer with a strong foundation in UX/UI and a passion for creating meaningful digital experiences. I currently work at Figure UX and have had the opportunity to work on various impactful projects, including the Invio eCommerce App, the Reads eBook App, and a FinPal Budgeting App geared toward Gen Z. My technical toolkit includes Figma, Framer, and Adobe XD, which I use to craft user-centered, visually engaging designs. I’m eager to bring my skills to your team, learn from experienced designers, and continue growing my expertise in product design.",https://victorious-shares-452097.framer.app/,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1730139571877_resume_orru_temisan.pdf,6717598e301a84ab876896e0,Product (UI/UX) Designer Intern,2024-10-28T18:19:35.291Z,2024-10-28T18:19:35.291Z,,,,,,,,,
671fd5bcaa636ae4bac9999b,Salamatu Umar Yahaya,+2349032690424,salamatuumar412@gmail.com,Nigeria,"Thank you very much for giving me this opportunity. Having studied the Job Description, I am confident that I have the skills to excel in this Position. I am a strong communicator, a decisive Problem-solver and I have the skills to make a difference in the team.\n\nI possess time management, Organization and Prioritizing skills and would complete my work very quickly. I have a strong work-ethic and a focus on achieving goals. I am a creative innovator and would bring new ideas to the team.\n\nOne of my greatest strength is curosity and eagerness to learn new things, which would help Organizations take advantage of emerging trends in the industries.",,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1730139578188_VA SALMA RESUME.pdf,6717598e301a84ab876896e0,Product (UI/UX) Designer Intern,2024-10-28T18:19:40.244Z,2024-10-28T18:19:40.244Z,,,,,,,,,
671fd5eaaa636ae4bac999a7,Oreoluwa Bankole-George,+23409058627935,oreoluwabankole312@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am a certified product designer equipped with comprehensive theoretical knowledge \nand practical skills, particularly proficient in utilizing Figma. I possess the requisite skills \nto empathize with users understand their needs and translate those needs into tangible \nproduct solutions. I design aligning with business goals, conducting user research, \ndeveloping product strategies and much more",https://www.figma.com/design/iJLeMx8uD48IOPAcBGR4l4/Untitled?node-id=1-6&node-type=frame&t=EqtKwbhQtCDHtQBq-0 ,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1730139623978_My CV (2) (1).pdf,6717598e301a84ab876896e0,Product (UI/UX) Designer Intern,2024-10-28T18:20:26.756Z,2024-10-28T18:20:26.756Z,,,,,,,,,
671fd5f9aa636ae4bac999ad,Onyinye Anene Michelle,+2347046490653,onyinyemitchelle@gmail.com,Nigeria,"My name is Anene Onyinye. I am writing to express my interest in the Product Designer intern role at Tobams Group. I have a maximum of two years of experience and I believe my skills and experience are a good fit for this role. strong passion for creative aesthetically pleasing designs, solving user problems, I am creating a user friendly and seamless Interface for users.\n\nIn my previous role, I successfully worked on the mobile application for an E-Commerce website . . I developed wireframes, interactive prototypes, designed user interfaces that aligned with products goals. I was able to understand the user needs, conducted user research that contributed to a seamless experiences. I created a design systems and UI components to ensure design consistency across numerous platforms. I also collaborated with product managers and developers which yielded satisfaction concerning the product. I believe my skills combined with the passion I have for designing would be a plus while contributing to the success and mission of Tobams Group.\n\nMy ability to get along as well as my experience as a product designer and ensuring there's a solution to a problem will make me ideally suited for this job. I am confident that my skills and approach to creativity, analytical thinking, and collaboration make me a strong fit for this role. I believe that my proficiency with Figma allows me to put together designs that match requirements of the project given.\n\nThank you for considering my application. I look forward to the possibility of working with Tobams Group.",https://www.behance.net/onyinyeanene,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1730139639084_Onyinye Anene's CV.pdf,6717598e301a84ab876896e0,Product (UI/UX) Designer Intern,2024-10-28T18:20:41.380Z,2024-10-28T18:20:41.380Z,,,,,,,,,
671fd63baa636ae4bac999ba,Abdulkareem Temitope Shakirah,+23408136144208,ranishakirat@gmail.com,Nigeria,"As a passionate UX Designer, my journey began with a unique blend of education and psychology, driving me to craft products that seamlessly integrate functionality and user empathy. With over 7 years of graphics design experience and valuable internship stints, I've honed my ability to create intuitive, problem-solving designs.\n\nMy transition from graphics to product design refined my design process, ensuring deliberate and conscious decision-making. Through collaborative projects and presentations, I developed strong communication skills, learning to effectively articulate design decisions.\n\nMy background in education and psychology informs my design decisions, providing a holistic perspective. I thrive on tackling complex challenges, fueled by a passion for problem-solving and improving users' lives.\n\nI'm confident in my ability to conduct user research and testing, develop intuitive designs, collaborate with cross-functional teams, and drive design decisions with data-driven insights. I'm excited to bring my skills and passion to a role where I can contribute meaningfully to a product team and drive success.\n\nI'm eager to join Tobams Group's dynamic team, leveraging my expertise to deliver impactful, user-centered designs that drive success.\n\nThis version maintains your original voice and structure while making minor adjustments for clarity and concision.",https://www.notion.so/Abdulkareem-Temitope-Shakirah-ed361c7af7b64dc585e863c4a8e8aee0?pvs=4,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1730139705674_CV-Oct 2024 Shakirah Temitope ABDULKAREEM.docx,6717598e301a84ab876896e0,Product (UI/UX) Designer Intern,2024-10-28T18:21:47.564Z,2024-10-28T18:21:47.564Z,,,,,,,,,
671fd6c2aa636ae4bac999c8,Amarachi Ordor,+2349060977348,amarachiordor2@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I'm Amarachi Ordor, an experienced UI/UX designer, proficient in visual design, prototyping, and wireframing on Figma. I'm experienced in user research and user testing. Recently I have designed a lot of websites, mainly local businesses, on the side, worked on personal projects for mobile apps, etc.\nI'd love to learn and help out wherever I can, with offering development and design services to Tobams. ",https://amarachiordor.carrd.co/,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1730139839150_Amarachi's UX design Resume (1).pdf,6717598e301a84ab876896e0,Product (UI/UX) Designer Intern,2024-10-28T18:24:02.453Z,2024-10-28T18:24:02.453Z,,,,,,,,,
671fd6c3aa636ae4bac999cc,Christie Ogunsanwo,+23409043722931,christiesanwo72@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am Christie Ogunsanwo, a digital marketing intern currently volunteering as a social media manager creating content for a self awareness brand.\n\nAs a creative individual seeking opportunities for self development, I went for a traing in Digital marketing and obtained a certification in Social media management & Advertising from Digital Marketing Skills Institute. \n\nAfterwards I put in for Elites Global AI training in content creation which gave me the opportunity to have a one month Externship with a fortune 500 company remotely.\n\n I just concluded the  Workplace Foundational Skills training with I-TRAIN-AFRICA where I learnt soft skills to enhance my employability and work successfully in remote jobs. \n\nI love what I'm doing as a digital marketing intern as it challenges me towards continued self improvement.\n\n I want to work my way up into strategic roles where I can lead campaigns, create business growth, and determine brand direction, starting as an digital marketing intern. \n\n I'm dedicated to lifelong learning and certification, and I'll keep up with industry developments to provide firms with outstanding marketing outcomes.\n\nMaking impact is one of my core values and as the founder of Girls Tech Hub; a budding future vision for young girls in Africa, I love opportunities that will enable me birth this vision.  \n\nI love digital marketing because it creates new opportunities that challenges me to develop new abilities which in turn ignites me to think outside the box by applying creative thinking and bring up solutions in innovative ways. \n\nEmbracing these challenges not only makes me better at what I do, but also allows me to deliver even greater value to the brands I work with.\n\nI'm excited to come on board Tobams group as I learn more and bring value to the table.",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Nskp6v-WtBOq3jo6YvFeKeeRekG2vvSe/view?usp=sharing,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1730139840562_Christie Ogunsanwo Resume.pdf,67175c7b301a84ab876896e6,Social Media Management Intern,2024-10-28T18:24:03.434Z,2024-10-28T18:24:03.434Z,,,,,,,,,
671fd6e3aa636ae4bac999d3,Olayemi Victor ,+2348131312711,olayemevictor@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I'm Olayemi Victor, a passionate and creative product designer with a strong foundation in graphic design. Graduating from Ekiti State University, I've dedicated over 8 years to perfecting my design skills, with 6 years in graphic design and the past 2 years focused on crafting user-centered product designs.\n\nThroughout my career, I've built a solid understanding of visual communication, branding, and user experience principles. My portfolio includes diverse projects that showcase my creativity and problem-solving capabilities. A notable project I recently completed is Elite Career Connect, a job employment site I designed from scratch. I also assisted a colleague in creating a movie-streaming mobile app. You can explore my work in more detail on my portfolio: https://olayemivictor.crevado.com/ui-ux-designs\nand view a walkthrough of Elite Career Connect on my YouTube page: https://youtu.be/mAJfplboHzk.\n\nI’d be happy to showcase the rest of my product designs in the next stage. I’m excited about the opportunity to bring my skills and experience to a dynamic team as a product design intern, where I’m confident my expertise can contribute to innovative projects.\n\nThank you for considering my application. I look forward to discussing how my background aligns with your needs.",https://olayemivictor.crevado.com/ui-ux-designs,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1730139872253_OLAYEMI VICTOR BAM RESUME NEW.pdf,6717598e301a84ab876896e0,Product (UI/UX) Designer Intern,2024-10-28T18:24:35.566Z,2024-10-28T18:24:35.566Z,,,,,,,,,
671fd789aa636ae4bac999e8,Unique Iwuanoruo,+2347034837048,iwuanoruounique@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I would like to communicate my sincere interest in the Social Media Manager Internship position. \n\nMy keen skills are well demonstrated in my over two years in social media management while focusing on important projects where my attention to detail and other skills were essential to the success of my team and projects.\n\nI have acquired an understanding of the responsibilities required in the job description as well as how to meet and exceed the goals and standards set by the companies I have had the pleasure of working with.\n\nI believe I am prepared to handle the exciting challenges this position presents, and I hope you allow me to further discuss my qualifications with you in an interview. I have attached a copy of my resume to this application for your review. Please let me know if you require additional information.\n\nThank you for your time and consideration. I look forward to hearing from you.",,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1730140038451_Social Media Intern Resume - Unique Iwuanoruo.pdf,67175c7b301a84ab876896e6,Social Media Management Intern,2024-10-28T18:27:21.162Z,2024-10-28T18:27:21.162Z,,,,,,,,,
671fd7edaa636ae4bac999f3,Samuel Nwaokocha,+2348054811801,nwaokochasamuel@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I'm Samuel Nwaokocha, a Chemistry and Education graduate from the University of Lagos Nigeria. By combining my skills as a chemist with my passion for design, I aim to excel in the field of UI/UX. With a strong foundation in observations, structures, systems, and problem-solving, I bring valuable transferable \nskills to digital spaces. I'm excited to collaborate with clients, stakeholders, and team members, using my \nchemistry experience to fuel my curiosity and drive my growth as a UI/UX designer.",www.behance.net/itzrealsam,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1730140138606_Resume_SamuelNwaokocha_.pdf,6717598e301a84ab876896e0,Product (UI/UX) Designer Intern,2024-10-28T18:29:01.101Z,2024-10-28T18:29:01.101Z,,,,,,,,,
