672207d1aa636ae4bac99dac,Athini Solontsi,+270788897630,athiniamkhitha@gmail.com,South Africa,"Growing up in Mthatha, Eastern Cape, I saw firsthand the gap that exists between technology and those it can exclude. Watching my grandmother struggle to navigate an ATM left a deep impression on me. This experience opened my eyes to the reality that technology, without thoughtful design, can become a barrier rather than a bridge. Inspired by these early memories, I discovered my passion for UX/UI design as a means to empower marginalized communities with access to technology that is intuitive, inclusive, and impactful.\n\nThis commitment led me to pursue an Honors degree in Information Systems and to take on roles that make a real difference. At ReCreax, where I’m currently leading a health and wellness tech project, I’ve designed interfaces that support user well-being, conducted in-depth user research, and collaborated closely with developers to bring meaningful solutions to life. My internship with Ngwekazi Technologies further strengthened my skills in wireframing, prototyping, and user testing—where every design choice was grounded in real user insights.\n\nTo me, design is more than aesthetics; it’s a responsibility to create experiences that resonate with and empower users. I am excited by the opportunity to bring my unique perspective, empathy, and dedication to your team, creating user-centered products that align with both my values and the innovative mission of your company. This internship is more than a role to me; it’s a chance to continue building technology that speaks to people in a language they can understand and trust.",,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1730283471205_My CV 2024.pdf,6717598e301a84ab876896e0,Product (UI/UX) Designer Intern,2024-10-30T10:17:53.361Z,2024-10-30T10:17:53.361Z,,,,,,,,,
