6731c5bd862b0900d0d7e63e,Olumuyiwa Akintade ,+23408163306586,harkintademuyiwa@gmail.com,Nigeria,"My name is Akintade, and I'm a Front-End developer with a good foundation in JavaScript, ReactJS, and modern tools like Tailwind for styling and Axios for API integration. While I have been on this journey for a few years, my experience has mostly been self-taught, and I am eager to deepen my skills through hands-on work. \n\nOne thing I value is creating meaningful connections and helping others. Whether it's through teaching students in rural areas, where I focus on subjects like Chemistry and Physics, or providing solutions for underserved communities, I'm self driven to make a positive impact and I am interested in sustainable technologies and practical solutions for healthcare, education, and financial inclusion in rural areas.\n\nOn a personal level, I’m someone who resonates with empathy and humanitarian work, as well as creating environments where everyone feels included and supported. I am continuously developing my communication skills and am currently improving my understanding of grammar and rhetoric to be even more effective.\n\nGenerally, I am passionate about learning, growth, and contributing to projects that have a real impact. I see myself in the future at the forefront of tech innovation, leading initiatives that make technology accessible and valuable for everyone.",Https://portf-app.netlify.app,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1731315130668_Akintade Olumuyiwa Resume-1.pdf,672dfb22862b0900d0d7e03d,Frontend Developer Intern,2024-11-11T08:52:13.589Z,2024-11-11T08:52:13.589Z,,,,,,,,,
6731c88b862b0900d0d7e679,Enofua Etue Divine,+23408166925491,divineenofua@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I consider myself a builder. I love building things and my interest in that made me study engineering as my major, later on I learnt about software engineering and it piqued my interest and in no time i started building simple web pages with html and css.  I have over 2 years of experience in software engineering, specializing in front-end development. This journey has solidified my understanding of web technologies and has equipped me with the skills to create robust, user-friendly applications.  I recently built a web application for my school  called Fupps its  has a portal and blog section. The purpose of building it is to help students access resources, check schedules, and connect with staff. In this project, I was hands-on with both front-end and back-end tasks, which  deepened my understanding of full-stack development and taught me the importance of clean, maintainable code.\n\nI’m looking for a place where I can work alongside senior developers and be in a team  who can help me raise my standards for what's expected of any developer.\n",https://deecode-divineenofuas-projects.vercel.app/,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1731315848775_ divineenofua_resume_FE.pdf,672dfb22862b0900d0d7e03d,Frontend Developer Intern,2024-11-11T09:04:11.575Z,2024-11-11T09:04:11.575Z,,,,,,,,,
