6731d367862b0900d0d7e761,Nnaemeka Okalla,+2348103938766,emyokalla@gmail.com,Nigeria,"Dear Hiring Manager,\nI am writing to express my enthusiastic interest in the Frontend Developer intern position. I believe my skillset and passion for the web align perfectly with your company's values and goals.\nWhile I hold a Master’s Degree in Geographic Information System, my journey into frontend development began as I always had interest in providing useful digital solutions that solve real world problems. Since then, I have diligently honed my skills in the core building blocks of web development, mastering the intricacies of HTML, CSS, and JavaScript/Typescript. This foundation empowers me to craft, expanding my skillset in designing pixel-perfect and dynamic user interfaces, interactive and responsive layouts in single page applications. I also bring a robust skill set in Python and Java programming, including expertise in object-oriented design, multithreading, and performance optimization. My hands-on experience has enabled me to deliver scalable and efficient solutions in previous roles.\nMy experience stretches beyond theoretical knowledge. I have contributed in building web applications that serve various niches and industries. During my role as a frontend engineer at Credib, I was involved with designing and implementing the functionalities of the events-planning application, I have also tackled web service and server-side technicalities in my initial role as a backend engineer at Novugrid. Most recent achievement is my contribution towards implementing a major core banking solution (SeaBass) with Sterling bank and the Peerless team as a React Frontend Engineer. SeaBass is a large micro-service and micro-frontend full core-banking enterprise solution. I have also developed personal projects to demonstrate my mastery of important technology stacks and connecting the technical knowledge to problem solving. Shoppay-bazar and Borcelle are personal projects tailored to render Ecommerce services, Agric-trail is another project that improves business records and can be used as a farm inventory solution.\nFurthermore, I am an ardent learner, constantly seeking out new technologies and frameworks to keep up with the ever-evolving landscape of web development. I have strong background in React js, Next js, Nodejs, Typescript, Vue js and other framework libraries, employing aesthetic design patterns from UI frameworks such as SASS, Chakra UI, Material UI and Tailwind CSS. I also have a solid knowledge in backend development using Express js, Nest js, advanced state management with technologies such as Redux and Apollo-client as well as implementing web services using Graphql (Apollo) and REST API.\nBeyond technical competence, I possess valuable interpersonal skills that thrive in collaborative environments. These relevant soft skills which include excellent communication, active listening, teamwork and willingness to learn will enable me to seamlessly integrate into your team, readily receiving feedback and contributing effectively to shared goals.\nJoining this company would be not only a career progression but also a chance to contribute to a company pushing the boundaries of the web. I am eager to learn from your experienced team, delve into the company's innovative projects, and apply my skills to create stunning, user-centric experiences that resonate with your audience. \nThank you for your time and consideration. I have attached my resume for your review and look forward to discussing my qualifications further.\nSincerely,  \nNnaemeka Okalla.",https://nnaemeka-jr-okalla.vercel.app,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1731318628468_Nnaemeka Okalla_CV_Fullstack Developer_.pdf,672dfb22862b0900d0d7e03d,Frontend Developer Intern,2024-11-11T09:50:31.675Z,2024-11-11T09:50:31.675Z,,,,,,,,,
6731e841862b0900d0d7e8ee,Ehidiamhen Aigbiluese,+2349137108162,ehidiamhenaigbiluese@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I'm a frontend developer with a knack for building functional and practical user interfaces. I have 2 years of experience in the field and have worked with various tools including React, Typescript, TailwindCSS, Vite and others. I am constantly learning and keeping up to date with the best practices and tools in the field. I see myself as a great fit for this role because I will give my best to the team, and also learn and grow in the process.",https://ehiz.netlify.app,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1731323965457_Ehiz Resume.pdf,672dfb22862b0900d0d7e03d,Frontend Developer Intern,2024-11-11T11:19:29.830Z,2024-11-11T11:19:29.830Z,,,,,,,,,
673200f3862b0900d0d7ea2b,Iwuchukwu Bruce Odera,+2348068985238,iwuchukwuoderabruce@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I'm a frontend developer who’s all about crafting engaging and interactive user experiences. I love working with Next.js, TypeScript, and Redux to create applications that feel intuitive and responsive. Recently, I built a medical simulation app with interactive interfaces in Chakra UI, and I even incorporated some 3D elements using Three.js and custom shaders to enhance the experience visually.\n\nI’m big on teamwork and love a collaborative environment where I can learn from others and share ideas. Outside of work, I'm usually experimenting with new web animations or exploring 3D design, and I enjoy finding creative ways to bring tech to life. Looking forward to potentially bringing that same energy to your team.",,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1731330288347_Odera Bruce.pdf,672dfb22862b0900d0d7e03d,Frontend Developer Intern,2024-11-11T13:04:51.075Z,2024-11-11T13:04:51.075Z,,,,,,,,,
67320558862b0900d0d7ea4f,Oluwatomi Taiwo,+4407761312090,tomisinatansuyi@gmail.com,United Kingdom,"I am a motivated and tech-savvy professional with a passion for creating user-friendly and innovative products. Experienced in designing, writing, and testing software for new systems, I thrive in dynamic environments with a strong desire for continuous learning and growth. Proficient in JavaScript, TypeScript, React, React Native, Python, Node, and ExpressJS, I excel at delivering high-quality solutions. My technical skills and creativity enable me to tackle complex challenges and drive impactful results.",https://www.linkedin.com/in/oluwatomitaiwo/,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1731331413714_OLUWATOMI TAIWO ats cv (1).pdf,672dfb22862b0900d0d7e03d,Frontend Developer Intern,2024-11-11T13:23:36.132Z,2024-11-11T13:23:36.132Z,,,,,,,,,
67320865862b0900d0d7ea6e,Idris Abdulqudus,+23407067828232,idrisabdulqudus2020@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am Idris Abdulqudus, a seasoned Full-Stack Software Engineer from Nigeria with expertise in building responsive web applications and RESTful services using JavaScript, React.js, Node.js, and MongoDB. I have years of experience in front-end and back-end development, cloud services (AWS, Azure), and API integration, complemented by a proven track record in project management and performance optimization. I have led initiatives that improved operational efficiency and enhanced page load times by up to 30%. I hold dual Bachelor's degrees in Criminology and Tourism and possess multiple certifications, including ICT and Business Skills. I am fluent in English and open to relocation and remote opportunities.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n",https://portfolio.holyentgoldconcept.com/,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1731332194066_Abdulqudus Resume_page-0001.jpg,672dfb22862b0900d0d7e03d,Frontend Developer Intern,2024-11-11T13:36:37.690Z,2024-11-11T13:36:37.690Z,,,,,,,,,
67322013862b0900d0d7eb15,Prince Chukwuemeka Ngumoha,+2347089699162,chukwuemekangumoha@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I'm a software developer with experience in crafting responsive and aesthetically pleasing web sites and apps. Here is a list of some of the projects I've worked on or contributed to over time:\n\n- Inkspire (https://inkspire-three.vercel.app/): The goal of this project was to build out a simple and easy to use online bookstore which would provide users with the ability to search for and order their favorite books online. Built with React.js, JavaScript, SASS (CSS preprocessor for styling) and the React Context API (for state management).\n\n- Nova (https://nova-sable-eta.vercel.app/): A pet project of mine in which I attempted to create a blog for space lovers like myself who would love to get some information about current happenings in the global space industry. I built this out using React.js, JavaScript,  TailwindCSS (for styling) and React Context API (for state management).\n\n- SMPIN official website (https://www.smpin.net/): This is a job I'm currently working on part time. In it's current form, it mostly features information on the programs currently offered by the organization and the current process to apply for membership. But, as the project goes on, we plan to add the ability for users to register for courses from the organization through the website, take their certification exams on the website among other cool features. The project is built using React and TypeScript. TailwindCSS is used extensively for styling.\n\nAmong many other projects currently in the works.\n\nIn addition to being a Software Developer, I'm also a corps member currently serving as the President of the Sustainable Development Goals (SDG) Community Development Scheme (CDS) under the National Youth Service Scheme (NYSC) in Kaduna South Local Government Area (LGA). And in this capacity, I've done and am still doing a lot of work to champion the cause of Sustainability in the local community through various initiatives and projects.\n\nI'm really passionate about learning new technologies and working as part of a team to create and ship digital products that have the potential to positively impact on people's lives. I'd be very happy to join your team.\n\nThank you.",https://prince-teal.vercel.app/,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1731338253861_Resume (3).pdf,672dfb22862b0900d0d7e03d,Frontend Developer Intern,2024-11-11T15:17:39.040Z,2024-11-11T15:17:39.040Z,,,,,,,,,
67322625862b0900d0d7eb2c,Derricks Otieno Opany,+254795154903,opanyderricks@gmail.com,Kenya,"My name is Derricks Opany, a recent Diploma graduate in Information Technology at the Technical University of Kenya. I am writing to express my interest in applying for an internship opportunity within your ICT department.\n\nI am eager to gain hands-on experience in areas such as network administration, IT support, web development,cybersecurity and software development. I am confident that working with your team will provide me with valuable insights and enhance my practical skills, while also allowing me to contribute to your organization’s ICT operations.",www.linkedin.com/in/derricks-opany-240b9b23a,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1731339809859_CvLatest.pdf,672dfb22862b0900d0d7e03d,Frontend Developer Intern,2024-11-11T15:43:33.172Z,2024-11-11T15:43:33.172Z,,,,,,,,,
6732369a862b0900d0d7eb6d,Henry Tochukwu Uzor,+23408038707304,h.uzor17@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I’m Henry Tochukwu Uzor, a passionate and result-oriented software engineer with about two years of experience in frontend development. I specialize in modern web technologies like HTML5, CSS3, Bootstrap5, TailwindCSS, Git, GitHub, JavaScript(ES6), TypeScript, and frontend frameworks like React, and Vue.js. Currently, I work as a Frontend Software Engineer at CypherCrescent Ltd., where I collaborate with cross-functional teams to build high-quality, user-centric web applications.\nAlthough my focus has primarily been on frontend technologies, I have gained some foundational knowledge in backend development with tools like Node.js and MongoDB, allowing me to work effectively across the full stack. My experience also includes working with RESTful APIs, and maintaining scalable backend systems.\nIn addition to my technical skills, I’m a strong communicator and a proactive team player, ensuring efficient collaboration in remote or hybrid environments. I’m excited about the opportunity to bring my skills in both frontend and backend development to your team and help Tobams Group continue to shape the future of tech talent development in Africa.\nI look forward to contributing to your projects and helping Tobams Group deliver outstanding solutions.",https://www.linkedin.com/in/henry-uzor-gmnse/,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1731344023805_Henry Uzor_CV.pdf,672dfb22862b0900d0d7e03d,Frontend Developer Intern,2024-11-11T16:53:46.819Z,2024-11-11T16:53:46.819Z,,,,,,,,,
