67367ff95cfc5403be6ac671,Akaninyene Bartholomew Sunday ,+2348051814481,akabasu2010@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am a seasoned software engineer with specialty in MERN and PERN stack applications where M is for MySQL.\nI and my team were recently involved in the building  of an e-commerce app with a company called Shop Online New York, USA.\nWe were using Redux for state management and axios API library to GET/POST/PUT/DELETE data to/from the database at the backend server.\nI am familiar with the use of Git and GitHub as well as use of Slack for communication amongst team members.\nI played a leadership role as a FrontEnd and Backend lead in the organization.\nThe knowledge gained there is what I intend to bring to Tobams Group which comprises an amazing team of technocrats(developers,etc.).\n\nThank you so much.",https://www.linkedin.com/in/akaninyene-sunday-953039b6,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1731624949904_Akaninyene_Sunday_Resume (1).PDF,672dfb22862b0900d0d7e03d,Frontend Developer Intern,2024-11-14T22:55:53.998Z,2024-11-14T22:55:53.998Z,,,,,,,,,
6736bfd95cfc5403be6ac698,David Omotara,+23408168114402,tomyomo@gmail.com,Nigeria,"Good day. My name is Omotara Ayotomiwa David, and I'm a Mobile App developer based in Lagos, Nigeria, with extensive experience in both frontend and backend development. My career in Tech began with an academic background in Geophysics at the University of Lagos, where I gained a solid foundation in analytical thinking and computational methodologies. During my studies, I grew interested in programming and software development, specifically how technology can provide efficient solutions and improve user experiences. This piqued my interest, and I decided to pursue a career in software development, where I could combine creativity with problem solving.\n\nI worked as a React Native Developer at IBXPeers Marketplace, where I was in charge of continuously improving and expanding the mobile application's features. My responsibilities included building user-friendly interface components, designing reusable UI components, managing state with Redux, and ensuring consistent functioning across both the iOS and Android platforms. In this capacity, I've also honed my skills in integrating backend services and adapting code to platform-specific requirements. Working with IBX has been really satisfying because I have had the opportunity to play a vital role in improving the user experience of a popular app while also growing my knowledge of TypeScript and React Native.\n\nI also worked as a Frontend Developer for Zenolynk Technology Limited, where I helped develop LagRide, an advanced transportation app. I had the opportunity to work on several areas of the app's UI, with an emphasis on performance optimisation and user-centric design. At Zenolynk, I worked directly with backend engineers to ensure the smooth integration and functionality of user-facing features. I also engaged in code reviews to ensure that our codebase was maintainable and scalable. This work strengthened my front-end skills and showed me the value of a smooth integration of design and functionality.\n\nIn my previous work at Yoris Africa, I was part of a team that created a super app with a variety of functions, merging elements of social media, banking, and e-commerce in one application. This was a large project in which I created and implemented user profiles, chat features, and feeds while incorporating complicated functionality such as push alerts. Working on this project helped me to learn about React Native, Redux for state management, and Firebase, as well as the crucial components of deploying apps across iOS and Android platforms with Expo. The fast-paced workplace required me to strike a balance between quality and efficiency, which is a skill I still use at work.\n\nAside from front-end work, I've worked extensively as a backend developer. For example, while working with Silid Link Solutions, I created RESTful APIs in Node.js and Express to support an e-commerce store backend. This project involves extensive business logic for product, order, and user administration, with data stored in MongoDB. Integrating a payment gateway with Stripe, establishing user authentication with JWT, and developing unit tests with Mocha and Chai gave me a comprehensive understanding of backend systems. My brief participation with Olandan Consult also allowed me to make a significant contribution to backend performance optimisation and security, emphasising the necessity of documentation, testing, and deployment.\n\nOn a personal level, I'm constantly working on projects that challenge my technical abilities and allow me to expand on what I've learnt professionally. Tara Social App, one of my side projects, is a tiny social media network that includes user authentication and post creation capabilities. It's been a terrific opportunity to learn about app architecture from the ground up and try out new problem-solving techniques. Another project of mine, an Employee REST API, demonstrates my backend talents by enabling CRUD operations on a MongoDB-based employee database. I also created a Hotels REST API, which was a wonderful way to merge my passion for travel and backend software by developing a searchable hotel database.\n\nMy technical capabilities include React, React Native, Node.js, Firebase, Redux, and Next.js, to name a few, but I also think that my development is driven by the core values I bring to my work, which are continual learning, cooperation, and creativity. I enjoy collaborating with designers, product managers, and other developers to bring ideas to life, and it's rewarding to create products that aren't just functional but also improve the user experience.\n\nAside from my technical life, I am an avid problem solver. I'm always seeking for new ways to challenge myself, whether it's refining chess strategies, solving Rubik's cubes, or increasing my basketball skills. These interests allow me to exercise both my intellect and my body, providing a new perspective and resilience to my work in technology.\n\nIn short, I'm extremely committed to developing technology that solves real-world problems and adds value to people's lives. I'm pleased about the opportunity to offer my talents and grow with a company that values innovation, quality, and user experience. I'm excited to use my technical expertise and enthusiasm for development to make a difference.",https://luxury-kitten-ce3474.netlify.app/,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1731641302767_taraResume (6).pdf,672dfb22862b0900d0d7e03d,Frontend Developer Intern,2024-11-15T03:28:25.550Z,2024-11-15T03:28:25.550Z,,,,,,,,,
6736d1f65353184bdaa70b9a,Akinbode Joshua,+2348143513619,ajosh22.aj@gmail.com,Nigeria,"With over three years of experience as a Full Stack Software Developer, I specialize in building scalable, user-focused web applications using the MERN stack (MongoDB, Express.js, React, and Node.js). My work revolves around crafting seamless user experiences and highly optimized backend systems that drive user engagement and operational efficiency.\n\nIn my recent role at JAK Technologies, I led key projects that increased application efficiency by 30% and boosted user engagement by 35%, leveraging my expertise in ReactJS, NextJS, TypeScript, and NodeJs \n\nCore Technical Skills:\n\n	•	Frontend: Building interactive and responsive interfaces using ReactJS, NextJS, HTML, CSS, and TypeScript\n	•	Backend: Developing robust, efficient server-side applications with Node.js and Express.js, and also MongoDB and SQL for the Database including real-time features and API integration\n	•	Performance Optimization: Dedicated to fine-tuning applications for speed, reliability, and scalability\n\nTeam & Collaboration: I thrive in team-oriented settings, where problem-solving, communication, and collaboration drive project success. My approach is rooted in continuous learning and innovation, staying current with the latest in software development.",https://portfolied.netlify.app/,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1731645939010_Akinbode Joshua Resumes 22.pdf,672dfb22862b0900d0d7e03d,Frontend Developer Intern,2024-11-15T04:45:42.899Z,2024-11-15T04:45:42.899Z,,,,,,,,,
