6779850b76e2ceead6592a01,Modupeola Tunde-Fabiyi,+23408139107044,tundefabiyimodupeola@gmail.com,Nigeria,"\nDear Recruitment Team,     \n                                               \nI am a passionate Human Resource Strategist, with years in managing People across roles, functions in large corporations as well as Start Ups and SMEs.\n\n\n\nI have particular skills in Performance Management administrator across banking sector, fintech, Start Ups and SMEs. Also across different industries to create and design a Performance Management system from Start to finish both with using Excel(Balanced Scorecard) and also to using an HRIS.\n\n \n\n I have also been a part of a multinational company HCM team, where I head the Performance and Resourcing Team for the Nigerian affiliate and over 2000 staff strength. I have experience in presenting HR Analytic reports to the management using PowerPoints & Excel such as Pivot Table, Graph and other Excel skills required to prepare the report as it is relevant to the Personnel Management of the organization. \n\n\n\nMy experience has allowed me to conduct Performance Appraisals from Start to finish and present the report of this to the management team for insight into the company's human resource performance.  \n\n\n\nI have handled the OKR check ins for a Health-Tech organization and also created a Performance Appraisal Scorecard/KPI to reflect the Company's Strategic goals and direction. I redesigned and realigned the KPIs to reflect the current realities of the organization.\n\nI am skilled at employee relations. I have the experience and knowledge to handle employee grievances in the most professional manner.\n\n\nI know I am capable of bringing the same dedication and superb experience to your organization and hope to meet you to further discuss my skills and experience, and how I can add to your already set organizational goals.\n\n\n\nRegards\n\n\nModupeola Tunde-Fabiyi\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n",,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1736017161214_Modupeola Tunde-Fabiyi Nov 2023 (1)-6.pdf,6779024e76e2ceead659295a,Career Development Consultant,2025-01-04T18:59:23.851Z,2025-01-04T18:59:23.851Z,,,,,,,,,
67798aee76e2ceead6592a0c,Oyelere Oluwatosin,+23408140805489,olugbejaoluwatosin@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am a dedicated professional with a strong background in career coaching and development, specializing in guiding individuals through career transitions, goal-setting, and skill development. With a deep understanding of job market trends and employer needs, I help clients identify their strengths and align them with their career aspirations. My approach is client-focused, ensuring tailored strategies to enhance job search success, improve interview skills, and foster professional growth. I am passionate about empowering individuals to reach their full potential and thrive in their careers.",,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1736018667488_Oluwatosin Oyelere_CV-1 (2).pdf,6779024e76e2ceead659295a,Career Development Consultant,2025-01-04T19:24:30.034Z,2025-01-04T19:24:30.034Z,,,,,,,,,
6779929b76e2ceead6592a28,CLEMENT ABIDEMI ABOLARIN,+23408145579769,clementabolarin48@gmail.com,Nigeria,"My name is Clement Abolarin, I'm a highly motivated and dedicated individual with a strong passion for delivering exceptional results and building meaningful relationships. I'm excited to learn, grow, and contribute to a dynamic team.",https://www.linkedin.com/in/clement-abolarin/,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1736020628140_CLEMENT ABOLARIN_CV.pdf,6779024e76e2ceead659295a,Career Development Consultant,2025-01-04T19:57:15.517Z,2025-01-04T19:57:15.517Z,,,,,,,,,
6779ad9676e2ceead6592a48,Amenze Irabor,+23408129674293,amenzeirabor01@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am a Career Development Consultant with over six years of experience in talent management, recruitment, and intercultural training across diverse global markets. I specialize in career coaching, employee engagement, and matching high-performing talent to the right opportunities, with a focus on helping individuals grow professionally and achieve their career goals.\n\nMy career journey began at African Leadership Group and The Room, where I launched the careers of young professionals across Africa by connecting them with dignified work opportunities. Since then, I’ve expanded my reach to global markets, supporting clients in 25+ countries by delivering career guidance, training programs, and bespoke development strategies to professionals at different stages of their career journey.\n\nI hold a Bachelor’s degree in Economics and I am currently pursuing a Master’s in Business Psychology, which enhances my ability to understand workplace dynamics, motivation, and well-being — critical elements in effective career counseling and development.\n\nAs someone who is passionate about helping people unlock their potential, I am committed to creating impactful career paths, fostering professional growth, and empowering individuals to navigate career transitions successfully.",,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1736027539503_Amenze Irabor - CV (Updated CV).pdf,6779024e76e2ceead659295a,Career Development Consultant,2025-01-04T21:52:22.350Z,2025-01-04T21:52:22.350Z,,,,,,,,,
6779b25a76e2ceead6592a4f,Itunu Oluremi Awogboro,+2348067382721,awogboroitunu@gmail.com,Nigeria,"Itunu Awogboro has evolved as an audacious Management Consultant and Communications Expert, with a career in banking that spanned over 15 years. She has worked extensively in the areas of customer services, organisational operations and administration, and marketing communications. She had her first degree in Mass Communication, and an MBA specialising in Human Resources. She is a Fellow of the Institute of Management Consultants, Nigeria (FIMC), a Certified Management Consultant (CMC), a Member of the Nigerian Institute of Public Relations (NIPR), an Associate of the Chartered Institute of Finance and Control of Nigeria (CIFCN) and the Women in Management, Business and Public Service (WIMBIZ).\n\nItunu is a fashion enthusiast, prolific writer and author, public speaker, coach, and corporate trainer.\n\nShe mentors, volunteers, and partners with several Non-profits and social enterprises such as the School of Purpose and Influence- SPIN, Kingdom Leaders Global Alliance- KGA, Awesome Treasures Foundation- ATF and Young Disciples International –YDI.\n",,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1736028759476_Itunu Awogboro CV (Updated).docx,6779024e76e2ceead659295a,Career Development Consultant,2025-01-04T22:12:42.970Z,2025-01-04T22:12:42.970Z,,,,,,,,,
