6779ed3476e2ceead6592a82,Ogunleye faith Mituogbo ,+2348126104624,mituogbofaith@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am a graduate of Business Education from the Federal University, Oye Ekiti, Nigeria. During my academic journey, I excelled as a student, earning a prestigious Federal Government scholarship awarded to only five students in my faculty. Beyond academics, I gained hands-on teaching experience during my teaching practice at Ayede Grammar School and Iworoko Community College, where I developed strong communication and organizational skills.\n\nAfter graduating, I worked as a customer service representative at Jendol Superstores, where I honed my interpersonal and problem-solving abilities.\n\nI have always been passionate about communication, inspired by my childhood dream of becoming a moderator . My diverse experiences reflect my dedication to learning, adaptability, and ambition to make a meaningful impact in any endeavor I pursue.",,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1736043824889_Cv Ogunleye faith .docx.pdf,6779024e76e2ceead659295a,Career Development Consultant,2025-01-05T02:23:48.249Z,2025-01-05T02:23:48.249Z,,,,,,,,,
677a29aa76e2ceead6592ab5,Anthony Oluwatoyosi Olomola ,+2348138745295,anthonyolomola28@gmail.com,Nigeria,"\nI am a Learning and Development Specialist who analyzes and provides training and coaching support for staff in development of their career. Having check out the job description I am confident that I will excel in this position and contribute effectively to your organization.\n\nI have worked as a Learning and Development professional, where I developed and delivered impactful training programs that align with organizational goals. My experience includes conducting needs assessments, designing training materials, and evaluating program effectiveness. These skills, combined with my project management expertise, allow me to deliver training that is not only engaging but also measurable and results-driven.\n\nThat being said, I have acquired an understanding of this role such as fostering collaboration through community management of learners, coordinating training logistics and schedules, and providing onboarding and learner support. These would be vital for this role and your organization.\n\nI am prepared to contribute to your organization’s growth and success through effective learning and development initiatives. I hope you allow me to further discuss my qualifications with you in an interview. I look forward to discussing how I can bring value to your team.\n\nThank you for your time and consideration, I will be available should you need to contact me or want to learn more about my expertise.",,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1736059303168_Olomola Anthony O.pdf,6779024e76e2ceead659295a,Career Development Consultant,2025-01-05T06:41:46.021Z,2025-01-05T06:41:46.021Z,,,,,,,,,
