677a8da076e2ceead6592c4e,Akiba Asuquo ,+23407069447585,akibaetim7@gmail.com,Nigeria,"\nDear Sir/Madam,\n\nI was pleased to come across your job posting for a Graphic Designer, which immediately captured my attention.\n\nUpon reviewing the responsibilities outlined in the posting, I found that they closely align with my professional background. Consequently, I am enthusiastic about submitting my resume for your review and consideration.\n\nDuring my tenure as a Graphic Designer at The Nigerian Institute of Chartered Arbitrators (NICArb), I had the privilege of engaging directly with clientele, adeptly discerning their needs and effectively communicating these insights to the marketing department. Additionally, I collaborated closely with the Social Media Manager/Business Development Executive, lending support in IT administration and operational oversight, among other responsibilities.\n\nMy hands-on experience in graphic design equips me with a proficient command of various software and applications, ensuring a seamless and efficient execution of my duties in this role.\n\nI have enclosed my resume for your perusal. Please do not hesitate to reach out should you require any further details regarding my background, qualifications or some of my designs\n\nThank you for considering my application. I eagerly anticipate the opportunity to discuss how my skills and experiences can contribute to your team.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nAkiba Asuquo \n\n\n",,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1736084893104_Akiba Asuquo Cv (2).pdf,67794d8455e80fecb1db68e1,Graphic Designer,2025-01-05T13:48:16.237Z,2025-01-05T13:48:16.237Z,,,,,,,,,
677a8de276e2ceead6592c57,Luca Cecconi,+393465982675,cecconiluca6@gmail.com,Italy,"Good evening,\nI'm Luca Cecconi, I'm 26 years old and I live near Milan, Italy.\nAfter a diploma in Figurative Arts, I attended a three-year Graphic & Visual Design course in Milan, developing knowledge of both pure graphics and web design.\nI have always had a great interest in creativity, communication and art, sectors in which I am currently working.\nIn my 5 years of experience as a Graphic Designer, I have developed an excellent knowledge of the Adobe Creative Suite package, especially Photoshop, Illustrator, InDesign, After Effects, Premiere and Figma, with good skills also in Cinema 4D.\nWhen I work I am precise, focused and extremely ambitious.\nI like working with people who believe in what they do, from whom I can learn and to whom I can offer commitment and ideas.\nThis is why I see in you a fantastic reality, in which I represent myself.\nIn thanking you for your time and opportunity, I await your kind feedback. Best regards\nLuca",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1IWpBAxVd-ovwHm7WH8YPIag14cBHCHZa/view,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1736084960016_Resume Luca Cecconi.pdf,67794d8455e80fecb1db68e1,Graphic Designer,2025-01-05T13:49:22.301Z,2025-01-05T13:49:22.301Z,,,,,,,,,
677a8f9e76e2ceead6592c60,Ebenezer Adegoke,+23408104810864,olatunmise007@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am an expert in graphic designing and brand identity, I have more than 7 years of experience in this field of mine. I have demonstrated high level of service and commitment to the organisations I have worked for in the past. I have had the opportunity to work with start-up brands, local businesses and an entertainment industry. I am proficient in Adobe Creative Suite like Photoshop and Illustrator and also CorelDraw. I am confident in my skills in visual storytelling and to translate complex ideas into compelling deigns to contribute to the brand I work with. ",https://www.behance.net/ebunebenezer,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1736085403672_ADEGOKE EBENEZER'S CV.pdf,67794d8455e80fecb1db68e1,Graphic Designer,2025-01-05T13:56:46.948Z,2025-01-05T13:56:46.948Z,,,,,,,,,
677a919f76e2ceead6592c69,Kelvin Joseph ,+2349135097504,kelvinjosechi442@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I'm Joseph Kelvin, a graphic designer who breathes life into ideas through graphic design, UI/UX, and 3D animation. Design is my passion, my language – it's how I express myself, connect with the world, and make magic happen. \n\nA friend recently opened my eyes to the power of LinkedIn and the importance of a strong portfolio. So, here I am, diving headfirst into this exciting new chapter, building my online presence and hunting for opportunities to unleash my creativity. Let's see what we can create together.",https://www.linkedin.com/in/kelvin-kelvin-69a57531a?utm_source=share&utm_campaign=share_via&utm_content=profile&utm_medium=android_app,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1736085916894_KELVIN JOSEPH for Multigate.pdf,67794d8455e80fecb1db68e1,Graphic Designer,2025-01-05T14:05:19.690Z,2025-01-05T14:05:19.690Z,,,,,,,,,
677a91fe76e2ceead6592c72,Samuel Mbachu,+2349115343079,samuelmbachu9@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am thrilled to apply for the Graphic Designer role at Tobams Group. I am confident that my four years of experience in graphic and visual design across diverse industries have equipped me with the skills needed to contribute meaningfully to this role. \n\nIn my recent role at ZendWallet, a company at the intersection of traditional finance and crypto, I have led initiatives that elevated the company’s brand presence. I successfully led and executed the rebranding effort, Improving both digital and physical assets to strengthen brand recognition and drive awareness. I introduced and executed digital email campaigns, designing visuals and writing engaging copy to connect with our audience. Additionally, I played an integral role in a large-scale digital marketing campaign, developing designs and advertisements that drove significant promotional success. \n\nPreviously, as the Lead Visual Designer at Financial Nigeria, I collaborated on high-profile projects for both local and international organizations, including MTN Nigeria. These projects deepened my expertise in media production and marketing solutions that delivered measurable results.  \n\nA standout achievement in my career is serving as the Creative Art Director for Tech Summit Nigeria, a Microsoft-sponsored tech conference. I led branding, video editing, motion graphics, and overall art direction for the summit, developing a visually cohesive and impactful experience that contributed to its success.  \n\nThese experiences have equipped me with advanced skills in brand identity, typography, advertising, and conceptual storytelling. I bring a passion for visual narratives that resonate with audiences and a strategic mindset that delivers results.  \n\nI am eager to bring my creative expertise to your team and contribute to the success of your organization.  \n\nI look forward to the opportunity to discuss this exciting role further.  \n\n",https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1OsfjkDAieYBjamr8ljz-xAdYkWUlZI3W,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1736086011303_Samuel Chibuike Mbachu CV.pdf,67794d8455e80fecb1db68e1,Graphic Designer,2025-01-05T14:06:54.350Z,2025-01-05T14:06:54.350Z,,,,,,,,,
