67868df542ba92331072db94,Ademola Omikunle,+23407032517660,demostat1995@gmail.com,Nigeria,"My Name is Omikunle Ademola Samuel, React Developer with more than one year experience.\n\nI have experience integrating React with APIs, managing global state with tools like Redux or Context API, and optimizing application performance using React.memo, lazy loading, and code splitting.\n\nSome of the projects I’m proud of but not added to my portfolio because of the NDA I signed are WOPA Dashboard which helps in keeping track of welfare contributions, it was built with Next JS. The other project is HR 360 dashboard at seven up bottling company. In this project, I used React to dynamic user interface that interacted with a backend API, managing state transitions and handling real-time data updates efficiently. Additionally, I have worked with React Router for navigation.\n\nI also stay up-to-date with the latest React features and best practices. I enjoy learning and experimenting with new React libraries and tools to optimize development and improve user experiences.",https://my-react-portfolio-omikunle-ademola.vercel.app,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1736871410094_Ademola_OmikunleCV.pdf,672dfb22862b0900d0d7e03d,Frontend Developer Intern,2025-01-14T16:16:53.248Z,2025-01-14T16:16:53.248Z,,,,,,,,,
67868f8d42ba92331072db9e,Jeremiah Oyedele,+2348144602273,oyedelejeremiah.ng@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am a passionate Frontend Developer with four years of experience building responsive, user-friendly, and visually appealing web applications. I specialize in using modern technologies like React.js, Next.js, and Tailwind CSS to create seamless user experiences. I have a strong background in collaborating with cross-functional teams to deliver high-quality solutions, and I take pride in writing clean, efficient, and maintainable code.\nIn addition to my technical skills, I am constantly learning and staying up-to-date with the latest trends in frontend development. I enjoy solving complex problems and bringing creative ideas to life through code. My goal is to create impactful digital experiences that not only meet business objectives but also delight users.",https://findjerrified.vercel.app/,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1736871815621_JEREMIAH OYEDELE.pdf,678627a442ba92331072d7b6,Associate Frontend Developer,2025-01-14T16:23:41.063Z,2025-01-14T16:23:41.063Z,,,,,,,,,
67868ff842ba92331072dba5,Mary Oluwaseun Salau,+2348145509593,marrizzsalau7@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am writing to express my passionate interest in the Software Developer internship posted earlier. With a strong foundation in software development and a passion for backend engineering, I am eager to contribute to your team and further improve my skills in a dynamic and innovative environment.\nI have developed a robust understanding of various backend technologies and frameworks. My proficiency in JavaScript, TypeScript, Node.js, Nest.js, and Express, combined with my experience in working with databases such as PostgreSQL, MongoDB, and Prisma has equipped me with the skills necessary to build and maintain efficient and great backend systems.\nThroughout my academic and personal projects, I have had the opportunity to develop several backend applications. These projects highlight my ability to design RESTful APIs, implement GraphQL, Debugging, and work with both SQL and NoSQL databases. Additionally, my knowledge of HTML, CSS, Next.js and understanding of front-end integration further enhances my capability to deliver comprehensive full-stack solutions.\nOne of the highlights of my experience was developing a bank Application with permission including the following roles (ADMIN, CUSTOMER, AUDIT), which taught me the importance of writing clean, maintainable code and collaborating effectively within a team.\n\nImplementing a user authentication system with secure login and registration functionality. Users will be able to sign up for an account, log in securely, and access protected routes only after successful authentication. Using standard mechanisms to handle password hashing, session management, and user role-based access control. Protected routes should restrict unauthorized access to sensitive functionalities.\n\nDeveloped an Expense Management System that helps users manage their expenses.\n\nDeveloped a QuickPay application where users can pay for their Utilities, purchase Data and Airtime, and convert airtime to cash.\n\nDeveloping a web application that allows administrators to perform CRUD\n(Create, Read, Update, Delete) operations on employee records. Users will be able to add new employees, view existing employee details, update employee information, and delete employee records. Ensuring the system has proper validation and authentication mechanisms to protect sensitive employee data.\n\nCreated an e-commerce website for a local store, enabling customers to browse and purchase products online.\nThe platform featured product listings with images, descriptions, prices, and a shopping cart functionality.\n\nI am confident that this opportunity will provide me with the invaluable opportunity to apply my knowledge in real-world scenarios, gain new insights from experienced professionals, and contribute meaningfully to your projects.\nThank you for considering my application. I look forward to the possibility of discussing how my background, skills, and enthusiasm can be in alignment with the goals of your team.\nWarm regards",https://mary-salau.vercel.app/,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1736871924968_Salau-Seun-Mary CV.pdf,672dfb22862b0900d0d7e03d,Frontend Developer Intern,2025-01-14T16:25:28.332Z,2025-01-14T16:25:28.332Z,,,,,,,,,
678690b442ba92331072dbac,Ogolo Jones ,+2347061075203,jones.ogolo@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am a Frontend Engineer with over 5 years of experience specializing in building responsive and user-friendly web applications. My expertise lies in using modern tools like Next.js, React, and TypeScript to create scalable and high-performance solutions.\n\nI have a strong background in developing reusable components, optimizing applications for speed and SEO, and collaborating with cross-functional teams to bring ideas to life. In my previous roles, I've worked on projects like MAAS (Canonical), Blurbkit, Codaflix, where I led frontend development efforts to deliver seamless user experiences, achieving measurable results like increased engagement and improved subscription retention rates.\n\nI'm passionate about solving problems, constantly improving my skill set, and contributing to innovative projects. I thrive in environments where I can collaborate with others, tackle challenges, and push the limits of what frontend technologies can achieve.",https://www.jonesogolo.com/,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1736872113418_Jones cv.pdf,678627a442ba92331072d7b6,Associate Frontend Developer,2025-01-14T16:28:36.405Z,2025-01-14T16:28:36.405Z,,,,,,,,,
