678774b542ba92331072e208,Adeleye Remi-Alarape,+23408108301202,adeleyealarape@outlook.com,Nigeria,"I am a passionate and results-driven Frontend Engineer with over four years of experience in designing and building scalable, user-centric web applications. My expertise lies in leveraging modern technologies like React (Next.js, TypeScript) and ASP.NET MVC to create intuitive and efficient solutions for industries ranging from insurance to banking and pharmaceuticals.\n\nWhat truly excites me is the intersection of technology and problem-solving—whether it’s optimizing user interfaces to enhance engagement, implementing complex state management systems, or collaborating with cross-functional teams to deliver impactful projects ahead of schedule.\n\nBeyond coding, I enjoy exploring emerging technologies, mentoring junior developers, and contributing to team success by fostering collaboration and innovation. I’m always eager to learn and adapt, striving to create solutions that not only meet but exceed user expectations.\n\nIn my next role, I aim to continue growing technically while contributing to impactful projects that align with both user needs and business goals.",,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1736930482488_Adeleye_Frontend_Engineering CV.pdf,678627a442ba92331072d7b6,Associate Frontend Developer,2025-01-15T08:41:25.201Z,2025-01-15T08:41:25.201Z,,,,,,,,,
6787755442ba92331072e212,Faith Amos Oyebode,+23408068579532,faithamosoyebode@gmail.com,Nigeria,"My name is Faith Oyebode. I previously worked as a Senior Full Stack Engineer at a Japanese software development company named Fake Inc. and I have over five years experience in Software development. I'm seeking for a React Developer role at Tobams Group so that I can utilize my skills to bring various ideas of the organisation to life and also improve existing products in such a way that they are world class, scalable and performant.\n\nI have extensive experience with Nodejs, Nestjs, Nextjs, React.js, Gatsby, Javascript, HTML5, CSS3, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, PHP, Laravel, Material UI and other modern web application development libraries / tools including state management tools (Redux), and version control (Git). I have worked on building a fintech app, e-commerce apps, company information apps, Learning Management System, car repair booking app, kanban app, etc. I have also created a plugin for Gatsby (a React framework) and Strapi ( a headless CMS). I have worked on a monorepo using Lerna and I have also worked with build tools like babel and rollup.\n I've worked with developers from Asia, Australia, South America, North America and Africa. I've built web apps for users from: Australia, USA, Germany, Canada, Japan and Nigeria.\n\nThe links to some of the web apps I've built are listed below:\nhttps://vicprop.com.au (Australian users) \nhttps://mrcbc.com (Canadian users)\nhttps://hongshing.com (Canadian users)\nhttps://vankable.co.jp/lp (Japanese users)\nhttps://redgp.com\nhttps://www.baccprep.com\nhttps://sutori.com.au\nhttps://pro-urban.com\nhttps://gethappyfolks.com/ (Multilingual website) \nhttps://www.healthmarkets.com (USA users)\n\nI am a problem solver, team player, critical thinker and resilient goal-getter. I like to improve on my skills daily so that I can give my best in any project I'm working on.\n\nThank you for your time and consideration. I look forward to an interview with you where I can tell you more about my experience as a Software Engineer and also discuss this opportunity further.\n\nKind regards,\nFaith Oyebode",https://github.com/faithoyebode,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1736930641948_Faith Oyebode resumeÌ.pdf,678627a442ba92331072d7b6,Associate Frontend Developer,2025-01-15T08:44:04.829Z,2025-01-15T08:44:04.829Z,,,,,,,,,
678775f242ba92331072e21a,Christian Peters,+2347066389644,auraqule@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am a skilled frontend developer with over 5 years of professional experience specializing in building modern, high-performance web applications. My expertise lies in React.js, Next.js, TypeScript, and Redux, which have enabled me to deliver scalable and user-centric solutions for various clients and projects.\n\nThroughout my career, I’ve developed a strong passion for creating intuitive and responsive user interfaces. I have experience working in Agile teams, collaborating with designers, product managers, and backend developers to deliver seamless experiences. My hands-on familiarity with tools like Git, RESTful APIs, and Cypress has ensured that I can build efficient, maintainable, and testable applications.\n\nI’m particularly interested in performance optimization, SEO-friendly development, and staying updated with the latest technologies to enhance my work. Beyond coding, I take pride in problem-solving and continuously improving both my technical and communication skills to contribute effectively to team success.\n\nIn this role, I look forward to bringing my expertise in Next.js and frontend best practices to develop impactful projects and grow alongside a dynamic team like yours.",https://github.com/auraqule,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1736930799655_Christian Peters Frontend Resume - updated.pdf,678627a442ba92331072d7b6,Associate Frontend Developer,2025-01-15T08:46:42.252Z,2025-01-15T08:46:42.252Z,,,,,,,,,
