6787782442ba92331072e23c,Vincent Ekene Nwafor,+23408137962688,vincentwilliamsjohn9626@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am an experienced and dedicated full-stack software developer with over seven years of practical expertise in the development of advanced mobile and web applications. I possess proficiency across a diverse array of technologies and specialize in creating seamless user experiences that drive revenue growth and enhance organizational performance. As a collaborative team player, I am skilled at fostering talent, achieving ambitious objectives, and embracing innovation to produce impactful results.",https://www.linkedin.com/in/vincent-nwafor-b1195415b/,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1736931361709_My Resume (3).pdf,678627a442ba92331072d7b6,Associate Frontend Developer,2025-01-15T08:56:04.693Z,2025-01-15T08:56:04.693Z,,,,,,,,,
678779c442ba92331072e245,SUCCESS ISAIAH,+2348065373835,rabbiincode@gmail.com,Nigeria,"With 5 years of experience in software development, I specialize in JavaScript and have developed a strong expertise in modern frameworks such as Angular, ReactJS, and NextJS. Throughout my career, I have successfully designed, built, and deployed scalable and high-performance web applications that deliver excellent user experiences.\n\nMy deep understanding of JavaScript, combined with my focus on creating modular, reusable, and maintainable code, allows me to develop web applications that not only meet functional requirements but also perform exceptionally well. I am highly proficient in implementing responsive, pixel-perfect layouts that adapt seamlessly across all devices and screen sizes. Additionally, my commitment to SEO best practices ensures that the applications I build are optimized for maximum visibility and search engine ranking.\n\nI have a strong background in working within agile teams, collaborating with cross-functional stakeholders to deliver high-quality software solutions. I also prioritize maintaining best practices, including version control, code reviews, automated testing, and comprehensive documentation to ensure robust, scalable, and well-maintained codebases.\n\nFurthermore, I am passionate about staying updated on the latest technology and continuously improving my skills. I regularly explore emerging trends in the JavaScript ecosystem and beyond, always looking for ways to integrate new tools and methodologies into my work to deliver even better results.\n\nI would love the opportunity to discuss how my skills and experience could contribute to the continued success of your team. I am confident that I can bring value to your organisation and help drive impactful, innovative solutions.\n\nCan we schedule a call to discuss the position in more detail? I look forward to learning more about the role and sharing how I can contribute to your organization’s goals.\n\nThank you for your time and consideration. I am eager to connect!\n\nBest regards,\nSuccess Isaiah",,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1736931777515_SUCCESS-RESUME.pdf,678627a442ba92331072d7b6,Associate Frontend Developer,2025-01-15T09:03:00.641Z,2025-01-15T09:03:00.641Z,,,,,,,,,
67877acd42ba92331072e24c,David Etuk,+23408084982962,djetuk@gmail.com,Nigeria,"In 2017, I embarked on a journey to study Software Engineering at the American University of Nigeria, drawn by my interest in games. A few years into the program, I discovered the practicality of programming and its potential for solving real-world challenges. I explored various areas of software engineering and ultimately gravitated toward frontend development.\n\nAfter graduating, I worked with a fitness startup in the UK focused on encouraging users to prioritize their health through fitness challenges, with financial incentives as added motivation. In this role, I primarily worked with React Native and React, with a greater emphasis on React Native. I implemented features such as FCM push notifications, Fitbit integration, badge counts for notifications, and ensured general UI consistency throughout the app.\n\nFor my next role, I joined a fintech startup in Nigeria, developing a credit-based application that enables users to purchase items and pay in installments. In this role, I utilized Next.js to implement dashboard components, ensured UI consistency across the application with Radix UI, and consumed REST APIs.\n\nI am now seeking a new challenge where I can step out of my comfort zone, learn new technologies, and bring my ideas and passion for building robust systems to life while contributing to an impactful project.",https://github.com/Dhei-vid,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1736932042257_Etuk_David_work_experience.pdf,678627a442ba92331072d7b6,Associate Frontend Developer,2025-01-15T09:07:25.173Z,2025-01-15T09:07:25.173Z,,,,,,,,,
