6787afa942ba92331072e420,GODSWILL UGOCHUKWU,+23408039406130,godswillugochukwu88@gmail.com,Nigeria,"Dear Hiring Team at Tobams,\n\nI am excited to apply for the React Developer role at Tobams Group. With over four years of experience as a frontend developer, coupled with a strong background in crafting intuitive user experiences and scalable web applications, I am eager to contribute to your mission of empowering emerging markets through innovative financial solutions.\n\nIn my current role at First City Monument Bank, I have honed my expertise in React.js and JavaScript, leading the development of customer-centric platforms that integrate seamlessly with complex backend systems. One of my most rewarding projects involved developing a payment gateway solution leveraging Mastercard Payment Gateway Services (MPGS) APIs, now actively used by businesses to streamline transactions. This experience underscores my ability to deliver high-quality software aligned with both user needs and business goals.\n\nKey highlights of my experience include:\n\nFrontend Excellence: Proficient in building responsive, high-performance web applications using React.js, Next.js, and modern JavaScript frameworks.\n\nTechnical Leadership: Successfully led cross-functional teams, ensuring timely delivery of scalable and maintainable solutions.\n\nProblem-Solving Aptitude: Adept at debugging complex systems and implementing efficient solutions, contributing to system reliability and user satisfaction.\n\nCollaboration and Growth: Committed to fostering a culture of learning and innovation, regularly mentoring junior developers and sharing knowledge within teams.\n\nMoniepoint’s emphasis on redefining industries through customer-focused engineering resonates deeply with me. The opportunity to work with a team that processes significant transaction volumes while leveraging big data analytics aligns perfectly with my passion for building impactful solutions at scale.\n\nI am confident in my ability to work independently while collaborating effectively across teams to drive technical excellence. I am also keen to embrace new challenges and contribute to Moniepoint’s culture of innovation and growth.\n\nThank you for considering my application. I would welcome the chance to discuss how my skills and experiences align with Moniepoint’s goals.",youfoundmalik.com,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1736945574024_GodswillUgochukwuDeveloperResume.pdf,678627a442ba92331072d7b6,Associate Frontend Developer,2025-01-15T12:52:57.341Z,2025-01-15T12:52:57.341Z,,,,,,,,,
6787b24d42ba92331072e429,Louis Idundun,+23407039557809,idundunlouis@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am Louis Ureune Idundun, a versatile professional with a background in software development, operations management, and data quality assurance. My academic foundation includes a Bachelor’s degree in Civil Engineering from the University of Benin and a Diploma in Computer Engineering with Java from Decagon Institute, where I deepened my technical expertise.\n\nIn my role as an Associate Software Engineer at Decagon, I contributed to the development and deployment of over five software applications, improved system performance by 25% through code refactoring, and ensured 95% code coverage by designing and executing unit and integration tests. My experience at FlexiSaf as a Software Engineering Intern allowed me to enhance my backend development skills and collaborate effectively within a team environment to support feature updates and bug fixes.\n\nI have a strong command of frontend and backend technologies, including JavaScript, HTML5, and APIs, and I am proficient in tools like Git, AWS, and Microsoft Office. My technical expertise is complemented by a keen eye for detail and a commitment to producing high-quality user experiences.\n\nWhat excites me most about the Associate Frontend Engineer Intern role is the opportunity to apply my knowledge of creating seamless and intuitive user interfaces, leveraging my problem-solving abilities, and contributing to impactful projects. I thrive in collaborative environments and am eager to learn and grow within your team.",github.com/louis-idundun,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1736946251322_Louis Ureune Idundun FS Resume.pdf,678627a442ba92331072d7b6,Associate Frontend Developer,2025-01-15T13:04:13.808Z,2025-01-15T13:04:13.808Z,,,,,,,,,
