6793cbc8d3b815f599f64d39,Osatohamhen Ebhohon,+2349136117011,j.s.oebhohon@gmail.com,Nigeria,"My name is Osatohamhen Ebhohon, and I am an enthusiastic self-taught junior frontend\ndeveloper with a strong foundation in JavaScript and its libraries like React.js and\nTypeScript. I am interested in the role you posted: Frontend Developer. Based on my\nexperience as a Software React Developer, my drive to build my professional career,\nimprove my stack and knowledge, and contribute my expertise to the company and team I\nam part of, I believe I am a good fit for the Frontend Developer position.\nMy technical skills include the following:\n1) Proficiency in HTML5, CSS, JavaScript, TypeScript React.js, jQuery, Next.js, and Redux\nToolkit.\n2) Experience with backend technologies like Node.js, Express.js Firebase and MongoDB\nfor full-stack development.\n3) Experience with RESTful APIs and integration of back-end services.\n4) Experience with UI/UX design tools like Figma, Sketch, or Adobe XD is a plus.\n5) Strong understanding of application optimisation, responsive design, UI/UX principles and\ncross-browser compatibility.\n6) Strong Understanding of the Version Control System (Git).\nI am confident that my ability to work and collaborate with other developers in your company\nwill facilitate the creation of intuitive and user-friendly applications that enhance the user's\nexperience with web applications. I excel at simplifying complex tasks and empowering\ndevelopers to achieve their goals seamlessly by prioritising usability and efficiency. I am also\na quick learner; this allows me to learn new stacks to meet your company’s\ndemands.Regarding my professional achievements, I have been able to demonstrate my\nproficiency in the design development and management of applications. Some of my most\nrecent professional achievements are the following:\n1) Developed and managed a full-stack web application called Share-X. Share-X allows\nusers to create and, like posts in real-time, edit and delete posts, upload pictures, and\ncomments and follow friends and display notifications.\n\n2) Engineered a Location-pinning web-based system that users can use to pin customer\nlocations on a Google Map interface. The system allows users to add customer information\nalong with their location, and display the customer's distance from their predefined location.\n3) Developed a responsive automobile web application with cross-browser compatibility\ncalled Showroom that allows users to place orders on cars. The showroom was built with\nReact.js (the database is in the works).\nLinks to these projects can be accessed through their repo on GitHub;\nhttps://github.com/alwayswantedtocode/share-x\nhttps://github.com/alwayswantedtocode/Pinning-Location\nhttps://github.com/alwayswantedtocode/ShowRoom-Project\nNote: Dummy emails will suffice to bypass the authentication.\nIf you are open to a quick chat to discuss the position, I’d love to learn more about it, and\nshare more about my own qualifications. I am thrilled at the prospect of contributing my\nexpertise to your company and playing a role in transforming how enterprises build and run\nsoftware applications. I'm looking forward to talking with you about how my qualifications fit\nthe front-end developer position. Thank you for your time and consideration, I look forward to\nhearing from you.","https://github.com/alwayswantedtocode/share-x, https://github.com/alwayswantedtocode/Pinning-Location, https://github.com/alwayswantedtocode/ShowRoom-Project",https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1737739204757_Osatohamhen Application Resume Intl-2.pdf,672dfb22862b0900d0d7e03d,Frontend Developer Intern,2025-01-24T17:20:08.176Z,2025-01-24T17:20:08.176Z,,,,,,,,,
