6793e8ebd3b815f599f650b0,JOHNPETER IGBOAYAKA,+23409160944188,sapphirecreativity@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am Johnpeter, a graphics designer, website designer and entry-level frontend developer. My journey began with a love for creativity, starting as a graphics designer,  then transitioned to designing and developing user-friendly websites, and I’ve honed my skills in HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and frameworks like React and Tailwind. Through personal projects and freelance work, I’ve developed a knack for translating design concepts into functional and interactive web applications. I also bring a keen eye for design, leveraging tools like Photoshop and Illustrator to enhance web aesthetics.\nBeyond technical skills, I’m a visual enthusiat, I enjoy exploring design trends and see how to implement them in practial projects within my capacity. I am a problem solver who enjoys tackling challenges and collaborating with others to bring ideas to life. I’m always eager to learn, adapt, and contribute to innovative projects.\nJoining your team as a frontend development intern would be an exciting opportunity to apply my skills while growing alongside experienced professionals. I’m enthusiastic about adding value through creativity, hard work, and a commitment to excellence.\n\n",https://sapphirecreativity.com.ng/,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1737746664028_IgboayakaJohnpeterIzuchukwuResume.pdf,672dfb22862b0900d0d7e03d,Frontend Developer Intern,2025-01-24T19:24:27.805Z,2025-01-24T19:24:27.805Z,,,,,,,,,
6793edacd3b815f599f650c5,Oladipo David,+2348125130782,timilehind5@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am Oladipo David Oluwajomiloju, a dedicated and creative Software Engineer with a strong focus on building practical and user-friendly solutions. As a third-year student at Babcock University, I have worked on various projects, including developing Skycast, a weather forecasting application that delivers accurate and real-time weather updates, and CryptoPulse, a platform for tracking live cryptocurrency prices, market trends, and conversions.\n\nI specialize in frontend development, and crafting seamless user experiences. My work is driven by a desire to solve everyday problems through technology, whether by helping users stay informed about the weather, simplifying cryptocurrency management, or creating tools that boost productivity.\n\nI am currently exploring the intersection of AI and software engineering, with plans to integrate smart features into my projects. My approach is hands-on, detail-oriented, and collaborative, ensuring that I deliver high-quality solutions while learning and growing in the process.\n\nIn the long term, I aspire to launch a software company focused on delivering innovative, user-centric applications that improve lives globally.",www.linkedin.com/in/david-oladipo-4a6862288,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1737747881337_ResumeRevamped.pdf,672dfb22862b0900d0d7e03d,Frontend Developer Intern,2025-01-24T19:44:44.887Z,2025-01-24T19:44:44.887Z,,,,,,,,,
6793ee50d3b815f599f650d3,Ogechi Juliet Uhegbu,+23408138780831,julietogechi27@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I'm Uhegbu Ogechi Juliet, a dedicated computer science graduate with a solid foundation in programming, web development, and software engineering principles. My expertise lies in designing and building user-friendly websites and web applications, with a focus on intuitive and engaging user interfaces. I am proficient in HTML, CSS, JavaScript, ReactJS, Next.js, Git, GitHub, SEO, technical writing, system design, and more. Beyond my technical skills, I possess strong problem-solving abilities, in-depth knowledge of modern technologies, and effective communication skills, enabling seamless collaboration within teams. My passion for front-end development began in 2020 when I joined the Google Developer Student Club, where I developed a single-page website that ignited my interest in web development. In 2022, I further enhanced my skills in HTML, CSS, Sass, JavaScript, ReactJS and Next.js through the STUTERN Accelerator program, supported by the Afro-Girls scholarship.\n\nToday, I have proven my ability to contribute to innovative and impactful projects across diverse environments, including startups, large corporations, and open-source communities. ",https://uhegbu-ogechi-juliet.netlify.app/,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1737748043604_Intern Frontend Resume.pdf,672dfb22862b0900d0d7e03d,Frontend Developer Intern,2025-01-24T19:47:28.276Z,2025-01-24T19:47:28.276Z,,,,,,,,,
6793f521d3b815f599f650e1,Habib Lawal,+2348107082266,habiblawaltemitope@gmail.com,Nigeria,"If I had to describe myself, I would say I'm a front-end developer with a creative eye and a real knack for detail. I'm really passionate about making sure designs actually work well, bridging that gap between how something looks and how it functions. That's what initially pulled me into front-end development, I've always been fascinated by where technology meets user experience. This role, in particular, gets me excited because of the opportunity to build smooth, user-friendly interfaces that people actually remember. I love taking designs and turning them into reality using HTML, CSS, JavaScript and React. I'm also a bit of a stickler for clean, efficient code and making sure everything runs smoothly. I genuinely enjoy working with other people, bouncing ideas off designers, figuring out tricky problems with other developers. Outside of coding, I'm just naturally curious. I'm always trying to learn new things and keep up with what's happening in the industry. Whether I'm diving into a new framework or exploring different design systems, I get a real buzz from tackling challenges and pushing myself to grow as a developer. I'm also really big on making sure designs are user-friendly, so accessibility and responsiveness are always top of mind for me. Basically, I'm a developer who cares deeply about both the quality of the code and the impact it has on the people who use it. I'm really excited about the possibility of joining your team and continuing to grow in a field that I truly love.",habiblassz-portfolio.vercel.app,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1737749790368_HABIB LAWAL CV.pdf,672dfb22862b0900d0d7e03d,Frontend Developer Intern,2025-01-24T20:16:33.991Z,2025-01-24T20:16:33.991Z,,,,,,,,,
