67b469ed797571ab1a64877f,Valerie Nwokoye,+23408109268030,valerienwokoye@gmail.com,Nigeria,"Hi, I’m Valerie Nwokoye, \n\nA passionate and results-driven content writer and specialist with a flair for storytelling, creative communication, and social media. I help brands and businesses tell their stories in the most engaging way, connect with their audience, and achieve real results.\n\nI craft compelling blog posts, web copies, landing pages, and ad scripts, and I create relatable live social media content that resonates with people. I currently work with top brands like Konga, Nigerian Breweries, and Oracle, constantly refining my skills in delivering content that adds value.\nWhat sets me apart? I blend creativity with efficiency. I use advanced AI tools to enhance my writing process and have hands-on experience with video editing tools like Canva and CapCut. By combining technology with a human touch, I ensure that my content is not just high-quality but also engaging and impactful.\n\nBeyond work, I love singing, vibing to great music, and, of course, enjoying good food. I’m also a huge dog lover, and I take pride in my collection of potted plants, which bring a little greenery and calm to my space. Whether I’m brainstorming fresh ideas, crafting the perfect campaign, or just enjoying a chill moment, I bring energy and passion to everything I do.\n\nI believe content has the power to make a difference, and I’m always looking for ways to add value to every project I take on.",https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1aCTmE33PJPpaehsHGqyB7UFYXk1DyqnU,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1739876842678_Valerie Nwokoye's CV.pdf,67af2ae8cd5ffcbe9f474fad,Social Media Management Intern,2025-02-18T11:07:25.693Z,2025-02-18T11:07:25.693Z,,,,,,,,,
67b46a88797571ab1a648790,Gabriella Eze,+23409039413920,gabriellaeze.va@gmail.com,Nigeria,"Hi, I’m Gabriella, a creative and passionate social media enthusiast who loves bringing brands to life online. My journey started with a simple curiosity: how do brands connect with people in a way that feels real? That curiosity turned into a passion, and now, I help businesses grow their presence on social media by creating engaging content and building strong online communities.\n\nWhen I designed a landing page for a skincare brand, I saw firsthand how the right words, visuals, and strategy can turn visitors into loyal customers. That experience made me realize how much I love crafting content that not only grabs attention but also drives results.\n\nAt Tobams Group, I see an opportunity to bring fresh, creative ideas to the team, engage audiences, and help the brand stand out in the digital space. I’m eager to learn, adapt, and grow in this role while contributing my skills in social media management, content creation, and community engagement.\n\nI believe social media is more than just posts and likes—it’s about storytelling, building trust, and creating meaningful connections. I’m excited to be part of a team that values creativity and innovation, and I can’t wait to bring my energy and ideas to Tobams Group!\n\nLooking forward to this exciting opportunity!\nGabriella",https://www.canva.com/design/DAGeq-DRyuE/nBd4N8ws-vlVFWegFX_fdg/edit?utm_content=DAGeq-DRyuE&utm_campaign=designshare&utm_medium=link2&utm_source=sharebutton,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1739876997371_Gabriella_Eze_Remote Social Media Management Intern.docx.pdf,67af2ae8cd5ffcbe9f474fad,Social Media Management Intern,2025-02-18T11:10:00.044Z,2025-02-18T11:10:00.044Z,,,,,,,,,
67b47153797571ab1a6487c4,Zinachidi Nwachukwu,+23407015858147,zinachidinwachukwu781@gmail.com,Nigeria,"Dear Hiring Manager,\n\n I am writing to express my enthusiastic interest in the Social Media Management Intern role as advertised. I am a Computer Science graduate with internship experience in Business Development and Data Analysis. My technical background equips me with a deep understanding of technology, enabling me to communicate complex technical concepts to clients and stakeholders effectively. This is essential for identifying client needs, presenting suitable solutions, and building trust.\n\nMy internship experiences have provided practical insights into the Business Development and Data Analytics processes, such as lead generation, market research, client relationship management, data analysis, and visualization. I understand sales cycle dynamics and I am familiar with strategies to identify and capitalize on new business opportunities.\n\nAdditionally, my problem-solving skills, developed through computer science studies, enable me to address client concerns with innovative solutions. My analytical abilities help me derive insights from market trends, customer behaviors, and sales performance, informing strategic decisions.\n\nI thrive in dynamic, fast-paced environments, I am capable of working with cross-functional teams and I am adept at balancing multiple priorities to deliver results under tight deadlines. Overall, I have a proactive attitude, coupled with a strong desire to learn and grow and my blend of technical knowledge, practical business development experience, and strong analytical skills makes me confident that I would be a valuable asset for this organization.\n\nThank you for considering my application. I have attached my resume and I look forward to the possibility of discussing how my background, skills, and aspirations align with the goals of this organization.\n\nSincerely,\nZinachidi Nwachukwu\n07015858147",https://www.behance.net/zinachinwachuk,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1739878737216_Resume_Zinachidi Nwachukwu.pdf,67af2ae8cd5ffcbe9f474fad,Social Media Management Intern,2025-02-18T11:38:59.954Z,2025-02-18T11:38:59.954Z,,,,,,,,,
67b47326797571ab1a6487e1,Solomon Chinedu Anaba,+23408080000296,solomondewise009@gmail.com,Nigeria,"My name is Solomon,  from Abuja Nigeria, and I am writing to fill in the above mentioned position in your organization.\n\nI am a seasoned sales professional with over 8 years of comprehensive experience in B2B sales, customer service, telemarketing, and cold calling. In my career as a salesperson, I have demonstrated a remarkable ability to build strong client relationships, being able to identify customer needs, and provide tailored solutions that drive business growth. \n\nMy expertise includes; appointment setting, lead generation, Customer resolution, Sales Representative and customer service representative. Where I've excelled in scheduling high-value meetings with key decision-makers, ensuring a steady pipeline of opportunities. Adept at leveraging CRM platforms like; (Bitrix24, Zoho, Apollo, and Salesforce), to effectively track and manage leads, monitor sales performance, and streamline customer interactions to enhance efficiency and deliver results. \n\nI have a proven track record of consistently meeting and exceeding sales targets, showcasing my exceptional communication skills, resilience, and strategic approach to challenges.\n\nThe ability to engage clients with professionalism and confidence has been one of my key secrets, coupled with a deep understanding of the market dynamics, has made me a valuable asset to any sales team.\nI am very passionate about delivering outstanding services, thriving in fast-paced environments, and have been committed to achieving long-term success for both my clients and the organization.\n\nMy vast experience in the US market and the working time zone makes me a good fit for the above mentioned role, and  hope to be a good addition to the team as I become part of it.\n\n\nBest regards,\nSolomon ",,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1739879200709_Edu's recent PDF(1).pdf,67b35613797571ab1a647f1c