683847d2d88672837443a60a,AKINBONI AYODELE,+2340967626157,ayoakinboni90@gmail.com,Nigeria,"My WOW factor as an Operations Manager is my ability to bring order and clarity to complex situations. I’m very hands-on I don’t just sit behind a desk; I’m out there with the team, identifying bottlenecks, solving problems on the ground, and making sure that every part of the operation runs smoothly. Over the years, I’ve developed a knack for spotting inefficiencies that others might overlook, and I use data to back up decisions  not just gut feelings.\n\nWhat really sets me apart is how I connect strategy to execution. For example, I once took a process that used to take three days and got it down to one by simply reworking the workflow and reallocating resources based on performance data. I also focus a lot on team dynamics — making sure people are motivated, clear on expectations, and actually understand how their work ties into the bigger picture. That’s where the magic really happens: when a team feels empowered and aligned, results follow.\n\nSo if I had to sum up my WOW factor, it’s a mix of being operationally sharp, data-aware, and people-focused. I get things done  efficiently, reliably, and in a way that builds team morale rather than burns it out.",https://sites.google.com/d/1eqO9cgwWjLMJx3vS3kllgDPT4-EaweBr/p/1WuR-j-1EptkHPMQPU3PBFsnhR5dbRCx3/edit,,6837261ac04303ad82747d7b,Junior Business Operations Manager,2025-05-29T11:41:06.757Z,2025-05-29T11:41:06.757Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1748518863715_Ayodele. Resume.pdf,Applied,,,,,
68384ad0d88672837443a62a,Muyiwa Taiwo ,+2347017305164,taiwo.muyiwa@outlook.com,Nigeria,"I’m Muyiwa a Business Analyst with over seven years of experience helping teams turn big ideas into working solutions. I’ve worked across government, FMCG, and consulting, most recently at the Central Bank of Nigeria where I was part of key projects like the launch of Africa’s first digital currency and the development of a data-driven inflation model.\n\nWhat I enjoy most is bringing structure to chaos, whether it’s through process improvement, clear documentation, or simply asking the right questions. I’ve built business cases, strategy decks, and supported teams through change, and I’m currently deepening my skills through a Master’s in Data Science.\n\nI’m based in Lagos and really excited about the kind of work Tobams is doing. The chance to support international expansion and work on operations from the ground up is exactly the type of challenge I’m looking for next.\n",,,6837261ac04303ad82747d7b,Junior Business Operations Manager,2025-05-29T11:53:52.983Z,2025-05-29T11:53:52.983Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1748519629566_MasterCV-MT160325.pdf,Applied,,,,,
68384bebd88672837443a636,Moses Adaviriku Peter,+23408068376580,petdrock06@gmail.com,Nigeria,"As a young and motivated individual, I am extremely interested in submitting an application for the position. In December, 2016 I completed my studies in Ahmadu Bello University Zaria in the department of Agricultural Engineering and also obtained certificate in Agricultural Engineering. This has given me a range of practical capabilities that will meet the needs of this role and during my service I was train as Peers Educator Trainee. On completion of my National Youth Service Corps (NYSC) I worked as an Assistant Supervisor at Rufai Poultry Farm Holding Nigeria Limited. I also worked Tonia Pharmacy Limited Gariki II, Abuja as Cashier Officer where I received items being Supplied to the organization and also how is being given out. I also analyzed daily activities of the company returns and this had given opportunity about how to analyze issues related to chain supply and also relating with Customers. I also worked in Pirotti Projects and Properties Limited as maintenance officer which are into house estate development. I am currently working in Mangal Cement Industry Limited Iluoba in Kogi State as Packer Plant Operator/Supervisor. My duties are Inspects products prior to packaging and returns rejected products to production departments. Observes packaging operations and inspects containers to verify conformance to specifications starts, adjusts, and repairs packaging machinery, or notifies maintenance department Trains workers in operation of equipment. Requisitions containers and other supplies for delivery to workstations. Analyze and determine all standards for packaging limes and ensure compliance\nto all schedule for processes and develop and maintain all packing orders effectively.\nMonitor and recommend improvements to process and develop and maintain all packing orders effectively. Coordinate with quality and warehouse departments to monitor everyday activities of units and ensure efficient working of both manufacturing. Performs other duties as describe. Manage packing plant shift teams to ensure effective and efficient execution of packing plant activities and achievement of daily production targets. Act as shift in-charge for respective shift team. Assist with reviewing of ATCs for respective shift team and ensure Shift Manager Signs off in a timely manner. Assist in supervising the loading of cement into trucks during respective shift. ·Supervise the operation of packing plant equipment during respective shift. ·Liaise with maintenance engineers for the maintenance of packing plant machine and ensure prompt repairs are carried out when required. Enforce the use of personal protection equipment during respective shift to prevent accidents. ·Ensure effective on-the-job training of packing plant operators. Perform any other duty assigned by the Shift Manager. My motivations include learning new things and challenges of meeting key objectives.",,,6837261ac04303ad82747d7b,Junior Business Operations Manager,2025-05-29T11:58:35.294Z,2025-05-29T11:58:35.294Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1748519911821_MOSES ADAVIRIKU PETER 2 CV and Cover Letter (1).pdf,Applied,,,,,
68384e5fd88672837443a652,Olugbenga  Ezekiel,+2348138580442,10gbenga.ezekiel@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I’m a driven and detail-oriented project professional with hands-on experience leading and supporting complex operations across tech events, partnerships, and product deployments. I’ve led initiatives that required coordinating cross-functional teams, managing logistics, streamlining documentation, and delivering operational excellence. From managing vendor relations at Lagos Tech Fest to implementing automation at Sweez that cut manual error by 80%, I bring a track record of turning plans into tangible results. I’m also deeply familiar with tools like Asana, which I used to optimize workflows and improve team efficiency. With a solid background in tech, event production, and stakeholder engagement, I thrive in fast-moving environments where precision and execution matter.",,,6837261ac04303ad82747d7b,Junior Business Operations Manager,2025-05-29T12:09:03.619Z,2025-05-29T12:09:03.619Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1748520540301_[PROJECT MANAGER] OLUGBENGA EZEKIEL RESUME .docx.pdf,Applied,,,,,
