684ad8598562ff36006dc033,Chidinma Odion Davies ,+2347018531907,dinmaodion@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am a purpose-driven professional with over five years of experience in administration, logistics, and operations coordination. My career journey has equipped me with a strong ability to oversee projects, manage resources, and drive process improvements across different sectors. I currently serve as a protocol officer in my local church, where I lead with intentionality and a passion for impact. Additionally, I co-founded a software company focused on helping SMEs and event-based businesses build digital solutions tailored to their needs. I bring a people-centered approach, a heart for excellence, and a drive to contribute meaningfully to visionary teams like Tobams Group.",,,6837261ac04303ad82747d7b,Junior Business Operations Manager,2025-06-12T13:38:33.915Z,2025-06-12T13:38:33.915Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1749735510819_CHIDINMA-ODION-DAVIES.pdf,Applied,,,,,
684adfab8562ff36006dc044,Nancy Akuffo-Henaku,+233201895707,nancyhenaku@gmail.com,Ghana,"My name is Nancy Akuffo-Henaku, and I am a high-performing Operations and Administrative Specialist with a passion for turning ambitious ideas into streamlined, scalable realities. With a background that cuts across business operations, strategic coordination, and international project support, I bring the firepower of someone who is not just administratively excellent but operationally invaluable.\n\nI have worked remotely across international teams, managed cross-border operations, and built systems that improved collaboration by up to 23% using tools like Notion, Trello, and Airtable. At Efluence, I led cross-functional coordination across legal, risk, and operations teams, managed full-cycle recruitment, conducted market research for expansion into Africa, and even supported sustainability initiatives. At Brook-Land Trust Consult, I worked side-by-side with the CEO to negotiate contracts, streamline workflows by over 37%, and lead talent coordination that reduced turnover by 30%. Whether I am preparing strategic decks, overseeing intern performance, or optimizing operational pipelines, I do not just support, I transform.\n\nWhat sets me apart is my ability to merge structure with speed, logic with creativity, and ambition with action. I see documentation not just as paperwork, but as strategy. I see KPIs not as boxes to tick, but as opportunities to outperform. I move seamlessly between planning and execution, internal systems and external expansion, remote collaboration and local relevance. I am that rare mix of strategist, executor, and team amplifier, all in one.",,,6837261ac04303ad82747d7b,Junior Business Operations Manager,2025-06-12T14:09:47.565Z,2025-06-12T14:09:47.565Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1749737384351_Resumeâ¢[Nancy Akuffo-Henaku].pdf,Applied,,,,,
684aecba8562ff36006dc058,Grace Opigbe ,+23408067036292,queengrace316.daystar@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I’m someone who values creativity and meaningful work. I thrive in organized, collaborative spaces—especially remote environments where everyone brings something valuable to the table.\n\nI’ve worked in remote teams where deadlines were respected, communication was clear, and everyone felt seen. Tools like Google Docs, Excel, and Mailchimp helped me stay organized, track tasks, and collaborate smoothly.\n\nRight now, I volunteer with TIBA (The Iconic Brand Africa) as part of the content team. I contribute articles around personal growth, branding, and entrepreneurship. Collaboration has been a vital part this journey — receiving feedback, refining content, and helping build a strong, helpful brand voice. It’s taught me how to work in harmony with people who share different ideas but pursue the same goal.\n\nSeparately, I serve as a team leader with SGS Ministry, a Bible-based community focused on daily scripture reading and accountability. I manage a small group of readers, acknowledge their daily submissions, encourage consistency, and follow up with those falling behind. I also share strategies with fellow team leaders, helping them organize their groups more effectively. This role blends leadership with genuine care and team building.\n\nOutside work, I enjoy playing musical instruments and creating art. I’m passionate about spreading light and positivity, and I believe in the power of charity and education to uplift disadvantaged communities.",https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1trI7EljXHXo-21t1uMfHRhavqCGZu_lc,,6837261ac04303ad82747d7b,Junior Business Operations Manager,2025-06-12T15:05:30.283Z,2025-06-12T15:05:30.283Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1749740726542_Grace Opigbe - CV.pdf,Applied,,,,,
