68a7a3497d811edda3bfa3ff,Paschal Okonkwo,+23408108110450,paschal859@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I have a background in Mechanical Engineering and began my career during my National Service as an Assistant Project Delivery Engineer at Unilever Nigeria Plc, where I worked on projects to improve factory operations, including supervising the installation of a borehole system for the Foods Factory.\nAfter that, I joined IHS Towers as a Field Support Engineer, where I ensured steady network supply for the Badagry and Seme border areas. In that role, I relied heavily on data, using analytics to plan preventive maintenance and track generator fuel usage, which sparked my deeper interest in data science.\nTo build on that, I completed the Google Data Analytics Certificate, a Data Science Bootcamp with Utiva, and a 15-month Data Science program with ALX, where I worked on projects and collaborations that strengthened my analytical and technical skills.\nI am passionate about continuous learning, and I am currently exploring experiment tracking with MLflow and model deployment. With this mix of engineering, field experience, and data analytics, I am excited about opportunities to apply data-driven solutions to real business problems here at Tobams Group.",https://www.datascienceportfol.io/paschal_ugo,,68a6eadb7d811edda3bf9ecc,Business Analyst Associate,2025-08-21T22:52:57.459Z,2025-08-21T22:52:57.459Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1755816774183_Paschal Okonkwo Data Analyst.pdf,Applied,,,,,
68a7a4137d811edda3bfa40a,Olubunmi Oluwaseun Emmanuel,+2347066377948,olubunmioluwaseun253@gmail.com,Nigeria,"Sure! So, I would describe myself as a very driven and curious person, especially when it comes to working with data. I really enjoy digging into numbers to find the story they're telling and how that can help a business grow.\n\nOne thing I’ve always prided myself on is being a quick and adaptive learner. The tech world moves fast, and I make it a point to stay on top of new tools and trends, whether it’s mastering Tableau, Excel, Power BI, Python, R or getting into machine learning, like I did with my fraud detection project in school. In addition, I make a habit of reading articles from leading data science blogs and industry publications to stay on top of emerging trends and understand how other companies are leveraging data. This isn't just about knowing the latest tech; it's about seeing how to apply it to solve real business problems.\n\nBut beyond skills, I’d say my biggest strength is persistence. When I start something - whether it’s a personal project, a analysis for a client, or even training others - I make sure I see it through. I really value delivering on what I set out to do. Personally, I’ve always been conscious about living sustainably - whether it’s reducing my carbon footprint, minimizing waste, or making eco-friendly choices. Taking the Green Digital Skills certification really opened my eyes to how technology and data can be powerful tools for environmental good, and that’s a passion I’m eager to bring into my professional work.\n\nThat’s actually why I was so drawn to this role at Tobams. Your focus on sustainability and growing African tech talent really matches what I care about, and I believe my analytical skills and my commitment to sustainable practices would allow me to contribute meaningfully to your team’s mission.",https://datascienceportfol.io/oeolubunmi,,68a6eadb7d811edda3bf9ecc,Business Analyst Associate,2025-08-21T22:56:19.147Z,2025-08-21T22:56:19.147Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1755816975992_OLUWASEUN OLUBUNMI_Business Analyst.pdf,Applied,,,,,
68a7a5e87d811edda3bfa431,Somtobenna Emmanuel Ifechigha,+23408125423855,tobey.bonez@gmail.com,Nigeria,"Graduated from the University of Lagos in 2014. I started the NYSC in 2015, as an Assistant Accountant in Weststar Associates Limited (Distributors of Mercedes-Benz, Nigeria). I also became a skilled Data Analyst in the company, 2021, with proven expertise in analyzing complex data sets, identifying trends and patterns, and providing actionable insights to drive business growth.\n\nProficient in statistical analysis and data visualization tools. Seeking to become a Business Analyst in organizations, to leverage my analytical skills and contribute to data-driven decision-making processes. \n\nSkilled in Microsoft Excel, Power BI, Tableau and SQL. Strong operations professional with a Bachelor of Science (B.Sc.) focused in Mathematics and Statistics from University of Lagos.",https://lnkd.in/eX3dMYMW,,68a6eadb7d811edda3bf9ecc,Business Analyst Associate,2025-08-21T23:04:08.237Z,2025-08-21T23:04:08.237Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1755817443789_3. Resume (Somtobenna Emmanuel Ifechigha).pdf,Applied,,,,,
68a7c5057d811edda3bfa452,Ahmed Muminat Ayokunmi,+2348161781413,muminahsmail@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am an Economics graduate with certifications in Google Data Analytics, Business Intelligence, and Project Management. Over the past year, I have built hands-on experience analyzing business data and creating interactive dashboards in Power BI, where I focused on sales trends, customer behavior, and process improvement insights.\n\nI am recently concluded the NYSC program and actively developing my skills in business analysis and data-driven decision-making. My academic and project background has equipped me with strong analytical and problem-solving skills and I am proficient with tools such as Excel, Power BI, SQL and collaborative platforms.\n\nI am particularly excited about this role at Tobams Group because of my interest in technology-driven education and my passion for transforming data into actionable insights that support innovation and growth. I am eager to learn, contribute to meaningful projects and grow my career in business analysis.",medium.com/@muminatahmed,,68a6eadb7d811edda3bf9ecc,Business Analyst Associate,2025-08-22T01:16:53.991Z,2025-08-22T01:16:53.991Z,,,"https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1755825410717_Ahmed, Muminat Ayokunmi CV.pdf",Applied,,,,,
68a81c457d811edda3bfa486,Oluwabunmi Johnson ,+2349069970641,bunmij925@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I'm a driven and ambitious professional with a strong background in business studies. I hold a first degree in Business Studies and I'm currently pursuing my MBA to further enhance my knowledge and skills in business management. Additionally, I'm studying for the ICAN (Institute of Chartered Accountants of Nigeria) certification to deepen my expertise in accounting and finance.\nProfessionally, I'm currently working as a Virtual Relationship Manager at Stanbic IBTC, where I leverage technology to build and maintain strong relationships with clients, provide tailored financial solutions, and drive business growth. My experience in this role has equipped me with excellent communication, analytical, and problem-solving skills.\nI'm passionate about staying up-to-date with industry trends and best practices, and I'm excited about the opportunities that lie ahead in my career. I'm confident that my unique blend of academic pursuits and professional experience makes me a strong candidate for future opportunities.",https://www.linkedin.com/in/bunmi-johnson-720448277,,68a6eadb7d811edda3bf9ecc,Business Analyst Associate,2025-08-22T07:29:09.187Z,2025-08-22T07:29:09.187Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1755847746207_MY RESUME OLUWABUNMI JOHNSON.pdf,Applied,,,,,
68a9c9737d811edda3bfa566,Manasseh Walshak ,+2348106017834,walshakmanasseh@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I’m a frontend-focused developer with a strong eye for design and detail. My background combines building performant, scalable interfaces with a passion for clean user experiences and branding.\n\nMost of my work has been on projects where I’m responsible for translating ideas into code that looks great and works smoothly, whether that’s through modern JavaScript frameworks or ensuring responsive, accessible UI.\n\nBeyond frontend, I’ve also explored backend concepts and I’m currently learning Flutter to expand my skillset into mobile. I enjoy working in collaborative teams where I can contribute to both the visual polish and the technical structure of applications.",https://next-portfolio-ashen-eight.vercel.app,,68a8d3fa7d811edda3bfa505,Associate Frontend Developer,2025-08-23T14:00:19.577Z,2025-08-23T14:00:19.577Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1755957616433_Manasseh_Walshak.pdf,Applied,,,,,
68a9dc0c7d811edda3bfa582,Christopher Benson,+23408149979355,bensonate98@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I decided to specialize in backend development (node js) 2+ years ago even though I have been in and out of the tech space writing PHP. I am a programmer who love problem solving, over the last couple of years I've majorly worked collaboratively on projects using node.js, typescript and relational databases. Most of these projects are FinTech and few are Ecommerce. Currently, I am a working as a junior developer at MMG collaborating with my team in building a cross-border payment application. And right now I am seriously looking forward to delving into what you are building at Tobams Group.",https://bensonchristopher.vercel.app/,,68a8d1237d811edda3bfa4ff,Associate Backend Developer,2025-08-23T15:19:40.212Z,2025-08-23T15:19:40.212Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1755962376433_Benson's resume (5).pdf,Applied,,,,,
68a9f2067d811edda3bfa5ac,Joseph Echewisi,+2347081942536,josephechewisi@gmail.com,Nigeria,"\nAs a software engineer with over 4 years of experience in the freelance, full-time, part-time, and contract sectors respectively, I have developed a strong background in Django and node.js backend development, which are the primary skillbase of my career. During my tenure, I have also developed and maintained complex web applications with Golang, which have been instrumental in improving business processes, user experience, and overall productivity. I am confident in my ability to design scalable and reliable backend architectures, implement REST APIs, structure messaging queues and optimize database queries.",https://github.com/echewisi,,68a8d1237d811edda3bfa4ff,Associate Backend Developer,2025-08-23T16:53:26.637Z,2025-08-23T16:53:26.637Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1755968002884_JOSEPH echewisi resume-1.pdf,Applied,,,,,
