68aa0f687d811edda3bfa5ff,Adefokun Israel,+23407025654929,adefokunadeoluwaisrael@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am a senior backend engineer with over five years of experience specializing in building high-performance, scalable systems using Node.js and TypeScript. My core expertise lies in architecting robust APIs and microservices, with a proven track record of developing systems that handle over 2,500 transactions per second.\n\nWhat excites me about Tobams Group is the intersection of challenges you're tackling. I have direct experience integrating AI/ML models into production environments, similar to the work described in your job description, and I've built complete gamification systems featuring leaderboards, reward mechanisms, and progress tracking.\n\nI'm passionate about using technology to create impactful, data-driven user experiences, and I believe my skills in backend architecture, AI integration, and system optimization align perfectly with the innovative projects you're building.",https://github.com/adecom16/,,68a8d1237d811edda3bfa4ff,Associate Backend Developer,2025-08-23T18:58:48.956Z,2025-08-23T18:58:48.956Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1755975524593_Adefokun_Adeoluwa_Israel_Resume (2).pdf,Applied,,,,,
68aa11777d811edda3bfa60e,Damilola samson,+2349033007929,damilolasamson.ds@gmail.com,Nigeria,"Good day,\n\nI’m excited to bring my software engineering expertise to your team. \n\nAttached is my resume.\nLinkedIn: \nhttps://www.linkedin.com/in/damilola-olusinde/\nGitHub: https://www.github.com/6amson/\n\nProjects I am proud of:\nMonoRepo: a containerized repo utilizing github reusable workflow and Kubernetes clusters (EKS).\nDuduEntertainment: Portfolio website for a Canada-based event planner. \nGaze: An Nft notification platform for mints and transfers.\nStackduck: Distributed queuing system in Rust, eventually to be released as a crate.\n\nThe boldest challenge so far was building AirPlay’s infrastructure. Airplay is a music distribution service servicing up to 4,000 artists in Africa. The major feat was migrating existing analytics (Revenue and streams) into our new infrastructure, ensuring consistency, agnostic analytics parsing, and scalability.\n\nHope to speak soon.\n\nRegards,\nSamson.",,,68a8d1237d811edda3bfa4ff,Associate Backend Developer,2025-08-23T19:07:35.054Z,2025-08-23T19:07:35.054Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1755976052000_Damilola_Olusinde_Software_Engr_Resume.pdf,Applied,,,,,
