68ac6c6b7d811edda3bfad61,Somto Urigwe,+23407045812991,somtourigwe4@gmail.com,Nigeria,"As a backend developer with strong experience building scalable, modular, and real-time applications, I have developed and maintained production-ready systems using Node.js,Typescript,Express, MongoDB, Prisma, Sequelize, WebSockets, Redis, RabbitMQ, and Kafka.\n\nOne of my recent projects was a Community Service backend that supports real-time chat, polls, threaded replies, moderation workflows, file uploads to AWS S3, and WebSocket-based features such as typing indicators and message broadcasting. It integrates Redis for caching and pub/sub, RabbitMQ for inter-service messaging, and Kafka for analytics streaming—fully dockerized and structured for microservices.\n\nI also worked on the MOOOVES game platform, where I implemented core game logic, offline matchmaking via Bluetooth handshakes, win/draw detection, and tournament progression/bracketing. The system included rank calculation, result APIs, and dispute handling—all designed to ensure fairness and real-time synchronization.\n\nIn the Event Service, I built event collection management with S3 uploads, Kafka/RabbitMQ event publishing, and MongoDB integration, plus subscriber management (auto and manual), and collection admin features with invites, role assignment, and notifications. These workflows ensured organizers could manage events, devices, and participant access seamlessly.\n\nI also implemented a Book Collection API with Cloudinary image uploads, advanced search/filtering, pagination, CRUD, and Swagger docs, and an inspection booking system where payments controlled inspection access. Additionally, I built a chatbot API with NLP.js for multi-turn sessions and external API integration.\n\nAcross all my projects, I apply clean architecture principles, prioritize maintainability, and ensure thorough documentation. I enjoy solving complex problems, integrating distributed systems, and building efficient, developer-friendly platforms that scale.\n\nI’m now looking to contribute these skills to impactful backend or full-stack roles in environments that value real-time systems, microservices, and thoughtful design.\n\nSincerely,\nUrigwe Somto\n",https://github.com/urigwesomto201,,68a8d1237d811edda3bfa4ff,Associate Backend Developer,2025-08-25T14:00:11.753Z,2025-08-25T14:00:11.753Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1756130408344_ Resume2.pdf .pdf,Applied,,,,,
68ac6feb7d811edda3bfad7f,Akinrinade Tobiloba,+2348114675297,akinrinadetobilobasb@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I’m a fullstack developer who enjoys building real products that people actually use. I work mostly with React, TypeScript, Tailwind, and Node.js, and I’ve led a small team to build a Hospital Management System that’s now being used by 8+ hospitals. I also do data analysis  for example, I analyzed applications from 5,000+ students for the SAAF Foundation (2024 and 2025) and delivered a detailed breakdown they could act on. Over time, I’ve built dashboards, cybersecurity related project, content platforms education related project,, and even marketplace systems,  I like making sure the UI feels clean while the logic behind it scales well. I’m also explore w AI-driven features into the apps I build, since I believe that’s where the future is headed.",https://antimonycodes-umber.vercel.app/,,68a8d3fa7d811edda3bfa505,Associate Frontend Developer,2025-08-25T14:15:07.307Z,2025-08-25T14:15:07.307Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1756131303825_TOBILOBA AKINRINADE-1.pdf,Applied,,,,,
