68c58fcabbf87b18222469c7,Uchenna Franklin Nnajiofor,+2348084152918,nnajioforuchenna063@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I’m a Frontend Developer with over 5 years of experience building scalable and performant web applications, with a strong focus on Next.js, React, and TypeScript. My work has centered on creating seamless dashboards, real-time systems, and user-friendly products that balance performance with great design.\n\nI’m particularly excited about leveraging Three.js and React Fiber to craft immersive and interactive 3D experiences, and I’ve also integrated AI-driven features that improved automation and personalization in past projects. I enjoy exploring how emerging technologies like AI/ML and gamification can be applied to enhance engagement and create unique user experiences.\n\nI thrive in remote, collaborative environments and bring a mix of technical depth, product sense, and attention to detail that helps teams deliver impactful solutions.",https://github.com/uche7,,68bfe4fff06d9137747b1f7c,Associate Frontend Developer,2025-09-13T15:37:46.559Z,2025-09-13T15:37:46.559Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1757777863192_Uchenna  Franklin Nnajiofor Resume.pdf,Applied,,,,,
68c5ad26bbf87b18222469e9,TUNDE ELESHO,+23407067088193,gemtunde@gmail.com,Nigeria," I’m a Frontend Engineer with over 5 years of experience building high-impact web applications using React.js,Vue, Next.js, Typescript, and a modern frontend stack. I’m passionate about crafting interfaces that are both beautifully designed and highly performant.\n\n\nMy recent work includes building and scaling platforms across  logistic, algritech and fintech industries\n\nSabi Market (https://market.sabi.am/)  – I contributed to a digital marketplace connecting farmers and buyers, focusing on intuitive UI components, smooth data fetching, and responsive design. \n\nKatsu Microfinance Bank   (https://www.katsumfb.com/) – I worked on a financial services platform, collaborating with backend teams to integrate APIs and enforce a consistent, maintainable component architecture.\n\nHydrogenPay Dashboard  (https://hydrogenpay.com/merchant-portal/) – In this fintech platform, I handled performance tuning, built dynamic dashboards, and optimized state management for real-time transaction data.\n\nIndiecampers (https://indiecampers.com) -  Modernized monolithic booking platforms by replacing legacy Redux with TanStack Query, improving data flow and UI responsiveness. and collaborated with designers to deliver pixel-perfect, fully responsive logistic dashboards. \n\n\nMy technical toolbox includes React, Next.js, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, shadcn/ui, Zustand, Graphql, TanStack Query, Testing, and Zod validations. I also bring experience with component libraries, design systems, and API integrations and Nodejs, along with a focus on accessibility and performance. I’ve collaborated cross-functionally in both fast-paced startups and structured teams—comfortable in whatever environment supports great product work.",https://www.linkedin.com/in/tunde-elesho-551629137/,,68bfe4fff06d9137747b1f7c,Associate Frontend Developer,2025-09-13T17:43:02.564Z,2025-09-13T17:43:02.564Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1757785378859_Tunde_Elesho_Frontend_Updated.pdf,Applied,,,,,
68c5b767bbf87b1822246a09,FAHAD ADAMU,+23408069283552,adamufahad123@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I'm Fahad Adamu by name a graduate of BSC.ed Geography from the prestigious Ahmadu Bello University, Zaria.",,,68bfe4fff06d9137747b1f7c,Associate Frontend Developer,2025-09-13T18:26:47.554Z,2025-09-13T18:26:47.554Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1757788004781_Fahad_Adamu_CV (1).pdf,Applied,,,,,
68c5eab4bbf87b1822246a56,David Joseph Etuk,+23408084982962,djetuk@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I will talk about myself in two categories, highlighting my professional experience, and diving into what makes me the main fit.\n\nPROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE\nI am a software engineer - frontend, with over 3.5 years of experience in developing functional applications with reusable components, adhering to design patterns, clean architecture and documentation techniques. Nevertheless, I am not a conventional developer. I like exploring and dabbling into different areas of software development. \n\nDuring my first hire, I worked as a mobile developer for a fitness organization in the UK - Gr8fit, picking up skills in React Native and backend development with firebase and nodejs. I had no prior experience with the technology, but I picked up these skills quickly, leading me to take charge and ownership of feature implementations, like implementation of a badge count for important notifications and unread messages. \n\nFast forward to a few months ago, I interned with PM Accelerator in USA as an AI engineer. My main role in the team was to lead the frontend implementation of the AI-powered application we were working on - a tool for product managers and stakeholders to manage expectations, client relationships and timelines. Nevertheless, I got to work on integrating LLMS - GPT4.0 to analyze user data and email interactions to produce personalized AI responses and actions. I am generally not afraid to get my hands dirty and dig deep. \n\nI am currently working on a school management portal (ymss.netlify.ap, {email: admin@ymss.com, pw: adminpass}), with Postgresql Database, Prisma and Next JS. I had to learn new technology to execute this. The project is still in progress, and I am responsible for the design inspirations, it should be completed soon and we can see the full vision. Another project I am also working on is an energy application (https://africamoving.netlify.app/). \n\nPlease note the school management application is a side project, and the credentials shared is for the hosted local account. I would never share actual project details.\n\nWHY ME\nI have had interest in technology since when I was a kid. From Sega games to advance computing systems and now creating software. But over the years, I had realized that ideas need time to form and mature. So one of my strengths is being able to breakdown ideas into feasible implementation strategies. During my internship at PM Accelerator, I often had meetings with the product manager and other tech leads into the night (time zone), to draw up strategies on what we needed to accomplish. \n\nI am not afraid to take lead and ownership of projects, clearly mapping ways we can achieve progress each week. Furthermore, I saw on the job application that skills in 3D animation is relevant to the role. I do not have experience yet in this area, nevertheless, I see this as a challenge I welcome. I have worked with Framer animation, and I know I can learn this as well.  ",https://github.com/Dhei-vid,,68bfe4fff06d9137747b1f7c,Associate Frontend Developer,2025-09-13T22:05:40.043Z,2025-09-13T22:05:40.043Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1757801136996_David_Etuk.pdf,Applied,,,,,
68c62e70bbf87b1822246a7e,Khairat Adesina,+2348163341593,khairatadesina01@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I’m a frontend engineer with over three years of experience building scalable and user-friendly web and mobile applications. My background is strongly focused on Next.js and React Native, where I’ve delivered projects ranging from high-performance booking platforms to CRM systems that integrate third-party tools like OpenAI and Google APIs.\n\nI’ve also had hands-on experience integrating AI/ML models into frontend applications and optimizing performance using tools like Lighthouse, TanStack Query, and Cypress for testing. Recently, I’ve been exploring interactive experiences with React Fiber and Three.js, and I’m very interested in how gamification principles can improve engagement.\n\nWhat excites me about this role is the opportunity to work on cutting-edge projects that combine Next.js, React Native, AI integration, and immersive 3D experiences. I see it as a perfect match to my skill set, while also giving me room to deepen my expertise in gamification and interactive frontend design. I enjoy collaborating in cross-functional teams, and I’m eager to contribute to building innovative, user-focused products here.”",https://github.com/khairatAA,,68bfe4fff06d9137747b1f7c,Associate Frontend Developer,2025-09-14T02:54:40.929Z,2025-09-14T02:54:40.929Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1757818478012_Khairat-Frontend.pdf,Applied,,,,,
68c642cabbf87b1822246a8e,Fayemi Funmilayo,+2347067543251,fayemi.funmilayo55@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I’m Funmilayo, a software frontend heavy developer with over 3 years of experience building modern web applications. In my last role at a healthcare startup, I worked on the product from MVP to launch, developing responsive UIs, integrating APIs, and optimizing performance for scalability. \nI’m skilled in React, Next.js, JavaScript/TypeScript, and Tailwind CSS, and I also have experience integrating AI tools into web apps.\n I enjoy creating clean, user-friendly interfaces and I’m excited about the opportunity to contribute my skills to the innovative projects at Tobams Group.",https://byfunmilayo.pages.dev,,68bfe4fff06d9137747b1f7c,Associate Frontend Developer,2025-09-14T04:21:30.552Z,2025-09-14T04:21:30.552Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1757823687779_Funmilayo_Fayemi_Resume .pdf,Applied,,,,,
68c69440bbf87b1822246ad1,Chinenye Udo,+234760785187,udochinenye16@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am a motivated and detail-oriented Front-End Developer with a strong foundation in HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and React.js. Having completed projects using React hooks and modern front-end practices, I enjoy transforming ideas into responsive, user-friendly interfaces that enhance the overall user experience.\n\nI am currently seeking an unpaid internship opportunity where I can apply my technical skills, contribute to real-world projects, and continue expanding my knowledge in modern frameworks and industry best practices.\n\nWith hands-on experience building interactive web applications, managing state, and integrating APIs, I bring a problem-solving mindset and a passion for writing clean, maintainable code. I am eager to collaborate with a professional development team, gain practical exposure, and grow into a stronger developer while delivering value to the organization.",https://github.com/Nenyebaby24,,68bfe4fff06d9137747b1f7c,Associate Frontend Developer,2025-09-14T10:09:04.920Z,2025-09-14T10:09:04.920Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1757844542023_front end.pdf,Applied,,,,,
68c6b481bbf87b1822246af4,Daniel Victor Udo,+23409026876052,dannyudo15@gmail.com,Nigeria,"    My journey into web development started as a student who wanted to make learning easier and more engaging for others. That drive led me to create MyEasySchool, a digital learning platform that has supported students across 3 universities in Nigeria. Through this project, I built features like quizzes with progress tracking, gamified learning experiences, and payment integrations, helping students prepare more confidently for their exams. Seeing how it reduced exam panic and positively impacted hundreds of students motivated me to keep pushing my skills further.\n   Over the past 4 years, I’ve grown into a frontend developer specializing in Next.js and React, with additional experience in React Native for mobile apps and integrating AI/ML models to make applications smarter and more personalized. Beyond personal projects, I’ve also worked with various clients, delivering web solutions that not only meet their needs but also exceed their expectations. I place a strong emphasis on clear communication, collaboration, and ensuring client satisfaction, which has consistently led to positive feedback and long term relationships.\n    I also care deeply about building products that are optimized for performance and SEO, because I believe great applications should not only look and feel smooth but also reach the right audience effectively.\n    What excites me most is adding gamification principles into products, making digital experiences not only functional but also fun and motivating for users. I thrive in collaborative environments where I can share ideas, learn from others, and solve problems as a team.",https://danny-portfolio-lilac.vercel.app/,,68bfe4fff06d9137747b1f7c,Associate Frontend Developer,2025-09-14T12:26:41.016Z,2025-09-14T12:26:41.016Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1757852796890_My Resume-1.pdf,Applied,,,,,
68c6f9dcbbf87b1822246b2e,Sanusi Rasheed Babatunde,+2348124174008,sanrosheed01@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am a frontend developer with experience building responsive and user-friendly web applications. Most of my work has focused on modern JavaScript frameworks, especially React and Next.js, where I’ve developed scalable applications and worked closely with teams to deliver features that balance performance and design. What I enjoy most is taking a concept or design and turning it into something people can actually use, whether that’s a simple interface or a more complex, interactive experience.",http://san-portfolio-seven.vercel.app,,68bfe4fff06d9137747b1f7c,Associate Frontend Developer,2025-09-14T17:22:36.779Z,2025-09-14T17:22:36.779Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1757870553843_Sanusi Rasheed Resume.pdf,Applied,,,,,
68c71919bbf87b1822246b59,Abdullah Qaasim,+2348072589256,abdullahqaasim14@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I’m a Frontend Developer who loves turning ideas into smooth, responsive, and user-friendly web applications. Skilled in React, Next.js, and TypeScript, I enjoy writing clean code, solving problems creatively, and delivering products that make the web more enjoyable for users.",https:github.com/Bidex-03,,68bfe4fff06d9137747b1f7c,Associate Frontend Developer,2025-09-14T19:35:53.980Z,2025-09-14T19:35:53.980Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1757878550980_Abdullah Qaasim - myResume.pdf,Applied,,,,,
68c71a93bbf87b1822246b69,Austin Onueze,+23407065861622,austin7443@gmail.com,Nigeria,"Hi, I’m really excited to be applying for the Frontend Engineer role. I’ve spent the last 3+ years building fast, user-friendly web and mobile apps with React, and what I enjoy most is turning complex problems into clean, simple experiences that people actually love to use.\n\nAt StoreHarmony, I redesigned and built the company website, which boosted visibility and sales by 40%, and also worked on an e-commerce platform that really pushed my skills in performance and scalability. At Zealight Innovation Labs, I co-developed an estate management app that ended up being used by 1,000+ residents across four estates in its first year—seeing people use something I helped create in their daily lives was incredibly rewarding.\nI’m strongest with React, JavaScript, REST APIs, HTML, and CSS frameworks like Tailwind and Chakra UI, and I work best in Agile teams where collaboration and clear communication matter. I care a lot about writing clean, maintainable code and shipping products that feel smooth and polished for end users.\nI’d love the chance to bring that same energy and impact to your team.",https://austin-onueze.netlify.app/,,68bfe4fff06d9137747b1f7c,Associate Frontend Developer,2025-09-14T19:42:11.948Z,2025-09-14T19:42:11.948Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1757878929162_Austin's Resume.pdf,Applied,,,,,
68c71bb7bbf87b1822246b71,Ojo Dare,+23408100307953,js.dev.ojodare@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I’m Ojo Dare, a Full-Stack Developer with a strong focus on the frontend, particularly React with Tailwind CSS . Over the past 3+ years, I’ve worked on projects like Visibuy, where I built a responsive e-commerce frontend with React and Tailwind, and BookIt at Techwitclan, where I designed backend APIs with Django. I’ve been working on NewsLet, a personal full-stack project with Node.js and React. More recently, I worked on a fundraiser platform using express js, Nodejs, postgresql with sequelize. Along the way, I’ve expanded into TypeScript, Redux, and React Native for cross-platform apps.\n\nRight now, I’m looking to join a team where I can widen my expertise to Next.js and also contribute to cutting-edge interactive experiences with React Native, Three.js, and gamification principles—which is why this role really excites me.",https://codrexx.netlify.app/,,68bfe4fff06d9137747b1f7c,Associate Frontend Developer,2025-09-14T19:47:03.728Z,2025-09-14T19:47:03.728Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1757879220327_Dare_ojo_cv (1).pdf,Applied,,,,,
68c72a61bbf87b1822246b80,MOSES Tosin Israel,+2348138675286,mosestosin35@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am an ambitious and versatile web and mobile developer with an unwavering passion for technology. My journey into coding was the spark that ignited my ceaseless curiosity and commitment to excellence. Crafting applications that bring smiles to people's faces isn't just a job; it's my calling. I excel in developing responsive, mobile-first web/mobile applications that seamlessly blend creativity and functionality. My technical toolkit is robust and dynamic, featuring mastery skills • ReactJS • React Native • NextJS • MongoDB | Prisma | NodeJS | AWS • Coding Patterns | Problem Solving • System Design • Object Oriented Programming • API Design • Figma-to-code(Locofy AI) • Code-assistant(Devin AI) • AI-Prototyping(Penpot AI) • Documentation(Claude AI) • Testing(Testim) • AI Large Language Model • AI Model Context Protocol • ML In JavaScript • Accessibility(EqualWeb AI) • Animation(Dora AI) • Python | Web3(Cairo) • Typescript • Jest | Playwright • Redux | GraphQL • TailwindCSS | Bootstrap | Material UI | SASS • CI | CD • D3.JS | Three.JS | GSAP | Practical Accessibility • Websocket(Socket.io) • Microservices Architecture • Kubernates • Docker • Multi-Browser Extensions • Terraform • Reactive Programming(RXJX) and more. While soft skills are: Leadership, Teamwork, Teach and Teachable My work isn't just about coding; it's about crafting digital experiences that captivate and inspire",https://tboy-tosin.netlify.app/,,68bfe4fff06d9137747b1f7c,Associate Frontend Developer,2025-09-14T20:49:37.246Z,2025-09-14T20:49:37.246Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1757882973514_Tosin_Resume_Latest.pdf,Applied,,,,,
68c72db8bbf87b1822246b89,Ifedolapo Olawale,+2348072973202,ifemidolapooo@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am a motivated and detail-oriented Frontend Developer with a growing foundation in React and Next.js. Over the past months, I have built and deployed several personal and portfolio projects, focusing on clean UI, responsive design, and smooth user experience. Beyond coding, I am committed to continuous learning and enjoy exploring new technologies that enhance digital products. As a female in tech, I’m passionate about contributing to innovative teams while also inspiring greater diversity in the field.",ifedolly.vercel.app,,68bfe4fff06d9137747b1f7c,Associate Frontend Developer,2025-09-14T21:03:52.546Z,2025-09-14T21:03:52.546Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1757883829433_ifedolapo-CV.pdf,Applied,,,,,
68c73bacbbf87b1822246ba3,James Gbakon,+23409036807483,gbakonjames800@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I have a background in Statistics, which has given me strong analytical and problem-solving skills. In addition, I’ve gained hands-on experience in frontend engineering, utilizing technologies such as React, TypeScript, and Flutter to develop responsive and user-friendly applications. I enjoy combining data-driven thinking with software development to build practical solutions. I’m particularly drawn to this role because it offers the chance to grow as part of a collaborative team while contributing my skills in coding, problem-solving, and continuous learning. I’m excited about the opportunity to add value through both my technical expertise and my adaptability.",https://gbakon-web.netlify.app,,68bfe4fff06d9137747b1f7c,Associate Frontend Developer,2025-09-14T22:03:24.827Z,2025-09-14T22:03:24.827Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1757887401948_James Gbakon_Resume.pdf,Applied,,,,,
68c74113bbf87b1822246bc5,Olatunji Emmanuel Olusegun,+2348039522075,emmanuelolusegun.co@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I'm Emmanuel Olatunji, a passionate and versatile Software Engineer with over 6 years of experience building scalable, secure, and user-centric applications across web and mobile platforms. My journey has spanned backend-heavy roles, but I’ve consistently maintained a strong connection to frontend technologies—especially React.js and Next.js—where I enjoy crafting seamless user experiences.\nCurrently, I work at TM30 Global Limited, where I’ve led the development of machine learning pipelines and secure payment systems, including a card tokenization service integrated with Wibmo. I’ve also implemented NLP algorithms to enhance customer interactions and mentored junior developers in AI and system optimization.\nMy frontend experience includes building interactive dashboards, integrating APIs, and contributing to gamified platforms using React.js, Redux, and TypeScript. I’ve also worked with React Native to deliver cross-platform mobile apps and have hands-on experience with Three.js and React Fiber for immersive 3D experiences.\nI’m deeply interested in the intersection of frontend development, gamification, and AI/ML integration—making this role a perfect fit. I bring strong problem-solving skills, a collaborative mindset, and a commitment to continuous learning. I’m excited about the opportunity to contribute to innovative projects that push the boundaries of digital engagement.",,,68bfe4fff06d9137747b1f7c,Associate Frontend Developer,2025-09-14T22:26:27.728Z,2025-09-14T22:26:27.728Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1757888782043_Olatunji_Emmanuel__o_resume.pdf,Applied,,,,,
