68c82204bbf87b1822246f62,Chukwuemeka Morah,+23408174467822,morahstephen872@gmail.com,Nigeria,"Hi, I'm Morah, a Frontend Developer helping SaaS and Startup companies build blazing-fast, user-friendly web applications using React, Next.js, and TypeScript.\n\nWith 5+ years of professional experience, I help startups build blazing-fast, accessible UIs that boost user engagement and conversion rates using React, Next.js, and TypeScript. My expertise extends to building reusable component libraries, state-managed frontends (Redux, Zustand), and API-driven applications that integrate seamlessly with Node.js, NestJS, or Laravel backends.\n\nI thrive in fast-paced environments and love collaborating with teams to deliver innovative solutions that exceed expectations.",https://portfolio-stephen-morah.vercel.app/,,68bfe4fff06d9137747b1f7c,Associate Frontend Developer,2025-09-15T14:26:12.244Z,2025-09-15T14:26:12.244Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1757946369220_Resume_4.pdf,Applied,,,,,
68c82221bbf87b1822246f69,Luke Emmanuel,+23409032520207,emmaranking07@gmail.com,Nigeria,"Dear Hiring Manager’s,\n\nI am writing to express my interest in the Backend Engineer position. With a strong background in backend development, system architecture, and scalable infrastructure, I specialize in building secure, high-performance, and fault-tolerant backend systems capable of supporting millions of users.\n\nIn my experience as a Fullstack engineer, I have designed and implemented RESTful and GraphQL APIs using Node.js, Express.js, and Prisma, ensuring clean, maintainable, and performant code. I have also worked extensively with relational (MySQL, PostgreSQL) and non-relational (MongoDB) databases, optimizing queries and schemas for scalability and efficiency.\n\nA core part of my expertise lies in system design and architecture. I have architected solutions using microservices, enabling independent scaling, service isolation, and continuous deployment. I have also designed fault-tolerant systems that leverage load balancers, reverse proxies (NGINX), and API gateways to handle high traffic and ensure reliability. My experience includes designing event-driven architectures, applying caching strategies (Redis).\n\nSecurity and performance are always at the center of my work. I have implemented advanced security protocols, including HTTPS/TLS encryption, token-based authentication, role-based access control, and input validation to safeguard sensitive user data. Additionally, I utilize Docker and containerized environments to ensure consistency across deployments and to streamline CI/CD pipelines.\n\nI am particularly drawn to this opportunity because it allows me to apply both my backend engineering expertise and my system design architecture skills to build reliable platforms that directly support business growth and user satisfaction.\n\nI am confident that my background in backend engineering, combined with my ability to design scalable system architectures, makes me a strong fit for this role. I would welcome the opportunity to discuss how I can contribute to strengthening your backend systems and ensuring they scale securely and efficiently.\n\nThank you for considering my application. I look forward to the opportunity to contribute to the company goals.\n\nSincerely,\nLuke Emmanuel.",https://ranking-topnotch.github.io/Luke-Emmanuel-Portfolio/,,68c7f7d6df6a1461fb4c9f3f,Associate Backend Developer,2025-09-15T14:26:41.539Z,2025-09-15T14:26:41.539Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1757946397231_LUKE EMMANUEL C-1-1-1.pdf,Applied,,,,,
