68c9b402bbf87b1822247be0,Osaro Igbinovia,+2347053938894,emmyigbinovia@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I’m a backend engineer with over 6 years of experience building scalable, high-performance systems using Node.js and TypeScript. I’ve worked on projects that involve microservices, RESTful APIs, and cloud deployments across AWS and GCP. I also have hands-on experience integrating AI/ML models into production environments, and I enjoy building features that make user experiences engaging and interactive—like gamification systems, leaderboards, and rewards. I thrive in collaborative, fast-paced teams where I can contribute technically while also helping shape solutions end-to-end. I’d describe myself as highly self-motivated, adaptable, and someone who encourages a growth mindset within teams to get things done together.",https://osaroigbinovia.com,,68c7f7d6df6a1461fb4c9f3f,Associate Backend Developer,2025-09-16T19:01:22.868Z,2025-09-16T19:01:22.868Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1758049279719_Engineer_Osaro_Resume.pdf,Applied,,,,,
68c9ba71bbf87b1822247c2d,Alexander Ogbeide Egbe,+23407010447379,egbealexander05@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am Alexander Egbe, a full-stack developer with a strong focus on backend engineering. Over the past 3+ years, I have built production-ready applications, including multi-currency finance platforms with secure KYC systems and event-driven backends for real-time features. I work primarily with Node.js, Nest.js, PostgreSQL, and Prisma to design scalable APIs and reliable systems, but I am also familiar with frontend tools like React and Next.js, which makes me effective at collaborating across the stack. When I am not coding, I like to unwind by reading, exploring new tech trends, or spending time with friends and family.",https://alexander-egbe.vercel.app/,,68c7f7d6df6a1461fb4c9f3f,Associate Backend Developer,2025-09-16T19:28:49.261Z,2025-09-16T19:28:49.261Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1758050926198_Alexander_Egbe_Resume.pdf,Applied,,,,,
68c9be16bbf87b1822247c49,Jeremiah Kada,+2348180322527,tekenna06@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am a skilled software developer with solid experience building feature-rich and functional software solutions. My specialty is scalable and user-centric web and mobile software solutions.\nMy core expertise lies in Javascript and Its ecosystem with extensive hands-on experience in Reactjs, React-Native, Nextjs, Angularjs, Typescript, Nodejs, Expressjs, and Nestjs.\nI have worked across various industries with a significant portion of my experience in the fintech space.\nWith my experience, I have what it takes to take a project from its conceptual stage to a production-ready application and I belive I will be a valuable addition to your team.",,,68c7f7d6df6a1461fb4c9f3f,Associate Backend Developer,2025-09-16T19:44:22.075Z,2025-09-16T19:44:22.075Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1758051858092_cv (1).pdf,Applied,,,,,
68c9c451bbf87b1822247c5e,Cyprian Obi,+2348102992504,obicyprian160@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I’m a full-stack developer with a strong focus on backend development using Node.js, TypeScript, and React. I’ve worked on building APIs, integrating third-party services, and managing databases such as PostgreSQL and MongoDB. I’m comfortable working across the stack, but I enjoy the challenges of designing scalable backend systems and ensuring smooth integration with frontend and external services.\nI’m also interested in projects that involve AI integration and gamification features, and I’m confident I can quickly adapt to new tools and frameworks when needed.",https://cyprianobi.vercel.app,,68c7f7d6df6a1461fb4c9f3f,Associate Backend Developer,2025-09-16T20:10:57.933Z,2025-09-16T20:10:57.933Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1758053455171_cyprian-obi-web-developer-cv.pdf,Applied,,,,,
68c9d33ebbf87b1822247c94,Inioluwa Oyetunji,+23408140624086,theinioye@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I’m a Backend Engineer with strong experience in NestJS, TypeScript, and PostgreSQL, focused on building scalable, fault-tolerant systems. My work has centred on gamification features, payments, and blockchain reward systems, giving me experience across fintech, utilities, and Web3. My engineering philosophy is that for a solution to be truly great, it must solve a real-world problem and be profitable without compromise.\n\nAt East Atlantic Telecoms, I built a payment factory that dynamically switched between providers for reliability, a gamified rewards platform with leaderboards, quizzes, and a daily lottery, and implemented role-based access control with a secure admin panel for managing users, subscriptions, and rewards. At Euterpe, I led the backend for a Web3 music discovery platform, designing engagement verification and blockchain-based reward distribution that helped the team secure a grant. And at Bexxle, I developed scalable backend systems for influencer ad scheduling, attendance management, and business discovery.\n\nI enjoy solving problems that require both technical scalability and user engagement, and Tobams’ focus on AI-powered applications and gamification aligns very closely with the kind of impactful systems I’ve been building.",https://github.com/theinioye,,68c7f7d6df6a1461fb4c9f3f,Associate Backend Developer,2025-09-16T21:14:38.377Z,2025-09-16T21:14:38.377Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1758057275292_Inioluwa Oyetunji Backend Engineer..docx (1).pdf,Applied,,,,,
68c9dccbbbf87b1822247cbd,Augustus Onyekachi,+2349014700476,onyekachiaugustus111@gmail.com,Nigeria,"My name is Augustus Onyekachi, a software engineer with over 6 years of working experience in different technology sectors. I’m experienced in mobile , web , backend and blockchain development. A computer science student in my final level. I am a fast learner .",,,68c7f7d6df6a1461fb4c9f3f,Associate Backend Developer,2025-09-16T21:55:23.744Z,2025-09-16T21:55:23.744Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1758059720648_Augustus BD.pdf,Applied,,,,,
68c9e9c1bbf87b1822247cd9,Alamin Ahmed,+23408136899907,alameensnr@gmail.com,Nigeria,"My name is Ahmed Al-Amin, and my journey into technology has been anything but ordinary. I actually started out in Physics Education, where I spent years not only learning the science but also teaching it. Physics taught me to think deeply about how the world works, how small principles connect to big systems, and how curiosity can lead to discovery.\n\nBut while I loved Physics, I realized something was missing I wasn’t just fascinated by theories; I wanted to build, invent, and create. I wanted to take that same curiosity I had in Physics and channel it into solving real-life problems in a way that touched people’s daily lives. That’s where technology came in.\n\nI transitioned into software development, first teaching myself, then sharpening my skills through structured learning programs like Univelcity, MentorLed, and the Power Learn Project. I learned to build both front-end and back-end systems with technologies like React, Node.js, Express, and MongoDB. Along the way, I worked on meaningful projects from creating an expense tracker to help people manage their finances, to building Peenly, a platform that helps parents track and celebrate their children’s achievements.\n\nWhat excites me about tech is the same thing that excited me about Physics: problem-solving and impact. In Physics, it was about explaining the natural world; in tech, it’s about shaping the digital one. And unlike traditional physics teaching where sometimes students felt the subject was too abstract I’ve added a little sauce to the way I approach tech. For me, it’s about making things practical, engaging, and user-friendly, so people not only understand the system but enjoy using it.\n",https://workfolio-navy.vercel.app/,,68c7f7d6df6a1461fb4c9f3f,Associate Backend Developer,2025-09-16T22:50:41.142Z,2025-09-16T22:50:41.142Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1758063032339_Al-amin FULLSTACK new.pdf,Applied,,,,,
