6915ba1b786d84594286883d,Daniel Indira,+2630771143600,dannyanesu@gmail.com,Zimbabwe,Civil and water engineering with half a decade experience in construction and consultancy projects.,,,69145d3186e2bdfb100d2f55,Associate Social Media Manager,2025-11-13T10:59:39.064Z,2025-11-13T10:59:39.064Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1763031575271_Daniel Indira CV 2.pdf,Applied,,,,,
6915bbbf786d845942868847,Oluoma Francisca Akamadu ,+23407034848846,akamaduoluomafrancisca@gmail.com,Nigeria,"When I got enrolled in an online academy to learn social media management, the first person I shared the news with was my best friend, Cheta. There was no other person that came to my mind, after all she was my best friend. \n\nI didn't prepare for the aftermath. I could remember how her lips parted in a disdaining laughter when I shared my joy with her. I could also remember how she stood from where she sat, folded her arms and asked if I was okay. \nI didn't say a word. \n\nThe next thing she did pierced my heart like a hot sharp knife. I wouldn't forget it in a hurry. The pain I felt after that incident was incomparable. I had watched her made mockery of me. I could remember her words vividly.\n\n""You want to manage social media? As per who naw? No go find better thing do.""\n\nI gulped down my saliva repeatedly and said nothing. I wanted to reply her but my lips stuck together, refusing to bring out a word. I just stood on the spot wondering where I got it wrong. \n\nI realized she was speaking out of ignorance or perhaps, lack of information relating to the field. I didn't give it much thought but rather took it as a motivation.\n\nMany call me The Storyteller, and a wordsmith because of how I'm able to transform a simple thought into a well crafted piece. \n\nThey are not entirely wrong but the truth is, I have added another feather to my cap. \n\nLast year, I got certified as a professional social media manager. I followed the training process judiciously:\n\n       – Completed all my assignments \n       – Was punctual to class\n       – Practiced more on my own \n        – Learnt other skills to complement my SMM skill \n\n...and at the end, I was certified.\n\nIt wasn't really a walk in the park.\n\n        – I thought of giving up\n        – I doubted my skills \n        – I almost lost hope \n        – I got burnt out \n\nI did it finally and the rest they say is history. It's been almost 2 years as a Social Media Manager and I have worked with clients who are happy with my services. This is what happens when one deliver well. \n\nIf you read till this point, I'm sure you already have an idea of who I'm.\n\nOluoma Francisca is your social media bestie, a social media manager who can transform your brand's online presence from 0 - 100 with the right social media strategies and quality content. \n\n",https://oluoma-francisca-portfolio.my.canva.site/,,69145d3186e2bdfb100d2f55,Associate Social Media Manager,2025-11-13T11:06:39.023Z,2025-11-13T11:06:39.023Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1763031995413_Oluoma Akamadu's CV (1) (1).pdf,Applied,,,,,
6915be2b786d845942868853,Esther Ifunanya Nwolisa ,+2349065888352,estherifunanya17@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I’m a Social Media Manager and Content Writer with over two years of experience helping brands grow online through creative storytelling, content planning, and smart digital marketing.\n\nI love turning ideas into strategies that increase engagement, build visibility, and turn followers into real customers. I believe great content isn’t just about posting — it’s about connecting with people and creating results that matter. I am goal driven and ready to do the work to improve a brand.",https://www.canva.com/design/DAGkPvfbE-A/-O6aD7S9VJO05d_wioqYpg/edit?utm_content=DAGkPvfbE-A&utm_campaign=designshare&utm_medium=link2&utm_source=sharebutton,,69145d3186e2bdfb100d2f55,Associate Social Media Manager,2025-11-13T11:16:59.618Z,2025-11-13T11:16:59.618Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1763032615905_IFUNANYA ESTHER NWOLISA RESUME  (2).pdf,Applied,,,,,
