693593ae606533d27c2d6f78,LALEYE GBOLAHAN DAMILOLA,+2348173075558,gbolahanlaleye1@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am naturally curious about how things grow. I like to grow things from the ground up like businesses, ideas and even people. That curiosity is what pulled me into business development over a decade ago, and it's what's kept me excited about building partnerships across different industries. I enjoy understanding how systems work, how value is created, and how the right relationships can unlock opportunities that weren't obvious before. I really love challenges, this may be why I occasionally venture into new territory.\n\nProfessionally, I've spent my career helping companies scale by driving partnerships, building go-to-market strategies and expanding products across multiple regions. But beyond the revenue and strategy side, I genuinely enjoy working with people. I'm big on collaboration, listening, and making sure the people around me feel empowered and heard. Teams I've worked with would describe me as one who is steady under pressure, takes ownership, resilient and easy to work with. I also bring positive energy (good vibes, lol) when it's needed.\n\nOutside of work, I try to live a balanced life. I love swimming and go out with friends when I need to unwind. Family is also a big part of my life. I also enjoy road trips - solo or group, I've been to about 15 states by road and still looking to cover more states next year. I enjoy meeting people from different backgrounds and trying out new cuisine. While I am not doing one fun thing or the other, I would be indoors reading a good book or volunteering with an NGO.\n\nOverall, I'm someone who works hard, stays curious, enjoys people, and tries to make impact. I'm driven but also human and I think this balance is part of what makes me effective in my roles.",,,692820bd5e795ceb37985586,Business Development Manager,2025-12-07T14:48:14.443Z,2025-12-07T14:48:14.443Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazona