6967915d9465cf43d45a19a1,Oyinade Afe,+2349026522815,afeoyinade@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I'm a UX/UI Designer with over 4 years of experience creating digital products that are clean, intuitive, and accessible. I simplify complex workflows, improve usability, and bring clarity to messy product experiences.\n\nI enjoy the full spectrum of the design process, from talking to users and running tests, to wireframing, prototyping, and working closely with developers to bring ideas to life. I also care a lot about design systems and accessibility, making sure what we build is consistent, scalable, and works for everyone.\n\nKey skills:\n\nUX research, user interviews, journey mapping, usability testing\n\nWireframing, prototyping, interaction design, accessibility (WCAG)\n\nDesign systems, component libraries, visual consistency\n\nTools: Figma, Adobe XD, Miro, Rive, Blender",https://www.behance.net/oyinadeafe,,6966006701bf490134411807,Associate Product Designer,2026-01-14T12:51:41.452Z,2026-01-14T12:51:41.452Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1768395098725_Oyinade Afe Resume.pdf,Applied,,,,,
696791e79465cf43d45a19ad,Marious King Ndubueze,+23408118130114,mariousking07@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I’m a UI/UX and product-focused designer with over four years of experience creating user-centered digital products, mainly across web and mobile platforms. My strength lies in translating business goals and user needs into clear, intuitive design solutions that are both functional and scalable.\n\nOver the years, I’ve worked closely with developers, product managers, and stakeholders to design end-to-end experiences from research and wireframing to high-fidelity UI and prototyping. I’m very intentional about understanding user pain points, validating ideas through feedback, and iterating designs to improve usability and engagement.\n\nWhat excites me most about product design is impact. I enjoy designing solutions that not only look good but solve real problems and contribute to business growth. I’m also constantly learning and refining my craft, staying updated with modern design systems, accessibility standards, and tools like Figma.\n\nI see the Associate Product Designer role at Tobams Group as an opportunity to contribute meaningfully to a collaborative, innovation-driven team while growing under strong product leadership helping build digital solutions that truly serve users and clients.",https://2ly.link/23dW6,,6966006701bf490134411807,Associate Product Designer,2026-01-14T12:53:59.103Z,2026-01-14T12:53:59.103Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1768395236552_Marious_King_Ndubueze_CV_2025 2.pdf,Applied,,,,,
6967951f9465cf43d45a19e2,Adebisi Emmanuel,+23408100395178,princeniblemen@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I’m a creative and detail-oriented Product Designer with over six years of experience crafting user-centered digital experiences and building strong visual identities. I specialize in turning complex ideas into intuitive, functional, and visually engaging solutions. Over the years, I’ve worked with startups, agencies, and Web3 companies, collaborating with cross-functional teams to design products, marketing assets, and brand systems that drive real business impact. I’m passionate about solving problems through design, continuously improving user experiences, and creating products that are both useful and meaningful.","https://www.behance.net/emmanuelolusola, https://www.figma.com/design/z83kGy67WfvwKaOyZE3E0C/Fintech-App?node-id=57-1052&p=f&t=k3ubxlecqbipr7ki-0",,6966006701bf490134411807,Associate Product Designer,2026-01-14T13:07:43.124Z,2026-01-14T13:07:43.124Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1768396059090_EMMANUEL-ADEBISI-RESUME..pdf,Applied,,,,,
69679efd5e5dc78bd8d48ed1,Mark Ekpobiyere,+23407065292789,Ekpobiyeremark@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I’m a product designer with over four years of experience designing user-centered products across fintech, banking, investment, healthtech, and e-commerce. I specialize in simplifying complex systems—like crossx cross-border payments, KYC flows, wallets, and B2B financial platforms—into intuitive, scalable experiences.\n\nI’ve worked closely with product managers and engineers from early ideation through launch and iteration, contributing to products used across multiple markets. I’m especially passionate about designing for trust, accessibility, and growth in regulated environments.\n\nOutside of design, I’m a classical music enthusiast and trumpet player, which helps me stay creative, disciplined, and detail-oriented in my work.",https://www.behance.net/markEkpobiyere,,6966006701bf490134411807,Associate Product Designer,2026-01-14T13:49:49.734Z,2026-01-14T13:49:49.734Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1768398586701_Mark_Ekpobiyere_Resume (1) (1).pdf,Applied,,,,,
