6968afcd9f11096d75483497,Udoh James Godwin,+23408032496788,udohgodwin021@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am a passionate and detail-oriented UI/UX Designer with experience designing user-centered digital products across fintech, real estate, logistics, food, and service-based platforms. I enjoy solving problems through thoughtful design, clear user flows, and intuitive interfaces. Beyond design execution, I also facilitate learning, mentor aspiring designers, and collaborate closely with developers and stakeholders to deliver impactful solutions.",https://www.behance.net/udohjames/projects,,6966006701bf490134411807,Associate Product Designer,2026-01-15T09:13:49.434Z,2026-01-15T09:13:49.434Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1768468426673_Godwin UX Resume.pdf,Applied,,,,,
6968b2e69f11096d754834aa,Mohammed Momodu,+2347067255677,momodumohammedsuccess@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I’m a Product Designer with experience designing user-centered digital products across fintech, edtech, and defense sectors, serving diverse markets and user needs. My design approach is rooted in understanding users, business goals, and technical constraints to create intuitive, accessible, and visually compelling experiences. I collaborate closely with product managers, engineers, and researchers to translate complex ideas into clear and functional designs, from research and wireframing to high-fidelity interfaces and interactive prototypes. I also have strong experience building and maintaining design systems to ensure consistency and scalability across products and platforms.\n\nWorking in highly regulated and fast-evolving industries has strengthened my attention to detail, problem-solving skills, and ability to design with security, accessibility, and usability in mind. I thrive in agile environments, value continuous learning, and stay updated with industry trends and best practices. What drives me most is creating products that make real impact, whether by simplifying financial services, enhancing learning experiences, or supporting critical operations. I see design as a strategic tool for improving lives, driving business growth, and delivering meaningful user experiences across different markets.\n",https://linktr.ee/momodusuccess,,6966006701bf490134411807,Associate Product Designer,2026-01-15T09:27:02.541Z,2026-01-15T09:27:02.541Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1768469219754_CV_2025121509105719.pdf,Applied,,,,,
6968b7ab9f11096d754834d6,MOSES AYEJUYO O.,+23409055207226,wosmancreative@gmail.com,Nigeria,"With five years of experience as a graphic designer, I specialize in crafting visually stunning designs that do more than just look good—they drive results. In today’s crowded market, a brand’s visual identity is its most powerful tool. I bridge the gap between creativity and strategy, delivering customized design solutions that help my clients stand out and connect with their audience.\n\nI am driven by a sharp eye for detail and a genuine passion for the craft. Whether you are a startup looking for a fresh identity or an established business ready for an elevation, I provide a tailored approach to ensure your brand leaves a lasting impression.",,,6965fe9801bf490134411806,Associate Graphic Designer,2026-01-15T09:47:23.617Z,2026-01-15T09:47:23.617Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1768470438540_Moses-Ayejuyo-portfolio-nn.jpg,Applied,,,,,
6968c3c09f11096d754835ae,Otobong Morgan,+23408114117819,otobimorgan12@gmail.com,Nigeria,"My name is Otobong Morgan. I’m a product designer with about four years of experience designing user focused web and mobile products. My work sits at reconciling user needs, business goals, and technical feasibility. I’m very hands on across the entire design process, from research and problem framing to wireframes, high fidelity interfaces, prototyping, and developer handoff.\n\nIn my most recent role, I worked closely with product managers, engineers, and other stakeholders to translate ideas into intuitive and visually clear solutions. I’m used to working in agile environments where collaboration, iteration, and timely delivery really matter. I also have strong experience building and maintaining design systems, which helps ensure consistency and scalability across products.\n\nBeyond execution, usability and accessibility are important to how I design. I regularly validate ideas through testing and feedback, and I pay attention to details like hierarchy, clarity, and inclusive design so products work well for a wide range of users.\n\nOutside of my core product work, I’m intentional about giving back to the design community. I mentor and train aspiring designers, helping them develop strong design thinking, understand real world product constraints, and grow confidence in communicating their decisions. Teaching has reinforced my own fundamentals and made me a more thoughtful collaborator and problem solver.\n\nAt this stage, I’m looking to contribute to a team that values quality, collaboration, and impact, where I can bring my experience, continue learning, and help build products that genuinely improve how people interact with technology and I believe your team is the best fit. ",https://www.behance.net/otobongmorgan,,6966006701bf490134411807,Associate Product Designer,2026-01-15T10:38:56.220Z,2026-01-15T10:38:56.220Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.