6969256e9f11096d75486a80,Ebubechukwu Samuel,+2348058245236,samuellucky435@gmail.com,Nigeria,"My name is Ebubechukwu Samuel, I'm a Brand Identity Designer, I'm a moving force, I help business owners, companies, and entrepreneurs build brand identities that don’t just look good, but connect to deeply with their audience.\nFrom logos and flyers to full visual systems, I create designs that tell a story, build trust, and make people stop scrolling.",https://www.behance.net/ebubecsamuel,,6965fe9801bf490134411806,Associate Graphic Designer,2026-01-15T17:35:42.378Z,2026-01-15T17:35:42.378Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1768498538531_Ebubechukwu Samuel RESUME CV.docx,Applied,,,,,
69692ad99f11096d75486ab8,Mariam Amusa,+23407069948607,tajukesh@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am Amusa Mariam, a Brand Creative Designer passionate about creating designs that ignite emotions, spark conversations, and drive meaningful change. My work sits at the intersection of creativity, strategy, and impact, with a strong focus on building brands that connect deeply with their audiences.\n\nI bring solid technical expertise across branding, visual identity, and user-centered design. I am proficient in Adobe Creative Suite, including Photoshop and Illustrator, UI and UX prototyping, and Canva, allowing me to translate ideas into visually compelling and functional solutions.\n\nMy portfolio includes extensive contributions to national, community, and international initiatives. I have worked on government-backed projects such as the Nigerian Web Design Standards Workshop, a NITDA-supported initiative aimed at standardizing government digital platforms. A significant part of my work is dedicated to the 3 Million Technical Talent Initiative, where I designed materials for knowledge showcases, hackathons, stakeholder events, and recruitment-focused programs supporting Nigeria’s digital workforce development goals.\n\nI have also developed design collateral for international digital economy engagements, including Nigeria’s Digital Economy events at the United Nations General Assembly, covering high-level discussions on digital trade, artificial intelligence, infrastructure, and workforce development across Africa.\n\nBeyond public sector work, I collaborate with community and commercial brands. Notably, I designed for Remora’s Kitchen, a food brand rooted in authenticity, warmth, and community, helping translate its values into a cohesive and inviting visual identity.\n\nOverall, my work reflects a commitment to purposeful design, storytelling, and creating visual experiences that support growth, innovation, and social impact.",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1JM4bhRHuZGBXv9-bO_m