69692c0f9f11096d75486ad1,Mobolaji Olakunle Samuel,+23409030192034,mobolajiolakunle8@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am Olakunle Samuel Mobolaji, a creative and detail oriented Graphic Designer with hands-on experience designing visually engaging content for social media, digital marketing, and brand communications. I have a strong understanding of branding, layout, color, and typography, and I enjoy translating brand identity into compelling visuals that connect with audiences. Proficient in design tools, I am comfortable working remotely, meeting deadlines, and collaborating effectively with marketing and content teams to deliver consistent, high-quality designs.",https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1WPbKNMK_IrlFA6q_zFVaIbVSyuDCL-Lx?usp=drive_link,,6965fe9801bf490134411806,Associate Graphic Designer,2026-01-15T18:03:59.727Z,2026-01-15T18:03:59.727Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1768500230330_My Curriculum Vitae._20260115_190034_0000.png,Applied,,,,,
6969310e9f11096d75486b00,Moshood Okuniyi,+23409016438747,moshoodokuniyi@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I’m a creative Graphic Designer with over eight years of experience designing engaging visual content for digital and print platforms. I specialize in creating clean, impactful designs that communicate clearly and align with brand goals.\n\nMy background includes working on social media campaigns, marketing assets, promotional materials, and video content for individuals, startups, and established brands. I’m highly proficient in Adobe Creative Suite and have experience collaborating with marketing teams to deliver projects under tight deadlines.\n\nI’m detail-oriented, adaptable, and passionate about continuous learning. I enjoy solving visual problems creatively and bringing ideas to life through thoughtful design. I’m excited about the opportunity to grow professionally while contributing value to a forward-thinking organization like Tobams Group.",https://www.behance.net/gallery/135787721/Graphic-Design-Portfolio,,6965fe9801bf490134411806,Associate Graphic Designer,2026-01-15T18:25:18.318Z,2026-01-15T18:25:18.318Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1768501514186_Okuniyi Moshood Resume.pdf,Applied,,,,,
696934319f11096d75486b31,Ofoegbu Ugochukwu ,+2349035824976,hugokingsley001@outlook.com,Nigeria,"Hello Hiring Team,\n\nI’m writing to apply for the UIUX designer role. I came across your opening for a UIUX designer; based on my experience at Ecobank, and my level of ownership across product design work, I am applying for this position. My approach to design is centred on solving real problems through structured research, clear user flows, scalable interfaces, and close collaboration with engineering.\n\nAs a Product Designer on your team, you would be getting someone who can take a problem from ambiguity to clarity. I translate business and user needs into well-structured user journeys, intuitive interfaces, and practical design solutions that engineers can confidently build. I’m comfortable owning features end to end. That is from discovery and UX research through wireframing, high-fidelity UI, prototyping, and developer handoff, while keeping delivery efficient and grounded in real constraints.\n\nI work primarily with Figma and FigJam for ideation, journey mapping, prototyping, and maintaining clean, versioned design files. I place strong emphasis on systems thinking, ensuring consistency, reusability, and scalability rather than designing isolated screens. Accessibility, responsiveness, and interaction clarity are built into my decisions from the start, not added as an afterthought.\n\nCollaboration is central to how I work. I actively participate in design critiques, communicate design rationale clearly, and work closely with engineers to ensure smooth handoff and feasible implementation. I’m comfortable facilitating workshops, leading whiteboarding sessions, and turning abstract ideas into actionable tasks that move products forward.\n\nWhat excites me about this is the opportunity to contribute meaningfully within a structured environment that values learning, mentorship, and real product impact, also it is going to be remote. I’m curious, coachable, detail-oriented, and motivated to continuously improve my craft while delivering work that creates value for both users and the business.\n\nThank you for your time and consideration.\n\nWarm Regards,\n Ofoegbu Ugochukwu ",https://www.behance.net/hugoofoegbu001/projects,,6966006701bf490134411807,Associate Product Designer,2026-01-15T18:38:41.313Z,2026-01-15T18:38:41.313Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1768502318066_Ofoegbu Ugochukwu Resume.pdf,Applied,,,,,
696934999f11096d75486b3d,Jubril Babatunde Mudashiru ,+23408144855338,jbrlbabatunde@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am a creative problem solver with a strong background in graphic design, brand identity, and no code web design. I focus on helping brands communicate clearly and convert better through intentional design, not just aesthetics. I’ve worked with businesses and organizations within and outside Nigeria, handling everything from brand systems to digital assets. What sets me apart is my ability to understand a brand’s goal quickly and translate it into simple, effective visual solutions that drive results.",https://pin.it/1oUJ7xNmx,,6965fe9801bf490134411806,Associate Graphic Designer,2026-01-15T18:40:25.077Z,2026-01-15T18:40:25.077Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1768502422111_Olanrewaju CV.pdf,Applied,,,,,
