696a3299d8ebfb5489f4a532,Chikere Anyanwu Justin Udochukwu ,+23408102588632,Justinchikere54@gmail.com,Nigeria,"My name is Chikere Anyanwu Justin Udochukwu. I’m a passionate UI/UX designer with over 2 years of experience crafting intuitive digital experiences. I’m very good with user research, Wire-framing, and prototyping, with a keen eye for visual design. I’ve successfully delivered designs for various companies and organizations, driving users engagement and business goals. I’m excited to grow as an Associate Product Designer in your company, leveraging my skills to create impactful products and collaborate with cross-functional teams. ",http://be.net/skinodicee,,6966006701bf490134411807,Associate Product Designer,2026-01-16T12:44:09.109Z,2026-01-16T12:44:09.109Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1768567446388_Justin Chikere-Anyanwu (cv).pdf,Applied,,,,,
696a33a9d8ebfb5489f4a558,Jephthah Samuel Bacob,+23409074190328,jacobjephthah@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I’m Jephthah, a creative graphic and visual designer with over three years of hands-on experience designing impactful visuals across digital and print platforms. I specialise in transforming ideas into clear, engaging designs that connect with audiences and support brand goals.\n\nI work extensively with Adobe Photoshop, Illustrator, and InDesign, and I have a strong foundation in typography, colour theory, layout, and composition. Over time, I’ve designed a range of marketing assets, including social media graphics, banners, presentations, print materials, and website visuals, always ensuring consistency with brand guidelines and project objectives.\n\nI enjoy collaborating with teams, receiving feedback, and refining designs to deliver the best possible outcome. I’m highly adaptable, comfortable working in fast-paced remote environments, and I take pride in meeting deadlines without compromising quality. I also remain curious and continually improve my skills by staying up-to-date with design trends and best practices.\n\nWhat drives me most is the opportunity to contribute creatively to meaningful projects while growing professionally within a collaborative team. I’m excited about the chance to bring my creativity, problem-solving mindset, and attention to detail to your team and help build a strong, visually compelling brand.",https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1eIgfMOnIj8wSRuKzoBNIFslgsAwXrxKC,,6965fe9801bf490134411806,Associate Graphic Designer,2026-01-16T12:48:41.320Z,2026-01-16T12:48:41.320Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1768567716718_JEPHTHAH-jACOB-(1).jpg,Applied,,,,,
696a3cd3d8ebfb5489f4a903,Blessing Bello,+23408037511096,oritselayemi@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I’m Blessing Bello, a Product (UI/UX) Designer with a strong focus on designing intuitive, human-centered digital experiences that solve real problems and scale with business growth. My work sits at the intersection of user research, interaction design, and visual design, and I’m particularly intentional about clarity, usability, and systems thinking.\n\nOver the years, I’ve worked across fintech, agritech, SaaS, and service-based platforms, collaborating with cross-functional teams that include product managers, engineers, founders, and business stakeholders. At companies like Babban Gona, WashStack, Mage, Nazza, and LakexIO Technologies, I’ve contributed to products at different stages; early discovery, MVP definition, feature expansion, and design refinement. I’m comfortable translating abstract ideas and business requirements into well-structured user flows, wireframes, and high-fidelity interfaces.\n\nI approach design with a strong problem-first mindset. I spend time understanding user behavior, constraints, and motivations before jumping into solutions. This helps me design experiences that reduce friction, improve adoption, and support measurable outcomes. I also care deeply about design systems and consistency, ensuring products are easy to maintain and evolve over time.\n\nBeyond execution, I enjoy documentation and communication; writing clear design rationales, collaborating asynchronously, and aligning teams around a shared product vision. I’m also passionate about community building, mentoring, and faith, and I try to bring empathy, excellence, and intentionality into both my work and personal life.\n\nUltimately, I design to create products that are not just visually appealing, but useful, usable, and meaningful to the people who rely on them every day.\n",bit.ly/bobello,,6966006701bf490134411807,Associate Product Designer,2026-01-16T13:27:47.372Z,2026-01-16T13:27:47.372Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1768570064647_Blessing Bello's CV.pdf,Applied,,,,,
