696b71876b4632601d56eb3e,Princess Sokowonchi Elokun,+23408085240360,elokunprincess360@gmail.com,Nigeria,"My name is Princess Sokowonchi Elokun and I’m a graduate of Elizade University, Nigeria. I’m a Product designer and over the last couple of years I have created multiple user-centered digital experiences that are both intuitive and impactful. My journey into design started from a being a graduate in International Relations and Diplomacy to taking professional certification courses on user experience and user interface design to finally working in an IT company which shaped how I think about people, systems, and real-world problems. \nI’ve spent the last few years designing and researching products across health, fintech, education, and social-impact sectors.\n\nWhat really drives me is designing with context in mind, especially for emerging products in Nigeria is where usability, accessibility, and real-life constraints matter deeply. I enjoy working through the full design process, from user research and wireframing to high-fidelity design and usability testing, always guided by data and user insights.\n\nI’m excited about roles where I can contribute meaningfully, continue learning, and build products that genuinely improve people’s lives while delivering business value.\n",https://bit.ly/sokowonchiportfolio,,6966006701bf490134411807,Associate Product Designer,2026-01-17T11:24:55.932Z,2026-01-17T11:24:55.932Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1768649086802_Portfolio PRINCESS SOKOWONCHI ELOKUN.pdf,Applied,,,,,
696b78066b4632601d56eb54,Akinrolabu Victor Abiodun,+23408164401918,victorabiodun620@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I’m a creative graphic designer with over three years of hands-on experience designing across both digital and print mediums. I enjoy turning ideas into clear, visually engaging designs that communicate effectively and align with brand goals.\n\nOver the years, I’ve worked with different brands across multiple sectors, creating timeless brand designs and visual assets that are both strategic and impactful. I work confidently with Adobe Photoshop, Illustrator, and InDesign, and I also have solid experience creating clean, engaging presentations in PowerPoint. I’m comfortable working within brand guidelines while adapting designs based on feedback.\n\nI’m collaborative, detail-oriented, and thrive in fast-paced environments where priorities can evolve. I enjoy working with creative teams, solving design challenges, and continuously improving my craft while delivering high-quality work on time.",https://www.behance.net/gallery/194532813/My-Design-Portfolio,,6965fe9801bf490134411806,Associate Graphic Designer,2026-01-17T11:52:38.251Z,2026-01-17T11:52:38.251Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1768650755422_Akinrolabu Vic  CV.pdf,Applied,,,,,
696b83a46b4632601d56eb6f,Ato-abasi Macauley Umoh,+23409079899579,macauleuyumoh@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I’m a Figma UI/UX Designer with over 4 years of  experience who specializes in designing modern dashboards, SaaS platforms, mobile apps, AI tools, and Web3 products that are not just beautiful, but built to solve real user problems and drives business revenue.\n\nI help startups and product teams turn complex ideas into clean, intuitive, and conversion-focused digital experiences. My designs don’t just look great; they improve usability, retention, and overall product performance.\n\n🧭 My Design Process\n1. Discovery & Research: Understanding your users, business goals, and competitors.\n2. User Flow & Wireframing: Mapping intuitive navigation and interaction patterns.\n3. Visual Design & Prototyping: Crafting high-fidelity, interactive prototypes in Figma.\n4. Testing & Feedback: Conducting usability tests to refine the experience.\n5. Design System & Handoff: Building scalable components and collaborating closely with developers to ensure pixel-perfect implementation.\n\nThis process ensures that every product I design feels consistent, scalable, and ready for real-world use.\n\n💡 What I Can Help You With\n✅ UI/UX design for dashboards, SaaS, Web3, and AI applications\n✅ Mobile app and web app design (responsive and accessible)\n✅Wireframes, prototypes, and user flow mapping\n✅ Design systems & scalable Figma components\n✅ Product redesigns & MVP design for startups\n✅ UX research, usability testing, and product audits\n✅ Collaboration with developers and PMs for smooth delivery\n\n📊 Client Results\n✅ Improved user engagement by 40% on a gamified learning app through simplified navigation and progress feedback loops.\n✅ Increased checkout completion by 35% for a food delivery platform by redesigning the ordering flow and reducing friction points.\n✅ Helped a B2B SaaS dashboard reduce user onboarding time by 50%, using clearer information hierarchy and guided steps.\n✅ Boosted conversion rates by 28% on a fintech landing page through data-driven layout and CTA optimization.\n✅ Designed scalable Figma design systems that reduced developer rework and design inconsistency by over 60% across teams.\n\n🧠 Core Skills & Tools\nFigma (auto layout, variants, prototyping), FigJam, UX Research, Wireframing, Interaction Design, Usability Testing, Responsive UI Design, Design Systems, Notion, Miro, Adobe XD, Photoshop\n\n🎯 Industries I’ve Worked In\nFintech & Payments, SaaS & B2B Platforms, Web3 & Blockchain, AI & Emerging Tech, EdTech & E-learning, HRTech & Recruitment, Food & Delivery, Transportation & Logistics, Music & Entertainment Tech, Social & Community Platforms, Artisan & Service Marketplaces, Branding & Identity Design\n\nI’m passionate about designing products that feel effortless to use, look visually refined, and meet real business goals. I believe in designs that not only impress users but convert, retain, and scale.\n",https://www.behance.net/mccurhleeumoh,,6965fe9801bf490134411806,Associate Graphic Designer,2026-01-17T12:42:12.451Z,2026-01-17T12:42:12.451Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1768653729720_Umoh Ato-abasi Macauley CV (3).pdf,Applied,,,,,
