696c6d346b4632601d56ed93,Joel Osagie Aikhakhomon,+23408079829489,joel.aikhakhomon@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I’m a senior designer and design generalist with over seven years of experience across graphic design, branding, packaging, and product design. I’ve worked across both digital and print mediums, designing everything from marketing campaigns and brand systems to complex digital products used by thousands of users.\n\nCurrently, I lead product design initiatives, collaborating closely with product managers, engineers, and stakeholders to deliver scalable, accessible, and high-performing design solutions. Alongside product work, I maintain a strong foundation in visual design, with deep expertise in typography, layout systems, and brand consistency.\n\nI have a strong desire for continuous growth, which has consistently pushed me to expand my skill set. As part of my personal development goals for 2026 I’m intentionally deepening my skills in 3D modeling and motion graphics. I previously explored 3D and animation around 2020, and I’m now picking it up again with a clearer creative direction and improved workstation, focusing on product visuals, marketing assets, and motion-driven storytelling that complement my design work.\n\nI’m comfortable taking ownership of projects end to end, mentoring other designers, and maintaining a high standard of design quality across teams. I’m motivated by solving problems through design, improving processes, and delivering work that balances creativity with measurable business impact.",https://www.behance.net/jorelose551bcf,,6965fe9801bf490134411806,Associate Graphic Designer,2026-01-18T05:18:44.510Z,2026-01-18T05:18:44.510Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1768713520441_CV Joel O. Aikhakhomon.pdf,Applied,,,,,
696c6e4e6b4632601d56ed9e,Abdul Martin Faloye,+2349153824049,abdulmartinfaloye@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I'm a graphic designer with just over three years' experience working across digital and print. What I really enjoy is taking a brand's ideas or objectives and translating them into visuals that actually connect with people, whether that's through a clean identity system, social content, or marketing materials.\n\nI've worked on everything from brand identities and social media designs to print projects, mainly using Adobe Creative Suite (Photoshop and Illustrator), Figma, and Affinity. I'm comfortable jumping between different types of work, and I genuinely like the collaborative side of design, bouncing ideas around, getting feedback, and working through revisions until we land on something that works both creatively and strategically.\n\nI'm pretty detail-focused and quite organised, which helps when things get busy or priorities shift. I also just enjoy the problem-solving aspect of design, figuring out how to communicate something clearly or make something feel right visually. I try to keep learning and stay aware of what's happening in design, not just for the sake of it, but because it genuinely interests me.\n\nI'm excited about this opportunity because I'd love to contribute to a growing brand and be part of a team where creativity and collaboration are valued.",https://www.behance.net/theabdulmartin,,6965fe9801bf490134411806,Associate Graphic Designer,2026-01-18T05:23:26.877Z,2026-01-18T05:23:26.877Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1768713803648_Abdul-Martin Faloye .pdf,Applied,,,,,
