699c84ee1501fa3f95de4f70,Orodiran Ayomide John,+2348167965447,orodiranayomide@gmail.com,Nigeria,"am a business operations and banking professional with over four years of experience working across financial services and fintech environments, where I have supported operational execution, customer lifecycle management, process improvement, and cross-functional coordination.\nMy career started in Fidelity Bank, where I gained structured exposure to banking operations, customer support systems, compliance processes, and performance reporting. Working within the contact centre and MIS functions helped me build strong analytical skills, documentation discipline, and attention to operational accuracy. I was responsible for managing customer inquiries, generating operational reports, tracking service performance metrics, and supporting internal process reviews.\nI later transitioned into a more dynamic fintech environment at Waya Bank, where I took on broader responsibilities spanning customer success, operational oversight, settlement monitoring, and cross-team coordination. In that role, I worked closely with product, tech, risk, and finance teams to ensure smooth execution of internal processes, timely resolution of operational issues, and improved service delivery standards. I also supported workflow tracking, documentation updates, and process optimization initiatives, which strengthened my ability to manage multiple workstreams simultaneously.\nI am highly organized, detail-oriented, and comfortable working in fast-paced environments where structure and follow-through are critical. I enjoy building systems, tracking progress against targets, coordinating across teams, and ensuring that ideas move from strategy to execution. My strength lies in combining operational structure with proactive communication, ensuring that projects stay aligned, stakeholders remain informed, and deliverables are completed on time.",,,699c6e6cbe2e747d922bc7bd,Junior Business Operations Mana