699f0b364664ea526d618e2d,Daniel Riches Odafe ,+2348077498012,richesdaniel5@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am a highly organized and goal-oriented individual with strong management skills. I believe in planning, effective communication, teamwork, and accountability to achieve organizational goals.\nIn my previous and current roles, I have demonstrated the ability to:\n1)Coordinate tasks efficiently and meet deadlines.\n2)Supervise and motivate team members to improve productivity.\n3)Manage time and resources effectively.\n4)Solve problems quickly and make sound decisions under pressure.\n5)Maintain discipline and ensure smooth daily operations.\n6)Organizational Growth Achieved Through My Management Skills.\n\nAlso , through my management approach, I have contributed to:\n1)Increased productivity and improved workflow efficiency.\n2)Better team collaboration and reduced conflicts.\n3)Improved customer/client satisfaction.\n4)Proper record keeping and structured reporting systems.\n5)Achievement of set targets within stipulated timelines.\n6)Cost reduction through better planning and resource allocation.\n       I am committed to continuous improvement and always look for innovative ways to enhance organizational performance. My goal is not just to manage tasks but to add measurable value to the organization.",,,699c6e6cbe2e747d922bc7bd,Junior Business Operations Manager,2026-02-25T14:46:14.937Z,2026-02-25T14:46:14.937Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1772030772048_Daniel'CV-1.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
699f0ba34664ea526d618e3b,Jennifer Orji,+2349063894647,jenniferorjimba@gmail.com,Niger,"I am an operations-focused professional with over four years of experience coordinating business processes, managing teams, supporting recruitment, and overseeing inventory and vendor relationships. I thrive in structured but fast-paced environments where organization, communication, and execution are key. I’m highly detail-oriented, bilingual in English and French, and passionate about building systems that improve efficiency and team performance.","“I currently support business operations including recruitment coordination, inventory tracking, vendor management, CRM documentation, and staff training. Due to confidentiality, I cannot share internal company documents, but I am happy to provide structured sample templates or walk through my operational processes during an interview.",,699c6e6cbe2e747d922bc7bd,Junior Business Operations Manager,2026-02-25T14:48:03.307Z,2026-02-25T14:48:03.307Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1772030880365_Junior Operations Manager.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
699f0ba34664ea526d618e3d,Sunday Ashekong Beshel,+23407052514944,beshelsunday@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I’m a graduate chemical engineer and Graduate Automation and Control Sales Engineer with a blend of technical, teaching, and commercial experience. I’ve taught mathematics, physics, and chemistry for several years, which strengthened my communication, mentoring, and ability to simplify complex concepts for different stakeholders.\n\nOn the engineering side, I’ve worked with process plants, control systems, and HSE during internships in refinery, hospital, and research settings, gaining hands-on experience with troubleshooting, operations, and safety. As a Graduate Automation and Control Sales Engineer, I’ve interacted with clients, supported technical sales, and helped match automation solutions to customer needs, building my skills in customer relationship management, requirement gathering, and solution-based selling.\n\nTogether, these experiences make me comfortable in analytical, people-facing, and process-driven roles. I’m proficient with Microsoft Office and basic data analysis, and I’m excited to apply this mix of technical understanding, sales exposure, and operational discipline to support efficient workflows and business growth as a Junior Business Operations Manager at Tobams Group.",www.linkedin.com/in/sunday-beshel-03738286,,699c6e6cbe2e747d922bc7bd,Junior Business Operations Manager,2026-02-25T14:48:03.343Z,2026-02-25T14:48:03.343Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1772030878589_cerificates_merged_compressed.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
699f10ce4664ea526d618e7f,Oyelere Oluwatosin,+23408140805489,olugbejaoluwatosin@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I’m an operations-focused professional with a strong interest in how businesses run efficiently behind the scenes. I enjoy working at the intersection of people, process, and performance making sure the right systems are in place so teams can do their best work.\n\nIn my previous experience, I’ve supported day-to-day operations, improved internal workflows, and worked cross-functionally with finance, sales, and customer teams to keep projects on track. I’m naturally organised and detail-oriented, and I like turning complex or messy processes into something clear, structured, and scalable. Whether it’s tracking KPIs, managing budgets, coordinating vendors, or building documentation, I’m comfortable taking ownership and following through.\n\nI’m particularly drawn to junior business operations roles because they offer the opportunity to learn the business holistically from strategy to execution. I’m proactive, analytical, and always looking for ways to improve efficiency without sacrificing quality. At the same time, I value strong communication and collaboration, as I know operations works best when it enables others.\n\nOverall, I’m someone who thrives in structured but fast-paced environments, enjoys problem-solving, and is motivated by helping a business grow in a sustainable and well-organised way.",https://www.linkedin.com/in/oluwatosin-oyelere-6527a1b7,,699c6e6cbe2e747d922bc7bd,Junior Business Operations Manager,2026-02-25T15:10:06.756Z,2026-02-25T15:10:06.756Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1772032203924_OYELERE TOSIN OPERATIONS CV.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
699f13794664ea526d618ec7,Vivian Osemeke ,+2348167615236,ogechivv212@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am organized, willing to learn, and ready to support the team to achieve company goals. I always try to improve myself and add value wherever I work.\nI pay attention to details, follow instructions well, and work well with others.",Not available yet,,699c6e6cbe2e747d922bc7bd,Junior Business Operations Manager,2026-02-25T15:21:29.399Z,2026-02-25T15:21:29.399Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1772032885971_VIVIAN - CV.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
699f14444664ea526d618edd,Elijah Steven Iliyah,+2349064656344,stevenelijah01@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am a process-driven Project Manager and Business Developer with a B.Sc. in Physics and a track record of driving operational efficiency through high-level technology integration. I specialise in implementing digital ecosystems like Bitrix24, Odoo, and MS 365, which has previously increased team productivity by 40%. My experience spans managing complex energy project lifecycles, securing over 27 million dollars in funding, and navigating SEC regulatory frameworks. I have also coordinated large-scale social impact logistics where I managed the onboarding of over 5,000 beneficiaries across 10 states. Beyond my core operations expertise, I am a member of the African Astronomical Society, reflecting a deep analytical curiosity and a commitment to research-driven problem-solving that I bring to every business challenge.",https://www.linkedin.com/in/stevenelijah/,,699c6e6cbe2e747d922bc7bd,Junior Business Operations Manager,2026-02-25T15:24:52.400Z,2026-02-25T15:24:52.400Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1772033089239_2025Jun26_Steven Elijah-CV (2).pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
699f147b4664ea526d618ee9,Adeniran Victor,+23408103434309,Adeniran440@gmail.com,Nigeria,"My name is  Adeniran Samuel Victor, a business operations and strategy professional with experience spanning operations, partnerships, program management, and IT across Nigeria, the UK, and the US. Over the years, I’ve worked in various roles, including Operations Manager at P23 Africa, Programs Manager at Translation Commons, and Strategic Business Manager at United Bank for Africa, where I led cross-functional teams, coordinated projects, and drove both operational efficiency and business growth.\n\nI thrive in fast-paced environments where multiple stakeholders, projects, and teams need alignment. I enjoy building systems and processes that make operations seamless, supporting recruitment and onboarding, coordinating product delivery, and managing stakeholder relationships. With a strong blend of analytical skills, project management expertise, and people-first leadership, I’m passionate about driving execution while creating meaningful impact for both organizations and the communities they serve.\n\nI’m excited about the opportunity at Tobams Group because it combines my experience in operations, project coordination, and international collaboration with my passion for education and technology-driven solutions that create real-world impact.",https://www.linkedin.com/in/vadeniran/,,699c6e6cbe2e747d922bc7bd,Junior Business Operations Manager,2026-02-25T15:25:47.145Z,2026-02-25T15:25:47.145Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1772033143332_Adeniran Samuel Victor .pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
699f14b54664ea526d618ef1,Stephanas Sunday Effiong,+2349129355803,effiongstephanas2@gmail.com,Nigeria,"My name is stephanas sunday , I am 28 years old ,I currently live in calabar, Nigeria , I am a student in BYU pathway Iworldwide , studying business managemen , I have my first certificate in administrative assistant. I am a computer operative my profession, i love studying, singing , and playing football. I believe in my ability. Thank you.",,,699c6e6cbe2e747d922bc7bd,Junior Business Operations Manager,2026-02-25T15:26:45.130Z,2026-02-25T15:26:45.130Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1772033202195_RESUME- STEPHANAS - Copy.docx,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
699f161c4664ea526d618f0f,Miracle Amala Nebo,+23407033820966,nebomiraculous@gmail.com,Nigeria,"My name is Miracle, an Operations Specialist with over four years of experience managing complex\nworkflows and stakeholder logistics across the IT, construction, and\ntelecommunications industries. I have\nbuilt my career on creating structure within fast-paced environments, balancing rapid execution with an ownership mindset and a high level of autonomy.\nIn my most recent role at IHS Towers, I managed field service operations across 100 base stations, maintaining full responsibility for site uptime and SLA compliance. I led a cross-functional effort involving approximately 25 personnel across six teams, where I was tasked with identifying and resolving the root causes of poor-performing sites. By\nanalyzing technical data, network performance and vendor reports, I implemented immediate operational fixes that reduced downtime, reduced diesel consumption and optimized asset life-cycles. One of my key strategies involved prioritizing the availability\nof alternative power sources and escalating identified issues through appropriate channels until closure, ensuring consistent service delivery for mobile network operators.\nMy key highlights include;\n* Systems & Data Thinking: I am highly data-driven, with technical proficiency in SQL, Tableau, Power BI, and Excel. I have a proven track record of using advanced\nspreadsheet techniques to ensure high-level accuracy in project reporting and data analysis.\n* 0-1 Initiative & Execution: I have experience leading projects from acquisition through supply and logistics, including serving as a team lead for structural integrity assessments under tight deadlines for major clients like Lafarge Africa Plc. Efficiently closed over 25 new projects/initiatives in IHS Towers within 2 years.\n* Cross-Functional Collaboration: I am a master disambiguator who effectively\ncommunicates across technical and non-technical stakeholders. I have extensive\nexperience collaborating with remote field teams, vendors, and internal/external\nauditors to drive core operational processes.\n* Adaptability & Problem Solving: Whether monitoring alarms for 400 sites in real-time or conducting community liaison to resolve local blockers, I thrive in environments that require proactive, first-party problem-solving.",http://linkedin.com/in/miracle-nebo-3b9447113,,699c6e6cbe2e747d922bc7bd,Junior Business Operations Manager,2026-02-25T15:32:44.223Z,2026-02-25T15:32:44.223Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1772033561158_Miracle Nebo - Ops Resume.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
699f17ac4664ea526d618f1e,Akor Lucky,+2348148010358,luckyakor5@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am a results-driven Human Resource and administrative professional with a strong background in talent acquisition, project coordination, and organizational operations. Over the past few years, I have worked across remote and hybrid environments, leading end-to-end recruitment processes, managing cross-functional teams, and supporting business growth through structured HR systems and digital tools.\n\nI hold a BSc in Sociology (Second Class Upper), and I am currently pursuing an MSc in Employment Relations and Human Resource Management at the University of Ibadan, alongside my CIPM certification. My academic background strengthens my practical experience in workforce planning, employee relations, and HR compliance.\n\nProfessionally, I have managed recruitment campaigns that increased qualified applications by 40%, maintained high offer acceptance rates, and improved onboarding and retention through data-driven strategies. I am comfortable using tools such as Jira, ClickUp, LinkedIn Recruiter, Greenhouse, Google Workspace, and CRM systems to optimize operations and hiring processes.\n\nBeyond my technical skills, I am proactive, analytical, and highly organized. I enjoy solving operational challenges, building efficient systems, and contributing to teams that value growth, innovation, and continuous improvement. I am particularly motivated by opportunities that allow me to expand my strategic HR capabilities while delivering measurable impact to the organization.",https://www.linkedin.com/in/luckykosen,,699c6e6cbe2e747d922bc7bd,Junior Business Operations Manager,2026-02-25T15:39:24.260Z,2026-02-25T15:39:24.260Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1772033961266_AKOR RE.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
699f1c874664ea526d618f47,David Sunday,+2348109008373,davidsunday0900@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am an operations-focused growth professional with experience supporting business expansion, execution planning, and cross-functional coordination with strong marketing and business growth initiative. I’ve worked closely with leadership to structure initiatives, grow businesses, track KPIs, and ensure deliverables move efficiently from strategy to implementation.\n\nMy background includes supporting health and wellness businesses and working directly with a COO at Starnet to coordinate growth initiatives, documentation, and workflows. I enjoy building structured systems, improving team alignment, and ensuring accountability in fast-moving environments.",,,699c6e6cbe2e747d922bc7bd,Junior Business Operations Manager,2026-02-25T16:00:07.901Z,2026-02-25T16:00:07.901Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1772035204266_David Sunday Resume.docx,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
699f210d4664ea526d618f5f,Abiodun Raheenat Hakeem - Habeeb,+23408134990534,hakeemhabeebabiodun007@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I’m a business operations and project support professional with experience across operations management, HR, business development, and executive support. I studied Law at the University of Lagos, which helped me develop strong analytical and documentation skills.\n\nOver the past few years, I’ve worked in roles where I supported leadership directly, coordinated projects, improved workflows, and helped teams stay organized and accountable. In my previous role, I worked remotely as a Virtual Personal Assistant and Operations Manager, where I manage executive schedules, conduct market research, draft SOPs, oversee recruitment and onboarding, and support strategic decisions.\n\nBefore that, I worked as a Business Development Manager and HR Manager, where I handled recruitment, staff training, performance tracking, compliance, and cross-functional coordination. Across all my roles, one consistent thing is that I enjoy bringing structure to operations. I like building systems, tracking progress, and ensuring that ideas are not just discussed but properly executed.\n\nI’m very comfortable working remotely, managing multiple moving parts, and supporting leadership with both strategic documentation and day-to-day operations.",https://theflawlessva.my.canva.site ,,699c6e6cbe2e747d922bc7bd,Junior Business Operations Manager,2026-02-25T16:19:25.168Z,2026-02-25T16:19:25.168Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1772036361934_ABIODUN RAHEENAT HAKEEM-HABEEB .pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
699f3dda4664ea526d618fea,Stella Ezeamaeke,+2348138153457,ijezeamaeke@gmail.com,Nigeria,"My name is Stella Ezeamaeke, I hold a Bachelor’s degree in Arts from the University of Port-Harcourt Nigeria. \n\nI am a product manager with hands on experience in building and managing operations systems across tech and services driven industries. I currently work at Urello Technologies where I manage operational strategies for Tivro Africa. My role sits on the intersection of product, field operations and business teams. I focus on ensuring the smooth run of the daily operations. \n\nOverall, my career has been shaped by working in fast-paced, cross-functional environments where structure, accountability, and clear communication are critical to success.",http://linkedin.com/in/stellaezeamaeke,,699c6e6cbe2e747d922bc7bd,Junior Business Operations Manager,2026-02-25T18:22:18.572Z,2026-02-25T18:22:18.572Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1772043735877_Stella Ezeamaeke.....pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
699f42964664ea526d619012,Maureen Anayo ,+2347035184670,maureenanthony95@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am a results-driven business professional with hands-on experience in operations coordination, sales management, and administrative leadership. In my current role as a Branch Head and Administrative Officer, I oversee daily operations, supervise team performance, coordinate client engagements, and ensure smooth execution of projects from planning to delivery.\n\nI have practical experience managing sales meetings, handling client communications, tracking payments, preparing training materials, and supporting cross-functional teams including HR, legal, project, and executive management. This has strengthened my ability to organize workflows, improve efficiency, and maintain accountability within a team.\n\nI am highly detail-oriented, proactive, and comfortable working in fast-paced environments. I enjoy problem-solving, supporting team members to achieve targets, and ensuring that operational processes run smoothly. I am now seeking to further develop my expertise in business operations management where I can contribute to organizational growth while expanding my strategic and leadership capacity.",,,699c6e6cbe2e747d922bc7bd,Junior Business Operations Manager,2026-02-25T18:42:30.017Z,2026-02-25T18:42:30.017Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1772044946567_MAUREEN CV.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
