69a7ef40f0accb3224832f4d,Benjamin Ayomide Odeleye,+23408183437774,benjaminodeleye1@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I’m a Frontend Developer with over 4 years of experience creating user-friendly and responsive web applications. I’ve worked with tools like React, Vue, Next.js, Nuxt.js, JavaScript, TypeScript, and Tailwind CSS to build engaging and functional interfaces.\n\nI’m great at solving UI challenges, optimizing web performance, and bridging the gap between design and development using tools like Figma and Canva. Having worked in fast-paced environments, I adapt quickly and deliver quality work on tight deadlines. I’m also a strong team player who communicates clearly, takes feedback well, and is always open to learning new technologies to improve both my skills and the products I work on.\n",https://benjaminodeleye.vercel.app/,,69a6fe3c934396ba8bb60dec,Frontend Developer Intern,2026-03-04T08:37:20.926Z,2026-03-04T08:37:20.926Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1772613437872_Benjamin_Odeleye_Resume.docx.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69a85e2cdf4a0f3d42a30266,David Olaoluwa Ogunkoya,+23408143014095,ogunkoyadavid@gmail.com,Nigeria,"My name is David Ogunkoya, and I have over three years of experience working across Administration, Operations, and Business Development. Over the years, I’ve built a strong foundation in creating and implementing Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs), developing policy documents, and designing effective company structures.\n\nIn addition to process and operations work, I’ve also gained hands-on experience in client relationship management and sales. I enjoy building meaningful connections with clients, understanding their needs, and delivering solutions that drive tangible results.\n\nI’m passionate about helping organizations run more efficiently while also contributing to growth through smart business development strategies. I thrive at the intersection of operations and client engagement, where structure meets impact.",,,69a7e2fa934396ba8bb60df1,Business Operations Intern,2026-03-04T16:30:36.327Z,2026-03-04T16:30:36.327Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1772641832982_Ogunkoya David CV.docx.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69a9319de5676a11c67b1534,Omokorede Adeyeye,+2349024292976,adeyeyeomokorede@gmail.com,Nigeria,Able to work under pressure and guarantee quality of service.,www.linkedIn.com/me/omokorede-adeyeye,,6801567d578019ddec349c70,Machine Learning Developer,2026-03-05T07:32:45.891Z,2026-03-05T07:34:02.896Z,,"Dear Hiring Manager,\n\nI am writing to express my interest in the Backend / Machine Learning Engineer position at your organization. As a backend engineer with experience designing scalable systems and integrating AI-driven features into production platforms, I am particularly excited about opportunities that combine robust backend architecture with machine learning capabilities.\n\nIn my current role at Tobams Group, I design and maintain scalable backend services for a digital learning platform using Node.js, TypeScript, MongoDB, Redis, and distributed job pipelines. My work includes building RESTful APIs, optimizing aggregation-heavy database queries, implementing Redis-based caching strategies, and developing resilient asynchronous workers with retry and idempotency mechanisms. I have also contributed to AI-powered features by implementing schema-driven question generation pipelines that integrate machine learning outputs into production systems.\n\nBeyond my professional experience, I have built several backend-heavy platforms, including CryptoPay, a crypto payment API designed to simplify blockchain payments for businesses, and Adventurer, a mission-based messaging platform for university communities. These projects strengthened my ability to architect reliable systems, design extensible APIs, and integrate complex services such as blockchain networks and external data pipelines.\n\nI am particularly drawn to backend ML roles because they sit at the intersection of intelligent systems and production infrastructure—ensuring that machine learning models can operate reliably, scale effectively, and deliver measurable value to users. My experience building distributed systems and integrating AI-driven features positions me well to contribute meaningfully in such environments.\n\nI would welcome the opportunity to discuss how my backend engineering experience and interest in applied machine learning can contribute to your team. Thank you for your time and consideration.\n\nSincerely,\nOmokorede Adeyeye\n",https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1772695589912_Omokorede Elisha Adeyeye Resume (2).pdf,Applied,69a7eadaf0accb3224832ebf,Lagos,Talent,68015495578019ddec349c17,Collindigson Group of Companies
