69abaebbc4150aec38da6331,Iwasam Egbe,+2348154954955,iwasamegbe@gmail.com,Nigeria,"Iwasam Egbe is an aspiring economist with a deep interest in business operations and management. I have gained practical experience in supporting various business initiatives. \nI am particularly drawn to roles that allow me to integrate my research, project coordination, and administrative skills to improve operational efficiency. In my role, I have developed strong capabilities in planning, documentation, research, reporting, and consistently tracking goals and timelines to ensure prompt execution.\nCurrently, I am pursuing a master's programme in economics at Covenant University, which has sharpened my analytical and critical thinking skills, which I believe are needed for a successful business operations internship. \nMy experience working with entrepreneurial ventures like Scribble Green Limited has equipped me with a strong understanding of goal tracking and stakeholder engagement. I thrive in a fast-paced, remote environment and am adept at handling multiple workstreams, ensuring that all project deliverables align with set objectives.\nWith my proficiency in Google Workspace and Excel, coupled with a passion for learning and market research, I am eager to contribute to Tobams Group's mission to transform education and create opportunities for young learners through innovative learning solutions.",https://www.linkedin.com/in/egbe-iwasam/,,69a7e2fa934396ba8bb60df1,Business Operations Intern,2026-03-07T04:51:07.425Z,2026-03-07T04:51:07.425Z,,,"https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1772859064399_Egbe, Iwasam Eja_CV.pdf",Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
