69ac79a0c4150aec38da66ae,Precious Aderibigbe,+23408139350267,precidosaam@gmail.com,Nigeria,"My name is Precious Aderibigbe. I am a Statistics student with a strong passion for media and creative design. I have experience working with graphics, photography, videography, and livestream production, which has helped me develop a good eye for visual storytelling and branding.\n\nI enjoy creating designs that communicate clear messages and capture attention. Over time, I have worked on different creative projects, including social media graphics, event designs, and media content.\n\nI am applying for this Graphics Design Internship because I want to further improve my design skills, gain more professional experience, and contribute creatively to your team.",https://www.behance.net/precidoaderibi,,69a6fefa934396ba8bb60ded,Graphic Design Intern,2026-03-07T19:16:48.128Z,2026-03-07T19:16:48.128Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1772911004338_Precious Samuel ADERIBIGBE  CV.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69ac80d9c4150aec38da66c3,Festus Ayobami Olorundare ,+2349035252223,festusdare09@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am an enthusiastic and growth-driven individual with a strong interest in technology, business analysis, and problem-solving. I enjoy understanding how systems and businesses work and identifying ways to improve processes using data and insights.\n\nI am passionate about learning, developing analytical skills, and contributing to solutions that create real impact. As someone who is constantly seeking opportunities to grow, I am excited about gaining practical experience where I can apply my knowledge, collaborate with professionals, and continue building my career in the tech and business analysis space.",,,69a71dac934396ba8bb60def,Business Analyst Intern,2026-03-07T19:47:37.120Z,2026-03-07T19:47:37.120Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1772912853683_Festus PDFF.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69ac913dc4150aec38da66e5,Oyelude Favour,+2349057165905,favouroyelude@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am a first-class graduate of Electrical and Electronics Engineering at Covenant University. I started my data analysis journey while I was still in university, beginning with my small snacks business. Initially, I kept records on paper, but as the data volume increased, I had to migrate to Microsoft Excel. However, entering records into Excel alone was not enough, so I built a better solution that allowed me to type in a customer's name and have it return all their past sales records, especially if they are in debt. I also included an inventory management section and a dashboard to provide basic business insights. \nLater, I joined Enchant Gifts, an e-commerce business specialising in gift items. At the early stage, I just applied the same simple system I used for my own business, but as the company scaled, we started to have problems such as order mix-ups and delayed order processing. To address this, I developed a more advanced Excel and Power BI solution that integrated the sales, operations, and management teams into a single, structured workflow. \nI have undertaken multiple projects, including a comprehensive analysis of the root causes of power outages in the United States, in which a decade of historical data was analysed, and a step-by-step report was developed to significantly reduce outage frequency. Another was an A/B testing analysis for Maven cafe to understand how customers responded to various promotional offers and ad campaigns to determine the most effective marketing strategies. Additionally, I acted as an analytics consultant for Massachusetts General Hospital and developed a high-level dashboard to provide insights into their re-admission and mortality rates, and the effect of different health insurance programs on patient treatment. \nUltimately, I would say I am result-driven, resilient and a fast learner, which helps me pick up new tools quickly. As an analyst, I ensure I bridge the gap between business needs and technical solutions to deliver meaningful business impact.",https://github.com/FOyelude,,69a71dac934396ba8bb60def,Business Analyst Intern,2026-03-07T20:57:33.210Z,2026-03-07T20:57:33.210Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1772917049824_CV PDF.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69ac9776c4150aec38da6703,Moses Chinosa,+2349038307755,moses.chinosa@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I’m Moses Chinosa, a creative professional with over seven years of experience in graphic design, video editing, and digital media production. I started my design journey in 2015, when I trained with Compact Technologies in Ojuelegba, where I learned the fundamentals of graphic design and developed my interest in visual communication.\n\nIn 2016, I completed my IT with a printing firm, where I gained hands-on experience in printing design and production. This helped me understand the technical side of design — from layout preparation and color accuracy to how designs translate into final printed materials.\n\nOver the years, I’ve worked with branding companies, PR agencies, and currently within the media agency space, collaborating with marketing, sales, and development teams to deliver campaigns and visual assets that support business and communication goals.\n\nBeyond design execution, I’m also interested in creative strategy, storytelling, and how design can drive real business impact. I enjoy solving problems visually and continuously improving my skills by exploring new tools and technologies.",https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1QSsj7mAU8Kudd0r5dZusalocQvoXXuSd?usp=sharing,,69a6fefa934396ba8bb60ded,Graphic Design Intern,2026-03-07T21:24:06.712Z,2026-03-07T21:24:06.712Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1772918642009_Chinosa's Portfolio.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
