69b02fa40e6e0d602ab6962c,Ghazi Kwabena Anning,+233501191203,anningghazi25@gmail.com,Ghana,"\nMy name is Ghazi Kwabena Anning, and I'm a Ghanaian from the Fanti tribe. I'm a Christian and a proud alumnus of Kwame Nkrumah University of Science and Technology, where I earned a Bachelor of Science in Geomatic Engineering in 2020.\n\nMy professional journey began after graduation, and I was part of the first group to have an online graduation due to COVID-19. I was posted to the Ghana Highways Authority head office in Accra for my national service training, where I joined the Survey and Design division. There, I was trained in Autocad design and worked on various projects, developing my teamwork, Autocad, and public speaking skills.\n\nAfter my national service, I worked as a land surveyor at a construction company, where I took levels, set out pillars and building corners, and occasionally acted as a quantity surveyor. I also trained interns and national service personnel, sharing my knowledge and experience.\n\nDuring my time as a land surveyor, I realized the importance of remote work, especially after COVID-19. I pursued training and bootcamps in software engineering and honed my skills in backend development. I got a job as a junior backend engineer at an engineering firm, where I wrote APIs, collaborate with frontend teams and designers, and used third-party tools like Mailjet and AWS. I also leveraged AI to streamline tasks and explain complex code flows, ensuring clean and efficient code.",none,,69a7e52c934396ba8bb60df2,Backend Developer Intern,2026-03-10T14:50:12.391Z,2026-03-10T14:50:12.391Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1773154209565_Ghazi Kwabena Anning_CV.docx (1).pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
