69b12bc90e6e0d602ab69e83,SUNMIBOYE ELIZABETH FOLASHADE,+2348021093941,efolashade22@gmail.com,Nigeria,"My name is Folashade, and I hold a bachelor of science in Education and Economics from Olabisi Onabanjo University. I have experience working as a sales Administrator where I developed a strong communication and organizational skills. I am passionate about learning, growth and gaining practical experience in a dynamic work environment. I am particularly interested in opportunities that allow me to contribute, develop new skills, and expand my knowledge in business and administration. I am a proactive, detail-oriented individual who works well both independently and in a team.",https://www.linkedin.com/in/elizabeth-folashade-2a1aa5292?utm_source=share_via&utm_content=profile&utm_medium=member_ios,,69a71dac934396ba8bb60def,Business Analyst Intern,2026-03-11T08:46:01.885Z,2026-03-11T08:46:01.885Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1773218758575_Sunmiboye Elizabeth Folashade ResumÃ©.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69b12c220e6e0d602ab69eb6,Bello Salamot Damilola,+23408139183441,bellodamilola426@gmail.com,Nigeria,"My journey into design did not begin in a design academy or with a sketchbook full of UI ideas. It began somewhere quite different...with science.\n\nI studied zoology, a field that taught me to observe carefully, understand complex systems, and appreciate the beauty of the natural world. While learning about ecosystems, animal behavior, and the delicate balance of nature, I developed a deep curiosity about how things work and how different elements connect to create meaningful outcomes.\n\nBut somewhere along the way, I discovered another interest growing quietly beside my love for science, which is design.\n\nWhat first caught my attention was something simple: color and typography. I was fascinated by how the right combination of visuals and words could capture attention, communicate ideas clearly, and influence how people interact with information. That curiosity eventually led me into the world of UI/UX design.\n\nToday, I work as a Ux Designer, creating digital experiences that are both functional and visually engaging. My work often involves designing interfaces for applications, crafting landing pages, and thinking through how users move through a product. For me, design is not just about making things look good, it is about making them work better for people.\n\nWhat makes my journey unique is the way my scientific background shapes how I approach design. Studying zoology trained me to analyze patterns, ask questions, and understand systems. I now apply that same mindset when designing products, observing user behavior, solving problems, and building experiences that feel intuitive.\n\nI am particularly interested in designing solutions that simplify complex ideas and make information more accessible.\n\nBefore fully stepping into design, I also had experiences working as a sales representative and a science teacher. These roles helped me develop strong communication skills and a deeper understanding of how people think, learn, and make decisions.\n\nFor me, design is more than a profession; it is a way of connecting ideas, people, and technology to create meaningful experiences. And I am excited to keep exploring how thoughtful design can inform, inspire, and solve real-world problems.",https://linktr.ee/protoblack,,69aefa4c05d00a25722c84c2,Product Designer Intern,2026-03-11T08:47:30.590Z,2026-03-11T08:47:30.590Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1773218847676_Bello Salamot CV.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69b12c220e6e0d602ab69eb8,Nedu'm Victor Ogunmah ,+23407052746531,ogunmahvictor@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am an operations and communications professional based in Lagos, Nigeria. I have 4+ years of experience managing multi-workstream projects across remote environments.\n\nAt EkoSquare, I coordinated daily operations across multiple client accounts: maintaining SOPs, managing cross-functional teams, tracking KPIs, and reporting to stakeholders. \n\nAt Nigerian Bottling Company (Coca-Cola), I supervised a 40+ person warehouse team and built the Excel-based inventory and financial tracking systems the entire distribution centre relied on.\n\nI am highly organised, consistent with follow-ups, and comfortable moving between operational, research, and coordination tasks without losing momentum. \n\nI work well independently and thrive in environments where execution is taken seriously.\n\nOutside of work, I am deepening my skills in automation and workflow systems through ongoing certifications in N8N, Zapier, and Monday.com. \n\nI am always looking for ways to make processes faster and less dependent on manual effort.",https://www.clippings.me/bluechipcopy,,69a7e2fa934396ba8bb60df1,Business Operations Intern,2026-03-11T08:47:30.773Z,2026-03-11T08:47:30.773Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1773218847871_Nedum_Victor_Resume_TobamsGroup_BizOps.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
