69b19df00e6e0d602ab6c48f,Okorie Godson Chigozie,+23408167289870,godsonchigozie5@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am a Statistics graduate from the Federal University of Technology, Owerri, with a strong interest in data analysis and using data to support informed decision-making. My academic background gave me a solid foundation in analytical thinking, statistical methods, and problem-solving, which naturally led me to pursue data analytics and business analysis.\n\nI have gained practical experience through training and project work where I worked with tools such as Microsoft Excel, SQL, and Python to clean datasets, perform exploratory analysis, and generate insights. During my training at Datalab Analytics, I worked on datasets involving student outcomes, where I helped analyze factors influencing student dropout, graduation, and enrollment. I also completed a Web3 security and data analytics externship with Webacy, where I conducted correlation and frequency analysis on smart contract vulnerability datasets.\n\nBeyond technical work, I also have teaching experience, where I guide teenagers in mathematics and problem-solving. This experience has strengthened my ability to communicate complex ideas clearly, which is valuable in roles that involve stakeholder communication, reporting insights, and documenting requirements.\n\nOverall, I am someone who enjoys analyzing problems, working with data, and translating insights into information that can support better business decisions.\n\nWhy are you interested in this job?\n\nI am interested in this Business Analyst Internship because it aligns closely with my background in statistics, data analysis, and problem-solving. The role provides an opportunity to apply analytical thinking to real business problems while learning how organizations gather requirements, analyze processes, and make data-driven decisions.\n\nWhat particularly interests me about this position is the combination of data analysis, stakeholder engagement, and process improvement. I enjoy working with data to uncover patterns and insights, but I am also interested in understanding how those insights translate into practical business solutions and improved processes.\n\nAdditionally, I see this internship as an opportunity to further develop my skills in business analysis, documentation, reporting, and requirement gathering, while learning from experienced professionals in a structured environment. I am eager to contribute, learn quickly, and build the practical experience needed to grow into a strong business analyst.\n\n",https://adhesive-stretch-ea7.notion.site/Okorie-Godson-Data-Analytics-Portfolio-21925db8a5d580a78d42ce60d3f11169?source=copy_link,,69a71dac934396ba8bb60def,Business Analyst Intern,2026-03-11T16:53:04.300Z,2026-03-11T16:53:04.300Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1773247979307_OKORIE GODSON CHIGOZIE.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69b1a0750e6e0d602ab6c4c0,Esther Emejulu,+23409036104999,emejuluesther@gmail.com,Nigeria,"My name is Esther Chika Emejulu, a 24 year old Nigerian leader, STEM advocate, and graduate of Metallurgical and Materials Engineering. I am passionate about building systems and opportunities that help people grow, learn, and contribute meaningfully to society.\nOver the past two years, I have coordinated teams and communities while working on initiatives that focus on youth development and impact. I currently volunteer as a Communication Officer with Youth Climate Movement, an organization committed to increasing youth participation in climate action and environmental awareness.\nI am also a first time founder of TURNVE, a startup focused on the future of work. Through TURNVE, I am working to address the experiential learning and employability gap among young people by creating opportunities for practical workplace learning. The work we do contributes to advancing Sustainable Development Goals 4, 8, and 10, which focus on quality education, decent work, and reducing inequalities.\nRecently, I was honored to be recognized as one of the Global Changemakers in the fifth cohort of the Opportunity Desk Impact Challenge 2025, an experience that strengthened my commitment to building solutions that create meaningful opportunities for young people.\nI describe myself as a visionary servant leader, because I enjoy organizing systems, managing projects, and supporting people to do their best work while creating impact within communities",,,69a7e2fa934396ba8bb60df1,Business Operations Intern,2026-03-11T17:03:49.466Z,2026-03-11T17:03:49.466Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1773248626827_Esther_operation cv.docx,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
