69b1a4850e6e0d602ab6c54e,Benjamin Mazi,+2348103040431,benjaminmazi1738@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I'm a frontend developer with about 1 year of experience, familiar with frontend technologies such as html, CSS, JavaScript and React.",https://benjamin-mazi.vercel.app/,,69a6fe3c934396ba8bb60dec,Frontend Developer Intern,2026-03-11T17:21:09.486Z,2026-03-11T17:21:09.486Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1773249665442_benjamin-mazi-resume.docx,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69b1a5980e6e0d602ab6c58a,Christopher Umoh Emah,+23409169772398,intellectsmartestemah@gmail.com,Nigeria,"My name is Christopher Umoh Emah, and I am currently based in Uyo, Akwa Ibom State, Nigeria. I am a motivated and curious learner with a strong interest in business analysis, data, and problem-solving. I am currently pursuing a B.Sc. in Mathematics (2022–2026) and a B.Sc. in Computer Science (2023–2027) at the National Open University of Nigeria. My academic journey has strengthened my analytical thinking and structured approach to solving problems, which naturally led me to develop an interest in business analysis and data-driven decision making.\n\nOver the past few years, I have intentionally built skills that align with understanding people, processes, and data. I have completed several professional certifications in areas such as virtual assistance, customer service, business communication, CRM systems, and data analysis using Excel and Google Sheets. These learning experiences have helped me understand how organizations work, how data informs decisions, and how clear communication connects teams and stakeholders.\n\nBeyond academics and certifications, I have also had the opportunity to take on leadership and responsibility in different environments. I served as a Senior Prefect during my secondary school years and graduated as the Best Graduating Student in my school. I have also held leadership roles such as Director and Public Relations Officer in my church, Director of Public Duties at my workplace, and Coordinator, and business in a school I'm currently working . In addition, I currently serve as a Cowrywise Ambassador, where I help promote financial literacy and responsible financial habits among young people.\n\nThese experiences have helped me develop strong communication, organization, and stakeholder-management skills. They have also taught me how to listen carefully, coordinate people, document ideas clearly, and contribute to improving processes. All of which are skills I am excited to apply in a business analysis environment.\n\nI am particularly interested in this internship because it offers the opportunity to gain hands-on experience, learn from experienced professionals, and contribute meaningfully to projects. I enjoy analyzing problems, understanding how systems work, and finding ways to make processes clearer and more efficient. I am eager to learn, adaptable, and committed to continuous growth.\n\nOverall, I see this internship as an opportunity to grow professionally, contribute my analytical mindset and communication skills, and continue developing into a well-rounded business analyst.\n",,,69a71dac934396ba8bb60def,Business Analyst Intern,2026-03-11T17:25:44.486Z,2026-03-11T17:25:44.486Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1773249941028_CHRISTOPHER EMAH RESUME.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69b1a59e0e6e0d602ab6c592,AbdulMalik Hussein,+2347049209564,husseinabdulmalik0@gmail.com,Nigeria,"My background is in public administration, which gave me a strong foundation in how organizations structure their decisions and processes. Since graduating, I've worked across operations and digital content, supporting businesses as a virtual assistant, social media assistant, and web content manager. In those roles I was able to see what was working, what wasn't, and how workflows could be tightened up and more importantly incorporate some of my ideas into my workflow.",,,69a71dac934396ba8bb60def,Business Analyst Intern,2026-03-11T17:25:50.597Z,2026-03-11T17:25:50.597Z,,,"https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1773249947759_Hussein, Abdulmalik Opetomiwa_ Resume.pdf",Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69b1a5be0e6e0d602ab6c59b,joseph bawo,+2349013550698,josephbawo@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I’m a motivated and curious individual with a strong interest in technology, problem solving, and building tools that help other developers work more efficiently. I enjoy learning new technologies and constantly improving my skills, particularly in areas related to JavaScript, React, and modern web development.\n\nOne of the ways I’ve been applying these skills is through open source development. I built and maintain developer tools such as create-bawo-frontend, a CLI that helps developers quickly scaffold modern frontend applications with tools like React, Tailwind, and different backend integrations.  \n\nWorking on open source has been especially meaningful to me because it allows me to build tools that others can use to solve real problems. I enjoy thinking about developer experience, simplifying complex setups, and creating tools that save other developers time.\n\nI’m particularly interested in roles where I can continue contributing to open source, improving developer tooling, and collaborating with other engineers to build products that make development faster, simpler, and more accessible. I’m always eager to learn, share knowledge, and contribute to projects that have a real impact on the developer community.\n",https://www.josephbawo.tech/,,69a6fe3c934396ba8bb60dec,Frontend Developer Intern,2026-03-11T17:26:22.886Z,2026-03-11T17:26:22.886Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1773249978784_Joseph_Bawo_Resume.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
