69b1b0260e6e0d602ab6c6e5,Opeyemi Omosehin,+23408112302940,oppasskybest@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I’m a self‑motivated front‑end enthusiast who learns by building. I started with YouTube tutorials, then quickly moved to hands‑on projects to solidify my understanding of JavaScript and modern frameworks. Right now I’m deepening my skills through the IBM Full Stack Development certificate on Coursera it’s giving me a broader view of how the entire development workflow fits together, from front‑end to back‑end.\n\nOver the past few months I’ve built and deployed several web applications, each using different technologies:\n\nBitdrip DCA app bitdripport.vercel.app a Next.js project (my first experience with server‑side rendering and file‑based routing)\n\ncrystal  crystaldevine.vercel.app  built with React + Vite for fast development \n\ne-plant-shopping  e-plant-shopping-phi-ten.vercel.app  another React + Vite project, focused on component composition and state management updated from my ibm lecture \n\nmy-portfolio opeyemijohn.vercel.app pure HTML, CSS, JavaScript with Tailwind CSS for styling\n\nstatic restaurant food shop  static-restaurant-food-shop.vercel.app  also HTML/CSS/JS + Tailwind\n\nbetframe  betframe.vercel.app  HTML/CSS/JS + Tailwind, focused on responsive dashboard layouts\n\nzenvora – zenvora-mu.vercel.app – an e‑commerce site built with HTML/CSS/JS + Tailwind\n\nAll code is on my GitHub (github.com/oppasskybest-ai). I’m comfortable with HTML, CSS, JavaScript, React, and I’m actively learning Next.js, state management, and API integration. I’m looking for an internship where I can contribute to a real product while learning from experienced developers.\n\n",https://opeyemijohn.vercel.app,,69a6fe3c934396ba8bb60dec,Frontend Developer Intern,2026-03-11T18:10:46.162Z,2026-03-11T18:10:46.162Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1773252642493_Omoshehin_Opeyemi_John_CV.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
