69b21768700560090278d390,Onyebuchi Genius OKONKWO,+23408100738389,okonkwoonyebu@gmail.com,Nigeria,"My name is Onyebuchi Genius Okonkwo. I hold a degree in Zoology from Nnamdi Azikiwe University, where my academic work focused on parasitology and public health. Over time, my professional experience has brought together three areas that interest me deeply: research, community engagement, and visual communication.\n\n\nDuring my service as a National Health Fellow with the Federal Ministry of Health in Nkanu West Local Government Area, I supported monitoring and documentation of improvements across primary healthcare facilities. Part of my responsibility involved preparing reports and PowerPoint presentations that organized field data into clear tables, charts, and visual summaries for state health authorities and community stakeholders. Through this work, I saw how thoughtful presentation of information can make complex findings easier to understand and more useful for decision-making.\n\n\nAlongside my public health work, I have also participated in youth education and sustainability initiatives through SDG advocacy projects. In one of these projects, I helped design and distribute printed learning materials used to introduce secondary school students to the Sustainable Development Goals. The goal was to present global ideas in a way that students could relate to their everyday lives. I have also facilitated basic graphic design training sessions where I introduced participants to simple design principles such as layout balance, color use, and visual clarity.\n\n\nThese experiences gradually shaped a personal creative brand I call Genius Craft. Through it, I explore how design, storytelling, and structured presentation can help communicate information more clearly. \n\n\nMy interest in design grew from practical work—preparing reports, educational materials, and presentations that help people understand ideas that might otherwise feel distant or technical.\n\n\nAt this stage of my career, I am continuing to build my skills while learning how design can be applied thoughtfully in different professional settings.",https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1nDWo2FbqLd4BgqZJGAN1fS9g_aMQe6fI,,69a6fefa934396ba8bb60ded,Graphic Design Intern,2026-03-12T01:31:20.390Z,2026-03-12T01:31:20.390Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1773279076081_CV(Gd)_ONYEBUCHI Okonkwo.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
