69b25f1d700560090278d52e,Matilda Wanjiru Njau,+254254782909566,njaumatildawanjiru@gmail.com,Kenya,"I’ve always been drawn to the 'invisible' that makes an application reliable. Through my journey in backend development, I’ve confirmed that I enjoy designing the 'how', far more than the surface-level visuals.\n\nOne thing that defines me as a developer is that I’m a 'loud learner.' In my current internship, I'm the person always asking, 'Why are we doing it this way?' because I believe good software is a team sport. I don’t just want to write code that works; I want to understand the reasoning behind the design.\n\nI’m the kind of developer who spends as much time thinking about how a system might fail as I do about making it work—which is why I genuinely enjoy code reviews and technical brainstorming; I believe that’s where the best, most resilient architecture is born. Ultimately, I’m looking for a role where I can contribute to high-quality codebases while continuing to grow alongside experienced engineers.",https://github.com/njaumatilda,,69a7e52c934396ba8bb60df2,Backend Developer Intern,2026-03-12T06:37:17.822Z,2026-03-12T06:37:17.822Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1773297434481_MatildaNjau_BackEndDev Resume.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
