69b26357700560090278d5ad,John Tolulope Afariogun,+2348162127365,afariogun.john2002@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am a product-minded Backend Developer who loves operating at the intersection of engineering and business strategy. My journey into tech actually started with a degree in Chemical Engineering, which ingrained in me a deep appreciation for systems thinking, complex problem-solving, and optimizing processes. I’ve carried that analytical foundation directly into software engineering, where I now focus on building reliable, scalable, and data-driven systems.\n\nRecently, my work has been heavily focused on fintech and secure API integrations. I’ve built a backend wallet service with Paystack integration, developed a payment gateway and integrations marketplace, and contributed to open-source projects like a FastAPI Book Management API. During my time in the HNG Internship program, where I reached the finalist stage as a backend developer, I really honed my ability to deliver high-quality code under pressure while collaborating closely with cross-functional teams.\n\nTechnically, my strongest foundation is in Python, FastAPI, and Go. To bridge the gap between development and deployment, I actively integrate DevOps practices into my workflow—specifically using Docker and Kubernetes to containerize and orchestrate my backend APIs, ensuring the systems I build are highly scalable and deployment-ready. Because I look at engineering through a product lens, I don't just want to write code—I want to understand the 'why' behind the features, bridge the gap between technical execution and product strategy, and ultimately deliver seamless user experiences.\n\nI’m naturally curious, highly adaptable, and always looking to grow. Right now, I'm eager to bring my humble, hardworking mindset to a fast-paced team where I can leverage my backend and DevOps experience while diving into new challenges—like mastering your Node.js and TypeScript ecosystem.",http://github.com/johnafariogun/