69b2908f700560090278e2ad,Eniola Olashile Saliu,+2347036846996,eniolaolashile@gmail.com,Russian Federation,"I am a detail-driven, growth-focused professional who is passionate about business analysis and process improvement. I combine analytical thinking, research, and stakeholder management skills to drive data-informed decisions. My experience in fast-paced environments has taught me adaptability, strong communication, and presentation skills. I'm excited to contribute to TOBAMS' mission of transforming education and talent development by leveraging structured analysis to improve systems and drive impact.",,,69a71dac934396ba8bb60def,Business Analyst Intern,2026-03-12T10:08:15.432Z,2026-03-12T10:08:15.432Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1773310092269_Saliu Eniola Olashile - Curriculum Vitae.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69b290dd700560090278e2c8,Hamad Kamorudeen,+2349138058580,hamadkamorudeen@gmail.com,Nigeria,"My name is Hamad Kamorudeen. I study Actuarial Science at the University of Lagos, on track for a Second Class Upper, but the degree is honestly just the surface.\n\nWhat actually drives me is wanting to make something real. Not building a profile. Not collecting certificates. Actually producing work that means something. Earlier this year I worked through a 31,000 row dataset on my own, with no class attached to it, built four dashboards, and documented findings with direct business implications. Before that I interned at FATE Foundation where I worked with operational and financial data, produced stakeholder reports, and improved data accuracy by 25% within two months. I also run a few personal ventures on the side, which means I understand what a business decision actually costs when you get it wrong.\n\nI am at a stage where I want environments that take the work seriously. That is the version of me I am bringing here.",https://github.com/hamadkamorudeen,,69a71dac934396ba8bb60def,Business Analyst Intern,2026-03-12T10:09:33.892Z,2026-03-12T10:09:33.892Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1773310170656_Hamad_Kamorudeen_Tobams_BA_Intern_CV.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69b2911a700560090278e2d6,Promise Faith Emmanuel,+23409051762381,thepromiseemmanuel@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am Promise Emmanuel, a detail-oriented and proactive professional with hands-on experience in administrative support and customer service. I have worked as an Administrative Assistant at Island City Sports Ltd., where I coordinated workflows, tracked tasks, and supported cross-functional teams, and as a Customer Support Executive at Coollink.ng, where I managed client interactions and helped improve operational processes.\n\nI have completed professional training in Professional Assistant Skills and Virtual Assistant Skills, which strengthened my ability to work efficiently in remote environments, manage multiple tasks, and support project execution. I am passionate about business operations and excited to contribute to initiatives like Obams Group’s Recycled Learning, where I can apply my skills to streamline operations, support stakeholder engagement, and help implement technology-driven solutions that enhance learning experiences.",,,69a7e2fa934396ba8bb60df1,Business Operations Intern,2026-03-12T10:10:34.344Z,2026-03-12T10:10:34.344Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1773310231528_Promise Emmanuel CV.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69b2913e700560090278e2ea,Precious Chinecherem Alaike,+23408126107379,preciousalaike25@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I’m a recent graduate of Petroleum Engineering who is building a career in product design. Over time, I developed a strong interest in how digital products are designed and how thoughtful design can improve the way people interact with technology. I’ve been learning and practicing UI/UX design using tools like Figma, Canva, and Adobe Express, focusing on creating simple and user-friendly experiences. I’m a curious and strategic thinker who enjoys solving problems and continuously learning new skills in the tech space.",https://www.upwork.com/freelancers/~012bee57541240c096?p=1995884173226119168,,69aefa4c05d00a25722c84c2,Product Designer Intern,2026-03-12T10:11:10.736Z,2026-03-12T10:11:10.736Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1773310267674_Portfolio.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69b291a8700560090278e30a,Excellent Faruna Ojodua,+2348185509550,farunaexcel@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am a creative and detail-oriented designer with a background in Architecture and a strong passion for graphic design and visual communication. My experience in architecture has helped me develop a keen eye for composition, aesthetics, and problem-solving, which I apply to creating impactful visual designs.\nI am skilled in design tools and enjoy exploring creative solutions for branding, social media graphics, and visual content. I am eager to grow professionally, learn from experienced designers, and contribute my creativity and dedication to a collaborative remote team.",,,69a6fefa934396ba8bb60ded,Graphic Design Intern,2026-03-12T10:12:56.913Z,2026-03-12T10:12:56.913Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1773310373606_resume.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69b29222700560090278e330,Olumide Adebayo,+23408108591615,olumild998@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am seasoned developer with good programming language background covering both aspect of backend and frontend development. I have excelled in projects which has enable me to hone my skills. Overall, i have been able to impact my community by empowering youths in information technology skills as a one time digital ambassador with the African development bank. In this position, i was able to enhance youth productivity and employment by instilling in them modern software skills",,,69a7e52c934396ba8bb60df2,Backend Developer Intern,2026-03-12T10:14:58.957Z,2026-03-12T10:14:58.957Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1773310495921_olumide resume.docx,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69b29233700560090278e33a,Katheu Kilonzo,+254745434775,fkatheukilonzo@gmail.com,Kenya,"I’m a software engineering trainee and psychology graduate from Kenyatta University with a strong interest in building technology that solves real-world problems. Through the ALX Software Engineering program and my cloud training, I’ve been developing skills in backend development using JavaScript, Python, and cloud technologies like AWS. I enjoy working on systems that power meaningful applications, especially where data and user experience intersect.\n\nIn addition to my technical training, my background in psychology has shaped how I approach problem-solving and collaboration. I’ve worked on projects involving research, community initiatives, and technology for social impact, which has strengthened my analytical thinking and teamwork skills. I’m currently focused on growing as a backend engineer by building scalable APIs, understanding system architecture, and contributing to products that create real value for users.",https://github.com/kathFK1234,,69a7e52c934396ba8bb60df2,Backend Developer Intern,2026-03-12T10:15:15.467Z,2026-03-12T10:15:15.467Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1773310511681_Katheu_Kilonzo_CV.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69b2923f700560090278e343,Peter Oyishoma,+23408164804155,oyishomapeter@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I recently graduated from the Federal University of Technology, Minna, where I studied cybersecurity and related computing disciplines. My academic training provided me with a solid foundation in areas such as system security, networking, and risk analysis, with a particular focus on secure system design.\nAlongside my cybersecurity background, I have also developed early practical experience in full-stack web development using the MERN stack, which includes MongoDB, Express, React, and Node.js. During my National Youth Service Corps service at Natview Technology Ltd Abuja, I had the opportunity to work with modern web technologies and strengthen my understanding of how secure and scalable web applications are designed and built. This exposure helped me appreciate the importance of integrating security considerations into application and system architecture from the early stages of development. Now it has sparked my interest in also building with backend technologies.\nBefore now, I have gained practical industry experience through previous roles in technology support and development. I worked as a frontend developer and software support engineer at the same Natview Technology Ltd before going to the university, and earlier as a support front-end web developer at GESUSOFT Ltd. in Abuja. These roles helped me build strong troubleshooting abilities, technical support skills, and experience working collaboratively to deliver reliable technology solutions. Earlier in my career, I also served as an instructor at computer training centres where I trained beginners in foundational computing skills.\n\nMy goal is to build highly professional skills in technology, and particularly backend technolgies, while contributing to the development of secure and resilient digital systems.",https://github.com/oyishomapeter-tech,,69a7e52c934396ba8bb60df2,Backend Developer Intern,2026-03-12T10:15:27.405Z,2026-03-12T10:15:27.405Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1773310524491_PETER_OYISHOMA_CV (1).pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69b292a9700560090278e35a,Adeosun Favour Adewole ,+2348063530151,adeosunfavoradewole@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am a user-focused Product and UI/UX Designer with a strong passion for creating intuitive digital experiences that solve real problems for users. My interest in design started from a curiosity about how people interact with digital products and how thoughtful design can make those experiences simpler, more engaging, and more meaningful.\n\nOver time, I have developed practical experience in user research, wireframing, prototyping, and high-fidelity interface design. I enjoy translating ideas and user insights into clear, well-structured interfaces that balance usability, aesthetics, and functionality. I regularly use tools such as Figma, FigJam, and Miro to design interfaces, map user journeys, and collaborate with teams during the product design process.\n\nI have also worked on several projects where I collaborated with developers and stakeholders to turn product ideas into functional designs, applying user-centered design principles and iterative improvements through feedback and usability testing. These experiences helped me develop a strong appreciation for the collaborative nature of product design and the importance of aligning user needs with product goals.\n\nWhat excites me most about product design is the opportunity to combine creativity, problem-solving, and research to build products that truly improve people's experiences. I am always eager to learn, explore new design approaches, and contribute fresh ideas that help teams build better products.\n\nI am particularly excited about this internship because it offers the opportunity to work closely with experienced designers, participate in real product development processes, and continue growing as a designer while contributing meaningful ideas and thoughtful design solutions.",https://dribbble.com/FavyWorld,,69aefa4c05d00a25722c84c2,Product Designer Intern,2026-03-12T10:17:13.468Z,2026-03-12T10:17:13.468Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1773310628348_FAVOUR ADEOSUN CV Tobams Group.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69b29411700560090278e39d,Lydia Ngozi Azide,+23408063740821,lydiaazide@yahoo.com,Nigeria,"I graduated from the University of Port Harcourt with a degree in History and Diplomacy, and I began my professional career in 2019 as a Travel Consultant. During the COVID-19 disruption, when the travel industry slowed significantly, I expanded my skill set by volunteering as a social media manager and working as a content writer. Those roles strengthened my communication, digital, and problem-solving skills.\n\nWhen operations resumed, I returned to the travel industry and gradually took on more responsibility, eventually becoming an Operations Manager in 2023. In that role, I managed corporate client accounts and handled operational data such as invoicing, reporting, and tracking performance using Excel.\nWhile working with operational data, I became increasingly interested in how data could be analysed to support better decision-making. That led me to formally study data analysis in 2024 with Vephla Group, where I developed practical skills in Excel, SQL, Power BI, and Python for analysing and visualising data.\nI’m now focused on transitioning into a business or data analyst role where I can combine my operational experience with analytical tools to help organisations make more informed, data-driven decisions.\n",https://www.datascienceportfol.io/Lydiatheanalyst,,69a71dac934396ba8bb60def,Business Analyst Intern,2026-03-12T10:23:13.304Z,2026-03-12T10:23:13.304Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1773310988898_Lydia_Azide_Data_Analyst_CV.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
