69b2cedd9276d25980a810e8,Heritage Isaac Oludipe,+2347059804235,dipedeji@gmail.com,Nigeria,"My name is Heritage Isaac. I am a product designer with a focus on turning ideas into simple, useful digital experiences, from early strategy and research all the way through to design and implementation.\n\nI have worked across fintech, music tech, logistics, and edtech. Some of the products I have worked on includes Ordersounds by Creacove, a platform helping African music creators unlock their earnings, Matchchayn a web 3 focused dating app.\n\nBeyond client work, I build products of my own. Right now I am publicly building Preframe, a Figma plugin and web app that reads a PRD or brief and generates your entire UX research layer directly on the canvas. I am also working on Varro, a plugin that scans your existing Figma file and builds your design system automatically.\n\nWhat drives my work is a simple belief that good design is not just how something looks, it is how well it solves a real problem for a real person. That is the standard I hold everything to.",http://heritageisaac.xyz/,,69aefa4c05d00a25722c84c2,Product Designer Intern,2026-03-12T14:34:05.207Z,2026-03-12T14:34:05.207Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1773326041134_Heritage Isaac PD Resume.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69b2cedd9276d25980a810ed,Adeyemi Opeoluwa,+23408038098788,ade4startime@gmail.com,Nigeria,"My name is Adeyemi Opeoluwa Adedayo, and I am a passionate and creative aspiring graphic designer with a strong interest in visual communication and digital design. I enjoy transforming ideas into engaging visual content that communicates clearly and effectively.\nI have developed skills in graphic design tools and design principles such as layout, typography, color theory, and branding. I enjoy creating social media graphics, posters, and visual materials that help brands and organizations connect with their audience.\nAs a graphic design intern, I am eager to learn from experienced designers, improve my technical and creative skills, and contribute fresh ideas to real-world projects. I am highly motivated, detail-oriented, and always open to feedback that helps me grow professionally.\nMy goal is to build a strong career in graphic design while continuously improving my creativity, technical abilities, and understanding of modern design trends.",,,69a6fefa934396ba8bb60ded,Graphic Design Intern,2026-03-12T14:34:05.857Z,2026-03-12T14:34:05.857Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1773326043853_resume 1_022211.docx,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69b2cee59276d25980a810f5,Gabriel Ogbe,+2348102588002,ogbehg@gmail.com,Nigeria,"Born into a family of 15 in Lagos, Nigeria, I obtained my university degree in economics in 2023 at the federal university of Lafia, after a prolonged strike that lasted for over 2 years.\nDuring my time at school, I devoted lots of time to study and tutoring, helping me graduate with a cumulative score of 3.74. During this time, I took some professional courses at Coursera, including data analytics. Then I enrolled for a KPMG job simulation with Forage. Shortly after, I was accepted for a business development internship with GaoTek Inc. and received certificates upon completion then I went for my national youth service.\nWhile I served my country as a youth and graduate, I was assigned to a solar company for my primary place of assignment and was placed under the marketing team. My role involved helping the team and the company make sales by reaching out to prospects, creating and designing marketing materials, managing the team's email, proposals, and online contents, assisting with recruitment processes, and more.\nDuring this time, I enrolled and took part in the Tech4Dev competition for data analysis after scoring 85% in the test phase but I didn't get to win the competition.\nI have so much interest in data analysis, especially after learning about econometrics and how we solved problems using data and econometrics reasoning. I have decided to focus on building this path in my life and helping organisations and the society at large in ways I can. But to be able to do this and get better, I'm open to learning as well.",,,69a71dac934396ba8bb60def,Business Analyst Intern,2026-03-12T14:34:13.370Z,2026-03-12T14:34:13.370Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1773326049806_Gabriel Ogbe_CV.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
