69b2d61b9276d25980a813cb,Onyedika david,+23407015013393,samuesthero400@gmail.com,Nigeria,"My name is Nwene Onyedika David, and I am a frontend developer with a strong interest in building user-friendly and visually engaging web applications. I started my journey in tech with UI/UX design, which helped me develop a good understanding of user-centered design and how to create intuitive interfaces.\n\nOver time, I expanded into frontend development, where I work with technologies such as HTML, CSS, JavaScript and React. I enjoy turning design ideas into functional and responsive web interfaces.\n\nI have also worked on projects such as a fleet management system and other web-based applications, where I focused on building clean, responsive layouts and improving the user experience.\n\nI am passionate about learning new technologies, collaborating with teams, and building products that solve real-world problems while delivering a great user experience.\n\n",github.com/onyxs-prog,,69a6fe3c934396ba8bb60dec,Frontend Developer Intern,2026-03-12T15:04:59.121Z,2026-03-12T15:04:59.121Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1773327896037_d318e249-de8e-4da5-8d87-77326da5bdce.PDF,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69b2d69a9276d25980a813ed,AJAYI BUSAYO MARY ,+2349077362420,busayomaryajayi@gmail.com,Nigeria,"My name is Ajayi Busayo Mary, and I am an analytical and detail-oriented Economics graduate with a passion for understanding how businesses work and how to solve their problems.\n\nMy academic background in Economics taught me to think critically about business challenges, while my diploma in Statistics gave me the technical skills to work with data accurately and identify trends. I put these skills into practice during my SIWES internship at the Ondo State Bureau of Statistics, where I collected, validated, and managed data to support reporting. This experience made me proficient in Excel and taught me how to turn raw numbers into clear, useful information.\n\nBeyond the technical side, I am a strong communicator. During my NYSC year, I worked as a teacher in a rural community, which taught me patience and how to explain things clearly to different people. I also served as the Zonal Secretary for the NCCF, where I managed documentation and coordinated with team members—skills that are directly useful for understanding and documenting business needs.\n\nI am now eager to combine my love for data with my problem solving mindset as a Business Analysis Intern. I want to learn how to bridge the gap between business challenges and practical solutions, and I am excited to bring my strong work ethic and curiosity to your team",,,69a71dac934396ba8bb60def,Business Analyst Intern,2026-03-12T15:07:06.235Z,2026-03-12T15:07:06.235Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1773328022206_AJAYI BUSAYO MARY ajCV(1).pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69b2d7859276d25980a81426, Adebimpe Adeyemi,+23408136108334,adeyemiaishaadebimpe@gmail.com,Nigeria,"My name is Adeyemi Adebimpe, and I am a product designer with a background in Physics from the University of Ibadan. My journey into product design began in 2023 when I transitioned from science into technology, bringing with me a strong analytical and problem-solving mindset.\n\nI started my design career through a competitive scholarship at the Women Techsters Fellowship, where I spent a year building a solid foundation in product design. During the program, I gained hands-on experience in user research, interface design, and problem-solving while also volunteering as a designer, contributing to product development projects and learning how to translate real user needs into practical digital solutions.\n\nFollowing the fellowship, I further strengthened my practical experience through a product design internship, where I continued developing my skills in designing user-centered products and collaborating within cross-functional teams.\n\nCurrently, I serve as the Lead Product Design Instructor at the National Institute of Information Technology where I train and mentor aspiring designers in foundational product design skills. In this role, I help equip young talents with the practical knowledge needed to transition into the tech industry while guiding them through real-world design thinking and product development processes.\n\nOverall, my journey has been driven by a passion for solving meaningful problems through design and empowering others to build impactful digital products.",1. https://www.behance.net/adeyemiaishaa/projects     2. https://adedesigns.framer.website/,,69aefa4c05d00a25722c84c2,Product Designer Intern,2026-03-12T15:11:01.059Z,2026-03-12T15:11:01.059Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1773328258012_Adeyemi_ADEBIMPE_A_CV-2026.docx.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
