69b314529292616f7be52d4c,Noimot Kofoworola Azeez,+23409110305805,noimotazeez147@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am a product designer with a strong interest in creating intuitive and user-friendly digital experiences. My journey into UI/UX design started when I became interested in how products solve real problems for users, and since then I’ve been focused on learning how to design solutions that are both functional and visually appealing.\n\nI have experience working with tools like Figma to create wireframes, mockups, and interactive prototypes. I enjoy going through the full design process from understanding user problems and researching their needs, to designing interfaces that improve usability and overall product experience.\n\nOne thing I particularly enjoy about UI/UX design is the balance between creativity and problem-solving. I like thinking about how small design decisions, such as layout, typography, or interaction patterns, can significantly improve how users interact with a product.\n\nI’m also passionate about continuous learning and improving my design process. I enjoy collaborating with others, getting feedback, and iterating on designs to create better experiences for users. Overall, my goal as a designer is to build products that are simple, accessible, and meaningful for the people who use them.\n",https://www.figma.com/proto/KNGUstQm6fbDmbIDXIfU4f/My-Work?node-id=249-853&p=f&t=jT9cjHgc5GiAbsal-0&scaling=scale-down&content-scaling=fixed&page-id=244%3A296&starting-point-node-id=251%3A3753,,69aefa4c05d00a25722c84c2,Product Designer Intern,2026-03-12T19:30:26.750Z,2026-03-12T19:30:26.750Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1773343823426_Noimot I Cv.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69b314f79292616f7be52d75,Elizabeth Ayoola,+2349012184180,elizabethayoola05@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am a first-class Banking & Finance undergraduate at the University of Lagos with strong skills in project coordination, reporting, and process optimization. Through my professional and leadership experiences, I have managed multiple workstreams, tracked key metrics, maintained structured documentation, and supported data-driven decision-making. \n\nI enjoy coordinating teams and workflows, translating complex data into actionable insights, and ensuring projects are executed efficiently. I am particularly eager to apply these skills in a fast-paced operations environment, contributing to Tobams Group’s innovative initiatives while learning from experienced professionals.",,,69a7e2fa934396ba8bb60df1,Business Operations Intern,2026-03-12T19:33:11.229Z,2026-03-12T19:33:11.229Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1773343988401_ELIZABETH AYOOLA.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69b315339292616f7be52d89,Alabi Esther Funmilayo,+2348164766198,alabiesthe15@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am an aspiring Data and Business Analyst with a strong interest in using data and structured analysis to support business decision-making and process improvement. I have been developing my skills in tools such as Excel, SQL, Python, and Power BI, which I use to analyze data, identify trends, and present insights clearly.\n\nI have worked on projects such as customer churn analysis and industry carbon emission analysis, where I explored datasets, identified patterns, and created visual reports to communicate findings. These experiences strengthened my analytical thinking, problem-solving ability, and attention to detail.\n\nIn addition to my technical skills, I value continuous learning and adaptability. I am always eager to improve my knowledge, work with others, and apply what I learn to real-world problems. I am particularly interested in opportunities that allow me to grow as an analyst while contributing meaningfully to organizational goals.",https://www.linkedin.com/in/esther-alabi-funmilayo/,,69a71dac934396ba8bb60def,Business Analyst Intern,2026-03-12T19:34:11.992Z,2026-03-12T19:34:11.992Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1773344048642_Alabi_EstherCVDS.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69b3159a9292616f7be52d9b,Ibrahim Abubakar Opeyemi,+23407078322733,itzjst.ibrahim59@gmail.com,Nigeria,"Well, I'm currently a final-year Electrical and Electronics Engineering student at the Federal University of Technology, Minna, with a strong focus on software engineering and backend architecture. My engineering background has given me a rigorous foundation in problem solving, system design, and analytical thinking.\nOver the past year, I have actively applied these skills to build scalable digital solutions. I am currently developing the backend architecture for a campus marketplace application called Sturvs, where I utilize PostgreSQL (via Supabase) to manage complex relational data, user authentication, and real time state updates. I am a builder who is comfortable working with JavaScript/TypeScript and RESTful APIs, and I am highly adaptable, having recently completed a Design Thinking Bootcamp to ensure the solutions I engineer are always user centric and highly practical.",https://github.com/cujo-o,,69a7e52c934396ba8bb60df2,Backend Developer Intern,2026-03-12T19:35:54.880Z,2026-03-12T19:35:54.880Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1773344151013_Ibrahim Abubakar Opeyemi_cv.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69b315b09292616f7be52dab,Emele Chinwendu Treasure ,+2348146519032,chinwenduemele02@gmail.com,Nigeria,"My name is Emele Chinwendu Treasure, a recent graduate with a degree in Economics from Babcock University, where I developed strong analytical and research skills through various courses and my final research project. My project focused on evaluating Nigerian agricultural policies and their impact on employment, which involved analyzing data, reviewing policy frameworks, and presenting recommendations.\n\nBeyond academics, I have taken on leadership and service roles that helped me build communication, organization, and problem-solving skills. I served as a room assistant in my university, where I regularly worked hand in hand with hostel management to resolve resolved issues, maintained orderliness in residential areas and during meetings.\n\nI’m particularly interested in business analysis because I enjoy understanding problems, analyzing information, and helping organizations make better decisions based on data and structured insights. \n\nThis internship appeals to me because it offers the opportunity to learn from experienced professionals while contributing my analytical thinking, attention to detail, and willingness to learn in a practical environment",https://www.linkedin.com/in/chinwendu-emele-24b105322?utm_source=share&utm_campaign=share_via&utm_content=profile&utm_medium=android_app,,69a71dac934396ba8bb60def,Business Analyst Intern,2026-03-12T19:36:16.153Z,2026-03-12T19:36:16.153Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1773344172990_IMG-20260312-WA0135.jpg,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69b316e09292616f7be52dd8,JOY KOLAWOLE,+23409016881918,joykolawole99@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am a third-year Economics undergraduate at Lagos State University with a strong interest in data analysis and how structured insights support effective decision making. My academic training has developed my analytical thinking through courses such as financial economics, banking operations, and risk management.\n\nAlongside my studies, I have been building practical skills in tools such as Excel, Power BI, Tableau, and PowerPoint, which I use to analyze datasets, identify patterns, and communicate insights clearly. I am also actively involved in learning communities such as  SheCodeAfrica,  WomenTechSter, where I engage in discussions, projects, and collaborative learning that continue to strengthen my technical and analytical abilities.",www.linkedin.com/in/joy-kolawole-a1152a23a,,69a71dac934396ba8bb60def,Business Analyst Intern,2026-03-12T19:41:20.228Z,2026-03-12T19:41:20.228Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1773344476763_Joy_Kolawole_CV.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69b317a99292616f7be52e09,Emmanuella Itunuoluwa Bakare,+23408166910688,emmanuellaitunu8@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I’m a final-year student of History and International Studies at Redeemer’s University with an interest in research, analysis, and understanding how institutions and global systems work.\n My academic work has involved carrying out research on the history, development and impact of organizations such as the Nigeria Natural Medicine Development Agency, which has helped me build research and critical thinking skills.\nAlongside my studies, I’ve been developing technical skills in data analysis through self learning and practical projects. I’ve been working with tools like Microsoft Excel and introductory Python to understand how data can be cleaned, organized, and analyzed to uncover useful insights. I'm currently learning Power BI, Python, Excel, and SQL. \nMy first project involved analyzing a multi-year global sales dataset using excel, where I focused on identifying trends and interpreting the results into actionable insights.\nI also document and share my learning process through project summaries and GitHub repositories. This has helped me improve not just my technical skills but also my ability to explain complex ideas clearly.\nI enjoy learning, exploring new tools, and combining analytical thinking with practical problem-solving.\n",https://github.com/bakareitunuoluwa63,,69a71dac934396ba8bb60def,Business Analyst Intern,2026-03-12T19:44:41.619Z,2026-03-12T19:44:41.619Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1773344679059_Resume_Emmanuella_Bakare.docx,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69b317d69292616f7be52e1f,Benedict Achikeh ,+2349032416644,achikeh2003@gmail.com,Nigeria,"My name is Benedict Achikeh, and I am a Computer Engineering graduate from Veritas University with a strong interest in backend development and building data-driven applications. During my final year, I developed a Library Management System, where I worked on backend logic, database design, and system functionality for managing users and book transactions.\nAlongside my academic work, I have experience in data analysis and data management, which has helped me develop strong analytical and problem-solving skills when working with structured systems and databases.\nI am always looking for opportunities to improve my technical skills. I’m excited about working in a collaborative engineering environment where I can contribute, learn from experienced developers, and grow.",https://www.linkedin.com/in/benedict-achikeh-36021225b,,69a7e52c934396ba8bb60df2,Backend Developer Intern,2026-03-12T19:45:26.182Z,2026-03-12T19:45:26.182Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1773344723037_Benedict's backend intern cv.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69b318849292616f7be52e59,Bazunu Oghenefejiro Odinekachukwu,+2348165397512,odihandchi@gmail.com,Nigeria,"My name is Bazunu Oghenefejiro, and I’m a problem-solver at heart. With a background in Agricultural Economics and Extension, I’ve always been fascinated by how systems work—specifically how to take complex information and make it useful for others.\nI’ve spent the last few years building my own medical supply business, where I acted as my own analyst—optimizing my inventory, digitizing my processes, and managing client relationships. Recently, I completed my Google Data Analytics certification to sharpen my technical toolkit in SQL, R, and Tableau. I’ve already applied these skills to optimize my own business operations and a health-tech case study, and now I’m eager to bring that mix of entrepreneurial grit and data-driven insight to Tobams Group.",https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1CJLkkPz0RhOmwkDrxTM2J-Ijb1L2F3ycKN1z07ZS2Qs/edit?usp=drivesdk,,69a71dac934396ba8bb60def,Business Analyst Intern,2026-03-12T19:48:20.060Z,2026-03-12T19:48:20.060Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1773344896843_CURRICULUM VITAE.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69b318889292616f7be52e68,Adaeze Nnonyelu,+23407061779767,nnonyeluadaeze@gmail.com,Nigeria,"My name is Adaeze Nnonyelu, and I'm a data professional with a background in Electronic and Computer Engineering. Over the past two years, I've gained hands-on experience working with raw data and interpreting it to technical and non-technical audiences.\nAt the National Center for Artificial Intelligence and Robotics (NCAIR), I worked as a Data Science Intern, where I did a lot of the foundational work that business analysts do, gathering requirements from stakeholders/team leads, cleaning and analyzing data to extract meaningful insights, building dashboards that helped non-technical teams make informed decisions, and writing reports that translated complex findings into clear recommendations. I did this across industries like healthcare, finance, education, and agriculture, so I've learned to adapt my communication style to the audience.\nI also have a product management background from my time with Nsonye Women In Tech, where I ran user interviews, documented requirements, and collaborated with engineering and design teams, which gave me a solid appreciation for how business requirements feed into product development.\nMost recently, I've been part of the Tech4Dev Women Techsters Fellowship, where I led the design and development of HerVestAI, a mobile-first operational intelligence app for food-based SMEs. That project pushed me to think like a business analyst, identifying real user pain points, translating them into functional system requirements, and building solutions with measurable business impact.\nI'm someone who genuinely enjoys understanding how businesses work, finding inefficiencies, and helping teams make better decisions with better information.",https://github.com/techsisada,,69a71dac934396ba8bb60def,Business Analyst Intern,2026-03-12T19:48:24.487Z,2026-03-12T19:48:24.487Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1773344902013_Adae