69b327049292616f7be53119,Winifred Enakeno Taigbenu,+23407017864737,taigbenuw@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am a Quantity Surveying graduate from the University of Benin whose passion for technology and problem-solving led me into the UI/UX design space. Over the past four years, I have built experience designing user-centered digital products across different domains, focusing on creating intuitive interfaces and improving how people interact with technology. I enjoy translating complex ideas into clear, structured experiences through research, wireframing, prototyping, and high-fidelity design. Some of my work includes designing multiple modules for a complex enterprise platform (Orbit ERP), as well as publishing product case studies such as Eventa, a mobile platform designed to simplify how users discover events, purchase tickets, and connect with vendors. Through these experiences, I’ve developed strong product thinking, attention to detail, and the ability to collaborate effectively with cross-functional teams to deliver impactful solutions.\n\nOutside of work, I enjoy relaxing by watching movies—especially law series. I find them particularly fascinating because each episode usually unfolds like a puzzle, and there’s always that moment of satisfaction when the story pieces come together and the real culprit is revealed at the end. It’s a fun reminder of how much I enjoy solving problems and uncovering patterns, whether in storytelling or in design.",https://www.behance.net/winicarsonprofile,,69aefa4c05d00a25722c84c2,Product Designer Intern,2026-03-12T20:50:12.116Z,2026-03-12T20:50:12.116Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1773348608192_WinifredTaigbenu_Resume.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69b327289292616f7be53120,Jonathan Audu Egbe,+23408142419931,egbe.jonathan@yahoo.com,Nigeria,"I am an aspiring Data Analyst with a strong interest in turning data into meaningful insights that support better decision-making. I have experience working with tools such as Excel, SQL, and Power BI to clean, analyze, and visualize data. Through my projects and learning experiences, I have developed skills in data querying, dashboard creation, and data interpretation. I enjoy solving problems with data and identifying patterns that can help organizations improve their performance and strategy. I am particularly interested in learning how data can be used to support business growth and operational efficiency. As a Data Analyst Intern, I am eager to further develop my analytical skills, gain practical industry experience, and contribute positively to a team by supporting data-driven decision-making.\n",https://github.com/Jonathan-Analyst,,69a71dac934396ba8bb60def,Business Analyst Intern,2026-03-12T20:50:48.580Z,2026-03-12T20:50:48.580Z,,,"https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1773348645242_Egbe, Jonathan Audu_CV.pdf",Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69b328209292616f7be53134,Abdullateef Olamilekan Musa,+2348133427055,abdullateefolamilekanmusa@gmail.com,Nigeria,"Dear Hiring Manager, \r\nAs a recent graduate from the University of Ilorin with a Bachelor’s Degree in Industrial \r\nChemistry, I am excited to apply for the open position in your organization. I’m confident that my \r\nskills and experience as a Graduate have prepared me well for this opportunity.\r\nDuring my time as a Graduate, I developed three valuable skills that will be relevant in any team-\r\noriented position. Firstly, I gained experience working on cross-functional teams. This involved \r\ncollaborating with individuals from various departments to ensure that projects were completed \r\naccurately, on time, and within budget. I learned how to communicate effectively and prioritize \r\ntasks in a fast-paced environment. \r\nSecondly, I became skilled in problem-solving. I learnt how to analyze complex data sets and \r\nidentify opportunities for improvement. Furthermore, I honed my skills in critical thinking and \r\nmade strong business recommendations that helped to improve efficiency in the company. \r\nLastly, I became adept at handling multiple projects simultaneously and working under tight \r\ndeadlines. I learnt how to prioritize tasks effectively and manage my time efficiently, ensuring \r\nprompt and quality deliverables. \r\nAs a team player, I am committed to contributing my skills, passion, and energy to a team to \r\nachieve shared goals. I believe that open communication, constructive feedback, and mutual \r\nrespect are the key factors in building a collaborative team-oriented environment.\r\nThank you for considering my application. I look forward to the opportunity to discuss my \r\nqualifications further and to learn more about how I can contribute to your company.\r\nSincerely,\r\nAbdullateef Olamilekan Musa.",https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1T3C8dNcBHrc6JKuUmJV_DpYk1AqXIiRw,,69a71dac934396ba8bb60def,Business Analyst Intern,2026-03-12T20:54:56.047Z,2026-03-12T20:54:56.047Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1773348892599_AbdullateefOlamilekanMusaResume (2).pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
