69b40d82216006717186b391,Victor Wachira Mboche,+254702007733,wachiramboche2@gmail.com,Kenya,"I’ve always believed that the most powerful technology is the kind that feels effortless—where the user never has to see the complex machinery making it all work. I actually started my journey on the front lines, managing systems and networks at the Milimani Law Courts. It was an invaluable place to learn about reliability and the fundamentals of how tech serves people, but I quickly realized I wanted more. I didn't just want to be the one keeping systems running; I wanted to be the one exploring how to build them from the ground up.That curiosity is what led me to Moringa School, where I recently graduated after a deep immersion in backend engineering. To me, development is about the thrill of taking a raw idea and figuring out exactly how to bring it to life through architecture. In projects like VenueVibe, I loved the challenge of building the 'engine'—diving into FastAPI to handle intricate booking logic and securing it with JWT flows.There is a real sense of pride in creating a hidden system that handles massive complexity under the hood just so the user’s experience remains seamless. I’m looking to bring that same curiosity and focus on scalable logic to Tobams Group, where I can help your team build the kind of innovative, AI-driven platforms that empower businesses and individuals alike.",https://portfoliovictor-swart.vercel.app/,,69a7e52c934396ba8bb60df2,Backend Developer Intern,2026-03-13T13:13:38.496Z,2026-03-13T13:13:38.496Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1773407616043_Victor_Wachira_Backend_Intern_Softwaredeveloper.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69b40fb2216006717186b3ba,Victor Wachira Mboche,+254702007733,wachiramboche@gmail.com,Kenya,"I’ve always believed that the most powerful technology is the kind that feels effortless—where the user doesn't have to think about the complex machinery underneath because the interface just guides them through it. I actually started my journey on the front lines, managing systems at the Milimani Law Courts. That role was invaluable because I saw firsthand how even the most powerful software fails if the user finds it frustrating or confusing to use. That realization is what pushed me to transition from maintaining tech to building it.I recently graduated from Moringa School, where I focused on mastering the 'bridge' between logic and the user—the frontend. For me, development is about the thrill of taking a raw idea and figuring out how to bring it to life visually. In projects like VenueVibe, I loved the challenge of using React and Tailwind to build an experience that felt fast and intuitive, ensuring that complex tasks like multi-day bookings felt simple for the user. There is a real sense of pride in crafting a UI that is so clean and responsive that the technology essentially disappears, leaving only a great experience behind.",https://portfoliovictor-swart.vercel.app/,,69a6fe3c934396ba8bb60dec,Frontend Developer Intern,2026-03-13T13:22:58.325Z,2026-03-13T13:22:58.325Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1773408175815_Victor_Wachira_Frontend_Developer_CV.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69b41061216006717186b3ca,Fakehinde Taiwo Iyanuoluwa,+2349039614625,taiwoiyanuoluwa70@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am an aspiring Business Analyst with a strong background in accounting, finance, and data analysis. I recently completed a three-month Business Analysis training with Utiva, where I gained practical knowledge in requirement elicitation, stakeholder analysis, process mapping, and business documentation.\n\nI hold a Second-Class Upper Bachelor’s degree in Accounting from Obafemi Awolowo University and a National Diploma with Distinction from Federal Polytechnic Ede. My academic training developed my analytical thinking and problem-solving skills, which are essential for understanding business needs and translating them into actionable insights.\n\nCurrently, I work as a Tax Associate, where I support tax compliance engagements, analyze financial information, prepare documentation, and collaborate with different stakeholders to ensure accurate reporting and regulatory compliance.\n\nPreviously, I worked as a Fund Accountant at Capital Express Asset & Trust Limited, where I handled NAV computations, prepared investor reports, monitored financial risks, and maintained detailed documentation. I also worked at Workforce Group as a Finance Intern and later a Payroll Specialist, where I processed payroll, handled tax remittances, reconciled invoices, and responded to payroll-related inquiries.\n\nThrough these roles, I developed strong analytical, documentation, and stakeholder communication skills, which are highly relevant to business analysis. I am particularly interested in using data and structured analysis to identify trends, improve processes, and support better business decisions",,,69a71dac934396ba8bb60def,Business Analyst Intern,2026-03-13T13:25:53.474Z,2026-03-13T13:25:53.474Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1773408350469_FAKEHINDE TAIWO IYANUOLUWA CV-Business Analyst.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69b41799216006717186b40e,Esan James,+2348145962596,khingjames7@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I’m James Esan, a UI/UX designer with a background in Linguistics, which helps me understand how people think, communicate, and interact with digital products. I focus on creating simple, user-centered, and visually engaging designs that solve real problems. Trained at Perxels, I combine research, usability, and clean interface design to build experiences that are both functional and enjoyable for users.",https://www.behance.net/gallery/229745645/Student-Savings-App,,69aefa4c05d00a25722c84c2,Product Designer Intern,2026-03-13T13:56:41.924Z,2026-03-13T13:56:41.924Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1773410197959_My Resumeâ¦ James Esan.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
