69b4218befe26dde050507d2,Blessing Laweh,+2348026398077,blessinglaweh@gmail.con,Nigeria,"My name is Blessing Laweh, and I am a Computer Science student at the National Open University of Nigeria with a strong interest in data and business analytics. I enjoy exploring how data can be used to understand business problems, uncover patterns, and support better decision-making.\n\nOver the past few years, I have built practical experience working on data analysis projects during internships and personal projects. \nDuring my time as a Data Analyst intern, I worked on tasks such as SEO data analysis, financial analysis of undervalued companies, predictive analysis using machine learning techniques, and building dashboards to communicate insights. These experiences helped me develop skills in tools like SQL, Power BI, Excel, and Python for exploratory data analysis.\n\nWhat drives me most is my curiosity. I enjoy asking questions about why certain trends occur in data and how businesses can respond strategically. My goal when analyzing data is not just to present numbers, but to translate insights into recommendations that can improve processes, optimize performance, and support business growth.\n\nBeyond technical skills, I value collaboration, communication, and continuous learning. I am always looking for opportunities to deepen my analytical thinking and work on real business problems where data can make a measurable impact. This is why I am particularly excited about the opportunity to contribute and grow in a Business Analyst role.\n\n\n",https://github.com/B612Spac,,69a71dac934396ba8bb60def,Business Analyst Intern,2026-03-13T14:39:07.185Z,2026-03-13T14:39:07.185Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1773412743294_Blessing Laweh CV.docx.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69b422c2efe26dde050507e3,Ugonna Stanley Nwani,+2348124218960,ugonna.nwani@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am a Computer Engineering graduate with a strong interest in data analysis and data science. Over the past few years, I have developed experience working with data to generate insights that support strategic decisions. During my internship as a Data Engineer at TradeDepot, I worked with large datasets, wrote SQL queries, and helped transform raw data into meaningful insights that supported business operations and reporting.\n\nBeyond technical skills, I have also worked on several analytical projects where I analyzed user behavior, growth metrics, and transaction trends. These experiences strengthened my ability to interpret data, communicate insights clearly, and support data-driven decision-making. I enjoy breaking down complex problems, understanding stakeholder needs, and identifying opportunities for improvement.",https://stan-leigh.github.io/ugonna-nwani.github.io,,69a71dac934396ba8bb60def,Business Analyst Intern,2026-03-13T14:44:18.555Z,2026-03-13T14:44:18.555Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1773413055331_Resume.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
