69d0ee6fdba4f810e6375746,Ibrahim Abubakar Opeyemi,+23407078322733,itzjst.ibrahim59@gmail.com,Nigeria,"My name is Ibrahim abubakar, I'm a final-year Electrical and Electronics Engineering student at the Federal University of Technology, Minna, with a strong focus on software engineering and backend architecture. I'd say my engineering background has given me a rigorous foundation in problem solving, system design, and analytical thinking. I have actively applied these skills to build scalable digital solutions. I am currently developing the backend architecture for a campus marketplace application called Sturvs, where I utilize PostgreSQL (Supabase) to manage complex relational data, user authentication, and real time state updates. Beyond web applications, I have experience bridging the physical and digital worlds, having developed an IoT-based flood early warning system. I am a builder who is comfortable working with JavaScript/TypeScript and RESTful APIs, and I am highly adaptable, having recently completed a Design Thinking Bootcamp to ensure the backend solutions I engineer are always user centric and highly practical.",https://github.com/cujo-o,,69ca44f74e5d9fe46aef7611,Backend Developer Intern,2026-04-04T10:56:47.704Z,2026-04-04T10:56:47.704Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1775300204102_Ibrahim Abubakar Opeyemi_cv.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69d11d4fdba4f810e637578e,DAVID OGAH,+2348127683748,davidoogah@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am a graduate of History and International Relations with a strong interest in administration, communication, and development work. I have gained practical experience supporting office operations, managing records, and assisting with communication tasks through roles at the Standards Organisation of Nigeria and MicroBiz Inclusion Center. I am organized, detail-oriented, and able to work effectively in structured environments. I enjoy supporting teams, handling responsibilities with professionalism, and continuously learning to improve my skills. I am also motivated by opportunities that allow me to contribute to meaningful work while growing personally and professionally.",,,69ca45174e5d9fe46aef7612,Business Operations Intern,2026-04-04T14:16:47.159Z,2026-04-04T14:16:47.159Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1775312204325_CV_DAVID_OGAH.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69d126a9dba4f810e63757a2,Sule Hibatullah Ikojo,+2347012310009,hibatullahsule75@gmail.com,Nigeria,"My name is Sule Hibatullah Ikojo, and I am a 300-level student of Environmental Education at the University of Abuja. I am a curious, creative, and detail-oriented individual with a growing passion for product design and a strong desire to create solutions that are both functional and meaningful.\n\nAlthough my academic background is in environmental education, it has shaped the way I think as a designer. It has taught me to approach problems with a systems mindset, consider long-term impact, and design solutions that are user-centered and sustainable. This perspective influences how I approach digital products ensuring they are not only visually appealing but also purposeful and efficient.\n\nMy journey into product design began with an interest in digital creativity and has developed into hands-on experience. I have worked on projects such as designing interfaces for an AI styling application, where I focused on creating clean, intuitive, and engaging user experiences. Through these projects, I have gained practical skills in design thinking, wireframing, and visual communication, while learning how to balance aesthetics with usability.\n\nIn addition, I am actively involved in content creation, where I manage a growing social media presence. This has strengthened my ability to think visually, understand audience behavior, and communicate ideas effectively. It has also helped me stay in tune with modern design trends and storytelling techniques, which are essential in building impactful products.\n\nI am particularly interested in how product design can solve real-life problems and improve everyday experiences. I am eager to learn, open to feedback, and constantly seeking opportunities to grow and refine my skills.\n\nI am excited about the opportunity to intern at Tobams Group because of its commitment to innovation and growth. I am confident that this role will allow me to contribute my creativity while gaining valuable industry experience. I am ready to learn, collaborate, and bring fresh ideas to the team.",https://www.figma.com/design/9Vrd3qivwfBfXGPIYplchd/AI-Styling-Case-Study?node-id=0-1&p=f&t=RoI7pk1rvDUIgu3l-0,,69ca44c94e5d9fe46aef7610,Product Designer Intern,2026-04-04T14:56:41.786Z,2026-04-04T14:56:41.786Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1775314597689_Resume.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
