69d165f1dba4f810e6375812,Onyebuchi Promise,+23409049407852,onyebuchipromise44@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I’m Onyebuchi Promise, a frontend developer passionate about building clean, responsive, and intuitive digital experiences. I specialize in React, JavaScript (ES6+), HTML, CSS, SCSS, Tailwind, and modern UI/UX principles — creating interfaces that are not only visually appealing but highly performant, accessible, and user-focused.\n\nOver the years, I’ve worked on diverse projects that combine creativity with technical depth. I’ve worked on projects that reflect both creativity and technical depth, including:\n\n• WorldWise – A geolocation-based travel tracker built with React. Users can log cities they’ve visited, view them on an interactive map, leave trip notes, track their journeys over time, and enjoy a seamless navigation experience powered by React Router and custom hooks.\n\n• React Weather App – A real-time weather forecasting application where users can search any city and instantly access temperature, humidity, wind speed, and other conditions. Designed with a clean, responsive UI and integrated with a live weather API for accurate results.\n\n• JavaScript Expense Tracker – A fully interactive expense management tool built with vanilla JavaScript. Handles adding, editing, and categorizing expenses, with automatic balance calculations and persistent storage via localStorage.\nBeyond personal projects, I’ve gained professional experience working with teams at Locafy and River Bank Training, building interfaces with React, Tailwind, and CSS Modules while collaborating on real-world development tasks, Git/GitHub versioning, and user-centered feature implementations.\n\nMy approach to development is driven by consistency, discipline, and a deep interest in solving meaningful problems. I believe in writing clean, scalable code and building products that people genuinely enjoy using. Short-term, my goal is to lead impactful software projects, build platforms that educate and empower, and contribute to engineering teams solving real global challenges.\n\nI’m currently open to full-time roles, internships, freelance projects, and collaborative opportunities where I can contribute to building purposeful, high-quality digital products.",https://onyebuchipromise.netlify.app/,,69ca7ab1cc542dfc1db2f6d4,Frontend Developer Intern,2026-04-04T19:26:41.291Z,2026-04-04T19:26:41.291Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1775330798722_ONYEBUCHI_CHUKWUEMERIE_PROMISE (1).pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69d175cadba4f810e6375861,Joy Akpojiyovwi ,+2349010796356,ufomaakpos@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I’m a highly organized and results-driven project and M&E professional with about 3 years of experience supporting health and development programs . I’ve worked in roles ranging from project management to strategy and evaluation, where I coordinate teams, track performance, and ensure projects are delivered on time and within scope.\n\nI have strong skills in data analysis, reporting, and stakeholder engagement, and I’m comfortable using tools like Excel, Trello, Slack, and Smartsheet to improve efficiency and collaboration. I’ve also supported donor-funded programs, conducted field monitoring, and helped strengthen systems for better decision-making.\n\nOverall, I’m passionate about delivering impactful projects, using data to drive results, and contributing to meaningful development work.",,,69ca45174e5d9fe46aef7612,Business Operations Intern,2026-04-04T20:34:18.538Z,2026-04-04T20:34:18.538Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1775334855153_AKPOJIYOVWI UFUOMA JOY CV docx (1).docx,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
