69d2d005dba4f810e6375c01,Sabeeh Ajibade,+23408139589883,detunjinov@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I’m a full-stack web developer with a strong focus on building scalable and user-friendly applications across both web and backend systems. I’ve worked extensively with technologies like React, Next.js, Node.js and Laravel, where I’ve developed responsive interfaces, integrated APIs and implemented secure authentication systems.\n\nIn my recent role at Pintop Technologies, I built and maintained modern web applications using Next.js and Laravel, collaborating closely with designers and product teams to deliver seamless user experiences. I’ve also had the opportunity to lead development efforts and mentor others, particularly during my time as a Lead Full-Stack Instructor, where I taught and guided developers in modern web technologies including React.\n\nWhile my background is full-stack, I’m particularly passionate about frontend development, crafting intuitive, high-performance user interfaces and continuously improving user experience. I’ve also built several personal and production projects that involve React and modern frontend practices.\n\nI’m excited about this internship because it gives me the opportunity to deepen my expertise in React and Next.js, contribute to impactful products and grow within a collaborative engineering environment.",sabeeh-ajibade.vercel.app,,69ca7ab1cc542dfc1db2f6d4,Frontend Developer Intern,2026-04-05T21:11:33.949Z,2026-04-05T21:11:33.949Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1775423484143_Sabeeh_Ajibade_Laravel_Next_.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69d2e59edba4f810e6375c35,Tajudeen Maryam Oyenike,+23407061048054,tajudeenmaryam09@gmail.com,Nigeria,"My name is Tajudeen Maryam Oyenike, a first class Graduate of Agriculture from the University of Ilorin.\nI have gained about 3 years of practical experience solving real life business problems through data-driven decision making.\nI am proficient in the use of Microsoft office Applications, Google workspace, SQL and Tableau to clean, analyze and visualize data sets.\nThereafter, I uncover insights from my analyses and make recommendations for businesses through my data-driven approach.\nIn my most recent job role, I cleaned , analyzed and visualized the inventory sales data of some products, and proceeded to perform a product-profitability analysis on them.\nThrough my analysis, I was able to uncover a case of funds mismanagement by the employee charged with the responsibility of the record-keeping.\nThis was the reason why the products that generated higher revenues, has negative profit/profit margins.\nThen, my recommendations from the analysis generated about 15% increase in profitability from the following month.\nThis paved way for me to be selected as the Lead Data Analyst for the Abia state Enumeration Project in the Eastern part of Nigeria.\nHere, I cleaned, analyzed and visualized about 50,000 datasets using Koboltoolbox , TrackOS, and Tableau .\nThis enabled us to identity the active farmers and eradicated the ""paper farmers"" for effective resources allocation by the government.\nIt also helped solved the problem of food insecurity and hike in prices of food produce.\n\nAside from the technical aspect of being a data Analyst, soft skills like Paying attention to details, problem solving, Team collaboration and Effective communication gives me an edge above my peers and position me to contribute much better to the growth of any organization I find myself.",https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1EyN3Y-yodWFXFRQwtaeA_B_Vu0P8Bllc,,69ca45374e5d9fe46aef7613,B