69d3e67cdba4f810e6376529,Monicah Munyua,+2340717192945,monicahwamuhu2@gmail.com,Kenya,"I just graduated with a degree in software engineering from the Multimedia University of Kenya. During my uni life, I was very active in community building as I looked for a sense of belonging, especially in the tech world. I did see it through to a point where I took up a leadership role as a technical editor for our university tech club. I went ahead to co-found a women in STEM community called Geek-ssters where we support women in tech by hosting webinars and in-person events, and the team has garnered over 150 women thus far. This has been a learning experience, and it still is as I go on.",https://monicahwamuhu2.github.io/Portfolio/,,69ca44f74e5d9fe46aef7611,Backend Developer Intern,2026-04-06T16:59:40.277Z,2026-04-06T16:59:40.277Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1775494776484_Monicah Wamuhu CV.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69d3e6abdba4f810e6376533,Akinrinlola Ayoola Joy,+2348038365558,castrol2031@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am a detail-oriented Business Analyst with a strong background in Computer Science and extensive experience translating business needs into effective digital solutions. My journey in tech began as an Oracle Database Administrator, which built my foundation in data analysis and system thinking.\n\nAt Almond Careers, I played a key role in driving business analysis activities by working closely with stakeholders to gather, analyze, and document requirements. I facilitated requirement elicitation sessions, developed clear Business Requirement Documents (BRDs) and Functional Requirement Documents (FRDs), and ensured alignment between business objectives and technical delivery. I also collaborated with cross-functional teams to define user stories, acceptance criteria, and process flows, helping to streamline development and improve product outcomes.\n\nIn addition, I supported testing and validation processes by ensuring solutions met business expectations and user needs. My approach is highly analytical and user-focused, and I am passionate about identifying gaps, optimizing processes, and delivering value-driven solutions.\n\nI am particularly interested in this role because it provides an opportunity to leverage my business analysis expertise, stakeholder management skills, and passion for continuous improvement to contribute to impactful projects and organizational growth.\n\n",https://www.linkedin.com/in/castrol-ayo-b25042a7/,,69ca45374e5d9fe46aef7613,Business Analyst Intern,2026-04-06T17:00:27.525Z,2026-04-06T17:00:27.525Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1775494824574_Akinrinlola Ayoola CV.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69d3e878dba4f810e6376568,Akinniyi Osoro,+2348137548227,akinniyiosoroo@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am a highly organized administrative professional with over six years of experience in leadership and operational coordination. My background is rooted in managing complex environments—most recently as an Associate in Instructional Design at NewGlobe and previously as a Vice Principal and Head of School. \n\nThroughout my career, I’ve specialized in streamlining processes, managing high-level calendars, and using data to drive decision-making. For instance, I’ve moved from direct school leadership, where I oversaw staff and regulatory compliance, to more technical roles involving data reporting and stakeholder engagement. I’m a Graduate of the McKinsey Forward Program and have certifications in Data Analysis and Accounting, which allow me to bring a very analytical, detail-oriented approach to administrative tasks. I pride myself on being a proactive problem solver who can handle sensitive information with total discretion.",https://linkedin.com/in/akinniyi-osoro,,69ca45174e5d9fe46aef7612,Business Operations Intern,2026-04-06T17:08:08.216Z,2026-04-06T17:08:08.216Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1775495284131_Akinniyi O. Osoro.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69d3ea61dba4f810e637659c,Amadi,+23408144296476,miracleama17@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am a software engineer with a strong focus on backend development, passionate about building scalable, secure, and efficient systems. I have hands-on experience designing and developing APIs, managing server-side logic, and ensuring seamless communication between applications.\n\nI work with technologies in the JavaScript ecosystem, including Node.js, Express, and TypeScript, and I have experience with databases such as PostgreSQL, MySQL, and MongoDB. I also use Prisma ORM to efficiently manage and interact with relational databases, ensuring clean and maintainable data models.\n\nI enjoy designing robust system architectures, optimizing performance, and implementing best practices for security and reliability. Beyond development, I have experience mentoring and teaching, which has strengthened my problem-solving, communication, and collaboration skills.\n\nI am continuously learning and improving my backend expertise, with a strong interest in system design, cybersecurity, and building production-level applications that solve real-world problems.",https://github.com/Processor663,,69ca44f74e5d9fe46aef7611,Backend Developer Intern,2026-04-06T17:16:17.492Z,2026-04-06T17:16:17.492Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1775495774412_Amadi-Miracle-Resume-Backend.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69d3eb54dba4f810e63765bd,Abdulazeez Otu,+23407036989924,abdulazeez.oe@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am a result-oriented field professional with strong expertise in Immunization, program planning and management, monitoring and evaluation, community engagement and mobilization in health programs. I have supported 24+ development and public health projects across spanning over 8 years, with experience in coordination, training, supervision, data systems and large-scale program implementation. I have a proven ability to organise and manage large teams effectively, ensuring high performance, accountability, and timely achievement of goals. I am deeply committed to promoting community participation and encouraging community ownership of health interventions to ensure sustainability and lasting impact. My skills in data management, data analysis, and strategic reporting enables me to transform information into actionable insights that drive informed decision-making. Expert in Power BI, Google Workspace, DHIS, ODK, Kobo Toolbox and Microsoft Office Tools, I possess strong facilitation and interpersonal communication skills, MEAL, application troubleshooting skills, with great comfort using digital tools for data validation and visualization. Experience in banking and finance, I bring analytical thinking, attention to detail, and result-driven focus to every task. Self-motivated, transparent and passionate about excellence, I continuously seek opportunities to learn, adapt, and contribute meaningfully to organizations that value teamwork, innovation, and measurable impact.",,,69ca45174e5d9fe46aef7612,Business Operations Intern,2026-04-06T17:20:20.184Z,2026-04-06T17:20:20.184Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1775496015430_Abdulazeez Otu_CurriVitae(2).pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69d3eb9edba4f810e63765d7,Obiorah Gloria Ijeoma,+2349066032252,glo.obiorah@gmail.com,Nigeria,"Hi, I'm Gloria, I'm currently in my third year studying Math and Computer Science at Covenant University, and I'm a backend software engineer. I spend a lot of my time working with JavaScript and TypeScript to build systems that actually scale. Recently, I was a software engineer at Dila, where my main focus was integrating VFD and Paystack APIs. I'm also really big on building my own projects to challenge myself. For example, I built a real-time crypto converter, the backend for a poultry farm e-commerce platform, and I recently competed in the Heirs Insurance Hackathon and the Enyata X Interswitch Hackathon. I really enjoy solving complex logic problems and bringing ideas to life, but when I'm not writing code, you can usually find me trying to improve my chess game or just watching cartoons to unwind.",https://gloriaobiorah.vercel.app/,,69ca44f74e5d9fe46aef7611,Backend Developer Intern,2026-04-06T17:21:34.823Z,2026-04-06T17:21:34.823Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1775496091655_Obiorah_Gloria_CV.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69d3ec2cdba4f810e63765e8,Peter Oyishoma,+23408164804155,oyishomapeter@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am a tech enthusiast with a background in frontend web development and cybersecurity, and I enjoy building things that are both useful and secure. I studied cybersecurity at FUTMINNA, Nigeria, which gave me a solid foundation, but most of my growth has come from hands-on learning, projects, and continuous self-improvement.\n\nRight now, I am focusing on backend development to complete my skill set and become a more well-rounded engineer. I am particularly interested in learning how systems work behind the scenes, how data flows, how APIs are designed, and how to build scalable and secure applications.",https://github.com/oyishomapeter-tech,,69ca44f74e5d9fe46aef7611,Backend Developer Intern,2026-04-06T17:23:56.130Z,2026-04-06T17:23:56.130Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1775496233324_PETER_OYISHOMA_CV (1).pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69d3ed17dba4f810e63765f4,Matilda Wanjiru Njau,+254782909566,njaumatildawanjiru@gmail.com,Kenya,"I’ve always been drawn to the 'invisible' that makes an application reliable. \n\nOne thing that defines me as a developer is that I’m a 'loud learner.' In my current internship, I'm the person always asking, 'Why are we doing it this way?' because I believe good software is a team sport. I don’t just want to write code that works; I want to understand the reasoning behind the design.\n\nI’m the kind of developer who spends as much time thinking about how a system might fail as I do about making it work—which is why I genuinely enjoy code reviews and technical brainstorming; I believe that’s where the best, most resilient architecture is born. Ultimately, I’m looking for a role where I can contribute to high-quality codebases while continuing to grow my skills alongside experienced engineers. ",https://github.com/njaumatilda,,69ca44f74e5d9fe46aef7611,Backend Developer Intern,2026-04-06T17:27:51.215Z,2026-04-06T17:27:51.215Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1775496467348_MatildaNjau_BackEndDev Resume.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69d3ee10dba4f810e6376605,Uchenna Nduka,+2348145676785,uchenna8800@gmail.com,Nigeria,"My name is Uchenna Nduka, and I am a data analyst with hands-on experience analyzing procurement, supply chain, and operational data to support data-driven business decisions. During my internship at VURIN Limited, I developed Excel-based tracking systems, built KPI dashboards, and designed a vendor risk scoring model that improved procurement visibility, supplier evaluation, and cost efficiency.\nI have experience translating business and operational requirements into structured analytical solutions, including performance tracking systems and process optimization initiatives. I enjoy working at the intersection of data and business operations, and I am particularly interested in roles that combine data analysis, process improvement, and business problem-solving.",https://uchenna225.github.io/uchenna.io/,,69ca45374e5d9fe46aef7613,Business Analyst Intern,2026-04-06T17:32:00.428Z,2026-04-06T17:32:00.428Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1775496717597_Uchenna_Nduka_Data_and_Operational_Analyst.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69d3eeb7dba4f810e6376617,Tito Akinyemi,+2348163896110,ti.to.aj.bi@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am a Computer Science student and data analyst with experience in Python, SQL, and data visualization, focused on transforming data into actionable insights. I have worked on projects involving data analysis and system development, and I am particularly interested in building data-driven solutions that improve efficiency, optimization, and decision-making at scale.",,,69ca45374e5d9fe46aef7613,Business Analyst Intern,2026-04-06T17:34:47.648Z,2026-04-06T17:34:47.648Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1775496884556_AkinyemiTito_Resume.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69d3f97ddba4f810e6376653,Ohuchukwu Princewill Chinonyerem,+2348100662390,princewill9711@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I’m a full stack developer with about three years of experience, with a stronger focus on backend development. I work mainly with Node.js and TypeScript, building APIs, handling authentication, and designing scalable services, while also using React and Next.js on the frontend when needed.\n\nI’ve built and shipped real world projects, including a SaaS platform and a developer tool called Hookdropi. I’m now looking to grow in a team environment where I can deepen my backend skills and contribute to real systems.\n\n\nI’ve also been exploring backend architecture and best practices around performance and scalability through my projects. I’m really interested in this role because it gives me the opportunity to gain real world experience, grow as a backend engineer, and contribute to a professional team.\n",github.com/bobprince4u,,69ca44f74e5d9fe46aef7611,Backend Developer Intern,2026-04-06T18:20:45.092Z,2026-04-06T18:20:45.092Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1775499642456_Princewill_Ohuchukwu_Resume (3).pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69d3fcdbdba4f810e6376671,Enobakhare Efe ,+2347062370106,enobakharerichie@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I’m an electrical engineer with over four years of experience in fullstack development, with a strong focus on backend engineering and building scalable web applications. Over time, I’ve transitioned deeply into backend development, working primarily with the MERN stack, while also leveraging technologies like PHP and MySQL for building and managing server-side applications and relational databases.\n\nI have hands on experience designing RESTful APIs, handling authentication and authorization, and managing application state efficiently using tools like Redux. I’ve built real-world applications involving cart systems, secure payment integrations, and robust backend validation, ensuring data consistency between the frontend and backend.\n\nIn addition, I have experience working with DevOps tools such as Docker and Jenkins, which I’ve used for containerization and setting up CI/CD pipelines to streamline development and deployment processes.\n\nI’m particularly passionate about backend development because I enjoy working on the core logic, data flow, and system architecture that power applications. I’m continuously improving my skills.\n\nWhat sets me apart is my strong analytical thinking, attention to detail, and ability to quickly adapt to new technologies skills I’ve developed through both my engineering background and my professional experience.\n\n",https://aesthetics-uidesign.onrender.com/,,69ca44f74e5d9fe46aef7611,Backend Developer Intern,2026-04-06T18:35:07.989Z,2026-04-06T18:35:07.989Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1775500504854_Enobakhare_Efe_CV (1a).pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69d3fe89dba4f810e6376680,Enaibre Oghenetega Emmanuel ,+2348123270441,emmaenaibre@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am a Software Engineer with a focus on backend development and a recent Bachelor of Engineering  graduate in Electronics and Computer Engineering from the University of Port Harcourt. My expertise lies in the MERN stack specifically building RESTful APIs using Node.js, Express and MongoDB. I have hands-on experience developing full-stack applications like 'Ndigo Travels' and managing complex database systems. Additionally, I have a background in professional engineering environments from my time at Chevron, where I applied Agile/SCRUM methodologies to deliver technical projects.",github.com/Emmlass,,69ca44f74e5d9fe46aef7611,Backend Developer Intern,2026-04-06T18:42:17.541Z,2026-04-06T18:42:17.541Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1775500934659_Enaibre Resume Back End (4).pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69d40141dba4f810e637668e,odili triumph ifeatu,+23409067397822,odilitriumph9@gmail.com,Nigeria,"My interest in tech began in secondary school, where I joined a small group called Code Academy, founded by my computer teacher. There, I learned the fundamentals of web development — HTML, CSS, and JavaScript — and fell in love with the idea of building the same kind of websites I used every day.\nWhen it was time for university, my dad suggested Software Engineering. After doing my own research, I confirmed it was the right fit and enrolled at Babcock University, where I'm currently in my third year.\nNot wanting to be just another student chasing grades, I sought real-world growth. My sister connected me with a tech professional with nearly seven years of industry experience, who became my mentor. Through structured sessions — course recommendations, assignments, code reviews, and pull request feedback — I found my focus: backend engineering.\nUniversity projects exposed me to a wide range of stacks — frontend, full-stack, mobile, and backend — giving me versatility as a developer. Beyond academics, I've worked with startups, completed an internship, and am currently working alongside my mentor at his startup as a software engineer.\nI'm a feedback-oriented developer. Constructive criticism and progress tracking are core to how I grow — both technically and personally. I'm actively seeking new opportunities to continue developing as a student and software engineer.",https://www.artfolio.tech/odili_triumph_ifeatu,,69ca44f74e5d9fe46aef7611,Backend Developer Intern,2026-04-06T18:53:53.517Z,2026-04-06T18:53:53.517Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1775501630667_TRIUMPH'S CV (2).pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
