69d503ed081e2389a92dd82d,Abdulmuiz Busari ,+447448128653,Abdulmuizbusari797@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am currently a Master’s student in Data Science and Analytics at the University of Hertfordshire, having graduated in 2023 with a BSc in Computer Science from Afe Babalola University, Ado-Ekiti.\n\nI am proficient in programming languages such as Python, R, Java, and SQL, and I enjoy using these tools to analyse data and solve real-world problems. I consider myself an analytical thinker with strong attention to detail, particularly when working with data and identifying patterns that can drive better decision-making.\n\nMy experience spans both the agricultural and supply chain sectors. I worked as a Stock Manager at TASOMOB Ventures, where I helped improve inventory tracking and data accuracy, and during my NYSC, I worked in the logistics department at Nigerian Breweries, focusing on data analysis to support operational efficiency.\n\nThrough these experiences, I have developed a strong interest in roles that sit at the intersection of data science, data engineering, and business analysis, where I can not only work with data but also contribute to strategic decision-making and real-world impact. The main idea is to create value in Nigeria that would have real impact on people in and outside Nigeria. \n",,,69ca45374e5d9fe46aef7613,Business Analyst Intern,2026-04-07T13:17:33.841Z,2026-04-07T13:17:33.841Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1775567851362_Tobams_Cv.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69d5132c081e2389a92dd8c9,James Olalowo,+23408068335872,jamessy247@gmail.com,Nigeria,"My name is James Olalowo, and I have a strong interest in data analysis, business analysis, and technology-driven education solutions.\n\nMy background includes developing digital learning projects and educational programs, where I design technology-based learning experiences for students. Through this work, I have gained experience in problem solving, project development, and analyzing learning processes to improve outcomes.\n\nRecently, I have been expanding my skills in data analytics and business analysis, working with tools such as SQL, Python, and data visualization tools to analyze data, identify trends, and generate insights that support better decision-making.\n\nWhat excites me most is using data and technology to improve education systems, which aligns strongly with Tobams Group’s Recycled Learning initiative that integrates books, digital platforms, and AI-driven learning solutions for children.\n\nI am eager to contribute my analytical mindset, curiosity, and commitment to learning while gaining hands-on experience in business analysis and supporting projects that create real educational impact",https://james-olalowo-portfolio.netlify.app/,,69ca45374e5d9fe46aef7613,Business Analyst Intern,2026-04-07T14:22:36.708Z,2026-04-07T14:22:36.708Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1775571753890_Data Analyst Cv â James Olalowo.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
