69d51c12081e2389a92dd971,Promise Faith Emmanuel,+23409051762381,thepromiseemmanuel@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am a Business Administration graduate with hands-on experience in administrative support and customer operations. In my role as an Administrative Assistant at Island City Sports Ltd., I supported day-to-day operations by managing documentation, coordinating schedules, and following up on tasks to ensure timely execution. I also worked closely with different stakeholders, which strengthened my communication and organizational skills.\n\nBefore that, I worked in Customer Support, where I handled a high volume of inquiries, resolved issues, and identified patterns that could improve processes. These experiences helped me develop strong attention to detail and the ability to manage multiple priorities effectively.\n\nI have also completed training in Project Management, HR, and Virtual Assistance, which has given me a solid foundation in task tracking, recruitment processes, and remote collaboration. I am particularly interested in business operations because I enjoy supporting systems, improving workflows, and helping teams stay aligned and productive.\n\nI am now looking for an opportunity where I can contribute, continue learning, and grow in a fast-paced, structured environment.\n",,,69ca45174e5d9fe46aef7612,Business Operations Intern,2026-04-07T15:00:34.738Z,2026-04-07T15:00:34.738Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1775574031543_Promise Emmanuel - Business Operations Intern CV.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69d52a79081e2389a92dd9ea,Fathiat Abimbola  Odutayo ,+2348089684723,fathiat477odutayo@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I’m a recent Computer Science graduate with a strong interest in frontend development and data-driven problem solving. Through both my academic journey and personal projects, I’ve developed hands-on experience using technologies like React, Next.js, and Tailwind CSS to create user-centered applications.\nOne thing that stands out about me is that I learn more by building. Working on applications to solve real word problems like a job listing platform and a payroll all has taught me how to approach development from a user’s perspective, understanding their needs, simplifying interactions, and creating intuitive experiences.\nI also have a background in data analytics, which helps me think beyond just the interface. I tend to ask questions like “How will users interact with this?” and “What insights can we get from their behavior?” That combination of frontend development and analytical thinking is something I bring into my work.\nOverall, I’m someone who is curious, adaptable, and genuinely motivated to grow. I’m especially interested in opportunities where I can contribute to meaningful products, learn from experienced teams, and continue improving both my technical and problem-solving skills.\n",https://fathiat-portfolio.vercel.app/,,69ca7ab1cc542dfc1db2f6d4,Frontend Developer Intern,2026-04-07T16:02:01.626Z,2026-04-07T16:02:01.626Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1775577718729_Fathiat Abimbola Odutayo CV.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
