69d68bd4d9126eb277a789ff,Paulinus Michael Praise,+23407060797529,leahcimpraise@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am Paulinus Michael Praise, and I am Creative Designer, I am skilled in tools such as Adobe Photoshop, Illustrator, and Canva, Adobe Premiere pro and I have experience creating brand identities, social media designs, and marketing materials.\nI help brands reach their potential audience and increase sales performance.\n",https://www.instagram.com/mpp_designs?igsh=cXM0cHg2cDV2aXVu,,69ca456d4e5d9fe46aef7614,Graphic Design Intern,2026-04-08T17:09:40.639Z,2026-04-08T17:09:40.639Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1775668177806_Paulinus Michael Praise CV. _20260406_133021_0000.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69d68cb3d9126eb277a78a26,Khadijah Adeyinka Lawal,+23408147663860,lawalkhadijahh@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am a product designer with over two years of hands-on experience creating user centered digital experiences. My work focuses on translating complex ideas into intuitive, functional, and visually engaging solutions. I have developed strong skills in user research, wireframing, prototyping, and usability testing, and I enjoy collaborating with cross-functional teams to bring ideas to life.\nThroughout my experience, I have worked on a variety of projects that strengthened my ability to think critically and design with both users and business goals in mind. I am particularly passionate about solving real-world problems and continuously improving my design process through feedback and iteration. My approach combines creativity with a strong attention to detail, ensuring that every product I work on delivers value and a seamless user experience.\nI am excited about the opportunity to join Tobams Group as a product design intern, where I can contribute my skills, learn from experienced professionals, and grow within a dynamic and innovative environment.",http://behance.net/khadijahlawal1,,69ca44c94e5d9fe46aef7610,Product Designer Intern,2026-04-08T17:13:23.456Z,2026-04-08T17:13:23.456Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1775668399031_Lawal Khadijah A..docx,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69d68d99d9126eb277a78a38,Praise Bamidele,+2348165401657,praisebamidele2004@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am a highly motivated and analytical individual with a strong interest in business analysis and data-driven decision making.... I enjoy breaking down complex problems, identifying trends, and developing practical solutions that improve business performance.\n\nI have developed strong skills in data analysis, critical thinking, and problem-solving, with hands-on experience using tools such as Microsoft Excel, Python, and basic data visualization techniques to organize and interpret data effectively with two years experience I am also skilled at communicating insights clearly and working collaboratively to support informed business decisions.\n\n",https://www.linkedin.com/in/ene-praise-bamidele-2865833b4?utm_source=share&utm_campaign=share_via&utm_content=profile&utm_medium=android_app,,69ca45374e5d9fe46aef7613,Business Analyst Intern,2026-04-08T17:17:13.659Z,2026-04-08T17:17:13.659Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1775668630672_IMG_20260408_174412.jpg,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69d68f3ed9126eb277a78a54,Nnamdi Atu,+2347030850814,atunnamdi77@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am a Chartered Accountant with a strong interest in business analysis and using data to support decision-making. I have experience working with tools like Power BI, SQL, and Excel to analyze data and generate insights that help businesses understand performance and improve processes. Through my projects and professional experience, I have developed strong analytical and problem-solving skills. I am now looking to gain more hands-on experience in a Business Analyst role where I can continue learning and contribute to solving real business problems.",sites.google.com/view/nnamdi-atu-portfolio/,,69ca45374e5d9fe46aef7613,Business Analyst Intern,2026-04-08T17:24:14.209Z,2026-04-08T17:24:14.209Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1775669051349_Business Analyst-Nnamdi Atu-Cv.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69d692b1d9126eb277a78a9c,Funto Tosin Dada,+2349037203266,princessderin288@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am Funto Tosin Dada, an aspiring Product Designer with a background in Biochemistry and a strong interest in creating intuitive digital experiences. I recently completed a Product Design certification with Tech4Dev and am currently learning more with TS Academy. I enjoy practicing user centered design, creating wireframes, and building simple prototypes using Figma and FigJam. I am eager to gain hands-on experience, collaborate with experienced designers, and contribute to meaningful projects while continuing to grow my skills in product design.",https://www.figma.com/make/GmXO8GuTygX02q29LDU8cT/Contest-Registration-Sign-Up?t=9pTyyL4GitQC9RLy-1,,69ca44c94e5d9fe46aef7610,Product Designer Intern,2026-04-08T17:38:57.201Z,2026-04-08T17:38:57.201Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1775669931616_FUNTO TOSIN DADA product design CV.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69d69485d9126eb277a78ab3,Mgboh Ejiofor Fredrick,+2348059931642,mgbohfrederick@gmail.com,Nigeria,"Anytime I have the opportunity to talk about myself, I feel like there is not much thing to describe myself but I just have to admit curiosity shaped my path early but my decisions were a failure through university and after school. I studied Electronics Engineering, and in my final year I specialized in software engineering which had an abstract look in life in technology, with different looks on it I focused on Requirement Engineering, which is the foundation of engineering, without it Engineers would not achieve any success. I learned how to translate user needs into clear system requirements and how to guide development with structure and precision. This led me into programming, where I worked on building solutions with defined goals and measurable output. I also dived into data science, driven by my interest in prediction and the value of using data to anticipate outcomes. I focused on understanding patterns, building models, and applying logic to real situations.\nDuring the time ideas bubbling in me, I joined a startup where I applied these skills in a practical setting. I helped refine ideas into clear features and assigned roles based on each person’s strengths. I ensured each team member understood their responsibility and how their work contributed to the overall goal. I focused on clarity, execution, and alignment across the team. The startup failed due to separate ideas, but the experience gave me direct insight into decision making. I saw how weak requirement definition leads to confusion, how poor role allocation slows progress, and how strong coordination improves results. I apply these lessons in my work, with clear thinking, structured execution, and a focus on outcomes.\nAfter completing NYSC, the next phase felt uncertain. Opportunities are few, and talent is widespread. With limited skills, opportunities drop to zero. This pushed me to keep learning and improving. I chose to build up my skills and be multilingual in life to achieve greatness and avoid peer pressure, while focusing on the greater goal because the future is always bright.",https://datafolio-gamma.vercel.app/,,69ca45374e5d9fe46aef7613,Business Analyst Intern,2026-04-08T17:46:45.289Z,2026-04-08T17:46:45.289Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1775670402118_MGBOH EJIOFOR FREDRICK_CV.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69d69994d9126eb277a78ad9,Anawo Ngbede Michael,+2348148034290,michanawo@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I’m a Product Designer who believes design should simplify complexity and feel human at every touchpoint. I’ve worked across fintech, mobility, real estate, health, and lifestyle, shaping my understanding of trust, emotion, and usability. I’m a Computer Science graduate, and my design journey began shortly after i graduated. What started as a love for visuals grew into a passion for user experience and problem-solving. Outside of work, I’m a big anime and football fan, and I also enjoy movies, reading, and staying curious. Each part of my life keeps me grounded in empathy and exploration as a designer.",https://www.figma.com/proto/rgmNluGwgGaF92jcThFvzL/My-portfolio?node-id=89-7376&p=f&viewport=1232%2C275%2C0.1&t=lIPpNgtFe4WxRkLR-1&scaling=scale-down&content-scaling=fixed&starting-point-node-id=346%3A13102&show-proto-sidebar=1&page-id=0%3A3,,69ca44c94e5d9fe46aef7610,Product Designer Intern,2026-04-08T18:08:20.194Z,2026-04-08T18:08:20.194Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1775671696808_Anawo Ngbede Michael^.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69d69badd9126eb277a78af8,Akinfesola Evangel,+2348038402152,evon12ea@gmail.com,Nigeria,"Dear Hiring Manager,\n\nI am writing to express my interest in the Product Designer Intern position. I am currently transitioning into Product (UI/UX) Design and have been developing my skills through hands-on projects using tools such as Figma.\n\nI am particularly excited about this opportunity because of your focus on user-centered design and innovation. I enjoy solving real user problems and creating intuitive, visually engaging interfaces that improve user experiences.\n\nThrough my recent projects, I have worked on wire-framing, prototyping, and applying design thinking principles to create user-focused solutions. I am eager to contribute to your team, learn from experienced designers, and grow within a collaborative environment.\n\nThank you for considering my application. I would love the opportunity to further discuss how I can contribute to your team.\n\nKind regards,\nEvangel Akinfesola",https/www.behance.net/evangelakinfes,,69ca44c94e5d9fe46aef7610,Product Designer Intern,2026-04-08T18:17:17.760Z,2026-04-08T18:17:17.760Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1775672232563_PRODUCT DESIGNER cv.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69d69c1fd9126eb277a78b03,Ekekwe Daniel Promise ,+2348021358937,danielpromise1234@gmail.com,Nigeria,"My name is Ekekwe Daniel Promise, and I’m based in Lagos, Nigeria. \n\nI’m a passionate and creative graphic designer with hands-on experience in creating visual content, especially for church media and digital platforms.\n\n I’ve worked on various projects like flyers, social media designs, and event banners, using tools like Adobe Photoshop, Illustrator, and Canva.\n\nAn interesting fact about me is that I’ve always been curious and self-taught—I started designing just by exploring my parents’ phone and browsing design tools online. That curiosity still drives my growth today",https://drive.google.com/file/d/1-LKcxIJPnWXkSCh90lM9otkCSohgeX94/view?usp=drivesdk,,69ca456d4e5d9fe46aef7614,Graphic Design Intern,2026-04-08T18:19:11.937Z,2026-04-08T18:19:11.937Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1775672347545_Edited CV(Ekekwe Daniel Promise).pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
