69d804bb6469458c6f92034f,Onyebuchi Genius OKONKWO,+23408100738389,okonkwoonyebu@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am a Public Health professional and National Health Fellow who has spent the last year translating complex grassroots data into visual stories. \n\n\nMy work has ranged from designing community health awareness materials to creating technical reports for state-level stakeholders. \n\n\nI am a versatile creative who has handled diverse projects—from institutional branding for academies to social advocacy graphics. \n\n\nI am now transitioning into professional design, eager to apply my unique background in Visual Narrative to a global innovation setting.",https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1nDWo2FbqLd4BgqZJGAN1fS9g_aMQe6fI,,69ca456d4e5d9fe46aef7614,Graphic Design Intern,2026-04-09T19:57:47.681Z,2026-04-09T19:57:47.681Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1775764664402_Onyebuchi_Okonkwo_GraphicDesign_CV.docx,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69d805f66469458c6f920366,Victor Okoukoni,+2348060277430,victorokoukoni@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I'm a frontend developer based in Lagos, primarily working with React.js, JavaScript, and TypeScript. I've had a couple of roles where I got to contribute to real projects — working with React, TypeScript, Bootstrap, and Alpine.js across different teams — so I have a decent foundation, but I'm still very much in the learning phase of my career.\nI have a reasonable grasp of frontend development for the web, and I'm still actively looking to deepen that — learning industry best practices, writing better code, and getting sharper overall. But mobile is the missing piece for me. Getting proper exposure to React Native alongside that would kind of complete the picture — being able to build for both web and mobile means I can offer more complete solutions and ultimately make more of an impact, rather than being limited to just one side of the stack.\nI'm comfortable with things like responsive design, working with APIs, version control, and component architecture — but I know there's still a lot of ground left to cover. I learn well in structured environments where I can contribute meaningfully while also picking things up from people who've been doing this longer than I have.\nOutside of the technical side, I tend to be organised, communicative, and I take feedback well — which I think matters just as much at this stage.",https://victorokoukoni.vercel.app/,,69ca7ab1cc542dfc1db2f6d4,Frontend Developer Intern,2026-04-09T20:03:02.491Z,2026-04-09T20:03:02.491Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1775764979355_Victor_Okoukoni_CV.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
