69d806b46469458c6f920385,Ebisi Chekwubechukwu Solomon,+2349068972576,chekwubeebisi@gmail.com,Nigeria,"My name is Ebisi ChekwubechukwuSolomon. I am a motivated and hardworking professional with experience in project management, graphics design, and printing services. I also have a strong academic background in Geology, BSC level.\nOver the years, I have developed skills in organization, problem-solving, teamwork, and managing projects effectively. As the founder of Sustainable Community and a manager in a printing and publishing company, I have gained valuable experience in leadership, communication, and delivering quality results.\nI am passionate about learning, contributing positively to organizations, and using my skills to create value. I am particularly interested in opportunities that allow me to grow professionally while making meaningful contributions to the success of the organization.",https://www.behance.net/nostycorpora,,69ca456d4e5d9fe46aef7614,Graphic Design Intern,2026-04-09T20:06:12.853Z,2026-04-09T20:06:12.853Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1775765168976_IMG_20260311_124007.jpg,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69d810496469458c6f92048d,Osinusi Ayodeji Okiki,+2348116374393,ayodejiokiki2@gmail.com,Nigeria,"My name is Ayodeji Osinusi, a data analyst based in Lagos with a strong foundation in data analytics and a genuine passion for using data to support meaningful decisions. I have hands-on experience working with real-world datasets, which has helped me develop both my technical skills and my ability to translate data findings into clear, actionable insights.\nMy core strengths include data analysis, reporting, and visualization — with particular proficiency in Power BI, where I build dashboards and reports that tell coherent business stories. I also have developing skills in SQL and Python, and I am continuously expanding my analytical toolkit.\nBeyond technical skills, I value clear communication and structured thinking. I believe good analysis is only as useful as how well it is understood by the people it is meant to serve — and that belief shapes how I approach every project I work on.\nI am drawn to the Business Analyst internship at Tobams Group because of the Recycled Learning initiative. The idea of leveraging technology and data to close educational gaps for young learners is something I find genuinely exciting, and I would love the opportunity to contribute to that mission while growing under experienced mentorship.",https://github.com/OsinusiAyodeji,,69ca45374e5d9fe46aef7613,Business Analyst Intern,2026-04-09T20:47:05.184Z,2026-04-09T20:47:05.184Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1775767621657_Ayodeji Osinusi CV.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69d813236469458c6f9204b4,Olaoye Matthew ,+2348151066241,olaoyematthewabiodun20@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I’m a mathematics graduate with a strong interest in backend development and problem-solving. Over time, I’ve transitioned into tech, where I focus on building server-side applications and understanding how systems work behind the scenes.\n\nI have experience working with JavaScript, especially Node.js, and I’ve built projects involving APIs, data handling, and basic authentication systems. I enjoy writing clean, efficient code and breaking down complex problems into simple solutions.\n\nBeyond coding, I’m someone who is curious and always learning. I’ve been improving my skills by building projects, practicing algorithms, and exploring how real-world applications are structured.\n\nI’m applying for this backend internship because I want to gain hands-on experience, work with a team, and grow into a professional backend engineer while contributing meaningfully to your company.",https://www.linkedin.com/in/matthew-olaoye-aba99226a,,69ca44f74e5d9fe46aef7611,Backend Developer Intern,2026-04-09T20:59:15.626Z,2026-04-09T20:59:15.626Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1775768350065_Olaoye_Matthew_Fullstack_Resume.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
