69d83e516469458c6f9205bd,Edwin Aboje,+23409056424235,abojeedwin@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I'd describe myself as someone who is curious, practical, and always trying to improve how things work. I have completed my degree in an Biology Education and my NYSC, and along the way I’ve developed an interest in technology, problem-solving, and building useful solutions.\n\nWhile I do have experience in software development, what really stands out about me is how I approach challenges. I like to understand the bigger picture, ask questions, and figure out not just how something works, but why it works that way. That mindset has helped me both in technical projects and when working with others.\n\nOutside of the technical side, I’m someone who learns quickly, adapts easily, and takes responsibility for whatever I’m working on. I value growth, consistency, and being in environments where I can contribute while also learning from people around me.\n\nAt this stage, I’m looking for opportunities that will stretch me, expose me to new ways of thinking, and help me grow both professionally and personally.",https://www.linkedin.com/in/abojeedwin,,69ca44f74e5d9fe46aef7611,Backend Developer Intern,2026-04-10T00:03:29.376Z,2026-04-10T00:03:29.376Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1775779405392_Edwin_Aboje_Backend_Engineer_CV.docx.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
