69d88678f625e5d1a91175f8,Bolaji Olalekan Olamide,+2347036992232,laycon.devs@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I’m a backend-focused developer who enjoys building real-world systems and exploring how intelligent automation can improve them. I’ve built products like a health center management system with real-time features and a digital verification platform for schools.\nRecently, I’ve been expanding into building autonomous AI-driven systems similar to what I’ve worked on with Allsers; where systems can make decisions and act with minimal human input. As part of that, I’m currently exploring computer vision using OpenCV and YOLOv8, leveraging tools like Roboflow for dataset management, and using Python to handle model integration and APIs.\nWhat excites me is combining backend engineering with AI to build systems that are not just functional, but intelligent and scalable. I’m looking for this internship to gain hands-on experience working on production systems, collaborate with experienced engineers, and deepen my understanding of building robust backend architectures.",https://hyconcode.nathapam.co.uk/,,69ca44f74e5d9fe46aef7611,Backend Developer Intern,2026-04-10T05:11:20.799Z,2026-04-10T05:11:20.799Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1775797877910_Bolaji Olalekan CV_Resume 11_12_25.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69d88daff625e5d1a9117627,Emmanuel Akaolisa,+2347039250896,akaolisaemmanuel@gmail.com,Nigeria,"Hi, I'm Emmanuel Akaolisa, a Business Data Analyst enthusiast and Data Entry Specialist with a strong passion for transforming raw data into meaningful insights that drive informed decision-making. My professional experience spans data collection, validation, analysis, reporting, and administrative data management, equipping me with the ability to maintain accuracy, improve workflows, and support operations in dynamic environments.\n\nWith hands-on expertise in Microsoft Excel, Power BI, SQL, and data visualization, I enjoy solving problems, identifying patterns, and building clear, actionable reports for stakeholders. I bring a strong foundation in data cleaning, record management, and documentation, gained from roles where accuracy, confidentiality, and consistency were essential to success.\n\nI thrive in organized, analytical roles and enjoy helping teams make sense of their data. Whether I’m preparing dashboards, managing large datasets, validating records, or supporting administrative data processes, I approach every task with precision, professionalism, and a commitment to continuous improvement.\n\nWhat I’m great at:\n> Data Cleaning, Validation & Preparation\n> Data Entry & Administrative Record Management\n> Excel (Pivot Tables, Lookups, Charts, Formulas)\n> Power BI & Data Visualization\n> SQL for querying and organizing data\n\nIf you’re looking for someone analytical, organized, and passionate about turning data into clarity and value, I’d be glad to connect.",https://github.com/NuelzHeart,,69ca45374e5d9fe46aef7613,Business Analyst Intern,2026-04-10T05:42:07.967Z,2026-04-10T05:42:07.967Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1775799724984_Emmanuel Akaolisa_CV.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69d8a4e0f625e5d1a911766d,Ogunsakin oluwadamilare adedehinbo ,+23409074703557,oluwadamilareogunsakin@gmail.com,Nigeria,"My name is Ogunsakin Oluwadamilare Adedehinbo, a graduate of Adekule Ajasin University akungba Ondo State,, I graduated with Bsc in Economics. \nI love exploring the Internet for innovation that brings growth and development, I possess strong communication skills and effective time management abilities which allow me to collaborate well with others and handle my tasks efficiently.\n I am also eager to learn and contribute positively to any organization or team I'm part of. ",,,69ca45374e5d9fe46aef7613,Business Analyst Intern,2026-04-10T07:21:04.545Z,2026-04-10T07:21:04.545Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1775805661580_CV_OGUNSAKIN OLUWADAMILARE ADEDEHINBO .pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69d8a53df625e5d1a9117676,Okonkwo Victoria Iruoma,+2347038480137,vickyiru09@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I’ve always been the kind of person who notices how things work and more importantly, how they feel to use. Little things like confusing buttons, unclear flows, or even a smooth, satisfying experience tend to stick with me, also after looking at how a friend designed a company website, and asked me to test the product on how it works and give feedback, the curiosity naturally led me into product design.\nOutside of what is on my CV, I’m someone who genuinely enjoys understanding people. I pay attention to how they think, what frustrates them, and what makes things easier for them even in everyday situations, I also spend time learning on my own, trying new tools, breaking things down, and figuring out better ways to approach problems.\nI’m quite adaptable and open to feedback. I don’t mind starting small or making mistakes, as long as I’m improving. I also care a lot about doing things properly, not just quickly, which sometimes means I’ll take extra time to refine details until they feel right.\nFor me, design isn’t just about making things look good. It’s about making things make sense. And I’m excited about opportunities like this because they push me to grow, think deeper and build solutions that actually matter.","www.behance.net/victoriaokonkwo2,  https://www.figma.com/proto/pQqMHXGQqBMNdyfySw08Cb/SAFESCAN?node-id=471-5927&p=f&t=2s9xLCbFycEwUeZn…",,69ca44c94e5d9fe46aef7610,Product Designer Intern,2026-04-10T07:22:37.826Z,2026-04-10T07:22:37.826Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1775805755183_OKONKWO_VICTORIA_IRUOMA_Resume_2026-03-28.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
