69d900f0f625e5d1a9117db2,Christopher Emah,+2349169772398,intellectsmartestemah@gmail.com,Nigeria,"My name is Christopher Umoh Emah, and I'm an enthusiastic educator and aspiring business analyst residing in Uyo, Nigeria. I have a diverse background, encompassing teaching, technology, and practical customer interaction.\n\nDuring the past few years, I have gained experience as a Mathematics teacher and tutor. My teaching role has helped me to improve my problem-solving skills and learn how to translate complex problems into tangible solutions and recommendations. Such experience naturally helps with developing analysis and clear communication, both critical skills of a business analyst.\n\nIn addition, I have had customer-facing positions such as customer service and sales at both Market Square and Value Plus Shopping Center. These experiences were valuable for understanding user needs, dealing with data (reports and sales figures) and communication with people of different backgrounds.\n\nI am currently undertaking dual degrees in Mathematics and Computer Science from National Open University of Nigeria, both of which has ignited and grown my desire to pursue business analysis focused on data analysis, system enhancement and use of technology in delivering better services and products. In addition, I have practical experience with e-learning and basic data reporting which makes the Recycled Learning initiative very attractive to me.\n\nUltimately, I am driven by problem solving, efficiency improvements and making positive impact, especially with education and youth. I am a quick learner, adaptable and eager to be developed into a competent business analyst who can bring value to your team.",https://www.facebook.com/profile.php?id=61585967393949,,69ca45374e5d9fe46aef7613,Business Analyst Intern,2026-04-10T13:53:52.937Z,2026-04-10T13:53:52.937Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1775829229948_SALES  CHRISTOPHER EMAH.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
