69dbe32df625e5d1a91187d0,Peculiar Uzoma,+23408162145354,uzomapeculiar1@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I’m a final-year student of Economics at CovenantUniversity. I’m passionate about using data and analysis to solve business problems.\nI’ve built strong skills in data analysis, stakeholder engagement, and process improvement through my coursework and projects. I’m a quick learner with a keen interest in technology and business strategy, and I’m excited to apply these skills in a real-world setting like Tobams Group.",uzomapeculiar.github.io,,69ca45374e5d9fe46aef7613,Business Analyst Intern,2026-04-12T18:23:41.326Z,2026-04-12T18:23:41.326Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1776018218053_Uzoma Peculiar's Resume.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69dbea65f625e5d1a9118a49,Mercy Kabingu,+254792014534,nduta6550@gmail.com,Kenya,"My strengths lie in creating clear, user‑focused designs with strong branding and visual storytelling, while my weaknesses include perfectionism, occasionally taking on too much myself, and limited experience in motion design that I am actively improving.",https://dev-kabingu-portfolio.vercel.app/,,686519c9d83df753df842146, Senior Product Designer,2026-04-12T18:54:29.229Z,2026-04-12T18:54:29.229Z,,"Yesterday\nam applying for a design job answer this: explain your strengths and wicknesses\nHere’s a polished way you could frame your strengths and weaknesses for a design job application. The key is to highlight qualities that align with the role while showing self-awareness and growth:\n\nStrengths\nUI/UX Expertise: I have advanced skills in creating clear, engaging interfaces with strong hierarchy and branded consistency. My recent redesign of the Nairobi DevOps Community website demonstrates my ability to deliver modern, user-centered solutions.\n\nIterative Problem-Solving: I thrive in refining designs step by step, incorporating feedback to improve usability and aesthetics.\n\nBranding & Visual Storytelling: I excel at crafting distinctive, emotionally resonant color palettes and layouts that communicate authenticity and connect with users.\n\nTool Adaptability: While I’m highly proficient in Figma and Canva, I can quickly adapt to tools like Adobe XD, Photoshop, and Illustrator when needed.\n\nCommunication: I’m concise and clear when collaborating with teams or clients, ensuring expectations are aligned and deliverables are actionable.\n\nWeaknesses\nPerfectionism: I sometimes spend extra time fine-tuning details, which can slow me down. I’m actively working on balancing polish with efficiency by setting stricter iteration timelines.\n\nDelegation: Because I enjoy hands-on design, I occasionally take on too much myself. I’m learning to trust team members more and leverage collaboration to scale impact.\n\nMotion Design: My strengths are in static UI/UX and branding, but I have less experience with advanced motion graphics. I’m addressing this by exploring animation tools to expand my skill set.\n\nThis framing shows confidence in your strengths while presenting weaknesses as areas of growth. It positions you as self-aware, proactive, and committed to continuous improvement—qualities employers value.\n\nWould you like me to help you tailor this into a short interview-style answer (something you can say naturally in 1–2 minutes), or keep it as a written application response?\n\nmake them smallers\nHere’s a more compact version you can use in an application or interview:\n\nStrengths\n\nSkilled in UI/UX design with clear hierarchy and branded visuals.\n\nStrong at iterative problem-solving and refining designs with feedback.\n\nGood communicator, concise and collaborative.\n\nAdaptable with design tools (Figma, Canva, Adobe suite).\n\nWeaknesses\n\nPerfectionist tendencies can slow me down.\n\nSometimes take on too much instead of delegating.\n\nLimited experience in motion design, but actively learning.\n\nThis keeps it short, professional, and easy to deliver. Would you like me to make it even more interview-ready—like a 30‑second spoken answer?\n\nwrite a cover letter for me\nHere’s a tailored cover letter draft you can adapt for your design job application:\n\n[Your Name]  \n[Your Address]\n[City, Country]\n[Email Address]\n[Phone Number]\n[Date]\n\nHiring Manager  \n[Company Name]\n[Company Address]\n\nDear Hiring Manager,\n\nI am excited to apply for the [Design Position] at [Company Name]. With a background in software engineering and advanced expertise in UI/UX design, I bring a strong blend of technical knowledge and creative vision to crafting user-centered digital experiences.\n\nIn my recent role with the Nairobi DevOps Community, I led the redesign of their website and LMS landing page, focusing on clear hierarchy, branded visuals, and engaging interfaces. My approach emphasizes iterative refinement, ensuring that each design solution is both functional and emotionally resonant. I am proficient in Figma and Canva, and adaptable with tools such as Adobe XD, Photoshop, and Illustrator, which allows me to deliver versatile design solutions across platforms.\n\nBeyond technical skills, I value concise communication and collaboration. I excel at translating complex requirements into actionable design strategies, ensuring alignment with both client goals and user needs. My strengths in branding and visual storytelling help me create distinctive designs that connect authentically with audiences.\n\nI am eager to contribute these skills to [Company Name] and help elevate your design projects with creativity, precision, and user-focused solutions. Thank you for considering my application. I look forward to the opportunity to discuss how my experience and vision can support your team’s success.\n\nSincerely,\n[Your Name]\n\nWould you like me to make this more concise and conversational (ideal for startups or creative agencies), or keep it formal and professional (better for corporate roles)?\n\nam mercy, kirinyaga kenya, nduta6550@gmail.com, 0792014534\nPerfect, Mercy. Here’s your cover letter fully personalized with your details:\n\nMercy Nduta  \nDiaspora Village, Kirinyaga County, Kenya\nnduta6550@gmail.com\n0792014534\n11 April 2026\n\nHiring Manager  \n[Company Name]\n[Company Address]\n\nDear Hiring Manager,\n\nI am writing to express my interest in the [Design Position] at [Company Name]. As a product designer and UI/UX specialist with a background in software engineering, I bring a strong mix of creativity, technical expertise, and user-centered thinking to every project.\n\nRecently, I led the redesign of the Nairobi DevOps Community website and LMS landing page, focusing on clear hierarchy, branded visuals, and engaging interfaces. My strengths lie in iterative problem-solving, branding, and visual storytelling—skills that allow me to deliver designs that are both functional and emotionally resonant. I am proficient in Figma and Canva, and adaptable with Adobe XD, Photoshop, and Illustrator, ensuring versatility across different design environments.\n\nBeyond technical skills, I value concise communication and collaboration. I excel at translating complex requirements into actionable design strategies, aligning client goals with user needs. My passion for authentic, branded design drives me to create distinctive experiences that connect meaningfully with audiences.\n\nI am eager to contribute these strengths to [Company Name] and help elevate your design projects with creativity, precision, and user-focused solutions. Thank you for considering my application. I look forward to the opportunity to discuss how my experience and vision can support your team’s success.\n\nSincerely,\nMercy Nduta\n\nThis version is professional, concise, and tailored to highlight your design strengths.\n\nWould you like me to also shrink this into a shorter, one‑page “startup style” cover letter (more casual, punchy, and creative), or keep it in this formal corporate style?\n\nposition is product designer\nGot it, Mercy. Here’s a polished cover letter tailored specifically for a Product Designer role:\n\nMercy Nduta  \nDiaspora Village, Kirinyaga County, Kenya\nnduta6550@gmail.com\n0792014534\n11 April 2026\n\nHiring Manager  \n[Company Name]\n[Company Address]\n\nDear Hiring Manager,\n\nI am excited to apply for the Product Designer position at [Company Name]. With a background in software engineering and advanced expertise in UI/UX design, I bring a strong mix of creativity, technical knowledge, and user-centered thinking to product development.\n\nIn my recent work with the Nairobi DevOps Community, I led the redesign of their website and LMS landing page, focusing on clear hierarchy, branded visuals, and engaging interfaces. My approach emphasizes iterative refinement and problem-solving, ensuring that each design solution is both functional and emotionally resonant. I am proficient in Figma and Canva, and adaptable with Adobe XD, Photoshop, and Illustrator, which allows me to deliver versatile design solutions across platforms.\n\nBeyond technical skills, I value concise communication and collaboration. I excel at translating complex requirements into actionable design strategies, aligning client goals with user needs. My strengths in branding and visual storytelling help me create distinctive designs that connect authentically with audiences.\n\nI am eager to contribute these strengths to [Company Name] and help elevate your products with creativity, precision, and user-focused solutions. Thank you for considering my application. I look forward to the opportunity to discuss how my experience and vision can support your team’s success.\n\nSincerely,\nMercy Nduta\n\nThis version is direct, professional, and tailored to a product design role.\n\nWould you like me to also craft a shorter, punchier version (ideal if the company is a startup or values creativity over formality), so you have both options depending on where you apply?\n\noraganization is tobams group\nHere’s your cover letter tailored for the Product Designer position at Tobams Group:\n\nMercy Nduta  \nnduta6550@gmail.com\n0792014534\n11 April 2026\n\nHiring Manager  \nTobams Group\n\nDear Hiring Manager,\n\nI am excited to apply for the Product Designer position at Tobams Group. With a background in software engineering and advanced expertise in UI/UX design, I bring a strong mix of creativity, technical knowledge, and user-centered thinking to product development.\n\nIn my recent work with the Nairobi DevOps Community, I led the redesign of their website and LMS landing page, focusing on clear hierarchy, branded visuals, and engaging interfaces. My approach emphasizes iterative refinement and problem-solving, ensuring that each design solution is both functional and emotionally resonant. I am proficient in Figma and Canva, and adaptable with Adobe XD, Photoshop, and Illustrator, which allows me to deliver versatile design solutions across platforms.\n\nBeyond technical skills, I value concise communication and collaboration. I excel at translating complex requirements into actionable design strategies, aligning client goals with user needs. My strengths in branding and visual storytelling help me create distinctive designs that connect authentically with audiences.\n\nI am eager to contribute these strengths to Tobams Group and help elevate your products with creativity, precision, and user-focused solutions. Thank you for considering my application. I look forward to the opportunity to discuss how my experience and vision can support your team’s success.\n\nSincerely,\nMercy Nduta",https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1775910761493_Nduta Resume.pdf,Applied,69da35fbf625e5d1a91182e6,Nakuru,Intern,6865179998f0bca3fcb312ec,Ite Ego International
