69dd29c3f625e5d1a91192f6,Temilayo Adenike Adetona,+2349071520811,temilayoadetona@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am a Banking and Finance final year student at Lagos State University. During the course of my study, I have gained valuable knowledge on banking practices, corporate finance and international finance. I am also an Associate Accounting Technician and a Qualified Associate Chartered Accountant where I have gained in-depth knowledge on communication skills, and strategic financial management. These skills shaped and built my analytical skills helping me effectively apply tools such as Excel and PowerBI to present data in industry acceptable standards. Beyond the classrooms, I served as the campus coordinator of Campus recycling champions LASU chapter where I partnered with several government agencies and international organization and used Power Point Presentations to showcase our missions, visions, objectives, goals and achievement. I also gained valuable experience briefly when I worked as a freelance financial data researcher for a start up company where I supported market research by collecting and gathering industry data to the organizations request. Currently, I am interested in using these skills I have learnt in a Business Analyst internship where I can contribute meaningfully and gain additional experience during the period of the internship. ",https://www.linkedin.com/in/temilayo-adetona-a49663210?utm_source=share_via&utm_content=profile&utm_medium=member_android,,69ca45374e5d9fe46aef7613,Business Analyst Intern,2026-04-13T17:37:07.648Z,2026-04-13T17:37:07.648Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1776101824807_TEMILAYO ADENIKE ADETONA CV .pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69dd2b18f625e5d1a911930b,Ogunjirin Oluwasotun Goodness,+2348158946615,oluwasotunogunjirin@gmail.com,Nigeria,"My name is Oluwasotun Goodness Ogunjirin, and I am a data analyst and scientist. I have a Bachelor's degree in Anatomy from the University of Ilorin, and I am currently pursuing two postgraduate degrees, one being a Master's in Business Administration at Lagos Business School, and the other, a Master's in Public Health at Miva Open University. So far so good, these programmes have really shaped how I approach problems, both from a strategic business standpoint and with a people-first mindset.\nOn the professional side, I have spent over three years at McGeorge Consulting Limited as a Data Scientist and AI Intern. It was a role that also went beyond analysis. I coordinated intern teams, built performance dashboards for stakeholders, contributed to building an AI-powered medical chatbot, and translated technical work into clear documentation for non-technical audiences. That experience really grounded me in what it means to connect data with real business decisions.\nI have also completed job simulations with BCG, Deloitte, and Tata Consultancy Services through Forage, working through scenarios involving root cause analysis, data visualisation, and presenting insights to executive-level audiences. I also completed an Applied Data Science programme at WorldQuant University, and I work comfortably with tools like Python, SQL, Excel, Power BI, Tableau, and Google Looker Studio. Ultimately, I have a passion for using Data to solve real world problems especially in the health and finance sectors, and other sectors as well. Apart from my technical skills and education, I also enjoy watching educational YouTube content, participating in sports and sports analysis especially for football and basketball, and also listening to music and playing the bass guitar. I am also currently learning German through Duolingo.\n",https://www.datascienceportfol.io/oluwasotunogunjirind