69de39cbf625e5d1a911a13b,Chidimma Precious Mgbakogu,+23409134318394,mgbakoguchidinma@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I’m a curious and detail-oriented individual who is passionate about learning and self-improvement. I’ve been developing my skills in data analysis through hands-on projects and continuous learning, and I’m committed to building a strong career in this field.\n\nI take my growth seriously and always look for ways to improve, whether it’s learning new tools or refining my problem-solving skills. I’m also a good listener, which helps me understand problems clearly before working toward solutions.\n\nEven though I’m at the early stage of my career, I’m hardworking, adaptable, and open to challenges. I’m excited about opportunities where I can contribute, learn from experienced professionals, and continue growing both personally and professionally.",https://medium.com/@Mgbakogumma/coffee-order-analysis-24db01ec137b,,69ca45374e5d9fe46aef7613,Business Analyst Intern,2026-04-14T12:57:47.802Z,2026-04-14T12:57:47.802Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1776171465028_Business analyst  intern.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69de3c2cf625e5d1a911a176,Emmanuel Saviour Udoh,+23408075403508,udohe6802@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am Emmanuel Udoh, a Computer Science graduate with a growing passion for business analysis and solving real-world problems using data.\n\nMy journey into tech wasn’t easy at the start I struggled with understanding data concepts like SQL, analysis, and even how to approach problem-solving from a business perspective. There were moments I had to go back, relearn, and question myself. But I stayed consistent, kept practicing, and gradually started improving.\n\nWhat really changed things for me was working on real projects. I began to not just analyze data, but ask why it matters to the business looking at customer behavior, performance trends, and how insights can influence decisions. That shift helped me grow from just working with data to actually thinking like an analyst.\n\nThrough my Google Data Analytics certification and hands-on projects, I’ve developed skills in analyzing data, documenting findings, and presenting insights in a way that stakeholders can understand.\n\nWhat draws me to Tobams group is the opportunity to work more closely with stakeholders, understand business needs, and contribute to process improvement. I’m particularly interested in requirement gathering, documentation, and supporting projects that drive real impact.\n\nAt this stage, I’m focused on learning, adding value, and growing into a well-rounded Business Analyst. I’m resilient, adaptable, and always willing to put in the work to improve.",,,69ca45374e5d9fe46aef7613,Business Analyst Intern,2026-04-14T13:07:56.140Z,2026-04-14T13:07:56.140Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1776172073126_Emmanuel Udoh Resume #1.docx,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69de3fedf625e5d1a911a2b7,Oluwatosin Aina,+2348063255194,ainamichael2013@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am Oluwatosin Michael Aina, a results driven professional with over seven years of experience in accounting, administration, data management, and monitoring & evaluation.\n\nI hold a B.Sc in Accounting (Second Class Upper) from the University of Jos and postgraduate studies from the Nigerian College of Accountancy. My career includes:\n\n- Accounts/Admin Officer roles at Victory Polymer Ltd and Centro Lekki Shopping Centre, managing full-cycle accounting, reconciliations, VAT, payroll, cash control, and compliance.\n- Accounts Officer at Acorn Montessori School, handling finances, budgets, operations, and implementing 100% accountability systems.\n- Volunteer Monitoring & Evaluation/Account Officer at Faith Alive Foundation, focusing on data validation (100% accuracy), analysis, reporting, and QuickBooks bookkeeping.\n- Early teaching experience in Accounts and Business Studies at Nativity Secondary School, igniting my passion for education.\n\nI'm certified as a QuickBooks ProAdvisor, ScrumMaster, and Graduate Member of ANAN. I thrive on solving problems, optimizing processes, ensuring accuracy, and collaborating in teams with strong ethical standards.\n\nSelf-motivated and quick to learn, I enjoy leadership (e.g., Team Lead in community outreach) and am passionate about education, data-driven impact, and innovative solutions for young people, especially in edtech and talent development.\n\nCurrently based in Jos but fully flexible and eager to transition my analytical skills into business analysis roles.\n\n",,,69ca45374e5d9fe46aef7613,Business Analyst Intern,2026-04-14T13:23:57.281Z,2026-04-14T13:23:57.281Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1776173034413_Oluwatosin Michael Aina - JosR.docx,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69de4138f625e5d1a911a2ce,Samuel Effiom,+23408025495002,seffiom077@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I am a Global Management student with a strong foundation in business and management studies, in communication, analytical thinking and creativity, allowing me to approach problems from both structure and innovation.\n\nI have experience in design and digital art. For leisure, I read, write, draw and create stories.",,,69ca44f74e5d9fe46aef7611,Backend Developer Intern,2026-04-14T13:29:28.585Z,2026-04-14T13:29:28.585Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1776173365748_IMG-20260414-WA0015.jpg,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
69de437af625e5d1a911a2f7,Columbus Chiedozie Joseph,+23407061122956,chijonze@gmail.com,Nigeria,"I’m Columbus Chiedozie Joseph, an Economics and Statistics undergraduate at the University of Benin with a strong focus on full-stack web development. I’ve built a solid foundation in the MERN stack, along with TypeScript and Tailwind CSS, and I enjoy turning ideas into functional, user-friendly applications.\n\nI learn best by building, so I’ve worked on several hands-on projects, including a gym booking platform with an admin dashboard and a pet rescue eCommerce store that integrates authentication, cart systems, and crypto-based payments. I’m currently expanding my skills into areas like AI-powered systems and automation, particularly where software can solve real-world business problems.\n\nBeyond technical skills, I’m attentive, easy to work with, and focused on delivering value. I enjoy collaborating, following clear specifications, and continuously improving through feedback. My goal is to grow as a developer while contributing meaningfully to projects that have real impact.\n",https://github.com/Chijonze,,69ca44f74e5d9fe46aef7611,Backend Developer Intern,2026-04-14T13:39:06.247Z,2026-04-14T13:39:06.247Z,,,https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1776173943176_Chiedozie_Joseph_Resume_Updated.pdf,Applied,,,,,Tobams Group
