69e13482f625e5d1a911c241,Banjo Yinka,+2349152660115,banjoyinka0022@gmail.com,Nigeria,"i tend to help people more than i help myself, i work well with teams",https://banjotech.netlify.app/,,69456564af239e8238541b15,Backend & Frontend Developer,2026-04-16T19:12:02.193Z,2026-04-16T19:12:02.193Z,,"Subject: Application for Backend Developer Internship\n\nDear HR\n\nI am writing to express my strong interest in the Backend Developer Internship at Tobams group. As a developer with a deep focus on the MERN stack and a growing specialization in AI engineering, I am eager to contribute to your engineering team while further honing my skills in building scalable, efficient server-side architectures.\n\nMy technical foundation is built on modern web development workflows, with significant experience using Node.js, Express, and MongoDB to power complex applications. I have successfully designed and deployed several full-stack projects, including a comprehensive project management tool and a real estate platform. These projects required me to implement robust RESTful APIs, manage complex database schemas, and ensure seamless integration between the backend and frontend components.\n\nIn addition to core backend development, I am currently immersed in advanced AI engineering. My recent work involves implementing Large Language Models (LLMs), working with vector databases, and utilizing tools like Supabase for database management. This allow me to bring a unique perspective to backend tasks, particularly in how data-driven AI features can be integrated into traditional web architectures to improve user experience.\n\nMy background in accounting has also provided me with a highly analytical mindset and a meticulous approach to data integrity and logic—traits that are essential for high-quality backend engineering. Whether I am automating product data for e-commerce systems or optimizing search filters for property listings, I prioritize clean, maintainable code and performance.\n\nI am particularly drawn to tobams group because of your commitment to [mention a specific project or value of the company]. I am confident that my technical skills, combined with my drive to stay at the forefront of AI and backend technologies, make me a valuable candidate for this internship.\n\nThank you for your time and consideration. I look forward to the possibility of discussing how my background and skills can contribute to the continued success of the backend team at tobams.\n\nSincerely\n\nBanjo Yinka",https://dev-talent-form-test.s3.eu-north-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/1775482469110_BanjoYinkaResume(02) (1).pdf,Applied,69cbeffe49efb29554af674f,Abeokuta,Intern,690c63fc45047c4e4030fee3,Ericsson
69e1353af625e5d1a911c27d,Banjo Yinka,+2349152660115,banjoyinka0022@gmail.com,Nigeria,"hardworking and adaptable, can be too good",https://banjotech.netlify.app/,,693af131a15253f517fcf0b7,Backend Developer,2026-04-16T19:15:06.401Z,2026-04-16T19:15:06.401Z,,"Subject: Application for Backend Developer Internship\n\nDear HR,\n\nI am writing to express my strong interest in the Backend Developer Internship at tobams. As a developer with a deep focus on the MERN stack and a growing specialization in AI engineering, I am eager to contribute to your engineering team while further honing my skills in building scalable, efficient server-side architectures.\n\nMy technical foundation is built on modern web development workflows, with significant experience using Node.js, Express, and MongoDB to power complex applications. I have successfully designed and deployed several full-stack projects, including a comprehensive project management tool and a real estate platform. These projects required me to implement robust RESTful APIs, manage complex database schemas, and ensure seamless integration between the backend and frontend components.\n\nIn addition to core backend development, I am currently immersed in advanced AI engineering. My recent work involves implementing Large Language Models (LLMs), working with vector databases, and utilizing tools like Supabase for database management. This allow me to bring a unique perspective to backend tasks, particularly in how data-driven AI features can be integrated into traditional web architectures to improve user experience.\n\nMy background in accounting has also provided me with a highly analytical mindset and a meticulous approach to data integrity and logic—traits that are essential for high-quality backend engineering. Whether I am automating product data for e-commerce systems or optimizing search filters for property listings, I prioritize clean, maintainable code and performance.\n\nI am particularly drawn to tobams because of